-- WEB verses (5544). Requires books and chapters first.
insert into public.verses (chapter_id, number, osis_ref, text)
select c.id, x.verse, x.ref, x.body
from (values
('JOB', 24, 23, 'JOB.24.23', 'God gives them security, and they rest in it. His eyes are on their ways.'),
('JOB', 24, 24, 'JOB.24.24', 'They are exalted; yet a little while, and they are gone. Yes, they are brought low, they are taken out of the way as all others, and are cut off as the tops of the ears of grain.'),
('JOB', 24, 25, 'JOB.24.25', 'If it isn’t so now, who will prove me a liar, and make my speech worth nothing?”'),
('JOB', 25, 1, 'JOB.25.1', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,'),
('JOB', 25, 2, 'JOB.25.2', '“Dominion and fear are with him. He makes peace in his high places.'),
('JOB', 25, 3, 'JOB.25.3', 'Can his armies be counted? On whom does his light not arise?'),
('JOB', 25, 4, 'JOB.25.4', 'How then can man be just with God? Or how can he who is born of a woman be clean?'),
('JOB', 25, 5, 'JOB.25.5', 'Behold, even the moon has no brightness, and the stars are not pure in his sight;'),
('JOB', 25, 6, 'JOB.25.6', 'How much less man, who is a worm, and the son of man, who is a worm!”'),
('JOB', 26, 1, 'JOB.26.1', 'Then Job answered,'),
('JOB', 26, 2, 'JOB.26.2', '“How have you helped him who is without power! How have you saved the arm that has no strength!'),
('JOB', 26, 3, 'JOB.26.3', 'How have you counseled him who has no wisdom, and plentifully declared sound knowledge!'),
('JOB', 26, 4, 'JOB.26.4', 'To whom have you uttered words? Whose spirit came out of you?'),
('JOB', 26, 5, 'JOB.26.5', '“The departed spirits tremble, those beneath the waters and all that live in them.'),
('JOB', 26, 6, 'JOB.26.6', 'Sheol is naked before God, and Abaddon has no covering.'),
('JOB', 26, 7, 'JOB.26.7', 'He stretches out the north over empty space, and hangs the earth on nothing.'),
('JOB', 26, 8, 'JOB.26.8', 'He binds up the waters in his thick clouds, and the cloud is not burst under them.'),
('JOB', 26, 9, 'JOB.26.9', 'He encloses the face of his throne, and spreads his cloud on it.'),
('JOB', 26, 10, 'JOB.26.10', 'He has described a boundary on the surface of the waters, and to the confines of light and darkness.'),
('JOB', 26, 11, 'JOB.26.11', 'The pillars of heaven tremble and are astonished at his rebuke.'),
('JOB', 26, 12, 'JOB.26.12', 'He stirs up the sea with his power, and by his understanding he strikes through Rahab.'),
('JOB', 26, 13, 'JOB.26.13', 'By his Spirit the heavens are garnished. His hand has pierced the swift serpent.'),
('JOB', 26, 14, 'JOB.26.14', 'Behold, these are but the outskirts of his ways. How small a whisper do we hear of him! But the thunder of his power who can understand?”'),
('JOB', 27, 1, 'JOB.27.1', 'Job again took up his parable, and said,'),
('JOB', 27, 2, 'JOB.27.2', '“As God lives, who has taken away my right, the Almighty, who has made my soul bitter'),
('JOB', 27, 3, 'JOB.27.3', '(for the length of my life is still in me, and the spirit of God is in my nostrils);'),
('JOB', 27, 4, 'JOB.27.4', 'surely my lips will not speak unrighteousness, neither will my tongue utter deceit.'),
('JOB', 27, 5, 'JOB.27.5', 'Far be it from me that I should justify you. Until I die I will not put away my integrity from me.'),
('JOB', 27, 6, 'JOB.27.6', 'I hold fast to my righteousness, and will not let it go. My heart will not reproach me so long as I live.'),
('JOB', 27, 7, 'JOB.27.7', '“Let my enemy be as the wicked. Let him who rises up against me be as the unrighteous.'),
('JOB', 27, 8, 'JOB.27.8', 'For what is the hope of the godless, when he is cut off, when God takes away his life?'),
('JOB', 27, 9, 'JOB.27.9', 'Will God hear his cry when trouble comes on him?'),
('JOB', 27, 10, 'JOB.27.10', 'Will he delight himself in the Almighty, and call on God at all times?'),
('JOB', 27, 11, 'JOB.27.11', 'I will teach you about the hand of God. I will not conceal that which is with the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 27, 12, 'JOB.27.12', 'Behold, all of you have seen it yourselves; why then have you become altogether vain?'),
('JOB', 27, 13, 'JOB.27.13', '“This is the portion of a wicked man with God, the heritage of oppressors, which they receive from the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 27, 14, 'JOB.27.14', 'If his children are multiplied, it is for the sword. His offspring will not be satisfied with bread.'),
('JOB', 27, 15, 'JOB.27.15', 'Those who remain of him will be buried in death. His widows will make no lamentation.'),
('JOB', 27, 16, 'JOB.27.16', 'Though he heap up silver as the dust, and prepare clothing as the clay;'),
('JOB', 27, 17, 'JOB.27.17', 'he may prepare it, but the just will put it on, and the innocent will divide the silver.'),
('JOB', 27, 18, 'JOB.27.18', 'He builds his house as the moth, as a booth which the watchman makes.'),
('JOB', 27, 19, 'JOB.27.19', 'He lies down rich, but he will not do so again. He opens his eyes, and he is not.'),
('JOB', 27, 20, 'JOB.27.20', 'Terrors overtake him like waters. A storm steals him away in the night.'),
('JOB', 27, 21, 'JOB.27.21', 'The east wind carries him away, and he departs. It sweeps him out of his place.'),
('JOB', 27, 22, 'JOB.27.22', 'For it hurls at him, and does not spare, as he flees away from his hand.'),
('JOB', 27, 23, 'JOB.27.23', 'Men will clap their hands at him, and will hiss him out of his place.'),
('JOB', 28, 1, 'JOB.28.1', '“Surely there is a mine for silver, and a place for gold which they refine.'),
('JOB', 28, 2, 'JOB.28.2', 'Iron is taken out of the earth, and copper is smelted out of the ore.'),
('JOB', 28, 3, 'JOB.28.3', 'Man sets an end to darkness, and searches out, to the furthest bound, the stones of obscurity and of thick darkness.'),
('JOB', 28, 4, 'JOB.28.4', 'He breaks open a shaft away from where people live. They are forgotten by the foot. They hang far from men, they swing back and forth.'),
('JOB', 28, 5, 'JOB.28.5', 'As for the earth, out of it comes bread. Underneath it is turned up as it were by fire.'),
('JOB', 28, 6, 'JOB.28.6', 'Sapphires come from its rocks. It has dust of gold.'),
('JOB', 28, 7, 'JOB.28.7', 'That path no bird of prey knows, neither has the falcon’s eye seen it.'),
('JOB', 28, 8, 'JOB.28.8', 'The proud animals have not trodden it, nor has the fierce lion passed by there.'),
('JOB', 28, 9, 'JOB.28.9', 'He puts his hand on the flinty rock, and he overturns the mountains by the roots.'),
('JOB', 28, 10, 'JOB.28.10', 'He cuts out channels among the rocks. His eye sees every precious thing.'),
('JOB', 28, 11, 'JOB.28.11', 'He binds the streams that they don’t trickle. The thing that is hidden he brings out to light.'),
('JOB', 28, 12, 'JOB.28.12', '“But where will wisdom be found? Where is the place of understanding?'),
('JOB', 28, 13, 'JOB.28.13', 'Man doesn’t know its price, and it isn’t found in the land of the living.'),
('JOB', 28, 14, 'JOB.28.14', 'The deep says, ‘It isn’t in me.’ The sea says, ‘It isn’t with me.’'),
('JOB', 28, 15, 'JOB.28.15', 'It can’t be gotten for gold, neither will silver be weighed for its price.'),
('JOB', 28, 16, 'JOB.28.16', 'It can’t be valued with the gold of Ophir, with the precious onyx, or the sapphire.'),
('JOB', 28, 17, 'JOB.28.17', 'Gold and glass can’t equal it, neither will it be exchanged for jewels of fine gold.'),
('JOB', 28, 18, 'JOB.28.18', 'No mention will be made of coral or of crystal. Yes, the price of wisdom is above rubies.'),
('JOB', 28, 19, 'JOB.28.19', 'The topaz of Ethiopia will not equal it. It won’t be valued with pure gold.'),
('JOB', 28, 20, 'JOB.28.20', 'Where then does wisdom come from? Where is the place of understanding?'),
('JOB', 28, 21, 'JOB.28.21', 'Seeing it is hidden from the eyes of all living, and kept close from the birds of the sky.'),
('JOB', 28, 22, 'JOB.28.22', 'Destruction and Death say, ‘We have heard a rumor of it with our ears.’'),
('JOB', 28, 23, 'JOB.28.23', '“God understands its way, and he knows its place.'),
('JOB', 28, 24, 'JOB.28.24', 'For he looks to the ends of the earth, and sees under the whole sky.'),
('JOB', 28, 25, 'JOB.28.25', 'He establishes the force of the wind. Yes, he measures out the waters by measure.'),
('JOB', 28, 26, 'JOB.28.26', 'When he made a decree for the rain, and a way for the lightning of the thunder,'),
('JOB', 28, 27, 'JOB.28.27', 'then he saw it, and declared it. He established it, yes, and searched it out.'),
('JOB', 28, 28, 'JOB.28.28', 'To man he said, ‘Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom. To depart from evil is understanding.’”'),
('JOB', 29, 1, 'JOB.29.1', 'Job again took up his parable, and said,'),
('JOB', 29, 2, 'JOB.29.2', '“Oh that I were as in the months of old, as in the days when God watched over me;'),
('JOB', 29, 3, 'JOB.29.3', 'when his lamp shone on my head, and by his light I walked through darkness,'),
('JOB', 29, 4, 'JOB.29.4', 'as I was in my prime, when the friendship of God was in my tent,'),
('JOB', 29, 5, 'JOB.29.5', 'when the Almighty was yet with me, and my children were around me,'),
('JOB', 29, 6, 'JOB.29.6', 'when my steps were washed with butter, and the rock poured out streams of oil for me,'),
('JOB', 29, 7, 'JOB.29.7', 'when I went out to the city gate, when I prepared my seat in the street.'),
('JOB', 29, 8, 'JOB.29.8', 'The young men saw me and hid themselves. The aged rose up and stood.'),
('JOB', 29, 9, 'JOB.29.9', 'The princes refrained from talking, and laid their hand on their mouth.'),
('JOB', 29, 10, 'JOB.29.10', 'The voice of the nobles was hushed, and their tongue stuck to the roof of their mouth.'),
('JOB', 29, 11, 'JOB.29.11', 'For when the ear heard me, then it blessed me, and when the eye saw me, it commended me,'),
('JOB', 29, 12, 'JOB.29.12', 'because I delivered the poor who cried, and the fatherless also, who had no one to help him,'),
('JOB', 29, 13, 'JOB.29.13', 'the blessing of him who was ready to perish came on me, and I caused the widow’s heart to sing for joy.'),
('JOB', 29, 14, 'JOB.29.14', 'I put on righteousness, and it clothed me. My justice was as a robe and a diadem.'),
('JOB', 29, 15, 'JOB.29.15', 'I was eyes to the blind, and feet to the lame.'),
('JOB', 29, 16, 'JOB.29.16', 'I was a father to the needy. I researched the cause of him whom I didn’t know.'),
('JOB', 29, 17, 'JOB.29.17', 'I broke the jaws of the unrighteous and plucked the prey out of his teeth.'),
('JOB', 29, 18, 'JOB.29.18', 'Then I said, ‘I will die in my own house, I will count my days as the sand.'),
('JOB', 29, 19, 'JOB.29.19', 'My root is spread out to the waters. The dew lies all night on my branch.'),
('JOB', 29, 20, 'JOB.29.20', 'My glory is fresh in me. My bow is renewed in my hand.’'),
('JOB', 29, 21, 'JOB.29.21', '“Men listened to me, waited, and kept silence for my counsel.'),
('JOB', 29, 22, 'JOB.29.22', 'After my words they didn’t speak again. My speech fell on them.'),
('JOB', 29, 23, 'JOB.29.23', 'They waited for me as for the rain. Their mouths drank as with the spring rain.'),
('JOB', 29, 24, 'JOB.29.24', 'I smiled on them when they had no confidence. They didn’t reject the light of my face.'),
('JOB', 29, 25, 'JOB.29.25', 'I chose out their way, and sat as chief. I lived as a king in the army, as one who comforts the mourners.'),
('JOB', 30, 1, 'JOB.30.1', '“But now those who are younger than I have me in derision, whose fathers I considered unworthy to put with my sheep dogs.'),
('JOB', 30, 2, 'JOB.30.2', 'Of what use is the strength of their hands to me, men in whom ripe age has perished?'),
('JOB', 30, 3, 'JOB.30.3', 'They are gaunt from lack and famine. They gnaw the dry ground, in the gloom of waste and desolation.'),
('JOB', 30, 4, 'JOB.30.4', 'They pluck salt herbs by the bushes. The roots of the broom tree are their food.'),
('JOB', 30, 5, 'JOB.30.5', 'They are driven out from among men. They cry after them as after a thief,'),
('JOB', 30, 6, 'JOB.30.6', 'so that they live in frightful valleys, and in holes of the earth and of the rocks.'),
('JOB', 30, 7, 'JOB.30.7', 'They bray among the bushes. They are gathered together under the nettles.'),
('JOB', 30, 8, 'JOB.30.8', 'They are children of fools, yes, children of wicked men. They were flogged out of the land.'),
('JOB', 30, 9, 'JOB.30.9', '“Now I have become their song. Yes, I am a byword to them.'),
('JOB', 30, 10, 'JOB.30.10', 'They abhor me, they stand aloof from me, and don’t hesitate to spit in my face.'),
('JOB', 30, 11, 'JOB.30.11', 'For he has untied his cord, and afflicted me; and they have thrown off restraint before me.'),
('JOB', 30, 12, 'JOB.30.12', 'On my right hand rise the rabble. They thrust aside my feet. They cast their ways of destruction up against me.'),
('JOB', 30, 13, 'JOB.30.13', 'They mar my path. They promote my destruction without anyone’s help.'),
('JOB', 30, 14, 'JOB.30.14', 'As through a wide breach they come. They roll themselves in amid the ruin.'),
('JOB', 30, 15, 'JOB.30.15', 'Terrors have turned on me. They chase my honor as the wind. My welfare has passed away as a cloud.'),
('JOB', 30, 16, 'JOB.30.16', '“Now my soul is poured out within me. Days of affliction have taken hold of me.'),
('JOB', 30, 17, 'JOB.30.17', 'In the night season my bones are pierced in me, and the pains that gnaw me take no rest.'),
('JOB', 30, 18, 'JOB.30.18', 'My garment is disfigured by great force. It binds me about as the collar of my tunic.'),
('JOB', 30, 19, 'JOB.30.19', 'He has cast me into the mire. I have become like dust and ashes.'),
('JOB', 30, 20, 'JOB.30.20', 'I cry to you, and you do not answer me. I stand up, and you gaze at me.'),
('JOB', 30, 21, 'JOB.30.21', 'You have turned to be cruel to me. With the might of your hand you persecute me.'),
('JOB', 30, 22, 'JOB.30.22', 'You lift me up to the wind, and drive me with it. You dissolve me in the storm.'),
('JOB', 30, 23, 'JOB.30.23', 'For I know that you will bring me to death, to the house appointed for all living.'),
('JOB', 30, 24, 'JOB.30.24', '“However doesn’t one stretch out a hand in his fall? Or in his calamity therefore cry for help?'),
('JOB', 30, 25, 'JOB.30.25', 'Didn’t I weep for him who was in trouble? Wasn’t my soul grieved for the needy?'),
('JOB', 30, 26, 'JOB.30.26', 'When I looked for good, then evil came. When I waited for light, darkness came.'),
('JOB', 30, 27, 'JOB.30.27', 'My heart is troubled, and doesn’t rest. Days of affliction have come on me.'),
('JOB', 30, 28, 'JOB.30.28', 'I go mourning without the sun. I stand up in the assembly, and cry for help.'),
('JOB', 30, 29, 'JOB.30.29', 'I am a brother to jackals, and a companion to ostriches.'),
('JOB', 30, 30, 'JOB.30.30', 'My skin grows black and peels from me. My bones are burned with heat.'),
('JOB', 30, 31, 'JOB.30.31', 'Therefore my harp has turned to mourning, and my pipe into the voice of those who weep.'),
('JOB', 31, 1, 'JOB.31.1', '“I made a covenant with my eyes; how then should I look lustfully at a young woman?'),
('JOB', 31, 2, 'JOB.31.2', 'For what is the portion from God above, and the heritage from the Almighty on high?'),
('JOB', 31, 3, 'JOB.31.3', 'Is it not calamity to the unrighteous, and disaster to the workers of iniquity?'),
('JOB', 31, 4, 'JOB.31.4', 'Doesn’t he see my ways, and count all my steps?'),
('JOB', 31, 5, 'JOB.31.5', '“If I have walked with falsehood, and my foot has hurried to deceit'),
('JOB', 31, 6, 'JOB.31.6', '(let me be weighed in an even balance, that God may know my integrity);'),
('JOB', 31, 7, 'JOB.31.7', 'if my step has turned out of the way, if my heart walked after my eyes, if any defilement has stuck to my hands,'),
('JOB', 31, 8, 'JOB.31.8', 'then let me sow, and let another eat. Yes, let the produce of my field be rooted out.'),
('JOB', 31, 9, 'JOB.31.9', '“If my heart has been enticed to a woman, and I have laid wait at my neighbor’s door,'),
('JOB', 31, 10, 'JOB.31.10', 'then let my wife grind for another, and let others sleep with her.'),
('JOB', 31, 11, 'JOB.31.11', 'For that would be a heinous crime. Yes, it would be an iniquity to be punished by the judges,'),
('JOB', 31, 12, 'JOB.31.12', 'for it is a fire that consumes to destruction, and would root out all my increase.'),
('JOB', 31, 13, 'JOB.31.13', '“If I have despised the cause of my male servant or of my female servant, when they contended with me,'),
('JOB', 31, 14, 'JOB.31.14', 'what then will I do when God rises up? When he visits, what will I answer him?'),
('JOB', 31, 15, 'JOB.31.15', 'Didn’t he who made me in the womb make him? Didn’t one fashion us in the womb?'),
('JOB', 31, 16, 'JOB.31.16', '“If I have withheld the poor from their desire, or have caused the eyes of the widow to fail,'),
('JOB', 31, 17, 'JOB.31.17', 'or have eaten my morsel alone, and the fatherless has not eaten of it'),
('JOB', 31, 18, 'JOB.31.18', '(no, from my youth he grew up with me as with a father, I have guided her from my mother’s womb);'),
('JOB', 31, 19, 'JOB.31.19', 'if I have seen any perish for want of clothing, or that the needy had no covering;'),
('JOB', 31, 20, 'JOB.31.20', 'if his heart hasn’t blessed me, if he hasn’t been warmed with my sheep’s fleece;'),
('JOB', 31, 21, 'JOB.31.21', 'if I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless, because I saw my help in the gate;'),
('JOB', 31, 22, 'JOB.31.22', 'then let my shoulder fall from the shoulder blade, and my arm be broken from the bone.'),
('JOB', 31, 23, 'JOB.31.23', 'For calamity from God is a terror to me. Because of his majesty, I can do nothing.'),
('JOB', 31, 24, 'JOB.31.24', '“If I have made gold my hope, and have said to the fine gold, ‘You are my confidence;’'),
('JOB', 31, 25, 'JOB.31.25', 'If I have rejoiced because my wealth was great, and because my hand had gotten much;'),
('JOB', 31, 26, 'JOB.31.26', 'if I have seen the sun when it shined, or the moon moving in splendor,'),
('JOB', 31, 27, 'JOB.31.27', 'and my heart has been secretly enticed, and my hand threw a kiss from my mouth;'),
('JOB', 31, 28, 'JOB.31.28', 'this also would be an iniquity to be punished by the judges, for I would have denied the God who is above.'),
('JOB', 31, 29, 'JOB.31.29', '“If I have rejoiced at the destruction of him who hated me, or lifted up myself when evil found him'),
('JOB', 31, 30, 'JOB.31.30', '(I have certainly not allowed my mouth to sin by asking his life with a curse);'),
('JOB', 31, 31, 'JOB.31.31', 'if the men of my tent have not said, ‘Who can find one who has not been filled with his meat?’'),
('JOB', 31, 32, 'JOB.31.32', '(the foreigner has not camped in the street, but I have opened my doors to the traveler);'),
('JOB', 31, 33, 'JOB.31.33', 'if like Adam I have covered my transgressions, by hiding my iniquity in my heart,'),
('JOB', 31, 34, 'JOB.31.34', 'because I feared the great multitude, and the contempt of families terrified me, so that I kept silence, and didn’t go out of the door—'),
('JOB', 31, 35, 'JOB.31.35', 'oh that I had one to hear me! Behold, here is my signature! Let the Almighty answer me! Let the accuser write my indictment!'),
('JOB', 31, 36, 'JOB.31.36', 'Surely I would carry it on my shoulder, and I would bind it to me as a crown.'),
('JOB', 31, 37, 'JOB.31.37', 'I would declare to him the number of my steps. I would go near to him like a prince.'),
('JOB', 31, 38, 'JOB.31.38', 'If my land cries out against me, and its furrows weep together;'),
('JOB', 31, 39, 'JOB.31.39', 'if I have eaten its fruits without money, or have caused its owners to lose their life,'),
('JOB', 31, 40, 'JOB.31.40', 'let briers grow instead of wheat, and stinkweed instead of barley.” The words of Job are ended.'),
('JOB', 32, 1, 'JOB.32.1', 'So these three men ceased to answer Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes.'),
('JOB', 32, 2, 'JOB.32.2', 'Then the wrath of Elihu the son of Barachel, the Buzite, of the family of Ram, was kindled against Job. His wrath was kindled because he justified himself rather than God.'),
('JOB', 32, 3, 'JOB.32.3', 'Also his wrath was kindled against his three friends, because they had found no answer, and yet had condemned Job.'),
('JOB', 32, 4, 'JOB.32.4', 'Now Elihu had waited to speak to Job, because they were older than he.'),
('JOB', 32, 5, 'JOB.32.5', 'When Elihu saw that there was no answer in the mouth of these three men, his wrath was kindled.'),
('JOB', 32, 6, 'JOB.32.6', 'Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered, “I am young, and you are very old. Therefore I held back, and didn’t dare show you my opinion.'),
('JOB', 32, 7, 'JOB.32.7', 'I said, ‘Days should speak, and multitude of years should teach wisdom.’'),
('JOB', 32, 8, 'JOB.32.8', 'But there is a spirit in man, and the Spirit of the Almighty gives them understanding.'),
('JOB', 32, 9, 'JOB.32.9', 'It is not the great who are wise, nor the aged who understand justice.'),
('JOB', 32, 10, 'JOB.32.10', 'Therefore I said, ‘Listen to me; I also will show my opinion.’'),
('JOB', 32, 11, 'JOB.32.11', '“Behold, I waited for your words, and I listened for your reasoning, while you searched out what to say.'),
('JOB', 32, 12, 'JOB.32.12', 'Yes, I gave you my full attention, but there was no one who convinced Job, or who answered his words, among you.'),
('JOB', 32, 13, 'JOB.32.13', 'Beware lest you say, ‘We have found wisdom. God may refute him, not man;’'),
('JOB', 32, 14, 'JOB.32.14', 'for he has not directed his words against me; neither will I answer him with your speeches.'),
('JOB', 32, 15, 'JOB.32.15', '“They are amazed. They answer no more. They don’t have a word to say.'),
('JOB', 32, 16, 'JOB.32.16', 'Shall I wait, because they don’t speak, because they stand still, and answer no more?'),
('JOB', 32, 17, 'JOB.32.17', 'I also will answer my part, and I also will show my opinion.'),
('JOB', 32, 18, 'JOB.32.18', 'For I am full of words. The spirit within me constrains me.'),
('JOB', 32, 19, 'JOB.32.19', 'Behold, my breast is as wine which has no vent; like new wineskins it is ready to burst.'),
('JOB', 32, 20, 'JOB.32.20', 'I will speak, that I may be refreshed. I will open my lips and answer.'),
('JOB', 32, 21, 'JOB.32.21', 'Please don’t let me respect any man’s person, neither will I give flattering titles to any man.'),
('JOB', 32, 22, 'JOB.32.22', 'For I don’t know how to give flattering titles, or else my Maker would soon take me away.'),
('JOB', 33, 1, 'JOB.33.1', '“However, Job, please hear my speech, and listen to all my words.'),
('JOB', 33, 2, 'JOB.33.2', 'See now, I have opened my mouth. My tongue has spoken in my mouth.'),
('JOB', 33, 3, 'JOB.33.3', 'My words will utter the uprightness of my heart. That which my lips know they will speak sincerely.'),
('JOB', 33, 4, 'JOB.33.4', 'The Spirit of God has made me, and the breath of the Almighty gives me life.'),
('JOB', 33, 5, 'JOB.33.5', 'If you can, answer me. Set your words in order before me, and stand up.'),
('JOB', 33, 6, 'JOB.33.6', 'Behold, I am toward God even as you are. I am also formed out of the clay.'),
('JOB', 33, 7, 'JOB.33.7', 'Behold, my terror will not make you afraid, neither will my pressure be heavy on you.'),
('JOB', 33, 8, 'JOB.33.8', '“Surely you have spoken in my hearing, I have heard the voice of your words, saying,'),
('JOB', 33, 9, 'JOB.33.9', '‘I am clean, without disobedience. I am innocent, neither is there iniquity in me.'),
('JOB', 33, 10, 'JOB.33.10', 'Behold, he finds occasions against me. He counts me for his enemy.'),
('JOB', 33, 11, 'JOB.33.11', 'He puts my feet in the stocks. He marks all my paths.’'),
('JOB', 33, 12, 'JOB.33.12', '“Behold, I will answer you. In this you are not just, for God is greater than man.'),
('JOB', 33, 13, 'JOB.33.13', 'Why do you strive against him, because he doesn’t give account of any of his matters?'),
('JOB', 33, 14, 'JOB.33.14', 'For God speaks once, yes twice, though man pays no attention.'),
('JOB', 33, 15, 'JOB.33.15', 'In a dream, in a vision of the night, when deep sleep falls on men, in slumbering on the bed,'),
('JOB', 33, 16, 'JOB.33.16', 'then he opens the ears of men, and seals their instruction,'),
('JOB', 33, 17, 'JOB.33.17', 'that he may withdraw man from his purpose, and hide pride from man.'),
('JOB', 33, 18, 'JOB.33.18', 'He keeps back his soul from the pit, and his life from perishing by the sword.'),
('JOB', 33, 19, 'JOB.33.19', '“He is chastened also with pain on his bed, with continual strife in his bones,'),
('JOB', 33, 20, 'JOB.33.20', 'so that his life abhors bread, and his soul dainty food.'),
('JOB', 33, 21, 'JOB.33.21', 'His flesh is so consumed away that it can’t be seen. His bones that were not seen stick out.'),
('JOB', 33, 22, 'JOB.33.22', 'Yes, his soul draws near to the pit, and his life to the destroyers.'),
('JOB', 33, 23, 'JOB.33.23', '“If there is beside him an angel, an interpreter, one among a thousand, to show to man what is right for him,'),
('JOB', 33, 24, 'JOB.33.24', 'then God is gracious to him, and says, ‘Deliver him from going down to the pit, I have found a ransom.’'),
('JOB', 33, 25, 'JOB.33.25', 'His flesh will be fresher than a child’s. He returns to the days of his youth.'),
('JOB', 33, 26, 'JOB.33.26', 'He prays to God, and he is favorable to him, so that he sees his face with joy. He restores to man his righteousness.'),
('JOB', 33, 27, 'JOB.33.27', 'He sings before men, and says, ‘I have sinned, and perverted that which was right, and it didn’t profit me.'),
('JOB', 33, 28, 'JOB.33.28', 'He has redeemed my soul from going into the pit. My life will see the light.’'),
('JOB', 33, 29, 'JOB.33.29', '“Behold, God does all these things, twice, yes three times, with a man,'),
('JOB', 33, 30, 'JOB.33.30', 'to bring back his soul from the pit, that he may be enlightened with the light of the living.'),
('JOB', 33, 31, 'JOB.33.31', 'Mark well, Job, and listen to me. Hold your peace, and I will speak.'),
('JOB', 33, 32, 'JOB.33.32', 'If you have anything to say, answer me. Speak, for I desire to justify you.'),
('JOB', 33, 33, 'JOB.33.33', 'If not, listen to me. Hold your peace, and I will teach you wisdom.”'),
('JOB', 34, 1, 'JOB.34.1', 'Moreover Elihu answered,'),
('JOB', 34, 2, 'JOB.34.2', '“Hear my words, you wise men. Give ear to me, you who have knowledge.'),
('JOB', 34, 3, 'JOB.34.3', 'For the ear tries words, as the palate tastes food.'),
('JOB', 34, 4, 'JOB.34.4', 'Let us choose for us that which is right. Let us know among ourselves what is good.'),
('JOB', 34, 5, 'JOB.34.5', 'For Job has said, ‘I am righteous, God has taken away my right.'),
('JOB', 34, 6, 'JOB.34.6', 'Notwithstanding my right I am considered a liar. My wound is incurable, though I am without disobedience.’'),
('JOB', 34, 7, 'JOB.34.7', 'What man is like Job, who drinks scorn like water,'),
('JOB', 34, 8, 'JOB.34.8', 'who goes in company with the workers of iniquity, and walks with wicked men?'),
('JOB', 34, 9, 'JOB.34.9', 'For he has said, ‘It profits a man nothing that he should delight himself with God.’'),
('JOB', 34, 10, 'JOB.34.10', '“Therefore listen to me, you men of understanding: far be it from God, that he should do wickedness, from the Almighty, that he should commit iniquity.'),
('JOB', 34, 11, 'JOB.34.11', 'For the work of a man he will give to him, and cause every man to find according to his ways.'),
('JOB', 34, 12, 'JOB.34.12', 'Yes surely, God will not do wickedly, neither will the Almighty pervert justice.'),
('JOB', 34, 13, 'JOB.34.13', 'Who put him in charge of the earth? Or who has appointed him over the whole world?'),
('JOB', 34, 14, 'JOB.34.14', 'If he set his heart on himself, if he gathered to himself his spirit and his breath,'),
('JOB', 34, 15, 'JOB.34.15', 'all flesh would perish together, and man would turn again to dust.'),
('JOB', 34, 16, 'JOB.34.16', '“If now you have understanding, hear this. Listen to the voice of my words.'),
('JOB', 34, 17, 'JOB.34.17', 'Should even one who hates justice govern? Will you condemn him who is righteous and mighty,'),
('JOB', 34, 18, 'JOB.34.18', 'who says to a king, ‘Vile!’ or to nobles, ‘Wicked!’?'),
('JOB', 34, 19, 'JOB.34.19', 'He doesn’t respect the persons of princes, nor respect the rich more than the poor, for they all are the work of his hands.'),
('JOB', 34, 20, 'JOB.34.20', 'In a moment they die, even at midnight. The people are shaken and pass away. The mighty are taken away without a hand.'),
('JOB', 34, 21, 'JOB.34.21', '“For his eyes are on the ways of a man. He sees all his goings.'),
('JOB', 34, 22, 'JOB.34.22', 'There is no darkness, nor thick gloom, where the workers of iniquity may hide themselves.'),
('JOB', 34, 23, 'JOB.34.23', 'For he doesn’t need to consider a man further, that he should go before God in judgment.'),
('JOB', 34, 24, 'JOB.34.24', 'He breaks mighty men in pieces in ways past finding out, and sets others in their place.'),
('JOB', 34, 25, 'JOB.34.25', 'Therefore he takes knowledge of their works. He overturns them in the night, so that they are destroyed.'),
('JOB', 34, 26, 'JOB.34.26', 'He strikes them as wicked men in the open sight of others;'),
('JOB', 34, 27, 'JOB.34.27', 'because they turned away from following him, and wouldn’t pay attention to any of his ways,'),
('JOB', 34, 28, 'JOB.34.28', 'so that they caused the cry of the poor to come to him. He heard the cry of the afflicted.'),
('JOB', 34, 29, 'JOB.34.29', 'When he gives quietness, who then can condemn? When he hides his face, who then can see him? He is over a nation or a man alike,'),
('JOB', 34, 30, 'JOB.34.30', 'that the godless man may not reign, that there be no one to ensnare the people.'),
('JOB', 34, 31, 'JOB.34.31', '“For has any said to God, ‘I am guilty, but I will not offend any more.'),
('JOB', 34, 32, 'JOB.34.32', 'Teach me that which I don’t see. If I have done iniquity, I will do it no more’?'),
('JOB', 34, 33, 'JOB.34.33', 'Shall his recompense be as you desire, that you refuse it? For you must choose, and not I. Therefore speak what you know.'),
('JOB', 34, 34, 'JOB.34.34', 'Men of understanding will tell me, yes, every wise man who hears me:'),
('JOB', 34, 35, 'JOB.34.35', '‘Job speaks without knowledge. His words are without wisdom.’'),
('JOB', 34, 36, 'JOB.34.36', 'I wish that Job were tried to the end, because of his answering like wicked men.'),
('JOB', 34, 37, 'JOB.34.37', 'For he adds rebellion to his sin. He claps his hands among us, and multiplies his words against God.”'),
('JOB', 35, 1, 'JOB.35.1', 'Moreover Elihu answered,'),
('JOB', 35, 2, 'JOB.35.2', '“Do you think this to be your right, or do you say, ‘My righteousness is more than God’s,’'),
('JOB', 35, 3, 'JOB.35.3', 'that you ask, ‘What advantage will it be to you? What profit will I have, more than if I had sinned?’'),
('JOB', 35, 4, 'JOB.35.4', 'I will answer you, and your companions with you.'),
('JOB', 35, 5, 'JOB.35.5', 'Look to the skies, and see. See the skies, which are higher than you.'),
('JOB', 35, 6, 'JOB.35.6', 'If you have sinned, what effect do you have against him? If your transgressions are multiplied, what do you do to him?'),
('JOB', 35, 7, 'JOB.35.7', 'If you are righteous, what do you give him? Or what does he receive from your hand?'),
('JOB', 35, 8, 'JOB.35.8', 'Your wickedness may hurt a man as you are, and your righteousness may profit a son of man.'),
('JOB', 35, 9, 'JOB.35.9', '“By reason of the multitude of oppressions they cry out. They cry for help by reason of the arm of the mighty.'),
('JOB', 35, 10, 'JOB.35.10', 'But no one says, ‘Where is God my Maker, who gives songs in the night,'),
('JOB', 35, 11, 'JOB.35.11', 'who teaches us more than the animals of the earth, and makes us wiser than the birds of the sky?’'),
('JOB', 35, 12, 'JOB.35.12', 'There they cry, but no one answers, because of the pride of evil men.'),
('JOB', 35, 13, 'JOB.35.13', 'Surely God will not hear an empty cry, neither will the Almighty regard it.'),
('JOB', 35, 14, 'JOB.35.14', 'How much less when you say you don’t see him. The cause is before him, and you wait for him!'),
('JOB', 35, 15, 'JOB.35.15', 'But now, because he has not visited in his anger, neither does he greatly regard arrogance,'),
('JOB', 35, 16, 'JOB.35.16', 'therefore Job opens his mouth with empty talk, and he multiplies words without knowledge.”'),
('JOB', 36, 1, 'JOB.36.1', 'Elihu also continued, and said,'),
('JOB', 36, 2, 'JOB.36.2', '“Bear with me a little, and I will show you; for I still have something to say on God’s behalf.'),
('JOB', 36, 3, 'JOB.36.3', 'I will get my knowledge from afar, and will ascribe righteousness to my Maker.'),
('JOB', 36, 4, 'JOB.36.4', 'For truly my words are not false. One who is perfect in knowledge is with you.'),
('JOB', 36, 5, 'JOB.36.5', '“Behold, God is mighty, and doesn’t despise anyone. He is mighty in strength of understanding.'),
('JOB', 36, 6, 'JOB.36.6', 'He doesn’t preserve the life of the wicked, but gives justice to the afflicted.'),
('JOB', 36, 7, 'JOB.36.7', 'He doesn’t withdraw his eyes from the righteous, but with kings on the throne, he sets them forever, and they are exalted.'),
('JOB', 36, 8, 'JOB.36.8', 'If they are bound in fetters, and are taken in the cords of afflictions,'),
('JOB', 36, 9, 'JOB.36.9', 'then he shows them their work, and their transgressions, that they have behaved themselves proudly.'),
('JOB', 36, 10, 'JOB.36.10', 'He also opens their ears to instruction, and commands that they return from iniquity.'),
('JOB', 36, 11, 'JOB.36.11', 'If they listen and serve him, they will spend their days in prosperity, and their years in pleasures.'),
('JOB', 36, 12, 'JOB.36.12', 'But if they don’t listen, they will perish by the sword; they will die without knowledge.'),
('JOB', 36, 13, 'JOB.36.13', '“But those who are godless in heart lay up anger. They don’t cry for help when he binds them.'),
('JOB', 36, 14, 'JOB.36.14', 'They die in youth. Their life perishes among the unclean.'),
('JOB', 36, 15, 'JOB.36.15', 'He delivers the afflicted by their affliction, and opens their ear in oppression.'),
('JOB', 36, 16, 'JOB.36.16', 'Yes, he would have allured you out of distress, into a wide place, where there is no restriction. That which is set on your table would be full of fatness.'),
('JOB', 36, 17, 'JOB.36.17', '“But you are full of the judgment of the wicked. Judgment and justice take hold of you.'),
('JOB', 36, 18, 'JOB.36.18', 'Don’t let riches entice you to wrath, neither let the great size of a bribe turn you aside.'),
('JOB', 36, 19, 'JOB.36.19', 'Would your wealth sustain you in distress, or all the might of your strength?'),
('JOB', 36, 20, 'JOB.36.20', 'Don’t desire the night, when people are cut off in their place.'),
('JOB', 36, 21, 'JOB.36.21', 'Take heed, don’t regard iniquity; for you have chosen this rather than affliction.'),
('JOB', 36, 22, 'JOB.36.22', 'Behold, God is exalted in his power. Who is a teacher like him?'),
('JOB', 36, 23, 'JOB.36.23', 'Who has prescribed his way for him? Or who can say, ‘You have committed unrighteousness’?'),
('JOB', 36, 24, 'JOB.36.24', '“Remember that you magnify his work, about which men have sung.'),
('JOB', 36, 25, 'JOB.36.25', 'All men have looked on it. Man sees it afar off.'),
('JOB', 36, 26, 'JOB.36.26', 'Behold, God is great, and we don’t know him. The number of his years is unsearchable.'),
('JOB', 36, 27, 'JOB.36.27', 'For he draws up the drops of water, which distill in rain from his vapor,'),
('JOB', 36, 28, 'JOB.36.28', 'which the skies pour down and which drop on man abundantly.'),
('JOB', 36, 29, 'JOB.36.29', 'Indeed, can anyone understand the spreading of the clouds and the thunderings of his pavilion?'),
('JOB', 36, 30, 'JOB.36.30', 'Behold, he spreads his light around him. He covers the bottom of the sea.'),
('JOB', 36, 31, 'JOB.36.31', 'For by these he judges the people. He gives food in abundance.'),
('JOB', 36, 32, 'JOB.36.32', 'He covers his hands with the lightning, and commands it to strike the mark.'),
('JOB', 36, 33, 'JOB.36.33', 'Its noise tells about him, and the livestock also, concerning the storm that comes up.'),
('JOB', 37, 1, 'JOB.37.1', '“Yes, at this my heart trembles, and is moved out of its place.'),
('JOB', 37, 2, 'JOB.37.2', 'Hear, oh, hear the noise of his voice, the sound that goes out of his mouth.'),
('JOB', 37, 3, 'JOB.37.3', 'He sends it out under the whole sky, and his lightning to the ends of the earth.'),
('JOB', 37, 4, 'JOB.37.4', 'After it a voice roars. He thunders with the voice of his majesty. He doesn’t hold back anything when his voice is heard.'),
('JOB', 37, 5, 'JOB.37.5', 'God thunders marvelously with his voice. He does great things, which we can’t comprehend.'),
('JOB', 37, 6, 'JOB.37.6', 'For he says to the snow, ‘Fall on the earth,’ likewise to the shower of rain, and to the showers of his mighty rain.'),
('JOB', 37, 7, 'JOB.37.7', 'He seals up the hand of every man, that all men whom he has made may know it.'),
('JOB', 37, 8, 'JOB.37.8', 'Then the animals take cover, and remain in their dens.'),
('JOB', 37, 9, 'JOB.37.9', 'Out of its room comes the storm, and cold out of the north.'),
('JOB', 37, 10, 'JOB.37.10', 'By the breath of God, ice is given, and the width of the waters is frozen.'),
('JOB', 37, 11, 'JOB.37.11', 'Yes, he loads the thick cloud with moisture. He spreads abroad the cloud of his lightning.'),
('JOB', 37, 12, 'JOB.37.12', 'It is turned around by his guidance, that they may do whatever he commands them on the surface of the habitable world,'),
('JOB', 37, 13, 'JOB.37.13', 'whether it is for correction, or for his land, or for loving kindness, that he causes it to come.'),
('JOB', 37, 14, 'JOB.37.14', '“Listen to this, Job. Stand still, and consider the wondrous works of God.'),
('JOB', 37, 15, 'JOB.37.15', 'Do you know how God controls them, and causes the lightning of his cloud to shine?'),
('JOB', 37, 16, 'JOB.37.16', 'Do you know the workings of the clouds, the wondrous works of him who is perfect in knowledge?'),
('JOB', 37, 17, 'JOB.37.17', 'You whose clothing is warm when the earth is still by reason of the south wind?'),
('JOB', 37, 18, 'JOB.37.18', 'Can you, with him, spread out the sky, which is strong as a cast metal mirror?'),
('JOB', 37, 19, 'JOB.37.19', 'Teach us what we will tell him, for we can’t make our case by reason of darkness.'),
('JOB', 37, 20, 'JOB.37.20', 'Will it be told him that I would speak? Or should a man wish that he were swallowed up?'),
('JOB', 37, 21, 'JOB.37.21', 'Now men don’t see the light which is bright in the skies, but the wind passes, and clears them.'),
('JOB', 37, 22, 'JOB.37.22', 'Out of the north comes golden splendor. With God is awesome majesty.'),
('JOB', 37, 23, 'JOB.37.23', 'We can’t reach the Almighty. He is exalted in power. In justice and great righteousness, he will not oppress.'),
('JOB', 37, 24, 'JOB.37.24', 'Therefore men revere him. He doesn’t regard any who are wise of heart.”'),
('JOB', 38, 1, 'JOB.38.1', 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind,'),
('JOB', 38, 2, 'JOB.38.2', '“Who is this who darkens counsel by words without knowledge?'),
('JOB', 38, 3, 'JOB.38.3', 'Brace yourself like a man, for I will question you, then you answer me!'),
('JOB', 38, 4, 'JOB.38.4', '“Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth? Declare, if you have understanding.'),
('JOB', 38, 5, 'JOB.38.5', 'Who determined its measures, if you know? Or who stretched the line on it?'),
('JOB', 38, 6, 'JOB.38.6', 'What were its foundations fastened on? Or who laid its cornerstone,'),
('JOB', 38, 7, 'JOB.38.7', 'when the morning stars sang together, and all the sons of God shouted for joy?'),
('JOB', 38, 8, 'JOB.38.8', '“Or who shut up the sea with doors, when it broke out of the womb,'),
('JOB', 38, 9, 'JOB.38.9', 'when I made clouds its garment, and wrapped it in thick darkness,'),
('JOB', 38, 10, 'JOB.38.10', 'marked out for it my bound, set bars and doors,'),
('JOB', 38, 11, 'JOB.38.11', 'and said, ‘You may come here, but no further. Your proud waves shall be stopped here’?'),
('JOB', 38, 12, 'JOB.38.12', '“Have you commanded the morning in your days, and caused the dawn to know its place,'),
('JOB', 38, 13, 'JOB.38.13', 'that it might take hold of the ends of the earth, and shake the wicked out of it?'),
('JOB', 38, 14, 'JOB.38.14', 'It is changed as clay under the seal, and presented as a garment.'),
('JOB', 38, 15, 'JOB.38.15', 'From the wicked, their light is withheld. The high arm is broken.'),
('JOB', 38, 16, 'JOB.38.16', '“Have you entered into the springs of the sea? Or have you walked in the recesses of the deep?'),
('JOB', 38, 17, 'JOB.38.17', 'Have the gates of death been revealed to you? Or have you seen the gates of the shadow of death?'),
('JOB', 38, 18, 'JOB.38.18', 'Have you comprehended the earth in its width? Declare, if you know it all.'),
('JOB', 38, 19, 'JOB.38.19', '“What is the way to the dwelling of light? As for darkness, where is its place,'),
('JOB', 38, 20, 'JOB.38.20', 'that you should take it to its bound, that you should discern the paths to its house?'),
('JOB', 38, 21, 'JOB.38.21', 'Surely you know, for you were born then, and the number of your days is great!'),
('JOB', 38, 22, 'JOB.38.22', 'Have you entered the storehouses of the snow, or have you seen the storehouses of the hail,'),
('JOB', 38, 23, 'JOB.38.23', 'which I have reserved against the time of trouble, against the day of battle and war?'),
('JOB', 38, 24, 'JOB.38.24', 'By what way is the lightning distributed, or the east wind scattered on the earth?'),
('JOB', 38, 25, 'JOB.38.25', 'Who has cut a channel for the flood water, or the path for the thunderstorm,'),
('JOB', 38, 26, 'JOB.38.26', 'to cause it to rain on a land where there is no man, on the wilderness, in which there is no man,'),
('JOB', 38, 27, 'JOB.38.27', 'to satisfy the waste and desolate ground, to cause the tender grass to grow?'),
('JOB', 38, 28, 'JOB.38.28', 'Does the rain have a father? Or who fathers the drops of dew?'),
('JOB', 38, 29, 'JOB.38.29', 'Whose womb did the ice come out of? Who has given birth to the gray frost of the sky?'),
('JOB', 38, 30, 'JOB.38.30', 'The waters become hard like stone, when the surface of the deep is frozen.'),
('JOB', 38, 31, 'JOB.38.31', '“Can you bind the cluster of the Pleiades, or loosen the cords of Orion?'),
('JOB', 38, 32, 'JOB.38.32', 'Can you lead the constellations out in their season? Or can you guide the Bear with her cubs?'),
('JOB', 38, 33, 'JOB.38.33', 'Do you know the laws of the heavens? Can you establish its dominion over the earth?'),
('JOB', 38, 34, 'JOB.38.34', '“Can you lift up your voice to the clouds, that abundance of waters may cover you?'),
('JOB', 38, 35, 'JOB.38.35', 'Can you send out lightnings, that they may go? Do they report to you, ‘Here we are’?'),
('JOB', 38, 36, 'JOB.38.36', 'Who has put wisdom in the inward parts? Or who has given understanding to the mind?'),
('JOB', 38, 37, 'JOB.38.37', 'Who can count the clouds by wisdom? Or who can pour out the containers of the sky,'),
('JOB', 38, 38, 'JOB.38.38', 'when the dust runs into a mass, and the clods of earth stick together?'),
('JOB', 38, 39, 'JOB.38.39', '“Can you hunt the prey for the lioness, or satisfy the appetite of the young lions,'),
('JOB', 38, 40, 'JOB.38.40', 'when they crouch in their dens, and lie in wait in the thicket?'),
('JOB', 38, 41, 'JOB.38.41', 'Who provides for the raven his prey, when his young ones cry to God, and wander for lack of food?'),
('JOB', 39, 1, 'JOB.39.1', '“Do you know the time when the mountain goats give birth? Do you watch when the doe bears fawns?'),
('JOB', 39, 2, 'JOB.39.2', 'Can you count the months that they fulfill? Or do you know the time when they give birth?'),
('JOB', 39, 3, 'JOB.39.3', 'They bow themselves. They bear their young. They end their labor pains.'),
('JOB', 39, 4, 'JOB.39.4', 'Their young ones become strong. They grow up in the open field. They go out, and don’t return again.'),
('JOB', 39, 5, 'JOB.39.5', '“Who has set the wild donkey free? Or who has loosened the bonds of the swift donkey,'),
('JOB', 39, 6, 'JOB.39.6', 'whose home I have made the wilderness, and the salt land his dwelling place?'),
('JOB', 39, 7, 'JOB.39.7', 'He scorns the tumult of the city, neither does he hear the shouting of the driver.'),
('JOB', 39, 8, 'JOB.39.8', 'The range of the mountains is his pasture. He searches after every green thing.'),
('JOB', 39, 9, 'JOB.39.9', '“Will the wild ox be content to serve you? Or will he stay by your feeding trough?'),
('JOB', 39, 10, 'JOB.39.10', 'Can you hold the wild ox in the furrow with his harness? Or will he till the valleys after you?'),
('JOB', 39, 11, 'JOB.39.11', 'Will you trust him, because his strength is great? Or will you leave to him your labor?'),
('JOB', 39, 12, 'JOB.39.12', 'Will you confide in him, that he will bring home your seed, and gather the grain of your threshing floor?'),
('JOB', 39, 13, 'JOB.39.13', '“The wings of the ostrich wave proudly, but are they the feathers and plumage of love?'),
('JOB', 39, 14, 'JOB.39.14', 'For she leaves her eggs on the earth, warms them in the dust,'),
('JOB', 39, 15, 'JOB.39.15', 'and forgets that the foot may crush them, or that the wild animal may trample them.'),
('JOB', 39, 16, 'JOB.39.16', 'She deals harshly with her young ones, as if they were not hers. Though her labor is in vain, she is without fear,'),
('JOB', 39, 17, 'JOB.39.17', 'because God has deprived her of wisdom, neither has he imparted to her understanding.'),
('JOB', 39, 18, 'JOB.39.18', 'When she lifts up herself on high, she scorns the horse and his rider.'),
('JOB', 39, 19, 'JOB.39.19', '“Have you given the horse might? Have you clothed his neck with a quivering mane?'),
('JOB', 39, 20, 'JOB.39.20', 'Have you made him to leap as a locust? The glory of his snorting is awesome.'),
('JOB', 39, 21, 'JOB.39.21', 'He paws in the valley, and rejoices in his strength. He goes out to meet the armed men.'),
('JOB', 39, 22, 'JOB.39.22', 'He mocks at fear, and is not dismayed, neither does he turn back from the sword.'),
('JOB', 39, 23, 'JOB.39.23', 'The quiver rattles against him, the flashing spear and the javelin.'),
('JOB', 39, 24, 'JOB.39.24', 'He eats up the ground with fierceness and rage, neither does he stand still at the sound of the trumpet.'),
('JOB', 39, 25, 'JOB.39.25', 'As often as the trumpet sounds he snorts, ‘Aha!’ He smells the battle afar off, the thunder of the captains, and the shouting.'),
('JOB', 39, 26, 'JOB.39.26', '“Is it by your wisdom that the hawk soars, and stretches her wings toward the south?'),
('JOB', 39, 27, 'JOB.39.27', 'Is it at your command that the eagle mounts up, and makes his nest on high?'),
('JOB', 39, 28, 'JOB.39.28', 'On the cliff he dwells and makes his home, on the point of the cliff and the stronghold.'),
('JOB', 39, 29, 'JOB.39.29', 'From there he spies out the prey. His eyes see it afar off.'),
('JOB', 39, 30, 'JOB.39.30', 'His young ones also suck up blood. Where the slain are, there he is.”'),
('JOB', 40, 1, 'JOB.40.1', 'Moreover the LORD answered Job,'),
('JOB', 40, 2, 'JOB.40.2', '“Shall he who argues contend with the Almighty? He who argues with God, let him answer it.”'),
('JOB', 40, 3, 'JOB.40.3', 'Then Job answered the LORD,'),
('JOB', 40, 4, 'JOB.40.4', '“Behold, I am of small account. What will I answer you? I lay my hand on my mouth.'),
('JOB', 40, 5, 'JOB.40.5', 'I have spoken once, and I will not answer; Yes, twice, but I will proceed no further.”'),
('JOB', 40, 6, 'JOB.40.6', 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind:'),
('JOB', 40, 7, 'JOB.40.7', '“Now brace yourself like a man. I will question you, and you will answer me.'),
('JOB', 40, 8, 'JOB.40.8', 'Will you even annul my judgment? Will you condemn me, that you may be justified?'),
('JOB', 40, 9, 'JOB.40.9', 'Or do you have an arm like God? Can you thunder with a voice like him?'),
('JOB', 40, 10, 'JOB.40.10', '“Now deck yourself with excellency and dignity. Array yourself with honor and majesty.'),
('JOB', 40, 11, 'JOB.40.11', 'Pour out the fury of your anger. Look at everyone who is proud, and bring him low.'),
('JOB', 40, 12, 'JOB.40.12', 'Look at everyone who is proud, and humble him. Crush the wicked in their place.'),
('JOB', 40, 13, 'JOB.40.13', 'Hide them in the dust together. Bind their faces in the hidden place.'),
('JOB', 40, 14, 'JOB.40.14', 'Then I will also admit to you that your own right hand can save you.'),
('JOB', 40, 15, 'JOB.40.15', '“See now behemoth, which I made as well as you. He eats grass as an ox.'),
('JOB', 40, 16, 'JOB.40.16', 'Look now, his strength is in his thighs. His force is in the muscles of his belly.'),
('JOB', 40, 17, 'JOB.40.17', 'He moves his tail like a cedar. The sinews of his thighs are knit together.'),
('JOB', 40, 18, 'JOB.40.18', 'His bones are like tubes of bronze. His limbs are like bars of iron.'),
('JOB', 40, 19, 'JOB.40.19', 'He is the chief of the ways of God. He who made him gives him his sword.'),
('JOB', 40, 20, 'JOB.40.20', 'Surely the mountains produce food for him, where all the animals of the field play.'),
('JOB', 40, 21, 'JOB.40.21', 'He lies under the lotus trees, in the covert of the reed, and the marsh.'),
('JOB', 40, 22, 'JOB.40.22', 'The lotuses cover him with their shade. The willows of the brook surround him.'),
('JOB', 40, 23, 'JOB.40.23', 'Behold, if a river overflows, he doesn’t tremble. He is confident, though the Jordan swells even to his mouth.'),
('JOB', 40, 24, 'JOB.40.24', 'Shall any take him when he is on the watch, or pierce through his nose with a snare?'),
('JOB', 41, 1, 'JOB.41.1', '“Can you draw out Leviathan with a fish hook, or press down his tongue with a cord?'),
('JOB', 41, 2, 'JOB.41.2', 'Can you put a rope into his nose, or pierce his jaw through with a hook?'),
('JOB', 41, 3, 'JOB.41.3', 'Will he make many petitions to you, or will he speak soft words to you?'),
('JOB', 41, 4, 'JOB.41.4', 'Will he make a covenant with you, that you should take him for a servant forever?'),
('JOB', 41, 5, 'JOB.41.5', 'Will you play with him as with a bird? Or will you bind him for your girls?'),
('JOB', 41, 6, 'JOB.41.6', 'Will traders barter for him? Will they part him among the merchants?'),
('JOB', 41, 7, 'JOB.41.7', 'Can you fill his skin with barbed irons, or his head with fish spears?'),
('JOB', 41, 8, 'JOB.41.8', 'Lay your hand on him. Remember the battle, and do so no more.'),
('JOB', 41, 9, 'JOB.41.9', 'Behold, the hope of him is in vain. Won’t one be cast down even at the sight of him?'),
('JOB', 41, 10, 'JOB.41.10', 'None is so fierce that he dare stir him up. Who then is he who can stand before me?'),
('JOB', 41, 11, 'JOB.41.11', 'Who has first given to me, that I should repay him? Everything under the heavens is mine.'),
('JOB', 41, 12, 'JOB.41.12', '“I will not keep silence concerning his limbs, nor his mighty strength, nor his goodly frame.'),
('JOB', 41, 13, 'JOB.41.13', 'Who can strip off his outer garment? Who will come within his jaws?'),
('JOB', 41, 14, 'JOB.41.14', 'Who can open the doors of his face? Around his teeth is terror.'),
('JOB', 41, 15, 'JOB.41.15', 'Strong scales are his pride, shut up together with a close seal.'),
('JOB', 41, 16, 'JOB.41.16', 'One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.'),
('JOB', 41, 17, 'JOB.41.17', 'They are joined to one another. They stick together, so that they can’t be pulled apart.'),
('JOB', 41, 18, 'JOB.41.18', 'His sneezing flashes out light. His eyes are like the eyelids of the morning.'),
('JOB', 41, 19, 'JOB.41.19', 'Out of his mouth go burning torches. Sparks of fire leap out.'),
('JOB', 41, 20, 'JOB.41.20', 'Out of his nostrils a smoke goes, as of a boiling pot over a fire of reeds.'),
('JOB', 41, 21, 'JOB.41.21', 'His breath kindles coals. A flame goes out of his mouth.'),
('JOB', 41, 22, 'JOB.41.22', 'There is strength in his neck. Terror dances before him.'),
('JOB', 41, 23, 'JOB.41.23', 'The flakes of his flesh are joined together. They are firm on him. They can’t be moved.'),
('JOB', 41, 24, 'JOB.41.24', 'His heart is as firm as a stone, yes, firm as the lower millstone.'),
('JOB', 41, 25, 'JOB.41.25', 'When he raises himself up, the mighty are afraid. They retreat before his thrashing.'),
('JOB', 41, 26, 'JOB.41.26', 'If one attacks him with the sword, it can’t prevail; nor the spear, the dart, nor the pointed shaft.'),
('JOB', 41, 27, 'JOB.41.27', 'He counts iron as straw, and bronze as rotten wood.'),
('JOB', 41, 28, 'JOB.41.28', 'The arrow can’t make him flee. Sling stones are like chaff to him.'),
('JOB', 41, 29, 'JOB.41.29', 'Clubs are counted as stubble. He laughs at the rushing of the javelin.'),
('JOB', 41, 30, 'JOB.41.30', 'His undersides are like sharp potsherds, leaving a trail in the mud like a threshing sledge.'),
('JOB', 41, 31, 'JOB.41.31', 'He makes the deep to boil like a pot. He makes the sea like a pot of ointment.'),
('JOB', 41, 32, 'JOB.41.32', 'He makes a path shine after him. One would think the deep had white hair.'),
('JOB', 41, 33, 'JOB.41.33', 'On earth there is not his equal, that is made without fear.'),
('JOB', 41, 34, 'JOB.41.34', 'He sees everything that is high. He is king over all the sons of pride.”'),
('JOB', 42, 1, 'JOB.42.1', 'Then Job answered the LORD:'),
('JOB', 42, 2, 'JOB.42.2', '“I know that you can do all things, and that no purpose of yours can be restrained.'),
('JOB', 42, 3, 'JOB.42.3', 'You asked, ‘Who is this who hides counsel without knowledge?’ therefore I have uttered that which I didn’t understand, things too wonderful for me, which I didn’t know.'),
('JOB', 42, 4, 'JOB.42.4', 'You said, ‘Listen, now, and I will speak; I will question you, and you will answer me.’'),
('JOB', 42, 5, 'JOB.42.5', 'I had heard of you by the hearing of the ear, but now my eye sees you.'),
('JOB', 42, 6, 'JOB.42.6', 'Therefore I abhor myself, and repent in dust and ashes.”'),
('JOB', 42, 7, 'JOB.42.7', 'It was so, that after the LORD had spoken these words to Job, the LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite, “My wrath is kindled against you, and against your two friends; for you have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my servant Job has.'),
('JOB', 42, 8, 'JOB.42.8', 'Now therefore, take to yourselves seven bulls and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer up for yourselves a burnt offering; and my servant Job shall pray for you, for I will accept him, that I not deal with you according to your folly. For you have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my servant Job has.”'),
('JOB', 42, 9, 'JOB.42.9', 'So Eliphaz the Temanite and Bildad the Shuhite and Zophar the Naamathite went and did what the LORD commanded them, and the LORD accepted Job.'),
('JOB', 42, 10, 'JOB.42.10', 'The LORD restored Job’s prosperity when he prayed for his friends. The LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before.'),
('JOB', 42, 11, 'JOB.42.11', 'Then all his brothers, all his sisters, and all those who had been of his acquaintance before, came to him and ate bread with him in his house. They comforted him, and consoled him concerning all the evil that the LORD had brought on him. Everyone also gave him a piece of money, and everyone a ring of gold.'),
('JOB', 42, 12, 'JOB.42.12', 'So the LORD blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning. He had fourteen thousand sheep, six thousand camels, one thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand female donkeys.'),
('JOB', 42, 13, 'JOB.42.13', 'He had also seven sons and three daughters.'),
('JOB', 42, 14, 'JOB.42.14', 'He called the name of the first, Jemimah; and the name of the second, Keziah; and the name of the third, Keren Happuch.'),
('JOB', 42, 15, 'JOB.42.15', 'In all the land were no women found so beautiful as the daughters of Job. Their father gave them an inheritance among their brothers.'),
('JOB', 42, 16, 'JOB.42.16', 'After this Job lived one hundred forty years, and saw his sons, and his sons’ sons, to four generations.'),
('JOB', 42, 17, 'JOB.42.17', 'So Job died, being old and full of days.'),
('PSA', 1, 1, 'PSA.1.1', 'Blessed is the man who doesn’t walk in the counsel of the wicked, nor stand on the path of sinners, nor sit in the seat of scoffers;'),
('PSA', 1, 2, 'PSA.1.2', 'but his delight is in the LORD’s law. On his law he meditates day and night.'),
('PSA', 1, 3, 'PSA.1.3', 'He will be like a tree planted by the streams of water, that produces its fruit in its season, whose leaf also does not wither. Whatever he does shall prosper.'),
('PSA', 1, 4, 'PSA.1.4', 'The wicked are not so, but are like the chaff which the wind drives away.'),
('PSA', 1, 5, 'PSA.1.5', 'Therefore the wicked shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.'),
('PSA', 1, 6, 'PSA.1.6', 'For the LORD knows the way of the righteous, but the way of the wicked shall perish.'),
('PSA', 2, 1, 'PSA.2.1', 'Why do the nations rage, and the peoples plot a vain thing?'),
('PSA', 2, 2, 'PSA.2.2', 'The kings of the earth take a stand, and the rulers take counsel together, against the LORD, and against his Anointed, saying,'),
('PSA', 2, 3, 'PSA.2.3', '“Let’s break their bonds apart, and cast their cords from us.”'),
('PSA', 2, 4, 'PSA.2.4', 'He who sits in the heavens will laugh. The Lord will have them in derision.'),
('PSA', 2, 5, 'PSA.2.5', 'Then he will speak to them in his anger, and terrify them in his wrath:'),
('PSA', 2, 6, 'PSA.2.6', '“Yet I have set my King on my holy hill of Zion.”'),
('PSA', 2, 7, 'PSA.2.7', 'I will tell of the decree: The LORD said to me, “You are my son. Today I have become your father.'),
('PSA', 2, 8, 'PSA.2.8', 'Ask of me, and I will give the nations for your inheritance, the uttermost parts of the earth for your possession.'),
('PSA', 2, 9, 'PSA.2.9', 'You shall break them with a rod of iron. You shall dash them in pieces like a potter’s vessel.”'),
('PSA', 2, 10, 'PSA.2.10', 'Now therefore be wise, you kings. Be instructed, you judges of the earth.'),
('PSA', 2, 11, 'PSA.2.11', 'Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.'),
('PSA', 2, 12, 'PSA.2.12', 'Give sincere homage to the Son, lest he be angry, and you perish on the way, for his wrath will soon be kindled. Blessed are all those who take refuge in him.'),
('PSA', 3, 1, 'PSA.3.1', 'LORD, how my adversaries have increased! Many are those who rise up against me.'),
('PSA', 3, 2, 'PSA.3.2', 'Many there are who say of my soul, “There is no help for him in God.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 3, 3, 'PSA.3.3', 'But you, LORD, are a shield around me, my glory, and the one who lifts up my head.'),
('PSA', 3, 4, 'PSA.3.4', 'I cry to the LORD with my voice, and he answers me out of his holy hill. Selah.'),
('PSA', 3, 5, 'PSA.3.5', 'I laid myself down and slept. I awakened, for the LORD sustains me.'),
('PSA', 3, 6, 'PSA.3.6', 'I will not be afraid of tens of thousands of people who have set themselves against me on every side.'),
('PSA', 3, 7, 'PSA.3.7', 'Arise, LORD! Save me, my God! For you have struck all of my enemies on the cheek bone. You have broken the teeth of the wicked.'),
('PSA', 3, 8, 'PSA.3.8', 'Salvation belongs to the LORD. May your blessing be on your people. Selah.'),
('PSA', 4, 1, 'PSA.4.1', 'Answer me when I call, God of my righteousness. Give me relief from my distress. Have mercy on me, and hear my prayer.'),
('PSA', 4, 2, 'PSA.4.2', 'You sons of men, how long shall my glory be turned into dishonor? Will you love vanity and seek after falsehood? Selah.'),
('PSA', 4, 3, 'PSA.4.3', 'But know that the LORD has set apart for himself him who is godly; The LORD will hear when I call to him.'),
('PSA', 4, 4, 'PSA.4.4', 'Stand in awe, and don’t sin. Search your own heart on your bed, and be still. Selah.'),
('PSA', 4, 5, 'PSA.4.5', 'Offer the sacrifices of righteousness. Put your trust in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 4, 6, 'PSA.4.6', 'Many say, “Who will show us any good?” LORD, let the light of your face shine on us.'),
('PSA', 4, 7, 'PSA.4.7', 'You have put gladness in my heart, more than when their grain and their new wine are increased.'),
('PSA', 4, 8, 'PSA.4.8', 'In peace I will both lay myself down and sleep, for you alone, LORD, make me live in safety.'),
('PSA', 5, 1, 'PSA.5.1', 'Give ear to my words, LORD. Consider my meditation.'),
('PSA', 5, 2, 'PSA.5.2', 'Listen to the voice of my cry, my King and my God, for I pray to you.'),
('PSA', 5, 3, 'PSA.5.3', 'LORD, in the morning you will hear my voice. In the morning I will lay my requests before you, and will watch expectantly.'),
('PSA', 5, 4, 'PSA.5.4', 'For you are not a God who has pleasure in wickedness. Evil can’t live with you.'),
('PSA', 5, 5, 'PSA.5.5', 'The arrogant will not stand in your sight. You hate all workers of iniquity.'),
('PSA', 5, 6, 'PSA.5.6', 'You will destroy those who speak lies. The LORD abhors the bloodthirsty and deceitful man.'),
('PSA', 5, 7, 'PSA.5.7', 'But as for me, in the abundance of your loving kindness I will come into your house. I will bow toward your holy temple in reverence of you.'),
('PSA', 5, 8, 'PSA.5.8', 'Lead me, LORD, in your righteousness because of my enemies. Make your way straight before my face.'),
('PSA', 5, 9, 'PSA.5.9', 'For there is no faithfulness in their mouth. Their heart is destruction. Their throat is an open tomb. They flatter with their tongue.'),
('PSA', 5, 10, 'PSA.5.10', 'Hold them guilty, God. Let them fall by their own counsels. Thrust them out in the multitude of their transgressions, for they have rebelled against you.'),
('PSA', 5, 11, 'PSA.5.11', 'But let all those who take refuge in you rejoice. Let them always shout for joy, because you defend them. Let them also who love your name be joyful in you.'),
('PSA', 5, 12, 'PSA.5.12', 'For you will bless the righteous. LORD, you will surround him with favor as with a shield.'),
('PSA', 6, 1, 'PSA.6.1', 'LORD, don’t rebuke me in your anger, neither discipline me in your wrath.'),
('PSA', 6, 2, 'PSA.6.2', 'Have mercy on me, LORD, for I am faint. LORD, heal me, for my bones are troubled.'),
('PSA', 6, 3, 'PSA.6.3', 'My soul is also in great anguish. But you, LORD—how long?'),
('PSA', 6, 4, 'PSA.6.4', 'Return, LORD. Deliver my soul, and save me for your loving kindness’ sake.'),
('PSA', 6, 5, 'PSA.6.5', 'For in death there is no memory of you. In Sheol, who shall give you thanks?'),
('PSA', 6, 6, 'PSA.6.6', 'I am weary with my groaning. Every night I flood my bed. I drench my couch with my tears.'),
('PSA', 6, 7, 'PSA.6.7', 'My eye wastes away because of grief. It grows old because of all my adversaries.'),
('PSA', 6, 8, 'PSA.6.8', 'Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity, for the LORD has heard the voice of my weeping.'),
('PSA', 6, 9, 'PSA.6.9', 'The LORD has heard my supplication. The LORD accepts my prayer.'),
('PSA', 6, 10, 'PSA.6.10', 'May all my enemies be ashamed and dismayed. They shall turn back, they shall be disgraced suddenly.'),
('PSA', 7, 1, 'PSA.7.1', 'LORD, my God, I take refuge in you. Save me from all those who pursue me, and deliver me,'),
('PSA', 7, 2, 'PSA.7.2', 'lest they tear apart my soul like a lion, ripping it in pieces, while there is no one to deliver.'),
('PSA', 7, 3, 'PSA.7.3', 'LORD, my God, if I have done this, if there is iniquity in my hands,'),
('PSA', 7, 4, 'PSA.7.4', 'if I have rewarded evil to him who was at peace with me (yes, I have plundered him who without cause was my adversary),'),
('PSA', 7, 5, 'PSA.7.5', 'let the enemy pursue my soul, and overtake it; yes, let him tread my life down to the earth, and lay my glory in the dust. Selah.'),
('PSA', 7, 6, 'PSA.7.6', 'Arise, LORD, in your anger. Lift up yourself against the rage of my adversaries. Awake for me. You have commanded judgment.'),
('PSA', 7, 7, 'PSA.7.7', 'Let the congregation of the peoples surround you. Rule over them on high.'),
('PSA', 7, 8, 'PSA.7.8', 'The LORD administers judgment to the peoples. Judge me, LORD, according to my righteousness, and to my integrity that is in me.'),
('PSA', 7, 9, 'PSA.7.9', 'Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end, but establish the righteous; their minds and hearts are searched by the righteous God.'),
('PSA', 7, 10, 'PSA.7.10', 'My shield is with God, who saves the upright in heart.'),
('PSA', 7, 11, 'PSA.7.11', 'God is a righteous judge, yes, a God who has indignation every day.'),
('PSA', 7, 12, 'PSA.7.12', 'If a man doesn’t repent, he will sharpen his sword; he has bent and strung his bow.'),
('PSA', 7, 13, 'PSA.7.13', 'He has also prepared for himself the instruments of death. He makes ready his flaming arrows.'),
('PSA', 7, 14, 'PSA.7.14', 'Behold, he travails with iniquity. Yes, he has conceived mischief, and brought out falsehood.'),
('PSA', 7, 15, 'PSA.7.15', 'He has dug a hole, and has fallen into the pit which he made.'),
('PSA', 7, 16, 'PSA.7.16', 'The trouble he causes shall return to his own head. His violence shall come down on the crown of his own head.'),
('PSA', 7, 17, 'PSA.7.17', 'I will give thanks to the LORD according to his righteousness, and will sing praise to the name of the LORD Most High.'),
('PSA', 8, 1, 'PSA.8.1', 'LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name in all the earth! You have set your glory above the heavens!'),
('PSA', 8, 2, 'PSA.8.2', 'From the lips of babes and infants you have established strength, because of your adversaries, that you might silence the enemy and the avenger.'),
('PSA', 8, 3, 'PSA.8.3', 'When I consider your heavens, the work of your fingers, the moon and the stars, which you have ordained,'),
('PSA', 8, 4, 'PSA.8.4', 'what is man, that you think of him? What is the son of man, that you care for him?'),
('PSA', 8, 5, 'PSA.8.5', 'For you have made him a little lower than the angels, and crowned him with glory and honor.'),
('PSA', 8, 6, 'PSA.8.6', 'You make him ruler over the works of your hands. You have put all things under his feet:'),
('PSA', 8, 7, 'PSA.8.7', 'All sheep and cattle, yes, and the animals of the field,'),
('PSA', 8, 8, 'PSA.8.8', 'the birds of the sky, the fish of the sea, and whatever passes through the paths of the seas.'),
('PSA', 8, 9, 'PSA.8.9', 'LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name in all the earth!'),
('PSA', 9, 1, 'PSA.9.1', 'I will give thanks to the LORD with my whole heart. I will tell of all your marvelous works.'),
('PSA', 9, 2, 'PSA.9.2', 'I will be glad and rejoice in you. I will sing praise to your name, O Most High.'),
('PSA', 9, 3, 'PSA.9.3', 'When my enemies turn back, they stumble and perish in your presence.'),
('PSA', 9, 4, 'PSA.9.4', 'For you have maintained my just cause. You sit on the throne judging righteously.'),
('PSA', 9, 5, 'PSA.9.5', 'You have rebuked the nations. You have destroyed the wicked. You have blotted out their name forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 9, 6, 'PSA.9.6', 'The enemy is overtaken by endless ruin. The very memory of the cities which you have overthrown has perished.'),
('PSA', 9, 7, 'PSA.9.7', 'But the LORD reigns forever. He has prepared his throne for judgment.'),
('PSA', 9, 8, 'PSA.9.8', 'He will judge the world in righteousness. He will administer judgment to the peoples in uprightness.'),
('PSA', 9, 9, 'PSA.9.9', 'The LORD will also be a high tower for the oppressed; a high tower in times of trouble.'),
('PSA', 9, 10, 'PSA.9.10', 'Those who know your name will put their trust in you, for you, LORD, have not forsaken those who seek you.'),
('PSA', 9, 11, 'PSA.9.11', 'Sing praises to the LORD, who dwells in Zion, and declare among the people what he has done.'),
('PSA', 9, 12, 'PSA.9.12', 'For he who avenges blood remembers them. He doesn’t forget the cry of the afflicted.'),
('PSA', 9, 13, 'PSA.9.13', 'Have mercy on me, LORD. See my affliction by those who hate me, and lift me up from the gates of death,'),
('PSA', 9, 14, 'PSA.9.14', 'that I may show all of your praise. I will rejoice in your salvation in the gates of the daughter of Zion.'),
('PSA', 9, 15, 'PSA.9.15', 'The nations have sunk down in the pit that they made. In the net which they hid, their own foot is taken.'),
('PSA', 9, 16, 'PSA.9.16', 'The LORD has made himself known. He has executed judgment. The wicked is snared by the work of his own hands. Meditation. Selah.'),
('PSA', 9, 17, 'PSA.9.17', 'The wicked shall be turned back to Sheol, even all the nations that forget God.'),
('PSA', 9, 18, 'PSA.9.18', 'For the needy shall not always be forgotten, nor the hope of the poor perish forever.'),
('PSA', 9, 19, 'PSA.9.19', 'Arise, LORD! Don’t let man prevail. Let the nations be judged in your sight.'),
('PSA', 9, 20, 'PSA.9.20', 'Put them in fear, LORD. Let the nations know that they are only men. Selah.'),
('PSA', 10, 1, 'PSA.10.1', 'Why do you stand far off, LORD? Why do you hide yourself in times of trouble?'),
('PSA', 10, 2, 'PSA.10.2', 'In arrogance, the wicked hunt down the weak. They are caught in the schemes that they devise.'),
('PSA', 10, 3, 'PSA.10.3', 'For the wicked boasts of his heart’s cravings. He blesses the greedy and condemns the LORD.'),
('PSA', 10, 4, 'PSA.10.4', 'The wicked, in the pride of his face, has no room in his thoughts for God.'),
('PSA', 10, 5, 'PSA.10.5', 'His ways are prosperous at all times. He is arrogant, and your laws are far from his sight. As for all his adversaries, he sneers at them.'),
('PSA', 10, 6, 'PSA.10.6', 'He says in his heart, “I shall not be shaken. For generations I shall have no trouble.”'),
('PSA', 10, 7, 'PSA.10.7', 'His mouth is full of cursing, deceit, and oppression. Under his tongue is mischief and iniquity.'),
('PSA', 10, 8, 'PSA.10.8', 'He lies in wait near the villages. From ambushes, he murders the innocent. His eyes are secretly set against the helpless.'),
('PSA', 10, 9, 'PSA.10.9', 'He lurks in secret as a lion in his ambush. He lies in wait to catch the helpless. He catches the helpless when he draws him in his net.'),
('PSA', 10, 10, 'PSA.10.10', 'The helpless are crushed. They collapse. They fall under his strength.'),
('PSA', 10, 11, 'PSA.10.11', 'He says in his heart, “God has forgotten. He hides his face. He will never see it.”'),
('PSA', 10, 12, 'PSA.10.12', 'Arise, LORD! God, lift up your hand! Don’t forget the helpless.'),
('PSA', 10, 13, 'PSA.10.13', 'Why does the wicked person condemn God, and say in his heart, “God won’t call me into account”?'),
('PSA', 10, 14, 'PSA.10.14', 'But you do see trouble and grief. You consider it to take it into your hand. You help the victim and the fatherless.'),
('PSA', 10, 15, 'PSA.10.15', 'Break the arm of the wicked. As for the evil man, seek out his wickedness until you find none.'),
('PSA', 10, 16, 'PSA.10.16', 'The LORD is King forever and ever! The nations will perish out of his land.'),
('PSA', 10, 17, 'PSA.10.17', 'LORD, you have heard the desire of the humble. You will prepare their heart. You will cause your ear to hear,'),
('PSA', 10, 18, 'PSA.10.18', 'to judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that man who is of the earth may terrify no more.'),
('PSA', 11, 1, 'PSA.11.1', 'In the LORD, I take refuge. How can you say to my soul, “Flee as a bird to your mountain”?'),
('PSA', 11, 2, 'PSA.11.2', 'For, behold, the wicked bend their bows. They set their arrows on the strings, that they may shoot in darkness at the upright in heart.'),
('PSA', 11, 3, 'PSA.11.3', 'If the foundations are destroyed, what can the righteous do?'),
('PSA', 11, 4, 'PSA.11.4', 'The LORD is in his holy temple. The LORD is on his throne in heaven. His eyes observe. His eyes examine the children of men.'),
('PSA', 11, 5, 'PSA.11.5', 'The LORD examines the righteous, but his soul hates the wicked and him who loves violence.'),
('PSA', 11, 6, 'PSA.11.6', 'On the wicked he will rain blazing coals; fire, sulfur, and scorching wind shall be the portion of their cup.'),
('PSA', 11, 7, 'PSA.11.7', 'For the LORD is righteous. He loves righteousness. The upright shall see his face.'),
('PSA', 12, 1, 'PSA.12.1', 'Help, LORD; for the godly man ceases. For the faithful fail from among the children of men.'),
('PSA', 12, 2, 'PSA.12.2', 'Everyone lies to his neighbor. They speak with flattering lips, and with a double heart.'),
('PSA', 12, 3, 'PSA.12.3', 'May the LORD cut off all flattering lips, and the tongue that boasts,'),
('PSA', 12, 4, 'PSA.12.4', 'who have said, “With our tongue we will prevail. Our lips are our own. Who is lord over us?”'),
('PSA', 12, 5, 'PSA.12.5', '“Because of the oppression of the weak and because of the groaning of the needy, I will now arise,” says the LORD; “I will set him in safety from those who malign him.”'),
('PSA', 12, 6, 'PSA.12.6', 'The LORD’s words are flawless words, as silver refined in a clay furnace, purified seven times.'),
('PSA', 12, 7, 'PSA.12.7', 'You will keep them, LORD. You will preserve them from this generation forever.'),
('PSA', 12, 8, 'PSA.12.8', 'The wicked walk on every side, when what is vile is exalted among the sons of men.'),
('PSA', 13, 1, 'PSA.13.1', 'How long, LORD? Will you forget me forever? How long will you hide your face from me?'),
('PSA', 13, 2, 'PSA.13.2', 'How long shall I take counsel in my soul, having sorrow in my heart every day? How long shall my enemy triumph over me?'),
('PSA', 13, 3, 'PSA.13.3', 'Behold, and answer me, LORD, my God. Give light to my eyes, lest I sleep in death;'),
('PSA', 13, 4, 'PSA.13.4', 'lest my enemy say, “I have prevailed against him;” lest my adversaries rejoice when I fall.'),
('PSA', 13, 5, 'PSA.13.5', 'But I trust in your loving kindness. My heart rejoices in your salvation.'),
('PSA', 13, 6, 'PSA.13.6', 'I will sing to the LORD, because he has been good to me.'),
('PSA', 14, 1, 'PSA.14.1', 'The fool has said in his heart, “There is no God.” They are corrupt. They have done abominable deeds. There is no one who does good.'),
('PSA', 14, 2, 'PSA.14.2', 'The LORD looked down from heaven on the children of men, to see if there were any who understood, who sought after God.'),
('PSA', 14, 3, 'PSA.14.3', 'They have all gone aside. They have together become corrupt. There is no one who does good, no, not one.'),
('PSA', 14, 4, 'PSA.14.4', 'Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge, who eat up my people as they eat bread, and don’t call on the LORD?'),
('PSA', 14, 5, 'PSA.14.5', 'There they were in great fear, for God is in the generation of the righteous.'),
('PSA', 14, 6, 'PSA.14.6', 'You frustrate the plan of the poor, because the LORD is his refuge.'),
('PSA', 14, 7, 'PSA.14.7', 'Oh that the salvation of Israel would come out of Zion! When the LORD restores the fortunes of his people, then Jacob shall rejoice, and Israel shall be glad.'),
('PSA', 15, 1, 'PSA.15.1', 'LORD, who shall dwell in your sanctuary? Who shall live on your holy hill?'),
('PSA', 15, 2, 'PSA.15.2', 'He who walks blamelessly and does what is right, and speaks truth in his heart;'),
('PSA', 15, 3, 'PSA.15.3', 'he who doesn’t slander with his tongue, nor does evil to his friend, nor casts slurs against his fellow man;'),
('PSA', 15, 4, 'PSA.15.4', 'in whose eyes a vile man is despised, but who honors those who fear the LORD; he who keeps an oath even when it hurts, and doesn’t change;'),
('PSA', 15, 5, 'PSA.15.5', 'he who doesn’t lend out his money for usury, nor take a bribe against the innocent. He who does these things shall never be shaken.'),
('PSA', 16, 1, 'PSA.16.1', 'Preserve me, God, for I take refuge in you.'),
('PSA', 16, 2, 'PSA.16.2', 'My soul, you have said to the LORD, “You are my Lord. Apart from you I have no good thing.”'),
('PSA', 16, 3, 'PSA.16.3', 'As for the saints who are on the earth, they are the excellent ones in whom is all my delight.'),
('PSA', 16, 4, 'PSA.16.4', 'Their sorrows shall be multiplied who give gifts to another god. Their drink offerings of blood I will not offer, nor take their names on my lips.'),
('PSA', 16, 5, 'PSA.16.5', 'The LORD assigned my portion and my cup. You made my lot secure.'),
('PSA', 16, 6, 'PSA.16.6', 'The lines have fallen to me in pleasant places. Yes, I have a good inheritance.'),
('PSA', 16, 7, 'PSA.16.7', 'I will bless the LORD, who has given me counsel. Yes, my heart instructs me in the night seasons.'),
('PSA', 16, 8, 'PSA.16.8', 'I have set the LORD always before me. Because he is at my right hand, I shall not be moved.'),
('PSA', 16, 9, 'PSA.16.9', 'Therefore my heart is glad, and my tongue rejoices. My body shall also dwell in safety.'),
('PSA', 16, 10, 'PSA.16.10', 'For you will not leave my soul in Sheol, neither will you allow your holy one to see corruption.'),
('PSA', 16, 11, 'PSA.16.11', 'You will show me the path of life. In your presence is fullness of joy. In your right hand there are pleasures forever more.'),
('PSA', 17, 1, 'PSA.17.1', 'Hear, LORD, my righteous plea. Give ear to my prayer that doesn’t go out of deceitful lips.'),
('PSA', 17, 2, 'PSA.17.2', 'Let my sentence come out of your presence. Let your eyes look on equity.'),
('PSA', 17, 3, 'PSA.17.3', 'You have proved my heart. You have visited me in the night. You have tried me, and found nothing. I have resolved that my mouth shall not disobey.'),
('PSA', 17, 4, 'PSA.17.4', 'As for the deeds of men, by the word of your lips, I have kept myself from the ways of the violent.'),
('PSA', 17, 5, 'PSA.17.5', 'My steps have held fast to your paths. My feet have not slipped.'),
('PSA', 17, 6, 'PSA.17.6', 'I have called on you, for you will answer me, God. Turn your ear to me. Hear my speech.'),
('PSA', 17, 7, 'PSA.17.7', 'Show your marvelous loving kindness, you who save those who take refuge by your right hand from their enemies.'),
('PSA', 17, 8, 'PSA.17.8', 'Keep me as the apple of your eye. Hide me under the shadow of your wings,'),
('PSA', 17, 9, 'PSA.17.9', 'from the wicked who oppress me, my deadly enemies, who surround me.'),
('PSA', 17, 10, 'PSA.17.10', 'They close up their callous hearts. With their mouth they speak proudly.'),
('PSA', 17, 11, 'PSA.17.11', 'They have now surrounded us in our steps. They set their eyes to cast us down to the earth.'),
('PSA', 17, 12, 'PSA.17.12', 'He is like a lion that is greedy of his prey, as it were a young lion lurking in secret places.'),
('PSA', 17, 13, 'PSA.17.13', 'Arise, LORD, confront him. Cast him down. Deliver my soul from the wicked by your sword,'),
('PSA', 17, 14, 'PSA.17.14', 'from men by your hand, LORD, from men of the world, whose portion is in this life. You fill the belly of your cherished ones. Your sons have plenty, and they store up wealth for their children.'),
('PSA', 17, 15, 'PSA.17.15', 'As for me, I shall see your face in righteousness. I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with seeing your form.'),
('PSA', 18, 1, 'PSA.18.1', 'I love you, LORD, my strength.'),
('PSA', 18, 2, 'PSA.18.2', 'The LORD is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my rock, in whom I take refuge; my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower.'),
('PSA', 18, 3, 'PSA.18.3', 'I call on the LORD, who is worthy to be praised; and I am saved from my enemies.'),
('PSA', 18, 4, 'PSA.18.4', 'The cords of death surrounded me. The floods of ungodliness made me afraid.'),
('PSA', 18, 5, 'PSA.18.5', 'The cords of Sheol were around me. The snares of death came on me.'),
('PSA', 18, 6, 'PSA.18.6', 'In my distress I called on the LORD, and cried to my God. He heard my voice out of his temple. My cry before him came into his ears.'),
('PSA', 18, 7, 'PSA.18.7', 'Then the earth shook and trembled. The foundations also of the mountains quaked and were shaken, because he was angry.'),
('PSA', 18, 8, 'PSA.18.8', 'Smoke went out of his nostrils. Consuming fire came out of his mouth. Coals were kindled by it.'),
('PSA', 18, 9, 'PSA.18.9', 'He bowed the heavens also, and came down. Thick darkness was under his feet.'),
('PSA', 18, 10, 'PSA.18.10', 'He rode on a cherub, and flew. Yes, he soared on the wings of the wind.'),
('PSA', 18, 11, 'PSA.18.11', 'He made darkness his hiding place, his pavilion around him, darkness of waters, thick clouds of the skies.'),
('PSA', 18, 12, 'PSA.18.12', 'At the brightness before him his thick clouds passed, hailstones and coals of fire.'),
('PSA', 18, 13, 'PSA.18.13', 'The LORD also thundered in the sky. The Most High uttered his voice: hailstones and coals of fire.'),
('PSA', 18, 14, 'PSA.18.14', 'He sent out his arrows, and scattered them. He routed them with great lightning bolts.'),
('PSA', 18, 15, 'PSA.18.15', 'Then the channels of waters appeared. The foundations of the world were laid bare at your rebuke, LORD, at the blast of the breath of your nostrils.'),
('PSA', 18, 16, 'PSA.18.16', 'He sent from on high. He took me. He drew me out of many waters.'),
('PSA', 18, 17, 'PSA.18.17', 'He delivered me from my strong enemy, from those who hated me; for they were too mighty for me.'),
('PSA', 18, 18, 'PSA.18.18', 'They came on me in the day of my calamity, but the LORD was my support.'),
('PSA', 18, 19, 'PSA.18.19', 'He brought me out also into a large place. He delivered me, because he delighted in me.'),
('PSA', 18, 20, 'PSA.18.20', 'The LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness. According to the cleanness of my hands, he has recompensed me.'),
('PSA', 18, 21, 'PSA.18.21', 'For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.'),
('PSA', 18, 22, 'PSA.18.22', 'For all his ordinances were before me. I didn’t put away his statutes from me.'),
('PSA', 18, 23, 'PSA.18.23', 'I was also blameless with him. I kept myself from my iniquity.'),
('PSA', 18, 24, 'PSA.18.24', 'Therefore the LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight.'),
('PSA', 18, 25, 'PSA.18.25', 'With the merciful you will show yourself merciful. With the perfect man, you will show yourself perfect.'),
('PSA', 18, 26, 'PSA.18.26', 'With the pure, you will show yourself pure. With the crooked you will show yourself shrewd.'),
('PSA', 18, 27, 'PSA.18.27', 'For you will save the afflicted people, but the arrogant eyes you will bring down.'),
('PSA', 18, 28, 'PSA.18.28', 'For you will light my lamp, LORD. My God will light up my darkness.'),
('PSA', 18, 29, 'PSA.18.29', 'For by you, I advance through a troop. By my God, I leap over a wall.'),
('PSA', 18, 30, 'PSA.18.30', 'As for God, his way is perfect. The LORD’s word is tried. He is a shield to all those who take refuge in him.'),
('PSA', 18, 31, 'PSA.18.31', 'For who is God, except the LORD? Who is a rock, besides our God,'),
('PSA', 18, 32, 'PSA.18.32', 'the God who arms me with strength, and makes my way perfect?'),
('PSA', 18, 33, 'PSA.18.33', 'He makes my feet like deer’s feet, and sets me on my high places.'),
('PSA', 18, 34, 'PSA.18.34', 'He teaches my hands to war, so that my arms bend a bow of bronze.'),
('PSA', 18, 35, 'PSA.18.35', 'You have also given me the shield of your salvation. Your right hand sustains me. Your gentleness has made me great.'),
('PSA', 18, 36, 'PSA.18.36', 'You have enlarged my steps under me, My feet have not slipped.'),
('PSA', 18, 37, 'PSA.18.37', 'I will pursue my enemies, and overtake them. I won’t turn away until they are consumed.'),
('PSA', 18, 38, 'PSA.18.38', 'I will strike them through, so that they will not be able to rise. They shall fall under my feet.'),
('PSA', 18, 39, 'PSA.18.39', 'For you have armed me with strength to the battle. You have subdued under me those who rose up against me.'),
('PSA', 18, 40, 'PSA.18.40', 'You have also made my enemies turn their backs to me, that I might cut off those who hate me.'),
('PSA', 18, 41, 'PSA.18.41', 'They cried, but there was no one to save; even to the LORD, but he didn’t answer them.'),
('PSA', 18, 42, 'PSA.18.42', 'Then I beat them small as the dust before the wind. I cast them out as the mire of the streets.'),
('PSA', 18, 43, 'PSA.18.43', 'You have delivered me from the strivings of the people. You have made me the head of the nations. A people whom I have not known shall serve me.'),
('PSA', 18, 44, 'PSA.18.44', 'As soon as they hear of me they shall obey me. The foreigners shall submit themselves to me.'),
('PSA', 18, 45, 'PSA.18.45', 'The foreigners shall fade away, and shall come trembling out of their strongholds.'),
('PSA', 18, 46, 'PSA.18.46', 'The LORD lives! Blessed be my rock. Exalted be the God of my salvation,'),
('PSA', 18, 47, 'PSA.18.47', 'even the God who executes vengeance for me, and subdues peoples under me.'),
('PSA', 18, 48, 'PSA.18.48', 'He rescues me from my enemies. Yes, you lift me up above those who rise up against me. You deliver me from the violent man.'),
('PSA', 18, 49, 'PSA.18.49', 'Therefore I will give thanks to you, LORD, among the nations, and will sing praises to your name.'),
('PSA', 18, 50, 'PSA.18.50', 'He gives great deliverance to his king, and shows loving kindness to his anointed, to David and to his offspring, forever more.'),
('PSA', 19, 1, 'PSA.19.1', 'The heavens declare the glory of God. The expanse shows his handiwork.'),
('PSA', 19, 2, 'PSA.19.2', 'Day after day they pour out speech, and night after night they display knowledge.'),
('PSA', 19, 3, 'PSA.19.3', 'There is no speech nor language where their voice is not heard.'),
('PSA', 19, 4, 'PSA.19.4', 'Their voice has gone out through all the earth, their words to the end of the world. In them he has set a tent for the sun,'),
('PSA', 19, 5, 'PSA.19.5', 'which is as a bridegroom coming out of his room, like a strong man rejoicing to run his course.'),
('PSA', 19, 6, 'PSA.19.6', 'His going out is from the end of the heavens, his circuit to its ends. There is nothing hidden from its heat.'),
('PSA', 19, 7, 'PSA.19.7', 'The LORD’s law is perfect, restoring the soul. The LORD’s covenant is sure, making wise the simple.'),
('PSA', 19, 8, 'PSA.19.8', 'The LORD’s precepts are right, rejoicing the heart. The LORD’s commandment is pure, enlightening the eyes.'),
('PSA', 19, 9, 'PSA.19.9', 'The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring forever. The LORD’s ordinances are true, and righteous altogether.'),
('PSA', 19, 10, 'PSA.19.10', 'They are more to be desired than gold, yes, than much fine gold, sweeter also than honey and the extract of the honeycomb.'),
('PSA', 19, 11, 'PSA.19.11', 'Moreover your servant is warned by them. In keeping them there is great reward.'),
('PSA', 19, 12, 'PSA.19.12', 'Who can discern his errors? Forgive me from hidden errors.'),
('PSA', 19, 13, 'PSA.19.13', 'Keep back your servant also from presumptuous sins. Let them not have dominion over me. Then I will be upright. I will be blameless and innocent of great transgression.'),
('PSA', 19, 14, 'PSA.19.14', 'Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be acceptable in your sight, LORD, my rock, and my redeemer.'),
('PSA', 20, 1, 'PSA.20.1', 'May the LORD answer you in the day of trouble. May the name of the God of Jacob set you up on high,'),
('PSA', 20, 2, 'PSA.20.2', 'send you help from the sanctuary, grant you support from Zion,'),
('PSA', 20, 3, 'PSA.20.3', 'remember all your offerings, and accept your burned sacrifice. Selah.'),
('PSA', 20, 4, 'PSA.20.4', 'May he grant you your heart’s desire, and fulfill all your counsel.'),
('PSA', 20, 5, 'PSA.20.5', 'We will triumph in your salvation. In the name of our God, we will set up our banners. May the LORD grant all your requests.'),
('PSA', 20, 6, 'PSA.20.6', 'Now I know that the LORD saves his anointed. He will answer him from his holy heaven, with the saving strength of his right hand.'),
('PSA', 20, 7, 'PSA.20.7', 'Some trust in chariots, and some in horses, but we trust in the name of the LORD our God.'),
('PSA', 20, 8, 'PSA.20.8', 'They are bowed down and fallen, but we rise up, and stand upright.'),
('PSA', 20, 9, 'PSA.20.9', 'Save, LORD! Let the King answer us when we call!'),
('PSA', 21, 1, 'PSA.21.1', 'The king rejoices in your strength, LORD! How greatly he rejoices in your salvation!'),
('PSA', 21, 2, 'PSA.21.2', 'You have given him his heart’s desire, and have not withheld the request of his lips. Selah.'),
('PSA', 21, 3, 'PSA.21.3', 'For you meet him with the blessings of goodness. You set a crown of fine gold on his head.'),
('PSA', 21, 4, 'PSA.21.4', 'He asked life of you and you gave it to him, even length of days forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 21, 5, 'PSA.21.5', 'His glory is great in your salvation. You lay honor and majesty on him.'),
('PSA', 21, 6, 'PSA.21.6', 'For you make him most blessed forever. You make him glad with joy in your presence.'),
('PSA', 21, 7, 'PSA.21.7', 'For the king trusts in the LORD. Through the loving kindness of the Most High, he shall not be moved.'),
('PSA', 21, 8, 'PSA.21.8', 'Your hand will find out all of your enemies. Your right hand will find out those who hate you.'),
('PSA', 21, 9, 'PSA.21.9', 'You will make them as a fiery furnace in the time of your anger. The LORD will swallow them up in his wrath. The fire shall devour them.'),
('PSA', 21, 10, 'PSA.21.10', 'You will destroy their descendants from the earth, their posterity from among the children of men.'),
('PSA', 21, 11, 'PSA.21.11', 'For they intended evil against you. They plotted evil against you which cannot succeed.'),
('PSA', 21, 12, 'PSA.21.12', 'For you will make them turn their back, when you aim drawn bows at their face.'),
('PSA', 21, 13, 'PSA.21.13', 'Be exalted, LORD, in your strength, so we will sing and praise your power.'),
('PSA', 22, 1, 'PSA.22.1', 'My God, my God, why have you forsaken me? Why are you so far from helping me, and from the words of my groaning?'),
('PSA', 22, 2, 'PSA.22.2', 'My God, I cry in the daytime, but you don’t answer; in the night season, and am not silent.'),
('PSA', 22, 3, 'PSA.22.3', 'But you are holy, you who inhabit the praises of Israel.'),
('PSA', 22, 4, 'PSA.22.4', 'Our fathers trusted in you. They trusted, and you delivered them.'),
('PSA', 22, 5, 'PSA.22.5', 'They cried to you, and were delivered. They trusted in you, and were not disappointed.'),
('PSA', 22, 6, 'PSA.22.6', 'But I am a worm, and no man; a reproach of men, and despised by the people.'),
('PSA', 22, 7, 'PSA.22.7', 'All those who see me mock me. They insult me with their lips. They shake their heads, saying,'),
('PSA', 22, 8, 'PSA.22.8', '“He trusts in the LORD. Let him deliver him. Let him rescue him, since he delights in him.”'),
('PSA', 22, 9, 'PSA.22.9', 'But you brought me out of the womb. You made me trust while at my mother’s breasts.'),
('PSA', 22, 10, 'PSA.22.10', 'I was thrown on you from my mother’s womb. You are my God since my mother bore me.'),
('PSA', 22, 11, 'PSA.22.11', 'Don’t be far from me, for trouble is near. For there is no one to help.'),
('PSA', 22, 12, 'PSA.22.12', 'Many bulls have surrounded me. Strong bulls of Bashan have encircled me.'),
('PSA', 22, 13, 'PSA.22.13', 'They open their mouths wide against me, lions tearing prey and roaring.'),
('PSA', 22, 14, 'PSA.22.14', 'I am poured out like water. All my bones are out of joint. My heart is like wax. It is melted within me.'),
('PSA', 22, 15, 'PSA.22.15', 'My strength is dried up like a potsherd. My tongue sticks to the roof of my mouth. You have brought me into the dust of death.'),
('PSA', 22, 16, 'PSA.22.16', 'For dogs have surrounded me. A company of evildoers have enclosed me. They have pierced my hands and feet.'),
('PSA', 22, 17, 'PSA.22.17', 'I can count all of my bones. They look and stare at me.'),
('PSA', 22, 18, 'PSA.22.18', 'They divide my garments among them. They cast lots for my clothing.'),
('PSA', 22, 19, 'PSA.22.19', 'But don’t be far off, LORD. You are my help. Hurry to help me!'),
('PSA', 22, 20, 'PSA.22.20', 'Deliver my soul from the sword, my precious life from the power of the dog.'),
('PSA', 22, 21, 'PSA.22.21', 'Save me from the lion’s mouth! Yes, you have rescued me from the horns of the wild oxen.'),
('PSA', 22, 22, 'PSA.22.22', 'I will declare your name to my brothers. Among the assembly, I will praise you.'),
('PSA', 22, 23, 'PSA.22.23', 'You who fear the LORD, praise him! All you descendants of Jacob, glorify him! Stand in awe of him, all you descendants of Israel!'),
('PSA', 22, 24, 'PSA.22.24', 'For he has not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted, neither has he hidden his face from him; but when he cried to him, he heard.'),
('PSA', 22, 25, 'PSA.22.25', 'My praise of you comes in the great assembly. I will pay my vows before those who fear him.'),
('PSA', 22, 26, 'PSA.22.26', 'The humble shall eat and be satisfied. They shall praise the LORD who seek after him. Let your hearts live forever.'),
('PSA', 22, 27, 'PSA.22.27', 'All the ends of the earth shall remember and turn to the LORD. All the relatives of the nations shall worship before you.'),
('PSA', 22, 28, 'PSA.22.28', 'For the kingdom is the LORD’s. He is the ruler over the nations.'),
('PSA', 22, 29, 'PSA.22.29', 'All the rich ones of the earth shall eat and worship. All those who go down to the dust shall bow before him, even he who can’t keep his soul alive.'),
('PSA', 22, 30, 'PSA.22.30', 'Posterity shall serve him. Future generations shall be told about the Lord.'),
('PSA', 22, 31, 'PSA.22.31', 'They shall come and shall declare his righteousness to a people that shall be born, for he has done it.'),
('PSA', 23, 1, 'PSA.23.1', 'The LORD is my shepherd; I shall lack nothing.'),
('PSA', 23, 2, 'PSA.23.2', 'He makes me lie down in green pastures. He leads me beside still waters.'),
('PSA', 23, 3, 'PSA.23.3', 'He restores my soul. He guides me in the paths of righteousness for his name’s sake.'),
('PSA', 23, 4, 'PSA.23.4', 'Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil, for you are with me. Your rod and your staff, they comfort me.'),
('PSA', 23, 5, 'PSA.23.5', 'You prepare a table before me in the presence of my enemies. You anoint my head with oil. My cup runs over.'),
('PSA', 23, 6, 'PSA.23.6', 'Surely goodness and loving kindness shall follow me all the days of my life, and I will dwell in the LORD’s house forever.'),
('PSA', 24, 1, 'PSA.24.1', 'The earth is the LORD’s, with its fullness; the world, and those who dwell in it.'),
('PSA', 24, 2, 'PSA.24.2', 'For he has founded it on the seas, and established it on the floods.'),
('PSA', 24, 3, 'PSA.24.3', 'Who may ascend to the LORD’s hill? Who may stand in his holy place?'),
('PSA', 24, 4, 'PSA.24.4', 'He who has clean hands and a pure heart; who has not lifted up his soul to falsehood, and has not sworn deceitfully.'),
('PSA', 24, 5, 'PSA.24.5', 'He shall receive a blessing from the LORD, righteousness from the God of his salvation.'),
('PSA', 24, 6, 'PSA.24.6', 'This is the generation of those who seek Him, who seek your face—even Jacob. Selah.'),
('PSA', 24, 7, 'PSA.24.7', 'Lift up your heads, you gates! Be lifted up, you everlasting doors, and the King of glory will come in.'),
('PSA', 24, 8, 'PSA.24.8', 'Who is the King of glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.'),
('PSA', 24, 9, 'PSA.24.9', 'Lift up your heads, you gates; yes, lift them up, you everlasting doors, and the King of glory will come in.'),
('PSA', 24, 10, 'PSA.24.10', 'Who is this King of glory? The LORD of Armies is the King of glory! Selah.'),
('PSA', 25, 1, 'PSA.25.1', 'To you, LORD, I lift up my soul.'),
('PSA', 25, 2, 'PSA.25.2', 'My God, I have trusted in you. Don’t let me be shamed. Don’t let my enemies triumph over me.'),
('PSA', 25, 3, 'PSA.25.3', 'Yes, no one who waits for you will be shamed. They will be shamed who deal treacherously without cause.'),
('PSA', 25, 4, 'PSA.25.4', 'Show me your ways, LORD. Teach me your paths.'),
('PSA', 25, 5, 'PSA.25.5', 'Guide me in your truth, and teach me, for you are the God of my salvation. I wait for you all day long.'),
('PSA', 25, 6, 'PSA.25.6', 'LORD, remember your tender mercies and your loving kindness, for they are from old times.'),
('PSA', 25, 7, 'PSA.25.7', 'Don’t remember the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions. Remember me according to your loving kindness, for your goodness’ sake, LORD.'),
('PSA', 25, 8, 'PSA.25.8', 'Good and upright is the LORD, therefore he will instruct sinners in the way.'),
('PSA', 25, 9, 'PSA.25.9', 'He will guide the humble in justice. He will teach the humble his way.'),
('PSA', 25, 10, 'PSA.25.10', 'All the paths of the LORD are loving kindness and truth to such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.'),
('PSA', 25, 11, 'PSA.25.11', 'For your name’s sake, LORD, pardon my iniquity, for it is great.'),
('PSA', 25, 12, 'PSA.25.12', 'What man is he who fears the LORD? He shall instruct him in the way that he shall choose.'),
('PSA', 25, 13, 'PSA.25.13', 'His soul will dwell at ease. His offspring will inherit the land.'),
('PSA', 25, 14, 'PSA.25.14', 'The friendship of the LORD is with those who fear him. He will show them his covenant.'),
('PSA', 25, 15, 'PSA.25.15', 'My eyes are ever on the LORD, for he will pluck my feet out of the net.'),
('PSA', 25, 16, 'PSA.25.16', 'Turn to me, and have mercy on me, for I am desolate and afflicted.'),
('PSA', 25, 17, 'PSA.25.17', 'The troubles of my heart are enlarged. Oh bring me out of my distresses.'),
('PSA', 25, 18, 'PSA.25.18', 'Consider my affliction and my travail. Forgive all my sins.'),
('PSA', 25, 19, 'PSA.25.19', 'Consider my enemies, for they are many. They hate me with cruel hatred.'),
('PSA', 25, 20, 'PSA.25.20', 'Oh keep my soul, and deliver me. Let me not be disappointed, for I take refuge in you.'),
('PSA', 25, 21, 'PSA.25.21', 'Let integrity and uprightness preserve me, for I wait for you.'),
('PSA', 25, 22, 'PSA.25.22', 'God, redeem Israel out of all his troubles.'),
('PSA', 26, 1, 'PSA.26.1', 'Judge me, LORD, for I have walked in my integrity. I have trusted also in the LORD without wavering.'),
('PSA', 26, 2, 'PSA.26.2', 'Examine me, LORD, and prove me. Try my heart and my mind.'),
('PSA', 26, 3, 'PSA.26.3', 'For your loving kindness is before my eyes. I have walked in your truth.'),
('PSA', 26, 4, 'PSA.26.4', 'I have not sat with deceitful men, neither will I go in with hypocrites.'),
('PSA', 26, 5, 'PSA.26.5', 'I hate the assembly of evildoers, and will not sit with the wicked.'),
('PSA', 26, 6, 'PSA.26.6', 'I will wash my hands in innocence, so I will go about your altar, LORD,'),
('PSA', 26, 7, 'PSA.26.7', 'that I may make the voice of thanksgiving to be heard and tell of all your wondrous deeds.'),
('PSA', 26, 8, 'PSA.26.8', 'LORD, I love the habitation of your house, the place where your glory dwells.'),
('PSA', 26, 9, 'PSA.26.9', 'Don’t gather my soul with sinners, nor my life with bloodthirsty men'),
('PSA', 26, 10, 'PSA.26.10', 'in whose hands is wickedness; their right hand is full of bribes.'),
('PSA', 26, 11, 'PSA.26.11', 'But as for me, I will walk in my integrity. Redeem me, and be merciful to me.'),
('PSA', 26, 12, 'PSA.26.12', 'My foot stands in an even place. In the congregations I will bless the LORD.'),
('PSA', 27, 1, 'PSA.27.1', 'The LORD is my light and my salvation. Whom shall I fear? The LORD is the strength of my life. Of whom shall I be afraid?'),
('PSA', 27, 2, 'PSA.27.2', 'When evildoers came at me to eat up my flesh, even my adversaries and my foes, they stumbled and fell.'),
('PSA', 27, 3, 'PSA.27.3', 'Though an army should encamp against me, my heart shall not fear. Though war should rise against me, even then I will be confident.'),
('PSA', 27, 4, 'PSA.27.4', 'One thing I have asked of the LORD, that I will seek after: that I may dwell in the LORD’s house all the days of my life, to see the LORD’s beauty, and to inquire in his temple.'),
('PSA', 27, 5, 'PSA.27.5', 'For in the day of trouble, he will keep me secretly in his pavilion. In the secret place of his tabernacle, he will hide me. He will lift me up on a rock.'),
('PSA', 27, 6, 'PSA.27.6', 'Now my head will be lifted up above my enemies around me. I will offer sacrifices of joy in his tent. I will sing, yes, I will sing praises to the LORD.'),
('PSA', 27, 7, 'PSA.27.7', 'Hear, LORD, when I cry with my voice. Have mercy also on me, and answer me.'),
('PSA', 27, 8, 'PSA.27.8', 'When you said, “Seek my face,” my heart said to you, “I will seek your face, LORD.”'),
('PSA', 27, 9, 'PSA.27.9', 'Don’t hide your face from me. Don’t put your servant away in anger. You have been my help. Don’t abandon me, neither forsake me, God of my salvation.'),
('PSA', 27, 10, 'PSA.27.10', 'When my father and my mother forsake me, then the LORD will take me up.'),
('PSA', 27, 11, 'PSA.27.11', 'Teach me your way, LORD. Lead me in a straight path, because of my enemies.'),
('PSA', 27, 12, 'PSA.27.12', 'Don’t deliver me over to the desire of my adversaries, for false witnesses have risen up against me, such as breathe out cruelty.'),
('PSA', 27, 13, 'PSA.27.13', 'I am still confident of this: I will see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living.'),
('PSA', 27, 14, 'PSA.27.14', 'Wait for the LORD. Be strong, and let your heart take courage. Yes, wait for the LORD.'),
('PSA', 28, 1, 'PSA.28.1', 'To you, LORD, I call. My rock, don’t be deaf to me, lest, if you are silent to me, I would become like those who go down into the pit.'),
('PSA', 28, 2, 'PSA.28.2', 'Hear the voice of my petitions, when I cry to you, when I lift up my hands toward your Most Holy Place.'),
('PSA', 28, 3, 'PSA.28.3', 'Don’t draw me away with the wicked, with the workers of iniquity who speak peace with their neighbors, but mischief is in their hearts.'),
('PSA', 28, 4, 'PSA.28.4', 'Give them according to their work, and according to the wickedness of their doings. Give them according to the operation of their hands. Bring back on them what they deserve.'),
('PSA', 28, 5, 'PSA.28.5', 'Because they don’t respect the works of the LORD, nor the operation of his hands, he will break them down and not build them up.'),
('PSA', 28, 6, 'PSA.28.6', 'Blessed be the LORD, because he has heard the voice of my petitions.'),
('PSA', 28, 7, 'PSA.28.7', 'The LORD is my strength and my shield. My heart has trusted in him, and I am helped. Therefore my heart greatly rejoices. With my song I will thank him.'),
('PSA', 28, 8, 'PSA.28.8', 'The LORD is their strength. He is a stronghold of salvation to his anointed.'),
('PSA', 28, 9, 'PSA.28.9', 'Save your people, and bless your inheritance. Be their shepherd also, and bear them up forever.'),
('PSA', 29, 1, 'PSA.29.1', 'Ascribe to the LORD, you sons of the mighty, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.'),
('PSA', 29, 2, 'PSA.29.2', 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his name. Worship the LORD in holy array.'),
('PSA', 29, 3, 'PSA.29.3', 'The LORD’s voice is on the waters. The God of glory thunders, even the LORD on many waters.'),
('PSA', 29, 4, 'PSA.29.4', 'The LORD’s voice is powerful. The LORD’s voice is full of majesty.'),
('PSA', 29, 5, 'PSA.29.5', 'The LORD’s voice breaks the cedars. Yes, the LORD breaks in pieces the cedars of Lebanon.'),
('PSA', 29, 6, 'PSA.29.6', 'He makes them also to skip like a calf; Lebanon and Sirion like a young, wild ox.'),
('PSA', 29, 7, 'PSA.29.7', 'The LORD’s voice strikes with flashes of lightning.'),
('PSA', 29, 8, 'PSA.29.8', 'The LORD’s voice shakes the wilderness. The LORD shakes the wilderness of Kadesh.'),
('PSA', 29, 9, 'PSA.29.9', 'The LORD’s voice makes the deer calve, and strips the forests bare. In his temple everything says, “Glory!”'),
('PSA', 29, 10, 'PSA.29.10', 'The LORD sat enthroned at the Flood. Yes, the LORD sits as King forever.'),
('PSA', 29, 11, 'PSA.29.11', 'The LORD will give strength to his people. The LORD will bless his people with peace.'),
('PSA', 30, 1, 'PSA.30.1', 'I will extol you, LORD, for you have raised me up, and have not made my foes to rejoice over me.'),
('PSA', 30, 2, 'PSA.30.2', 'LORD my God, I cried to you, and you have healed me.'),
('PSA', 30, 3, 'PSA.30.3', 'LORD, you have brought up my soul from Sheol. You have kept me alive, that I should not go down to the pit.'),
('PSA', 30, 4, 'PSA.30.4', 'Sing praise to the LORD, you saints of his. Give thanks to his holy name.'),
('PSA', 30, 5, 'PSA.30.5', 'For his anger is but for a moment. His favor is for a lifetime. Weeping may stay for the night, but joy comes in the morning.'),
('PSA', 30, 6, 'PSA.30.6', 'As for me, I said in my prosperity, “I shall never be moved.”'),
('PSA', 30, 7, 'PSA.30.7', 'You, LORD, when you favored me, made my mountain stand strong; but when you hid your face, I was troubled.'),
('PSA', 30, 8, 'PSA.30.8', 'I cried to you, LORD. I made supplication to the Lord:'),
('PSA', 30, 9, 'PSA.30.9', '“What profit is there in my destruction, if I go down to the pit? Shall the dust praise you? Shall it declare your truth?'),
('PSA', 30, 10, 'PSA.30.10', 'Hear, LORD, and have mercy on me. LORD, be my helper.”'),
('PSA', 30, 11, 'PSA.30.11', 'You have turned my mourning into dancing for me. You have removed my sackcloth, and clothed me with gladness,'),
('PSA', 30, 12, 'PSA.30.12', 'to the end that my heart may sing praise to you, and not be silent. LORD my God, I will give thanks to you forever!'),
('PSA', 31, 1, 'PSA.31.1', 'In you, LORD, I take refuge. Let me never be disappointed. Deliver me in your righteousness.'),
('PSA', 31, 2, 'PSA.31.2', 'Bow down your ear to me. Deliver me speedily. Be to me a strong rock, a house of defense to save me.'),
('PSA', 31, 3, 'PSA.31.3', 'For you are my rock and my fortress, therefore for your name’s sake lead me and guide me.'),
('PSA', 31, 4, 'PSA.31.4', 'Pluck me out of the net that they have laid secretly for me, for you are my stronghold.'),
('PSA', 31, 5, 'PSA.31.5', 'Into your hand I commend my spirit. You redeem me, LORD, God of truth.'),
('PSA', 31, 6, 'PSA.31.6', 'I hate those who regard lying vanities, but I trust in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 31, 7, 'PSA.31.7', 'I will be glad and rejoice in your loving kindness, for you have seen my affliction. You have known my soul in adversities.'),
('PSA', 31, 8, 'PSA.31.8', 'You have not shut me up into the hand of the enemy. You have set my feet in a large place.'),
('PSA', 31, 9, 'PSA.31.9', 'Have mercy on me, LORD, for I am in distress. My eye, my soul, and my body waste away with grief.'),
('PSA', 31, 10, 'PSA.31.10', 'For my life is spent with sorrow, my years with sighing. My strength fails because of my iniquity. My bones are wasted away.'),
('PSA', 31, 11, 'PSA.31.11', 'Because of all my adversaries I have become utterly contemptible to my neighbors, a horror to my acquaintances. Those who saw me on the street fled from me.'),
('PSA', 31, 12, 'PSA.31.12', 'I am forgotten from their hearts like a dead man. I am like broken pottery.'),
('PSA', 31, 13, 'PSA.31.13', 'For I have heard the slander of many, terror on every side, while they conspire together against me, they plot to take away my life.'),
('PSA', 31, 14, 'PSA.31.14', 'But I trust in you, LORD. I said, “You are my God.”'),
('PSA', 31, 15, 'PSA.31.15', 'My times are in your hand. Deliver me from the hand of my enemies, and from those who persecute me.'),
('PSA', 31, 16, 'PSA.31.16', 'Make your face to shine on your servant. Save me in your loving kindness.'),
('PSA', 31, 17, 'PSA.31.17', 'Let me not be disappointed, LORD, for I have called on you. Let the wicked be disappointed. Let them be silent in Sheol.'),
('PSA', 31, 18, 'PSA.31.18', 'Let the lying lips be mute, which speak against the righteous insolently, with pride and contempt.'),
('PSA', 31, 19, 'PSA.31.19', 'Oh how great is your goodness, which you have laid up for those who fear you, which you have worked for those who take refuge in you, before the sons of men!'),
('PSA', 31, 20, 'PSA.31.20', 'In the shelter of your presence you will hide them from the plotting of man. You will keep them secretly in a dwelling away from the strife of tongues.'),
('PSA', 31, 21, 'PSA.31.21', 'Praise be to the LORD, for he has shown me his marvelous loving kindness in a strong city.'),
('PSA', 31, 22, 'PSA.31.22', 'As for me, I said in my haste, “I am cut off from before your eyes.” Nevertheless you heard the voice of my petitions when I cried to you.'),
('PSA', 31, 23, 'PSA.31.23', 'Oh love the LORD, all you his saints! The LORD preserves the faithful, and fully recompenses him who behaves arrogantly.'),
('PSA', 31, 24, 'PSA.31.24', 'Be strong, and let your heart take courage, all you who hope in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 32, 1, 'PSA.32.1', 'Blessed is he whose disobedience is forgiven, whose sin is covered.'),
('PSA', 32, 2, 'PSA.32.2', 'Blessed is the man to whom the LORD doesn’t impute iniquity, in whose spirit there is no deceit.'),
('PSA', 32, 3, 'PSA.32.3', 'When I kept silence, my bones wasted away through my groaning all day long.'),
('PSA', 32, 4, 'PSA.32.4', 'For day and night your hand was heavy on me. My strength was sapped in the heat of summer. Selah.'),
('PSA', 32, 5, 'PSA.32.5', 'I acknowledged my sin to you. I didn’t hide my iniquity. I said, I will confess my transgressions to the LORD, and you forgave the iniquity of my sin. Selah.'),
('PSA', 32, 6, 'PSA.32.6', 'For this, let everyone who is godly pray to you in a time when you may be found. Surely when the great waters overflow, they shall not reach to him.'),
('PSA', 32, 7, 'PSA.32.7', 'You are my hiding place. You will preserve me from trouble. You will surround me with songs of deliverance. Selah.'),
('PSA', 32, 8, 'PSA.32.8', 'I will instruct you and teach you in the way which you shall go. I will counsel you with my eye on you.'),
('PSA', 32, 9, 'PSA.32.9', 'Don’t be like the horse, or like the mule, which have no understanding, who are controlled by bit and bridle, or else they will not come near to you.'),
('PSA', 32, 10, 'PSA.32.10', 'Many sorrows come to the wicked, but loving kindness shall surround him who trusts in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 32, 11, 'PSA.32.11', 'Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, you righteous! Shout for joy, all you who are upright in heart!'),
('PSA', 33, 1, 'PSA.33.1', 'Rejoice in the LORD, you righteous! Praise is fitting for the upright.'),
('PSA', 33, 2, 'PSA.33.2', 'Give thanks to the LORD with the lyre. Sing praises to him with the harp of ten strings.'),
('PSA', 33, 3, 'PSA.33.3', 'Sing to him a new song. Play skillfully with a shout of joy!'),
('PSA', 33, 4, 'PSA.33.4', 'For the LORD’s word is right. All his work is done in faithfulness.'),
('PSA', 33, 5, 'PSA.33.5', 'He loves righteousness and justice. The earth is full of the loving kindness of the LORD.'),
('PSA', 33, 6, 'PSA.33.6', 'By the LORD’s word, the heavens were made: all their army by the breath of his mouth.'),
('PSA', 33, 7, 'PSA.33.7', 'He gathers the waters of the sea together as a heap. He lays up the deeps in storehouses.'),
('PSA', 33, 8, 'PSA.33.8', 'Let all the earth fear the LORD. Let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him.'),
('PSA', 33, 9, 'PSA.33.9', 'For he spoke, and it was done. He commanded, and it stood firm.'),
('PSA', 33, 10, 'PSA.33.10', 'The LORD brings the counsel of the nations to nothing. He makes the thoughts of the peoples to be of no effect.'),
('PSA', 33, 11, 'PSA.33.11', 'The counsel of the LORD stands fast forever, the thoughts of his heart to all generations.'),
('PSA', 33, 12, 'PSA.33.12', 'Blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD, the people whom he has chosen for his own inheritance.'),
('PSA', 33, 13, 'PSA.33.13', 'The LORD looks from heaven. He sees all the sons of men.'),
('PSA', 33, 14, 'PSA.33.14', 'From the place of his habitation he looks out on all the inhabitants of the earth,'),
('PSA', 33, 15, 'PSA.33.15', 'he who fashions all of their hearts; and he considers all of their works.'),
('PSA', 33, 16, 'PSA.33.16', 'There is no king saved by the multitude of an army. A mighty man is not delivered by great strength.'),
('PSA', 33, 17, 'PSA.33.17', 'A horse is a vain thing for safety, neither does he deliver any by his great power.'),
('PSA', 33, 18, 'PSA.33.18', 'Behold, the LORD’s eye is on those who fear him, on those who hope in his loving kindness,'),
('PSA', 33, 19, 'PSA.33.19', 'to deliver their soul from death, to keep them alive in famine.'),
('PSA', 33, 20, 'PSA.33.20', 'Our soul has waited for the LORD. He is our help and our shield.'),
('PSA', 33, 21, 'PSA.33.21', 'For our heart rejoices in him, because we have trusted in his holy name.'),
('PSA', 33, 22, 'PSA.33.22', 'Let your loving kindness be on us, LORD, since we have hoped in you.'),
('PSA', 34, 1, 'PSA.34.1', 'I will bless the LORD at all times. His praise will always be in my mouth.'),
('PSA', 34, 2, 'PSA.34.2', 'My soul shall boast in the LORD. The humble shall hear of it and be glad.'),
('PSA', 34, 3, 'PSA.34.3', 'Oh magnify the LORD with me. Let’s exalt his name together.'),
('PSA', 34, 4, 'PSA.34.4', 'I sought the LORD, and he answered me, and delivered me from all my fears.'),
('PSA', 34, 5, 'PSA.34.5', 'They looked to him, and were radiant. Their faces shall never be covered with shame.'),
('PSA', 34, 6, 'PSA.34.6', 'This poor man cried, and the LORD heard him, and saved him out of all his troubles.'),
('PSA', 34, 7, 'PSA.34.7', 'The LORD’s angel encamps around those who fear him, and delivers them.'),
('PSA', 34, 8, 'PSA.34.8', 'Oh taste and see that the LORD is good. Blessed is the man who takes refuge in him.'),
('PSA', 34, 9, 'PSA.34.9', 'Oh fear the LORD, you his saints, for there is no lack with those who fear him.'),
('PSA', 34, 10, 'PSA.34.10', 'The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger, but those who seek the LORD shall not lack any good thing.'),
('PSA', 34, 11, 'PSA.34.11', 'Come, you children, listen to me. I will teach you the fear of the LORD.'),
('PSA', 34, 12, 'PSA.34.12', 'Who is someone who desires life, and loves many days, that he may see good?'),
('PSA', 34, 13, 'PSA.34.13', 'Keep your tongue from evil, and your lips from speaking lies.'),
('PSA', 34, 14, 'PSA.34.14', 'Depart from evil, and do good. Seek peace, and pursue it.'),
('PSA', 34, 15, 'PSA.34.15', 'The LORD’s eyes are toward the righteous. His ears listen to their cry.'),
('PSA', 34, 16, 'PSA.34.16', 'The LORD’s face is against those who do evil, to cut off their memory from the earth.'),
('PSA', 34, 17, 'PSA.34.17', 'The righteous cry, and the LORD hears, and delivers them out of all their troubles.'),
('PSA', 34, 18, 'PSA.34.18', 'The LORD is near to those who have a broken heart, and saves those who have a crushed spirit.'),
('PSA', 34, 19, 'PSA.34.19', 'Many are the afflictions of the righteous, but the LORD delivers him out of them all.'),
('PSA', 34, 20, 'PSA.34.20', 'He protects all of his bones. Not one of them is broken.'),
('PSA', 34, 21, 'PSA.34.21', 'Evil shall kill the wicked. Those who hate the righteous shall be condemned.'),
('PSA', 34, 22, 'PSA.34.22', 'The LORD redeems the soul of his servants. None of those who take refuge in him shall be condemned.'),
('PSA', 35, 1, 'PSA.35.1', 'Contend, LORD, with those who contend with me. Fight against those who fight against me.'),
('PSA', 35, 2, 'PSA.35.2', 'Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand up for my help.'),
('PSA', 35, 3, 'PSA.35.3', 'Brandish the spear and block those who pursue me. Tell my soul, “I am your salvation.”'),
('PSA', 35, 4, 'PSA.35.4', 'Let those who seek after my soul be disappointed and brought to dishonor. Let those who plot my ruin be turned back and confounded.'),
('PSA', 35, 5, 'PSA.35.5', 'Let them be as chaff before the wind, the LORD’s angel driving them on.'),
('PSA', 35, 6, 'PSA.35.6', 'Let their way be dark and slippery, the LORD’s angel pursuing them.'),
('PSA', 35, 7, 'PSA.35.7', 'For without cause they have hidden their net in a pit for me. Without cause they have dug a pit for my soul.'),
('PSA', 35, 8, 'PSA.35.8', 'Let destruction come on him unawares. Let his net that he has hidden catch himself. Let him fall into that destruction.'),
('PSA', 35, 9, 'PSA.35.9', 'My soul shall be joyful in the LORD. It shall rejoice in his salvation.'),
('PSA', 35, 10, 'PSA.35.10', 'All my bones shall say, “LORD, who is like you, who delivers the poor from him who is too strong for him; yes, the poor and the needy from him who robs him?”'),
('PSA', 35, 11, 'PSA.35.11', 'Unrighteous witnesses rise up. They ask me about things that I don’t know about.'),
('PSA', 35, 12, 'PSA.35.12', 'They reward me evil for good, to the bereaving of my soul.'),
('PSA', 35, 13, 'PSA.35.13', 'But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth. I afflicted my soul with fasting. My prayer returned into my own bosom.'),
('PSA', 35, 14, 'PSA.35.14', 'I behaved myself as though it had been my friend or my brother. I bowed down mourning, as one who mourns his mother.'),
('PSA', 35, 15, 'PSA.35.15', 'But in my adversity, they rejoiced, and gathered themselves together. The attackers gathered themselves together against me, and I didn’t know it. They tore at me, and didn’t cease.'),
('PSA', 35, 16, 'PSA.35.16', 'Like the profane mockers in feasts, they gnashed their teeth at me.'),
('PSA', 35, 17, 'PSA.35.17', 'Lord, how long will you look on? Rescue my soul from their destruction, my precious life from the lions.'),
('PSA', 35, 18, 'PSA.35.18', 'I will give you thanks in the great assembly. I will praise you among many people.'),
('PSA', 35, 19, 'PSA.35.19', 'Don’t let those who are my enemies wrongfully rejoice over me; neither let those who hate me without a cause wink their eyes.'),
('PSA', 35, 20, 'PSA.35.20', 'For they don’t speak peace, but they devise deceitful words against those who are quiet in the land.'),
('PSA', 35, 21, 'PSA.35.21', 'Yes, they opened their mouth wide against me. They said, “Aha! Aha! Our eye has seen it!”'),
('PSA', 35, 22, 'PSA.35.22', 'You have seen it, LORD. Don’t keep silent. Lord, don’t be far from me.'),
('PSA', 35, 23, 'PSA.35.23', 'Wake up! Rise up to defend me, my God! My Lord, contend for me!'),
('PSA', 35, 24, 'PSA.35.24', 'Vindicate me, LORD my God, according to your righteousness. Don’t let them gloat over me.'),
('PSA', 35, 25, 'PSA.35.25', 'Don’t let them say in their heart, “Aha! That’s the way we want it!” Don’t let them say, “We have swallowed him up!”'),
('PSA', 35, 26, 'PSA.35.26', 'Let them be disappointed and confounded together who rejoice at my calamity. Let them be clothed with shame and dishonor who magnify themselves against me.'),
('PSA', 35, 27, 'PSA.35.27', 'Let those who favor my righteous cause shout for joy and be glad. Yes, let them say continually, “May the LORD be magnified, who has pleasure in the prosperity of his servant!”'),
('PSA', 35, 28, 'PSA.35.28', 'My tongue shall talk about your righteousness and about your praise all day long.'),
('PSA', 36, 1, 'PSA.36.1', 'A revelation is within my heart about the disobedience of the wicked: There is no fear of God before his eyes.'),
('PSA', 36, 2, 'PSA.36.2', 'For he flatters himself in his own eyes, too much to detect and hate his sin.'),
('PSA', 36, 3, 'PSA.36.3', 'The words of his mouth are iniquity and deceit. He has ceased to be wise and to do good.'),
('PSA', 36, 4, 'PSA.36.4', 'He plots iniquity on his bed. He sets himself in a way that is not good. He doesn’t abhor evil.'),
('PSA', 36, 5, 'PSA.36.5', 'Your loving kindness, LORD, is in the heavens. Your faithfulness reaches to the skies.'),
('PSA', 36, 6, 'PSA.36.6', 'Your righteousness is like the mountains of God. Your judgments are like a great deep. LORD, you preserve man and animal.'),
('PSA', 36, 7, 'PSA.36.7', 'How precious is your loving kindness, God! The children of men take refuge under the shadow of your wings.'),
('PSA', 36, 8, 'PSA.36.8', 'They shall be abundantly satisfied with the abundance of your house. You will make them drink of the river of your pleasures.'),
('PSA', 36, 9, 'PSA.36.9', 'For with you is the spring of life. In your light we will see light.'),
('PSA', 36, 10, 'PSA.36.10', 'Oh continue your loving kindness to those who know you, your righteousness to the upright in heart.'),
('PSA', 36, 11, 'PSA.36.11', 'Don’t let the foot of pride come against me. Don’t let the hand of the wicked drive me away.'),
('PSA', 36, 12, 'PSA.36.12', 'There the workers of iniquity are fallen. They are thrust down, and shall not be able to rise.'),
('PSA', 37, 1, 'PSA.37.1', 'Don’t fret because of evildoers, neither be envious against those who work unrighteousness.'),
('PSA', 37, 2, 'PSA.37.2', 'For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither like the green herb.'),
('PSA', 37, 3, 'PSA.37.3', 'Trust in the LORD, and do good. Dwell in the land, and enjoy safe pasture.'),
('PSA', 37, 4, 'PSA.37.4', 'Also delight yourself in the LORD, and he will give you the desires of your heart.'),
('PSA', 37, 5, 'PSA.37.5', 'Commit your way to the LORD. Trust also in him, and he will do this:'),
('PSA', 37, 6, 'PSA.37.6', 'he will make your righteousness shine out like light, and your justice as the noon day sun.'),
('PSA', 37, 7, 'PSA.37.7', 'Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him. Don’t fret because of him who prospers in his way, because of the man who makes wicked plots happen.'),
('PSA', 37, 8, 'PSA.37.8', 'Cease from anger, and forsake wrath. Don’t fret; it leads only to evildoing.'),
('PSA', 37, 9, 'PSA.37.9', 'For evildoers shall be cut off, but those who wait for the LORD shall inherit the land.'),
('PSA', 37, 10, 'PSA.37.10', 'For yet a little while, and the wicked will be no more. Yes, though you look for his place, he isn’t there.'),
('PSA', 37, 11, 'PSA.37.11', 'But the humble shall inherit the land, and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace.'),
('PSA', 37, 12, 'PSA.37.12', 'The wicked plots against the just, and gnashes at him with his teeth.'),
('PSA', 37, 13, 'PSA.37.13', 'The Lord will laugh at him, for he sees that his day is coming.'),
('PSA', 37, 14, 'PSA.37.14', 'The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have bent their bow, to cast down the poor and needy, to kill those who are upright on the path.'),
('PSA', 37, 15, 'PSA.37.15', 'Their sword shall enter into their own heart. Their bows shall be broken.'),
('PSA', 37, 16, 'PSA.37.16', 'Better is a little that the righteous has, than the abundance of many wicked.'),
('PSA', 37, 17, 'PSA.37.17', 'For the arms of the wicked shall be broken, but the LORD upholds the righteous.'),
('PSA', 37, 18, 'PSA.37.18', 'The LORD knows the days of the perfect. Their inheritance shall be forever.'),
('PSA', 37, 19, 'PSA.37.19', 'They shall not be disappointed in the time of evil. In the days of famine they shall be satisfied.'),
('PSA', 37, 20, 'PSA.37.20', 'But the wicked shall perish. The enemies of the LORD shall be like the beauty of the fields. They will vanish— vanish like smoke.'),
('PSA', 37, 21, 'PSA.37.21', 'The wicked borrow, and don’t pay back, but the righteous give generously.'),
('PSA', 37, 22, 'PSA.37.22', 'For such as are blessed by him shall inherit the land. Those who are cursed by him shall be cut off.'),
('PSA', 37, 23, 'PSA.37.23', 'A man’s steps are established by the LORD. He delights in his way.'),
('PSA', 37, 24, 'PSA.37.24', 'Though he stumble, he shall not fall, for the LORD holds him up with his hand.'),
('PSA', 37, 25, 'PSA.37.25', 'I have been young, and now am old, yet I have not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his children begging for bread.'),
('PSA', 37, 26, 'PSA.37.26', 'All day long he deals graciously, and lends. His offspring is blessed.'),
('PSA', 37, 27, 'PSA.37.27', 'Depart from evil, and do good. Live securely forever.'),
('PSA', 37, 28, 'PSA.37.28', 'For the LORD loves justice, and doesn’t forsake his saints. They are preserved forever, but the children of the wicked shall be cut off.'),
('PSA', 37, 29, 'PSA.37.29', 'The righteous shall inherit the land, and live in it forever.'),
('PSA', 37, 30, 'PSA.37.30', 'The mouth of the righteous talks of wisdom. His tongue speaks justice.'),
('PSA', 37, 31, 'PSA.37.31', 'The law of his God is in his heart. None of his steps shall slide.'),
('PSA', 37, 32, 'PSA.37.32', 'The wicked watch the righteous, and seek to kill him.'),
('PSA', 37, 33, 'PSA.37.33', 'The LORD will not leave him in his hand, nor condemn him when he is judged.'),
('PSA', 37, 34, 'PSA.37.34', 'Wait for the LORD, and keep his way, and he will exalt you to inherit the land. When the wicked are cut off, you shall see it.'),
('PSA', 37, 35, 'PSA.37.35', 'I have seen the wicked in great power, spreading himself like a green tree in its native soil.'),
('PSA', 37, 36, 'PSA.37.36', 'But he passed away, and behold, he was not. Yes, I sought him, but he could not be found.'),
('PSA', 37, 37, 'PSA.37.37', 'Mark the perfect man, and see the upright, for there is a future for the man of peace.'),
('PSA', 37, 38, 'PSA.37.38', 'As for transgressors, they shall be destroyed together. The future of the wicked shall be cut off.'),
('PSA', 37, 39, 'PSA.37.39', 'But the salvation of the righteous is from the LORD. He is their stronghold in the time of trouble.'),
('PSA', 37, 40, 'PSA.37.40', 'The LORD helps them and rescues them. He rescues them from the wicked and saves them, because they have taken refuge in him.'),
('PSA', 38, 1, 'PSA.38.1', 'LORD, don’t rebuke me in your wrath, neither chasten me in your hot displeasure.'),
('PSA', 38, 2, 'PSA.38.2', 'For your arrows have pierced me, your hand presses hard on me.'),
('PSA', 38, 3, 'PSA.38.3', 'There is no soundness in my flesh because of your indignation, neither is there any health in my bones because of my sin.'),
('PSA', 38, 4, 'PSA.38.4', 'For my iniquities have gone over my head. As a heavy burden, they are too heavy for me.'),
('PSA', 38, 5, 'PSA.38.5', 'My wounds are loathsome and corrupt because of my foolishness.'),
('PSA', 38, 6, 'PSA.38.6', 'I am in pain and bowed down greatly. I go mourning all day long.'),
('PSA', 38, 7, 'PSA.38.7', 'For my waist is filled with burning. There is no soundness in my flesh.'),
('PSA', 38, 8, 'PSA.38.8', 'I am faint and severely bruised. I have groaned by reason of the anguish of my heart.'),
('PSA', 38, 9, 'PSA.38.9', 'Lord, all my desire is before you. My groaning is not hidden from you.'),
('PSA', 38, 10, 'PSA.38.10', 'My heart throbs. My strength fails me. As for the light of my eyes, it has also left me.'),
('PSA', 38, 11, 'PSA.38.11', 'My lovers and my friends stand aloof from my plague. My kinsmen stand far away.'),
('PSA', 38, 12, 'PSA.38.12', 'They also who seek after my life lay snares. Those who seek my hurt speak mischievous things, and meditate deceits all day long.'),
('PSA', 38, 13, 'PSA.38.13', 'But I, as a deaf man, don’t hear. I am as a mute man who doesn’t open his mouth.'),
('PSA', 38, 14, 'PSA.38.14', 'Yes, I am as a man who doesn’t hear, in whose mouth are no reproofs.'),
('PSA', 38, 15, 'PSA.38.15', 'For I hope in you, LORD. You will answer, Lord my God.'),
('PSA', 38, 16, 'PSA.38.16', 'For I said, “Don’t let them gloat over me, or exalt themselves over me when my foot slips.”'),
('PSA', 38, 17, 'PSA.38.17', 'For I am ready to fall. My pain is continually before me.'),
('PSA', 38, 18, 'PSA.38.18', 'For I will declare my iniquity. I will be sorry for my sin.'),
('PSA', 38, 19, 'PSA.38.19', 'But my enemies are vigorous and many. Those who hate me without reason are numerous.'),
('PSA', 38, 20, 'PSA.38.20', 'They who give evil for good are also adversaries to me, because I follow what is good.'),
('PSA', 38, 21, 'PSA.38.21', 'Don’t forsake me, LORD. My God, don’t be far from me.'),
('PSA', 38, 22, 'PSA.38.22', 'Hurry to help me, Lord, my salvation.'),
('PSA', 39, 1, 'PSA.39.1', 'I said, “I will watch my ways, so that I don’t sin with my tongue. I will keep my mouth with a bridle while the wicked is before me.”'),
('PSA', 39, 2, 'PSA.39.2', 'I was mute with silence. I held my peace, even from good. My sorrow was stirred.'),
('PSA', 39, 3, 'PSA.39.3', 'My heart was hot within me. While I meditated, the fire burned. I spoke with my tongue:'),
('PSA', 39, 4, 'PSA.39.4', '“LORD, show me my end, what is the measure of my days. Let me know how frail I am.'),
('PSA', 39, 5, 'PSA.39.5', 'Behold, you have made my days hand widths. My lifetime is as nothing before you. Surely every man stands as a breath.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 39, 6, 'PSA.39.6', '“Surely every man walks like a shadow. Surely they busy themselves in vain. He heaps up, and doesn’t know who shall gather.'),
('PSA', 39, 7, 'PSA.39.7', 'Now, Lord, what do I wait for? My hope is in you.'),
('PSA', 39, 8, 'PSA.39.8', 'Deliver me from all my transgressions. Don’t make me the reproach of the foolish.'),
('PSA', 39, 9, 'PSA.39.9', 'I was mute. I didn’t open my mouth, because you did it.'),
('PSA', 39, 10, 'PSA.39.10', 'Remove your scourge away from me. I am overcome by the blow of your hand.'),
('PSA', 39, 11, 'PSA.39.11', 'When you rebuke and correct man for iniquity, you consume his wealth like a moth. Surely every man is but a breath.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 39, 12, 'PSA.39.12', '“Hear my prayer, LORD, and give ear to my cry. Don’t be silent at my tears. For I am a stranger with you, a foreigner, as all my fathers were.'),
('PSA', 39, 13, 'PSA.39.13', 'Oh spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go away and exist no more.”'),
('PSA', 40, 1, 'PSA.40.1', 'I waited patiently for the LORD. He turned to me, and heard my cry.'),
('PSA', 40, 2, 'PSA.40.2', 'He brought me up also out of a horrible pit, out of the miry clay. He set my feet on a rock, and gave me a firm place to stand.'),
('PSA', 40, 3, 'PSA.40.3', 'He has put a new song in my mouth, even praise to our God. Many shall see it, and fear, and shall trust in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 40, 4, 'PSA.40.4', 'Blessed is the man who makes the LORD his trust, and doesn’t respect the proud, nor such as turn away to lies.'),
('PSA', 40, 5, 'PSA.40.5', 'Many, LORD, my God, are the wonderful works which you have done, and your thoughts which are toward us. They can’t be declared back to you. If I would declare and speak of them, they are more than can be counted.'),
('PSA', 40, 6, 'PSA.40.6', 'Sacrifice and offering you didn’t desire. You have opened my ears. You have not required burnt offering and sin offering.'),
('PSA', 40, 7, 'PSA.40.7', 'Then I said, “Behold, I have come. It is written about me in the book in the scroll.'),
('PSA', 40, 8, 'PSA.40.8', 'I delight to do your will, my God. Yes, your law is within my heart.”'),
('PSA', 40, 9, 'PSA.40.9', 'I have proclaimed glad news of righteousness in the great assembly. Behold, I will not seal my lips, LORD, you know.'),
('PSA', 40, 10, 'PSA.40.10', 'I have not hidden your righteousness within my heart. I have declared your faithfulness and your salvation. I have not concealed your loving kindness and your truth from the great assembly.'),
('PSA', 40, 11, 'PSA.40.11', 'Don’t withhold your tender mercies from me, LORD. Let your loving kindness and your truth continually preserve me.'),
('PSA', 40, 12, 'PSA.40.12', 'For innumerable evils have surrounded me. My iniquities have overtaken me, so that I am not able to look up. They are more than the hairs of my head. My heart has failed me.'),
('PSA', 40, 13, 'PSA.40.13', 'Be pleased, LORD, to deliver me. Hurry to help me, LORD.'),
('PSA', 40, 14, 'PSA.40.14', 'Let them be disappointed and confounded together who seek after my soul to destroy it. Let them be turned backward and brought to dishonor who delight in my hurt.'),
('PSA', 40, 15, 'PSA.40.15', 'Let them be desolate by reason of their shame that tell me, “Aha! Aha!”'),
('PSA', 40, 16, 'PSA.40.16', 'Let all those who seek you rejoice and be glad in you. Let such as love your salvation say continually, “Let the LORD be exalted!”'),
('PSA', 40, 17, 'PSA.40.17', 'But I am poor and needy. May the Lord think about me. You are my help and my deliverer. Don’t delay, my God.'),
('PSA', 41, 1, 'PSA.41.1', 'Blessed is he who considers the poor. The LORD will deliver him in the day of evil.'),
('PSA', 41, 2, 'PSA.41.2', 'The LORD will preserve him, and keep him alive. He shall be blessed on the earth, and he will not surrender him to the will of his enemies.'),
('PSA', 41, 3, 'PSA.41.3', 'The LORD will sustain him on his sickbed, and restore him from his bed of illness.'),
('PSA', 41, 4, 'PSA.41.4', 'I said, “LORD, have mercy on me! Heal me, for I have sinned against you.”'),
('PSA', 41, 5, 'PSA.41.5', 'My enemies speak evil against me: “When will he die, and his name perish?”'),
('PSA', 41, 6, 'PSA.41.6', 'If he comes to see me, he speaks falsehood. His heart gathers iniquity to itself. When he goes abroad, he tells it.'),
('PSA', 41, 7, 'PSA.41.7', 'All who hate me whisper together against me. They imagine the worst for me.'),
('PSA', 41, 8, 'PSA.41.8', '“An evil disease”, they say, “has afflicted him. Now that he lies he shall rise up no more.”'),
('PSA', 41, 9, 'PSA.41.9', 'Yes, my own familiar friend, in whom I trusted, who ate bread with me, has lifted up his heel against me.'),
('PSA', 41, 10, 'PSA.41.10', 'But you, LORD, have mercy on me, and raise me up, that I may repay them.'),
('PSA', 41, 11, 'PSA.41.11', 'By this I know that you delight in me, because my enemy doesn’t triumph over me.'),
('PSA', 41, 12, 'PSA.41.12', 'As for me, you uphold me in my integrity, and set me in your presence forever.'),
('PSA', 41, 13, 'PSA.41.13', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting and to everlasting! Amen and amen.'),
('PSA', 42, 1, 'PSA.42.1', 'As the deer pants for the water brooks, so my soul pants after you, God.'),
('PSA', 42, 2, 'PSA.42.2', 'My soul thirsts for God, for the living God. When shall I come and appear before God?'),
('PSA', 42, 3, 'PSA.42.3', 'My tears have been my food day and night, while they continually ask me, “Where is your God?”'),
('PSA', 42, 4, 'PSA.42.4', 'These things I remember, and pour out my soul within me, how I used to go with the crowd, and led them to God’s house, with the voice of joy and praise, a multitude keeping a holy day.'),
('PSA', 42, 5, 'PSA.42.5', 'Why are you in despair, my soul? Why are you disturbed within me? Hope in God! For I shall still praise him for the saving help of his presence.'),
('PSA', 42, 6, 'PSA.42.6', 'My God, my soul is in despair within me. Therefore I remember you from the land of the Jordan, the heights of Hermon, from the hill Mizar.'),
('PSA', 42, 7, 'PSA.42.7', 'Deep calls to deep at the noise of your waterfalls. All your waves and your billows have swept over me.'),
('PSA', 42, 8, 'PSA.42.8', 'The LORD will command his loving kindness in the daytime. In the night his song shall be with me: a prayer to the God of my life.'),
('PSA', 42, 9, 'PSA.42.9', 'I will ask God, my rock, “Why have you forgotten me? Why do I go mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?”'),
('PSA', 42, 10, 'PSA.42.10', 'As with a sword in my bones, my adversaries reproach me, while they continually ask me, “Where is your God?”'),
('PSA', 42, 11, 'PSA.42.11', 'Why are you in despair, my soul? Why are you disturbed within me? Hope in God! For I shall still praise him, the saving help of my countenance, and my God.'),
('PSA', 43, 1, 'PSA.43.1', 'Vindicate me, God, and plead my cause against an ungodly nation. Oh, deliver me from deceitful and wicked men.'),
('PSA', 43, 2, 'PSA.43.2', 'For you are the God of my strength. Why have you rejected me? Why do I go mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?'),
('PSA', 43, 3, 'PSA.43.3', 'Oh, send out your light and your truth. Let them lead me. Let them bring me to your holy hill, to your tents.'),
('PSA', 43, 4, 'PSA.43.4', 'Then I will go to the altar of God, to God, my exceeding joy. I will praise you on the harp, God, my God.'),
('PSA', 43, 5, 'PSA.43.5', 'Why are you in despair, my soul? Why are you disturbed within me? Hope in God! For I shall still praise him: my Savior, my helper, and my God.'),
('PSA', 44, 1, 'PSA.44.1', 'We have heard with our ears, God; our fathers have told us what work you did in their days, in the days of old.'),
('PSA', 44, 2, 'PSA.44.2', 'You drove out the nations with your hand, but you planted them. You afflicted the peoples, but you spread them abroad.'),
('PSA', 44, 3, 'PSA.44.3', 'For they didn’t get the land in possession by their own sword, neither did their own arm save them; but your right hand, your arm, and the light of your face, because you were favorable to them.'),
('PSA', 44, 4, 'PSA.44.4', 'God, you are my King. Command victories for Jacob!'),
('PSA', 44, 5, 'PSA.44.5', 'Through you, we will push down our adversaries. Through your name, we will tread down those who rise up against us.'),
('PSA', 44, 6, 'PSA.44.6', 'For I will not trust in my bow, neither will my sword save me.'),
('PSA', 44, 7, 'PSA.44.7', 'But you have saved us from our adversaries, and have shamed those who hate us.'),
('PSA', 44, 8, 'PSA.44.8', 'In God we have made our boast all day long. We will give thanks to your name forever. Selah.'),
('PSA', 44, 9, 'PSA.44.9', 'But now you rejected us, and brought us to dishonor, and don’t go out with our armies.'),
('PSA', 44, 10, 'PSA.44.10', 'You make us turn back from the adversary. Those who hate us take plunder for themselves.'),
('PSA', 44, 11, 'PSA.44.11', 'You have made us like sheep for food, and have scattered us among the nations.'),
('PSA', 44, 12, 'PSA.44.12', 'You sell your people for nothing, and have gained nothing from their sale.'),
('PSA', 44, 13, 'PSA.44.13', 'You make us a reproach to our neighbors, a scoffing and a derision to those who are around us.'),
('PSA', 44, 14, 'PSA.44.14', 'You make us a byword among the nations, a shaking of the head among the peoples.'),
('PSA', 44, 15, 'PSA.44.15', 'All day long my dishonor is before me, and shame covers my face,'),
('PSA', 44, 16, 'PSA.44.16', 'at the taunt of one who reproaches and verbally abuses, because of the enemy and the avenger.'),
('PSA', 44, 17, 'PSA.44.17', 'All this has come on us, yet we haven’t forgotten you. We haven’t been false to your covenant.'),
('PSA', 44, 18, 'PSA.44.18', 'Our heart has not turned back, neither have our steps strayed from your path,'),
('PSA', 44, 19, 'PSA.44.19', 'though you have crushed us in the haunt of jackals, and covered us with the shadow of death.'),
('PSA', 44, 20, 'PSA.44.20', 'If we have forgotten the name of our God, or spread out our hands to a strange god,'),
('PSA', 44, 21, 'PSA.44.21', 'won’t God search this out? For he knows the secrets of the heart.'),
('PSA', 44, 22, 'PSA.44.22', 'Yes, for your sake we are killed all day long. We are regarded as sheep for the slaughter.'),
('PSA', 44, 23, 'PSA.44.23', 'Wake up! Why do you sleep, Lord? Arise! Don’t reject us forever.'),
('PSA', 44, 24, 'PSA.44.24', 'Why do you hide your face, and forget our affliction and our oppression?'),
('PSA', 44, 25, 'PSA.44.25', 'For our soul is bowed down to the dust. Our body clings to the earth.'),
('PSA', 44, 26, 'PSA.44.26', 'Rise up to help us. Redeem us for your loving kindness’ sake.'),
('PSA', 45, 1, 'PSA.45.1', 'My heart overflows with a noble theme. I recite my verses for the king. My tongue is like the pen of a skillful writer.'),
('PSA', 45, 2, 'PSA.45.2', 'You are the most excellent of the sons of men. Grace has anointed your lips, therefore God has blessed you forever.'),
('PSA', 45, 3, 'PSA.45.3', 'Strap your sword on your thigh, O mighty one, in your splendor and your majesty.'),
('PSA', 45, 4, 'PSA.45.4', 'In your majesty ride on victoriously on behalf of truth, humility, and righteousness. Let your right hand display awesome deeds.'),
('PSA', 45, 5, 'PSA.45.5', 'Your arrows are sharp. The nations fall under you, with arrows in the heart of the king’s enemies.'),
('PSA', 45, 6, 'PSA.45.6', 'Your throne, God, is forever and ever. A scepter of equity is the scepter of your kingdom.'),
('PSA', 45, 7, 'PSA.45.7', 'You have loved righteousness, and hated wickedness. Therefore God, your God, has anointed you with the oil of gladness above your fellows.'),
('PSA', 45, 8, 'PSA.45.8', 'All your garments smell like myrrh, aloes, and cassia. Out of ivory palaces stringed instruments have made you glad.'),
('PSA', 45, 9, 'PSA.45.9', 'Kings’ daughters are among your honorable women. At your right hand the queen stands in gold of Ophir.'),
('PSA', 45, 10, 'PSA.45.10', 'Listen, daughter, consider, and turn your ear. Forget your own people, and also your father’s house.'),
('PSA', 45, 11, 'PSA.45.11', 'So the king will desire your beauty, honor him, for he is your lord.'),
('PSA', 45, 12, 'PSA.45.12', 'The daughter of Tyre comes with a gift. The rich among the people entreat your favor.'),
('PSA', 45, 13, 'PSA.45.13', 'The princess inside is all glorious. Her clothing is interwoven with gold.'),
('PSA', 45, 14, 'PSA.45.14', 'She shall be led to the king in embroidered work. The virgins, her companions who follow her, shall be brought to you.'),
('PSA', 45, 15, 'PSA.45.15', 'With gladness and rejoicing they shall be led. They shall enter into the king’s palace.'),
('PSA', 45, 16, 'PSA.45.16', 'Your sons will take the place of your fathers. You shall make them princes in all the earth.'),
('PSA', 45, 17, 'PSA.45.17', 'I will make your name to be remembered in all generations. Therefore the peoples shall give you thanks forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 46, 1, 'PSA.46.1', 'God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.'),
('PSA', 46, 2, 'PSA.46.2', 'Therefore we won’t be afraid, though the earth changes, though the mountains are shaken into the heart of the seas;'),
('PSA', 46, 3, 'PSA.46.3', 'though its waters roar and are troubled, though the mountains tremble with their swelling. Selah.'),
('PSA', 46, 4, 'PSA.46.4', 'There is a river, the streams of which make the city of God glad, the holy place of the tents of the Most High.'),
('PSA', 46, 5, 'PSA.46.5', 'God is within her. She shall not be moved. God will help her at dawn.'),
('PSA', 46, 6, 'PSA.46.6', 'The nations raged. The kingdoms were moved. He lifted his voice and the earth melted.'),
('PSA', 46, 7, 'PSA.46.7', 'The LORD of Armies is with us. The God of Jacob is our refuge. Selah.'),
('PSA', 46, 8, 'PSA.46.8', 'Come, see the LORD’s works, what desolations he has made on the earth.'),
('PSA', 46, 9, 'PSA.46.9', 'He makes wars cease to the end of the earth. He breaks the bow, and shatters the spear. He burns the chariots in the fire.'),
('PSA', 46, 10, 'PSA.46.10', '“Be still, and know that I am God. I will be exalted among the nations. I will be exalted on the earth.”'),
('PSA', 46, 11, 'PSA.46.11', 'The LORD of Armies is with us. The God of Jacob is our refuge. Selah.'),
('PSA', 47, 1, 'PSA.47.1', 'Oh clap your hands, all you nations. Shout to God with the voice of triumph!'),
('PSA', 47, 2, 'PSA.47.2', 'For the LORD Most High is awesome. He is a great King over all the earth.'),
('PSA', 47, 3, 'PSA.47.3', 'He subdues nations under us, and peoples under our feet.'),
('PSA', 47, 4, 'PSA.47.4', 'He chooses our inheritance for us, the glory of Jacob whom he loved. Selah.'),
('PSA', 47, 5, 'PSA.47.5', 'God has gone up with a shout, the LORD with the sound of a trumpet.'),
('PSA', 47, 6, 'PSA.47.6', 'Sing praises to God! Sing praises! Sing praises to our King! Sing praises!'),
('PSA', 47, 7, 'PSA.47.7', 'For God is the King of all the earth. Sing praises with understanding.'),
('PSA', 47, 8, 'PSA.47.8', 'God reigns over the nations. God sits on his holy throne.'),
('PSA', 47, 9, 'PSA.47.9', 'The princes of the peoples are gathered together, the people of the God of Abraham. For the shields of the earth belong to God. He is greatly exalted!'),
('PSA', 48, 1, 'PSA.48.1', 'Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised, in the city of our God, in his holy mountain.'),
('PSA', 48, 2, 'PSA.48.2', 'Beautiful in elevation, the joy of the whole earth, is Mount Zion, on the north sides, the city of the great King.'),
('PSA', 48, 3, 'PSA.48.3', 'God has shown himself in her citadels as a refuge.'),
('PSA', 48, 4, 'PSA.48.4', 'For, behold, the kings assembled themselves, they passed by together.'),
('PSA', 48, 5, 'PSA.48.5', 'They saw it, then they were amazed. They were dismayed. They hurried away.'),
('PSA', 48, 6, 'PSA.48.6', 'Trembling took hold of them there, pain, as of a woman in travail.'),
('PSA', 48, 7, 'PSA.48.7', 'With the east wind, you break the ships of Tarshish.'),
('PSA', 48, 8, 'PSA.48.8', 'As we have heard, so we have seen, in the city of the LORD of Armies, in the city of our God. God will establish it forever. Selah.'),
('PSA', 48, 9, 'PSA.48.9', 'We have thought about your loving kindness, God, in the middle of your temple.'),
('PSA', 48, 10, 'PSA.48.10', 'As is your name, God, so is your praise to the ends of the earth. Your right hand is full of righteousness.'),
('PSA', 48, 11, 'PSA.48.11', 'Let Mount Zion be glad! Let the daughters of Judah rejoice because of your judgments.'),
('PSA', 48, 12, 'PSA.48.12', 'Walk about Zion, and go around her. Number its towers.'),
('PSA', 48, 13, 'PSA.48.13', 'Notice her bulwarks. Consider her palaces, that you may tell it to the next generation.'),
('PSA', 48, 14, 'PSA.48.14', 'For this God is our God forever and ever. He will be our guide even to death.'),
('PSA', 49, 1, 'PSA.49.1', 'Hear this, all you peoples. Listen, all you inhabitants of the world,'),
('PSA', 49, 2, 'PSA.49.2', 'both low and high, rich and poor together.'),
('PSA', 49, 3, 'PSA.49.3', 'My mouth will speak words of wisdom. My heart will utter understanding.'),
('PSA', 49, 4, 'PSA.49.4', 'I will incline my ear to a proverb. I will solve my riddle on the harp.'),
('PSA', 49, 5, 'PSA.49.5', 'Why should I fear in the days of evil, when iniquity at my heels surrounds me?'),
('PSA', 49, 6, 'PSA.49.6', 'Those who trust in their wealth, and boast in the multitude of their riches—'),
('PSA', 49, 7, 'PSA.49.7', 'none of them can by any means redeem his brother, nor give God a ransom for him.'),
('PSA', 49, 8, 'PSA.49.8', 'For the redemption of their life is costly, no payment is ever enough,'),
('PSA', 49, 9, 'PSA.49.9', 'that he should live on forever, that he should not see corruption.'),
('PSA', 49, 10, 'PSA.49.10', 'For he sees that wise men die; likewise the fool and the senseless perish, and leave their wealth to others.'),
('PSA', 49, 11, 'PSA.49.11', 'Their inward thought is that their houses will endure forever, and their dwelling places to all generations. They name their lands after themselves.'),
('PSA', 49, 12, 'PSA.49.12', 'But man, despite his riches, doesn’t endure. He is like the animals that perish.'),
('PSA', 49, 13, 'PSA.49.13', 'This is the destiny of those who are foolish, and of those who approve their sayings. Selah.'),
('PSA', 49, 14, 'PSA.49.14', 'They are appointed as a flock for Sheol. Death shall be their shepherd. The upright shall have dominion over them in the morning. Their beauty shall decay in Sheol, far from their mansion.'),
('PSA', 49, 15, 'PSA.49.15', 'But God will redeem my soul from the power of Sheol, for he will receive me. Selah.'),
('PSA', 49, 16, 'PSA.49.16', 'Don’t be afraid when a man is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased;'),
('PSA', 49, 17, 'PSA.49.17', 'for when he dies he will carry nothing away. His glory won’t descend after him.'),
('PSA', 49, 18, 'PSA.49.18', 'Though while he lived he blessed his soul— and men praise you when you do well for yourself—'),
('PSA', 49, 19, 'PSA.49.19', 'he shall go to the generation of his fathers. They shall never see the light.'),
('PSA', 49, 20, 'PSA.49.20', 'A man who has riches without understanding, is like the animals that perish.'),
('PSA', 50, 1, 'PSA.50.1', 'The Mighty One, God, the LORD, speaks, and calls the earth from sunrise to sunset.'),
('PSA', 50, 2, 'PSA.50.2', 'Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God shines out.'),
('PSA', 50, 3, 'PSA.50.3', 'Our God comes, and does not keep silent. A fire devours before him. It is very stormy around him.'),
('PSA', 50, 4, 'PSA.50.4', 'He calls to the heavens above, to the earth, that he may judge his people:'),
('PSA', 50, 5, 'PSA.50.5', '“Gather my saints together to me, those who have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.”'),
('PSA', 50, 6, 'PSA.50.6', 'The heavens shall declare his righteousness, for God himself is judge. Selah.'),
('PSA', 50, 7, 'PSA.50.7', '“Hear, my people, and I will speak. Israel, I will testify against you. I am God, your God.'),
('PSA', 50, 8, 'PSA.50.8', 'I don’t rebuke you for your sacrifices. Your burnt offerings are continually before me.'),
('PSA', 50, 9, 'PSA.50.9', 'I have no need for a bull from your stall, nor male goats from your pens.'),
('PSA', 50, 10, 'PSA.50.10', 'For every animal of the forest is mine, and the livestock on a thousand hills.'),
('PSA', 50, 11, 'PSA.50.11', 'I know all the birds of the mountains. The wild animals of the field are mine.'),
('PSA', 50, 12, 'PSA.50.12', 'If I were hungry, I would not tell you, for the world is mine, and all that is in it.'),
('PSA', 50, 13, 'PSA.50.13', 'Will I eat the meat of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?'),
('PSA', 50, 14, 'PSA.50.14', 'Offer to God the sacrifice of thanksgiving. Pay your vows to the Most High.'),
('PSA', 50, 15, 'PSA.50.15', 'Call on me in the day of trouble. I will deliver you, and you will honor me.”'),
('PSA', 50, 16, 'PSA.50.16', 'But to the wicked God says, “What right do you have to declare my statutes, that you have taken my covenant on your lips,'),
('PSA', 50, 17, 'PSA.50.17', 'since you hate instruction, and throw my words behind you?'),
('PSA', 50, 18, 'PSA.50.18', 'When you saw a thief, you consented with him, and have participated with adulterers.'),
('PSA', 50, 19, 'PSA.50.19', '“You give your mouth to evil. Your tongue frames deceit.'),
('PSA', 50, 20, 'PSA.50.20', 'You sit and speak against your brother. You slander your own mother’s son.'),
('PSA', 50, 21, 'PSA.50.21', 'You have done these things, and I kept silent. You thought that I was just like you. I will rebuke you, and accuse you in front of your eyes.'),
('PSA', 50, 22, 'PSA.50.22', '“Now consider this, you who forget God, lest I tear you into pieces, and there be no one to deliver.'),
('PSA', 50, 23, 'PSA.50.23', 'Whoever offers the sacrifice of thanksgiving glorifies me, and prepares his way so that I will show God’s salvation to him.”'),
('PSA', 51, 1, 'PSA.51.1', 'Have mercy on me, God, according to your loving kindness. According to the multitude of your tender mercies, blot out my transgressions.'),
('PSA', 51, 2, 'PSA.51.2', 'Wash me thoroughly from my iniquity. Cleanse me from my sin.'),
('PSA', 51, 3, 'PSA.51.3', 'For I know my transgressions. My sin is constantly before me.'),
('PSA', 51, 4, 'PSA.51.4', 'Against you, and you only, I have sinned, and done that which is evil in your sight, so you may be proved right when you speak, and justified when you judge.'),
('PSA', 51, 5, 'PSA.51.5', 'Behold, I was born in iniquity. My mother conceived me in sin.'),
('PSA', 51, 6, 'PSA.51.6', 'Behold, you desire truth in the inward parts. You teach me wisdom in the inmost place.'),
('PSA', 51, 7, 'PSA.51.7', 'Purify me with hyssop, and I will be clean. Wash me, and I will be whiter than snow.'),
('PSA', 51, 8, 'PSA.51.8', 'Let me hear joy and gladness, that the bones which you have broken may rejoice.'),
('PSA', 51, 9, 'PSA.51.9', 'Hide your face from my sins, and blot out all of my iniquities.'),
('PSA', 51, 10, 'PSA.51.10', 'Create in me a clean heart, O God. Renew a right spirit within me.'),
('PSA', 51, 11, 'PSA.51.11', 'Don’t throw me from your presence, and don’t take your Holy Spirit from me.'),
('PSA', 51, 12, 'PSA.51.12', 'Restore to me the joy of your salvation. Uphold me with a willing spirit.'),
('PSA', 51, 13, 'PSA.51.13', 'Then I will teach transgressors your ways. Sinners will be converted to you.'),
('PSA', 51, 14, 'PSA.51.14', 'Deliver me from the guilt of bloodshed, O God, the God of my salvation. My tongue will sing aloud of your righteousness.'),
('PSA', 51, 15, 'PSA.51.15', 'Lord, open my lips. My mouth will declare your praise.'),
('PSA', 51, 16, 'PSA.51.16', 'For you don’t delight in sacrifice, or else I would give it. You have no pleasure in burnt offering.'),
('PSA', 51, 17, 'PSA.51.17', 'The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit. O God, you will not despise a broken and contrite heart.'),
('PSA', 51, 18, 'PSA.51.18', 'Do well in your good pleasure to Zion. Build the walls of Jerusalem.'),
('PSA', 51, 19, 'PSA.51.19', 'Then you will delight in the sacrifices of righteousness, in burnt offerings and in whole burnt offerings. Then they will offer bulls on your altar.'),
('PSA', 52, 1, 'PSA.52.1', 'Why do you boast of mischief, mighty man? God’s loving kindness endures continually.'),
('PSA', 52, 2, 'PSA.52.2', 'Your tongue plots destruction, like a sharp razor, working deceitfully.'),
('PSA', 52, 3, 'PSA.52.3', 'You love evil more than good, lying rather than speaking the truth. Selah.'),
('PSA', 52, 4, 'PSA.52.4', 'You love all devouring words, you deceitful tongue.'),
('PSA', 52, 5, 'PSA.52.5', 'God will likewise destroy you forever. He will take you up, and pluck you out of your tent, and root you out of the land of the living. Selah.'),
('PSA', 52, 6, 'PSA.52.6', 'The righteous also will see it, and fear, and laugh at him, saying,'),
('PSA', 52, 7, 'PSA.52.7', '“Behold, this is the man who didn’t make God his strength, but trusted in the abundance of his riches, and strengthened himself in his wickedness.”'),
('PSA', 52, 8, 'PSA.52.8', 'But as for me, I am like a green olive tree in God’s house. I trust in God’s loving kindness forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 52, 9, 'PSA.52.9', 'I will give you thanks forever, because you have done it. I will hope in your name, for it is good, in the presence of your saints.'),
('PSA', 53, 1, 'PSA.53.1', 'The fool has said in his heart, “There is no God.” They are corrupt, and have done abominable iniquity. There is no one who does good.'),
('PSA', 53, 2, 'PSA.53.2', 'God looks down from heaven on the children of men, to see if there are any who understood, who seek after God.'),
('PSA', 53, 3, 'PSA.53.3', 'Every one of them has gone back. They have become filthy together. There is no one who does good, no, not one.'),
('PSA', 53, 4, 'PSA.53.4', 'Have the workers of iniquity no knowledge, who eat up my people as they eat bread, and don’t call on God?'),
('PSA', 53, 5, 'PSA.53.5', 'There they were in great fear, where no fear was, for God has scattered the bones of him who encamps against you. You have put them to shame, because God has rejected them.'),
('PSA', 53, 6, 'PSA.53.6', 'Oh that the salvation of Israel would come out of Zion! When God brings back his people from captivity, then Jacob shall rejoice, and Israel shall be glad.'),
('PSA', 54, 1, 'PSA.54.1', 'Save me, God, by your name. Vindicate me in your might.'),
('PSA', 54, 2, 'PSA.54.2', 'Hear my prayer, God. Listen to the words of my mouth.'),
('PSA', 54, 3, 'PSA.54.3', 'For strangers have risen up against me. Violent men have sought after my soul. They haven’t set God before them. Selah.'),
('PSA', 54, 4, 'PSA.54.4', 'Behold, God is my helper. The Lord is the one who sustains my soul.'),
('PSA', 54, 5, 'PSA.54.5', 'He will repay the evil to my enemies. Destroy them in your truth.'),
('PSA', 54, 6, 'PSA.54.6', 'With a free will offering, I will sacrifice to you. I will give thanks to your name, LORD, for it is good.'),
('PSA', 54, 7, 'PSA.54.7', 'For he has delivered me out of all trouble. My eye has seen triumph over my enemies.'),
('PSA', 55, 1, 'PSA.55.1', 'Listen to my prayer, God. Don’t hide yourself from my supplication.'),
('PSA', 55, 2, 'PSA.55.2', 'Attend to me, and answer me. I am restless in my complaint, and moan'),
('PSA', 55, 3, 'PSA.55.3', 'because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked. For they bring suffering on me. In anger they hold a grudge against me.'),
('PSA', 55, 4, 'PSA.55.4', 'My heart is severely pained within me. The terrors of death have fallen on me.'),
('PSA', 55, 5, 'PSA.55.5', 'Fearfulness and trembling have come on me. Horror has overwhelmed me.'),
('PSA', 55, 6, 'PSA.55.6', 'I said, “Oh that I had wings like a dove! Then I would fly away, and be at rest.'),
('PSA', 55, 7, 'PSA.55.7', 'Behold, then I would wander far off. I would lodge in the wilderness.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 55, 8, 'PSA.55.8', '“I would hurry to a shelter from the stormy wind and storm.”'),
('PSA', 55, 9, 'PSA.55.9', 'Confuse them, Lord, and confound their language, for I have seen violence and strife in the city.'),
('PSA', 55, 10, 'PSA.55.10', 'Day and night they prowl around on its walls. Malice and abuse are also within her.'),
('PSA', 55, 11, 'PSA.55.11', 'Destructive forces are within her. Threats and lies don’t depart from her streets.'),
('PSA', 55, 12, 'PSA.55.12', 'For it was not an enemy who insulted me, then I could have endured it. Neither was it he who hated me who raised himself up against me, then I would have hidden myself from him.'),
('PSA', 55, 13, 'PSA.55.13', 'But it was you, a man like me, my companion, and my familiar friend.'),
('PSA', 55, 14, 'PSA.55.14', 'We took sweet fellowship together. We walked in God’s house with company.'),
('PSA', 55, 15, 'PSA.55.15', 'Let death come suddenly on them. Let them go down alive into Sheol. For wickedness is among them, in their dwelling.'),
('PSA', 55, 16, 'PSA.55.16', 'As for me, I will call on God. The LORD will save me.'),
('PSA', 55, 17, 'PSA.55.17', 'Evening, morning, and at noon, I will cry out in distress. He will hear my voice.'),
('PSA', 55, 18, 'PSA.55.18', 'He has redeemed my soul in peace from the battle that was against me, although there are many who oppose me.'),
('PSA', 55, 19, 'PSA.55.19', 'God, who is enthroned forever, will hear and answer them. Selah. They never change and don’t fear God.'),
('PSA', 55, 20, 'PSA.55.20', 'He raises his hands against his friends. He has violated his covenant.'),
('PSA', 55, 21, 'PSA.55.21', 'His mouth was smooth as butter, but his heart was war. His words were softer than oil, yet they were drawn swords.'),
('PSA', 55, 22, 'PSA.55.22', 'Cast your burden on the LORD and he will sustain you. He will never allow the righteous to be moved.'),
('PSA', 55, 23, 'PSA.55.23', 'But you, God, will bring them down into the pit of destruction. Bloodthirsty and deceitful men shall not live out half their days, but I will trust in you.'),
('PSA', 56, 1, 'PSA.56.1', 'Be merciful to me, God, for man wants to swallow me up. All day long, he attacks and oppresses me.'),
('PSA', 56, 2, 'PSA.56.2', 'My enemies want to swallow me up all day long, for they are many who fight proudly against me.'),
('PSA', 56, 3, 'PSA.56.3', 'When I am afraid, I will put my trust in you.'),
('PSA', 56, 4, 'PSA.56.4', 'In God, I praise his word. In God, I put my trust. I will not be afraid. What can flesh do to me?'),
('PSA', 56, 5, 'PSA.56.5', 'All day long they twist my words. All their thoughts are against me for evil.'),
('PSA', 56, 6, 'PSA.56.6', 'They conspire and lurk, watching my steps. They are eager to take my life.'),
('PSA', 56, 7, 'PSA.56.7', 'Shall they escape by iniquity? In anger cast down the peoples, God.'),
('PSA', 56, 8, 'PSA.56.8', 'You count my wanderings. You put my tears into your container. Aren’t they in your book?'),
('PSA', 56, 9, 'PSA.56.9', 'Then my enemies shall turn back in the day that I call. I know this: that God is for me.'),
('PSA', 56, 10, 'PSA.56.10', 'In God, I will praise his word. In the LORD, I will praise his word.'),
('PSA', 56, 11, 'PSA.56.11', 'I have put my trust in God. I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?'),
('PSA', 56, 12, 'PSA.56.12', 'Your vows are on me, God. I will give thank offerings to you.'),
('PSA', 56, 13, 'PSA.56.13', 'For you have delivered my soul from death, and prevented my feet from falling, that I may walk before God in the light of the living.'),
('PSA', 57, 1, 'PSA.57.1', 'Be merciful to me, God, be merciful to me, for my soul takes refuge in you. Yes, in the shadow of your wings, I will take refuge, until disaster has passed.'),
('PSA', 57, 2, 'PSA.57.2', 'I cry out to God Most High, to God who accomplishes my requests for me.'),
('PSA', 57, 3, 'PSA.57.3', 'He will send from heaven, and save me, he rebukes the one who is pursuing me. Selah. God will send out his loving kindness and his truth.'),
('PSA', 57, 4, 'PSA.57.4', 'My soul is among lions. I lie among those who are set on fire, even the sons of men, whose teeth are spears and arrows, and their tongue a sharp sword.'),
('PSA', 57, 5, 'PSA.57.5', 'Be exalted, God, above the heavens! Let your glory be above all the earth!'),
('PSA', 57, 6, 'PSA.57.6', 'They have prepared a net for my steps. My soul is bowed down. They dig a pit before me. They fall into the middle of it themselves. Selah.'),
('PSA', 57, 7, 'PSA.57.7', 'My heart is steadfast, God. My heart is steadfast. I will sing, yes, I will sing praises.'),
('PSA', 57, 8, 'PSA.57.8', 'Wake up, my glory! Wake up, lute and harp! I will wake up the dawn.'),
('PSA', 57, 9, 'PSA.57.9', 'I will give thanks to you, Lord, among the peoples. I will sing praises to you among the nations.'),
('PSA', 57, 10, 'PSA.57.10', 'For your great loving kindness reaches to the heavens, and your truth to the skies.'),
('PSA', 57, 11, 'PSA.57.11', 'Be exalted, God, above the heavens. Let your glory be over all the earth.'),
('PSA', 58, 1, 'PSA.58.1', 'Do you indeed speak righteousness, silent ones? Do you judge blamelessly, you sons of men?'),
('PSA', 58, 2, 'PSA.58.2', 'No, in your heart you plot injustice. You measure out the violence of your hands on the earth.'),
('PSA', 58, 3, 'PSA.58.3', 'The wicked go astray from the womb. They are wayward as soon as they are born, speaking lies.'),
('PSA', 58, 4, 'PSA.58.4', 'Their poison is like the poison of a snake, like a deaf cobra that stops its ear,'),
('PSA', 58, 5, 'PSA.58.5', 'which doesn’t listen to the voice of charmers, no matter how skillful the charmer may be.'),
('PSA', 58, 6, 'PSA.58.6', 'Break their teeth, God, in their mouth. Break out the great teeth of the young lions, LORD.'),
('PSA', 58, 7, 'PSA.58.7', 'Let them vanish like water that flows away. When they draw the bow, let their arrows be made blunt.'),
('PSA', 58, 8, 'PSA.58.8', 'Let them be like a snail which melts and passes away, like the stillborn child, who has not seen the sun.'),
('PSA', 58, 9, 'PSA.58.9', 'Before your pots can feel the heat of the thorns, he will sweep away the green and the burning alike.'),
('PSA', 58, 10, 'PSA.58.10', 'The righteous shall rejoice when he sees the vengeance. He shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked,'),
('PSA', 58, 11, 'PSA.58.11', 'so that men shall say, “Most certainly there is a reward for the righteous. Most certainly there is a God who judges the earth.”'),
('PSA', 59, 1, 'PSA.59.1', 'Deliver me from my enemies, my God. Set me on high from those who rise up against me.'),
('PSA', 59, 2, 'PSA.59.2', 'Deliver me from the workers of iniquity. Save me from the bloodthirsty men.'),
('PSA', 59, 3, 'PSA.59.3', 'For, behold, they lie in wait for my soul. The mighty gather themselves together against me, not for my disobedience, nor for my sin, LORD.'),
('PSA', 59, 4, 'PSA.59.4', 'I have done no wrong, yet they are ready to attack me. Rise up, behold, and help me!'),
('PSA', 59, 5, 'PSA.59.5', 'You, LORD God of Armies, the God of Israel, rouse yourself to punish the nations. Show no mercy to the wicked traitors. Selah.'),
('PSA', 59, 6, 'PSA.59.6', 'They return at evening, howling like dogs, and prowl around the city.'),
('PSA', 59, 7, 'PSA.59.7', 'Behold, they spew with their mouth. Swords are in their lips, “For”, they say, “who hears us?”'),
('PSA', 59, 8, 'PSA.59.8', 'But you, LORD, laugh at them. You scoff at all the nations.'),
('PSA', 59, 9, 'PSA.59.9', 'Oh, my Strength, I watch for you, for God is my high tower.'),
('PSA', 59, 10, 'PSA.59.10', 'My God will go before me with his loving kindness. God will let me look at my enemies in triumph.'),
('PSA', 59, 11, 'PSA.59.11', 'Don’t kill them, or my people may forget. Scatter them by your power, and bring them down, Lord our shield.'),
('PSA', 59, 12, 'PSA.59.12', 'For the sin of their mouth, and the words of their lips, let them be caught in their pride, for the curses and lies which they utter.'),
('PSA', 59, 13, 'PSA.59.13', 'Consume them in wrath. Consume them, and they will be no more. Let them know that God rules in Jacob, to the ends of the earth. Selah.'),
('PSA', 59, 14, 'PSA.59.14', 'At evening let them return. Let them howl like a dog, and go around the city.'),
('PSA', 59, 15, 'PSA.59.15', 'They shall wander up and down for food, and wait all night if they aren’t satisfied.'),
('PSA', 59, 16, 'PSA.59.16', 'But I will sing of your strength. Yes, I will sing aloud of your loving kindness in the morning. For you have been my high tower, a refuge in the day of my distress.'),
('PSA', 59, 17, 'PSA.59.17', 'To you, my strength, I will sing praises. For God is my high tower, the God of my mercy.'),
('PSA', 60, 1, 'PSA.60.1', 'God, you have rejected us. You have broken us down. You have been angry. Restore us, again.'),
('PSA', 60, 2, 'PSA.60.2', 'You have made the land tremble. You have torn it. Mend its fractures, for it quakes.'),
('PSA', 60, 3, 'PSA.60.3', 'You have shown your people hard things. You have made us drink the wine that makes us stagger.'),
('PSA', 60, 4, 'PSA.60.4', 'You have given a banner to those who fear you, that it may be displayed because of the truth. Selah.'),
('PSA', 60, 5, 'PSA.60.5', 'So that your beloved may be delivered, save with your right hand, and answer us.'),
('PSA', 60, 6, 'PSA.60.6', 'God has spoken from his sanctuary: “I will triumph. I will divide Shechem, and measure out the valley of Succoth.'),
('PSA', 60, 7, 'PSA.60.7', 'Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine. Ephraim also is the defense of my head. Judah is my scepter.'),
('PSA', 60, 8, 'PSA.60.8', 'Moab is my wash basin. I will throw my sandal on Edom. I shout in triumph over Philistia.”'),
('PSA', 60, 9, 'PSA.60.9', 'Who will bring me into the strong city? Who has led me to Edom?'),
('PSA', 60, 10, 'PSA.60.10', 'Haven’t you, God, rejected us? You don’t go out with our armies, God.'),
('PSA', 60, 11, 'PSA.60.11', 'Give us help against the adversary, for the help of man is vain.'),
('PSA', 60, 12, 'PSA.60.12', 'Through God we will do valiantly, for it is he who will tread down our adversaries.'),
('PSA', 61, 1, 'PSA.61.1', 'Hear my cry, God. Listen to my prayer.'),
('PSA', 61, 2, 'PSA.61.2', 'From the end of the earth, I will call to you when my heart is overwhelmed. Lead me to the rock that is higher than I.'),
('PSA', 61, 3, 'PSA.61.3', 'For you have been a refuge for me, a strong tower from the enemy.'),
('PSA', 61, 4, 'PSA.61.4', 'I will dwell in your tent forever. I will take refuge in the shelter of your wings. Selah.'),
('PSA', 61, 5, 'PSA.61.5', 'For you, God, have heard my vows. You have given me the heritage of those who fear your name.'),
('PSA', 61, 6, 'PSA.61.6', 'You will prolong the king’s life. His years will be for generations.'),
('PSA', 61, 7, 'PSA.61.7', 'He shall be enthroned in God’s presence forever. Appoint your loving kindness and truth, that they may preserve him.'),
('PSA', 61, 8, 'PSA.61.8', 'So I will sing praise to your name forever, that I may fulfill my vows daily.'),
('PSA', 62, 1, 'PSA.62.1', 'My soul rests in God alone. My salvation is from him.'),
('PSA', 62, 2, 'PSA.62.2', 'He alone is my rock, my salvation, and my fortress. I will never be greatly shaken.'),
('PSA', 62, 3, 'PSA.62.3', 'How long will you assault a man? Would all of you throw him down, like a leaning wall, like a tottering fence?'),
('PSA', 62, 4, 'PSA.62.4', 'They fully intend to throw him down from his lofty place. They delight in lies. They bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. Selah.'),
('PSA', 62, 5, 'PSA.62.5', 'My soul, wait in silence for God alone, for my expectation is from him.'),
('PSA', 62, 6, 'PSA.62.6', 'He alone is my rock and my salvation, my fortress. I will not be shaken.'),
('PSA', 62, 7, 'PSA.62.7', 'My salvation and my honor is with God. The rock of my strength, and my refuge, is in God.'),
('PSA', 62, 8, 'PSA.62.8', 'Trust in him at all times, you people. Pour out your heart before him. God is a refuge for us. Selah.'),
('PSA', 62, 9, 'PSA.62.9', 'Surely men of low degree are just a breath, and men of high degree are a lie. In the balances they will go up. They are together lighter than a breath.'),
('PSA', 62, 10, 'PSA.62.10', 'Don’t trust in oppression. Don’t become vain in robbery. If riches increase, don’t set your heart on them.'),
('PSA', 62, 11, 'PSA.62.11', 'God has spoken once; twice I have heard this, that power belongs to God.'),
('PSA', 62, 12, 'PSA.62.12', 'Also to you, Lord, belongs loving kindness, for you reward every man according to his work.'),
('PSA', 63, 1, 'PSA.63.1', 'God, you are my God. I will earnestly seek you. My soul thirsts for you. My flesh longs for you, in a dry and weary land, where there is no water.'),
('PSA', 63, 2, 'PSA.63.2', 'So I have seen you in the sanctuary, watching your power and your glory.'),
('PSA', 63, 3, 'PSA.63.3', 'Because your loving kindness is better than life, my lips shall praise you.'),
('PSA', 63, 4, 'PSA.63.4', 'So I will bless you while I live. I will lift up my hands in your name.'),
('PSA', 63, 5, 'PSA.63.5', 'My soul shall be satisfied as with the richest food. My mouth shall praise you with joyful lips,'),
('PSA', 63, 6, 'PSA.63.6', 'when I remember you on my bed, and think about you in the night watches.'),
('PSA', 63, 7, 'PSA.63.7', 'For you have been my help. I will rejoice in the shadow of your wings.'),
('PSA', 63, 8, 'PSA.63.8', 'My soul stays close to you. Your right hand holds me up.'),
('PSA', 63, 9, 'PSA.63.9', 'But those who seek my soul to destroy it shall go into the lower parts of the earth.'),
('PSA', 63, 10, 'PSA.63.10', 'They shall be given over to the power of the sword. They shall be jackal food.'),
('PSA', 63, 11, 'PSA.63.11', 'But the king shall rejoice in God. Everyone who swears by him will praise him, for the mouth of those who speak lies shall be silenced.'),
('PSA', 64, 1, 'PSA.64.1', 'Hear my voice, God, in my complaint. Preserve my life from fear of the enemy.'),
('PSA', 64, 2, 'PSA.64.2', 'Hide me from the conspiracy of the wicked, from the noisy crowd of the ones doing evil;'),
('PSA', 64, 3, 'PSA.64.3', 'who sharpen their tongue like a sword, and aim their arrows, deadly words,'),
('PSA', 64, 4, 'PSA.64.4', 'to shoot innocent men from ambushes. They shoot at him suddenly and fearlessly.'),
('PSA', 64, 5, 'PSA.64.5', 'They encourage themselves in evil plans. They talk about laying snares secretly. They say, “Who will see them?”'),
('PSA', 64, 6, 'PSA.64.6', 'They plot injustice, saying, “We have made a perfect plan!” Surely man’s mind and heart are cunning.'),
('PSA', 64, 7, 'PSA.64.7', 'But God will shoot at them. They will be suddenly struck down with an arrow.'),
('PSA', 64, 8, 'PSA.64.8', 'Their own tongues shall ruin them. All who see them will shake their heads.'),
('PSA', 64, 9, 'PSA.64.9', 'All mankind shall be afraid. They shall declare the work of God, and shall wisely ponder what he has done.'),
('PSA', 64, 10, 'PSA.64.10', 'The righteous shall be glad in the LORD, and shall take refuge in him. All the upright in heart shall praise him!'),
('PSA', 65, 1, 'PSA.65.1', 'Praise waits for you, God, in Zion. Vows shall be performed to you.'),
('PSA', 65, 2, 'PSA.65.2', 'You who hear prayer, all men will come to you.'),
('PSA', 65, 3, 'PSA.65.3', 'Sins overwhelmed me, but you atoned for our transgressions.'),
('PSA', 65, 4, 'PSA.65.4', 'Blessed is the one whom you choose and cause to come near, that he may live in your courts. We will be filled with the goodness of your house, your holy temple.'),
('PSA', 65, 5, 'PSA.65.5', 'By awesome deeds of righteousness, you answer us, God of our salvation. You who are the hope of all the ends of the earth, of those who are far away on the sea.'),
('PSA', 65, 6, 'PSA.65.6', 'By your power, you form the mountains, having armed yourself with strength.'),
('PSA', 65, 7, 'PSA.65.7', 'You still the roaring of the seas, the roaring of their waves, and the turmoil of the nations.'),
('PSA', 65, 8, 'PSA.65.8', 'They also who dwell in faraway places are afraid at your wonders. You call the morning’s dawn and the evening with songs of joy.'),
('PSA', 65, 9, 'PSA.65.9', 'You visit the earth, and water it. You greatly enrich it. The river of God is full of water. You provide them grain, for so you have ordained it.'),
('PSA', 65, 10, 'PSA.65.10', 'You drench its furrows. You level its ridges. You soften it with showers. You bless it with a crop.'),
('PSA', 65, 11, 'PSA.65.11', 'You crown the year with your bounty. Your carts overflow with abundance.'),
('PSA', 65, 12, 'PSA.65.12', 'The wilderness grasslands overflow. The hills are clothed with gladness.'),
('PSA', 65, 13, 'PSA.65.13', 'The pastures are covered with flocks. The valleys also are clothed with grain. They shout for joy! They also sing.'),
('PSA', 66, 1, 'PSA.66.1', 'Make a joyful shout to God, all the earth!'),
('PSA', 66, 2, 'PSA.66.2', 'Sing to the glory of his name! Offer glory and praise!'),
('PSA', 66, 3, 'PSA.66.3', 'Tell God, “How awesome are your deeds! Through the greatness of your power, your enemies submit themselves to you.'),
('PSA', 66, 4, 'PSA.66.4', 'All the earth will worship you, and will sing to you; they will sing to your name.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 66, 5, 'PSA.66.5', 'Come, and see God’s deeds— awesome work on behalf of the children of men.'),
('PSA', 66, 6, 'PSA.66.6', 'He turned the sea into dry land. They went through the river on foot. There, we rejoiced in him.'),
('PSA', 66, 7, 'PSA.66.7', 'He rules by his might forever. His eyes watch the nations. Don’t let the rebellious rise up against him. Selah.'),
('PSA', 66, 8, 'PSA.66.8', 'Praise our God, you peoples! Make the sound of his praise heard,'),
('PSA', 66, 9, 'PSA.66.9', 'who preserves our life among the living, and doesn’t allow our feet to be moved.'),
('PSA', 66, 10, 'PSA.66.10', 'For you, God, have tested us. You have refined us, as silver is refined.'),
('PSA', 66, 11, 'PSA.66.11', 'You brought us into prison. You laid a burden on our backs.'),
('PSA', 66, 12, 'PSA.66.12', 'You allowed men to ride over our heads. We went through fire and through water, but you brought us to the place of abundance.'),
('PSA', 66, 13, 'PSA.66.13', 'I will come into your temple with burnt offerings. I will pay my vows to you,'),
('PSA', 66, 14, 'PSA.66.14', 'which my lips promised, and my mouth spoke, when I was in distress.'),
('PSA', 66, 15, 'PSA.66.15', 'I will offer to you burnt offerings of fat animals, with the offering of rams, I will offer bulls with goats. Selah.'),
('PSA', 66, 16, 'PSA.66.16', 'Come and hear, all you who fear God. I will declare what he has done for my soul.'),
('PSA', 66, 17, 'PSA.66.17', 'I cried to him with my mouth. He was extolled with my tongue.'),
('PSA', 66, 18, 'PSA.66.18', 'If I cherished sin in my heart, the Lord wouldn’t have listened.'),
('PSA', 66, 19, 'PSA.66.19', 'But most certainly, God has listened. He has heard the voice of my prayer.'),
('PSA', 66, 20, 'PSA.66.20', 'Blessed be God, who has not turned away my prayer, nor his loving kindness from me.'),
('PSA', 67, 1, 'PSA.67.1', 'May God be merciful to us, bless us, and cause his face to shine on us. Selah.'),
('PSA', 67, 2, 'PSA.67.2', 'That your way may be known on earth, and your salvation among all nations,'),
('PSA', 67, 3, 'PSA.67.3', 'let the peoples praise you, God. Let all the peoples praise you.'),
('PSA', 67, 4, 'PSA.67.4', 'Oh let the nations be glad and sing for joy, for you will judge the peoples with equity, and govern the nations on earth. Selah.'),
('PSA', 67, 5, 'PSA.67.5', 'Let the peoples praise you, God. Let all the peoples praise you.'),
('PSA', 67, 6, 'PSA.67.6', 'The earth has yielded its increase. God, even our own God, will bless us.'),
('PSA', 67, 7, 'PSA.67.7', 'God will bless us. All the ends of the earth shall fear him.'),
('PSA', 68, 1, 'PSA.68.1', 'Let God arise! Let his enemies be scattered! Let them who hate him also flee before him.'),
('PSA', 68, 2, 'PSA.68.2', 'As smoke is driven away, so drive them away. As wax melts before the fire, so let the wicked perish at the presence of God.'),
('PSA', 68, 3, 'PSA.68.3', 'But let the righteous be glad. Let them rejoice before God. Yes, let them rejoice with gladness.'),
('PSA', 68, 4, 'PSA.68.4', 'Sing to God! Sing praises to his name! Extol him who rides on the clouds: to the LORD, his name! Rejoice before him!'),
('PSA', 68, 5, 'PSA.68.5', 'A father of the fatherless, and a defender of the widows, is God in his holy habitation.'),
('PSA', 68, 6, 'PSA.68.6', 'God sets the lonely in families. He brings out the prisoners with singing, but the rebellious dwell in a sun-scorched land.'),
('PSA', 68, 7, 'PSA.68.7', 'God, when you went out before your people, when you marched through the wilderness... Selah.'),
('PSA', 68, 8, 'PSA.68.8', 'The earth trembled. The sky also poured down rain at the presence of the God of Sinai— at the presence of God, the God of Israel.'),
('PSA', 68, 9, 'PSA.68.9', 'You, God, sent a plentiful rain. You confirmed your inheritance when it was weary.'),
('PSA', 68, 10, 'PSA.68.10', 'Your congregation lived therein. You, God, prepared your goodness for the poor.'),
('PSA', 68, 11, 'PSA.68.11', 'The Lord announced the word. The ones who proclaim it are a great company.'),
('PSA', 68, 12, 'PSA.68.12', '“Kings of armies flee! They flee!” She who waits at home divides the plunder,'),
('PSA', 68, 13, 'PSA.68.13', 'while you sleep among the camp fires, the wings of a dove sheathed with silver, her feathers with shining gold.'),
('PSA', 68, 14, 'PSA.68.14', 'When the Almighty scattered kings in her, it snowed on Zalmon.'),
('PSA', 68, 15, 'PSA.68.15', 'The mountains of Bashan are majestic mountains. The mountains of Bashan are rugged.'),
('PSA', 68, 16, 'PSA.68.16', 'Why do you look in envy, you rugged mountains, at the mountain where God chooses to reign? Yes, the LORD will dwell there forever.'),
('PSA', 68, 17, 'PSA.68.17', 'The chariots of God are tens of thousands and thousands of thousands. The Lord is among them, from Sinai, into the sanctuary.'),
('PSA', 68, 18, 'PSA.68.18', 'You have ascended on high. You have led away captives. You have received gifts among people, yes, among the rebellious also, that the LORD God might dwell there.'),
('PSA', 68, 19, 'PSA.68.19', 'Blessed be the Lord, who daily bears our burdens, even the God who is our salvation. Selah.'),
('PSA', 68, 20, 'PSA.68.20', 'God is to us a God of deliverance. To GOD, the Lord, belongs escape from death.'),
('PSA', 68, 21, 'PSA.68.21', 'But God will strike through the head of his enemies, the hairy scalp of such a one as still continues in his guiltiness.'),
('PSA', 68, 22, 'PSA.68.22', 'The Lord said, “I will bring you again from Bashan, I will bring you again from the depths of the sea,'),
('PSA', 68, 23, 'PSA.68.23', 'that you may crush them, dipping your foot in blood, that the tongues of your dogs may have their portion from your enemies.”'),
('PSA', 68, 24, 'PSA.68.24', 'They have seen your processions, God, even the processions of my God, my King, into the sanctuary.'),
('PSA', 68, 25, 'PSA.68.25', 'The singers went before, the minstrels followed after, among the ladies playing with tambourines,'),
('PSA', 68, 26, 'PSA.68.26', '“Bless God in the congregations, even the Lord in the assembly of Israel!”'),
('PSA', 68, 27, 'PSA.68.27', 'There is little Benjamin, their ruler, the princes of Judah, their council, the princes of Zebulun, and the princes of Naphtali.'),
('PSA', 68, 28, 'PSA.68.28', 'Your God has commanded your strength. Strengthen, God, that which you have done for us.'),
('PSA', 68, 29, 'PSA.68.29', 'Because of your temple at Jerusalem, kings will bring presents to you.'),
('PSA', 68, 30, 'PSA.68.30', 'Rebuke the wild animal of the reeds, the multitude of the bulls with the calves of the peoples. Trample under foot the bars of silver. Scatter the nations who delight in war.'),
('PSA', 68, 31, 'PSA.68.31', 'Princes shall come out of Egypt. Ethiopia shall hurry to stretch out her hands to God.'),
('PSA', 68, 32, 'PSA.68.32', 'Sing to God, you kingdoms of the earth! Sing praises to the Lord—Selah—'),
('PSA', 68, 33, 'PSA.68.33', 'to him who rides on the heaven of heavens, which are of old; behold, he utters his voice, a mighty voice.'),
('PSA', 68, 34, 'PSA.68.34', 'Ascribe strength to God! His excellency is over Israel, his strength is in the skies.'),
('PSA', 68, 35, 'PSA.68.35', 'You are awesome, God, in your sanctuaries. The God of Israel gives strength and power to his people. Praise be to God!'),
('PSA', 69, 1, 'PSA.69.1', 'Save me, God, for the waters have come up to my neck!'),
('PSA', 69, 2, 'PSA.69.2', 'I sink in deep mire, where there is no foothold. I have come into deep waters, where the floods overflow me.'),
('PSA', 69, 3, 'PSA.69.3', 'I am weary with my crying. My throat is dry. My eyes fail looking for my God.'),
('PSA', 69, 4, 'PSA.69.4', 'Those who hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of my head. Those who want to cut me off, being my enemies wrongfully, are mighty. I have to restore what I didn’t take away.'),
('PSA', 69, 5, 'PSA.69.5', 'God, you know my foolishness. My sins aren’t hidden from you.'),
('PSA', 69, 6, 'PSA.69.6', 'Don’t let those who wait for you be shamed through me, Lord GOD of Armies. Don’t let those who seek you be brought to dishonor through me, God of Israel.'),
('PSA', 69, 7, 'PSA.69.7', 'Because for your sake, I have borne reproach. Shame has covered my face.'),
('PSA', 69, 8, 'PSA.69.8', 'I have become a stranger to my brothers, an alien to my mother’s children.'),
('PSA', 69, 9, 'PSA.69.9', 'For the zeal of your house consumes me. The reproaches of those who reproach you have fallen on me.'),
('PSA', 69, 10, 'PSA.69.10', 'When I wept and I fasted, that was to my reproach.'),
('PSA', 69, 11, 'PSA.69.11', 'When I made sackcloth my clothing, I became a byword to them.'),
('PSA', 69, 12, 'PSA.69.12', 'Those who sit in the gate talk about me. I am the song of the drunkards.'),
('PSA', 69, 13, 'PSA.69.13', 'But as for me, my prayer is to you, LORD, in an acceptable time. God, in the abundance of your loving kindness, answer me in the truth of your salvation.'),
('PSA', 69, 14, 'PSA.69.14', 'Deliver me out of the mire, and don’t let me sink. Let me be delivered from those who hate me, and out of the deep waters.'),
('PSA', 69, 15, 'PSA.69.15', 'Don’t let the flood waters overwhelm me, neither let the deep swallow me up. Don’t let the pit shut its mouth on me.'),
('PSA', 69, 16, 'PSA.69.16', 'Answer me, LORD, for your loving kindness is good. According to the multitude of your tender mercies, turn to me.'),
('PSA', 69, 17, 'PSA.69.17', 'Don’t hide your face from your servant, for I am in distress. Answer me speedily!'),
('PSA', 69, 18, 'PSA.69.18', 'Draw near to my soul and redeem it. Ransom me because of my enemies.'),
('PSA', 69, 19, 'PSA.69.19', 'You know my reproach, my shame, and my dishonor. My adversaries are all before you.'),
('PSA', 69, 20, 'PSA.69.20', 'Reproach has broken my heart, and I am full of heaviness. I looked for some to take pity, but there was none; for comforters, but I found none.'),
('PSA', 69, 21, 'PSA.69.21', 'They also gave me poison for my food. In my thirst, they gave me vinegar to drink.'),
('PSA', 69, 22, 'PSA.69.22', 'Let their table before them become a snare. May it become a retribution and a trap.'),
('PSA', 69, 23, 'PSA.69.23', 'Let their eyes be darkened, so that they can’t see. Let their backs be continually bent.'),
('PSA', 69, 24, 'PSA.69.24', 'Pour out your indignation on them. Let the fierceness of your anger overtake them.'),
('PSA', 69, 25, 'PSA.69.25', 'Let their habitation be desolate. Let no one dwell in their tents.'),
('PSA', 69, 26, 'PSA.69.26', 'For they persecute him whom you have wounded. They tell of the sorrow of those whom you have hurt.'),
('PSA', 69, 27, 'PSA.69.27', 'Charge them with crime upon crime. Don’t let them come into your righteousness.'),
('PSA', 69, 28, 'PSA.69.28', 'Let them be blotted out of the book of life, and not be written with the righteous.'),
('PSA', 69, 29, 'PSA.69.29', 'But I am in pain and distress. Let your salvation, God, protect me.'),
('PSA', 69, 30, 'PSA.69.30', 'I will praise the name of God with a song, and will magnify him with thanksgiving.'),
('PSA', 69, 31, 'PSA.69.31', 'It will please the LORD better than an ox, or a bull that has horns and hoofs.'),
('PSA', 69, 32, 'PSA.69.32', 'The humble have seen it, and are glad. You who seek after God, let your heart live.'),
('PSA', 69, 33, 'PSA.69.33', 'For the LORD hears the needy, and doesn’t despise his captive people.'),
('PSA', 69, 34, 'PSA.69.34', 'Let heaven and earth praise him; the seas, and everything that moves therein!'),
('PSA', 69, 35, 'PSA.69.35', 'For God will save Zion, and build the cities of Judah. They shall settle there, and own it.'),
('PSA', 69, 36, 'PSA.69.36', 'The children also of his servants shall inherit it. Those who love his name shall dwell therein.'),
('PSA', 70, 1, 'PSA.70.1', 'Hurry, God, to deliver me. Come quickly to help me, LORD.'),
('PSA', 70, 2, 'PSA.70.2', 'Let them be disappointed and confounded who seek my soul. Let those who desire my ruin be turned back in disgrace.'),
('PSA', 70, 3, 'PSA.70.3', 'Let them be turned because of their shame who say, “Aha! Aha!”'),
('PSA', 70, 4, 'PSA.70.4', 'Let all those who seek you rejoice and be glad in you. Let those who love your salvation continually say, “Let God be exalted!”'),
('PSA', 70, 5, 'PSA.70.5', 'But I am poor and needy. Come to me quickly, God. You are my help and my deliverer. LORD, don’t delay.'),
('PSA', 71, 1, 'PSA.71.1', 'In you, LORD, I take refuge. Never let me be disappointed.'),
('PSA', 71, 2, 'PSA.71.2', 'Deliver me in your righteousness, and rescue me. Turn your ear to me, and save me.'),
('PSA', 71, 3, 'PSA.71.3', 'Be to me a rock of refuge to which I may always go. Give the command to save me, for you are my rock and my fortress.'),
('PSA', 71, 4, 'PSA.71.4', 'Rescue me, my God, from the hand of the wicked, from the hand of the unrighteous and cruel man.'),
('PSA', 71, 5, 'PSA.71.5', 'For you are my hope, Lord GOD, my confidence from my youth.'),
('PSA', 71, 6, 'PSA.71.6', 'I have relied on you from the womb. You are he who took me out of my mother’s womb. I will always praise you.'),
('PSA', 71, 7, 'PSA.71.7', 'I am a marvel to many, but you are my strong refuge.'),
('PSA', 71, 8, 'PSA.71.8', 'My mouth shall be filled with your praise, with your honor all day long.'),
('PSA', 71, 9, 'PSA.71.9', 'Don’t reject me in my old age. Don’t forsake me when my strength fails.'),
('PSA', 71, 10, 'PSA.71.10', 'For my enemies talk about me. Those who watch for my soul conspire together,'),
('PSA', 71, 11, 'PSA.71.11', 'saying, “God has forsaken him. Pursue and take him, for no one will rescue him.”'),
('PSA', 71, 12, 'PSA.71.12', 'God, don’t be far from me. My God, hurry to help me.'),
('PSA', 71, 13, 'PSA.71.13', 'Let my accusers be disappointed and consumed. Let them be covered with disgrace and scorn who want to harm me.'),
('PSA', 71, 14, 'PSA.71.14', 'But I will always hope, and will add to all of your praise.'),
('PSA', 71, 15, 'PSA.71.15', 'My mouth will tell about your righteousness, and of your salvation all day, though I don’t know its full measure.'),
('PSA', 71, 16, 'PSA.71.16', 'I will come with the mighty acts of the Lord GOD. I will make mention of your righteousness, even of yours alone.'),
('PSA', 71, 17, 'PSA.71.17', 'God, you have taught me from my youth. Until now, I have declared your wondrous works.'),
('PSA', 71, 18, 'PSA.71.18', 'Yes, even when I am old and gray-haired, God, don’t forsake me, until I have declared your strength to the next generation, your might to everyone who is to come.'),
('PSA', 71, 19, 'PSA.71.19', 'God, your righteousness also reaches to the heavens. You have done great things. God, who is like you?'),
('PSA', 71, 20, 'PSA.71.20', 'You, who have shown us many and bitter troubles, you will let me live. You will bring us up again from the depths of the earth.'),
('PSA', 71, 21, 'PSA.71.21', 'Increase my honor and comfort me again.'),
('PSA', 71, 22, 'PSA.71.22', 'I will also praise you with the harp for your faithfulness, my God. I sing praises to you with the lyre, Holy One of Israel.'),
('PSA', 71, 23, 'PSA.71.23', 'My lips shall shout for joy! My soul, which you have redeemed, sings praises to you!'),
('PSA', 71, 24, 'PSA.71.24', 'My tongue will also talk about your righteousness all day long, for they are disappointed, and they are confounded, who want to harm me.'),
('PSA', 72, 1, 'PSA.72.1', 'God, give the king your justice; your righteousness to the royal son.'),
('PSA', 72, 2, 'PSA.72.2', 'He will judge your people with righteousness, and your poor with justice.'),
('PSA', 72, 3, 'PSA.72.3', 'The mountains shall bring prosperity to the people. The hills bring the fruit of righteousness.'),
('PSA', 72, 4, 'PSA.72.4', 'He will judge the poor of the people. He will save the children of the needy, and will break the oppressor in pieces.'),
('PSA', 72, 5, 'PSA.72.5', 'They shall fear you while the sun endures; and as long as the moon, throughout all generations.'),
('PSA', 72, 6, 'PSA.72.6', 'He will come down like rain on the mown grass, as showers that water the earth.'),
('PSA', 72, 7, 'PSA.72.7', 'In his days, the righteous shall flourish, and abundance of peace, until the moon is no more.'),
('PSA', 72, 8, 'PSA.72.8', 'He shall have dominion also from sea to sea, from the River to the ends of the earth.'),
('PSA', 72, 9, 'PSA.72.9', 'Those who dwell in the wilderness shall bow before him. His enemies shall lick the dust.'),
('PSA', 72, 10, 'PSA.72.10', 'The kings of Tarshish and of the islands will bring tribute. The kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer gifts.'),
('PSA', 72, 11, 'PSA.72.11', 'Yes, all kings shall fall down before him. All nations shall serve him.'),
('PSA', 72, 12, 'PSA.72.12', 'For he will deliver the needy when he cries; the poor, who has no helper.'),
('PSA', 72, 13, 'PSA.72.13', 'He will have pity on the poor and needy. He will save the souls of the needy.'),
('PSA', 72, 14, 'PSA.72.14', 'He will redeem their soul from oppression and violence. Their blood will be precious in his sight.'),
('PSA', 72, 15, 'PSA.72.15', 'He will live; and Sheba’s gold will be given to him. Men will pray for him continually. They will bless him all day long.'),
('PSA', 72, 16, 'PSA.72.16', 'Abundance of grain shall be throughout the land. Its fruit sways like Lebanon. Let it flourish, thriving like the grass of the field.'),
('PSA', 72, 17, 'PSA.72.17', 'His name endures forever. His name continues as long as the sun. Men shall be blessed by him. All nations will call him blessed.'),
('PSA', 72, 18, 'PSA.72.18', 'Praise be to the LORD God, the God of Israel, who alone does marvelous deeds.'),
('PSA', 72, 19, 'PSA.72.19', 'Blessed be his glorious name forever! Let the whole earth be filled with his glory! Amen and amen.'),
('PSA', 72, 20, 'PSA.72.20', 'This ends the prayers by David, the son of Jesse.'),
('PSA', 73, 1, 'PSA.73.1', 'Surely God is good to Israel, to those who are pure in heart.'),
('PSA', 73, 2, 'PSA.73.2', 'But as for me, my feet were almost gone. My steps had nearly slipped.'),
('PSA', 73, 3, 'PSA.73.3', 'For I was envious of the arrogant, when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.'),
('PSA', 73, 4, 'PSA.73.4', 'For there are no struggles in their death, but their strength is firm.'),
('PSA', 73, 5, 'PSA.73.5', 'They are free from burdens of men, neither are they plagued like other men.'),
('PSA', 73, 6, 'PSA.73.6', 'Therefore pride is like a chain around their neck. Violence covers them like a garment.'),
('PSA', 73, 7, 'PSA.73.7', 'Their eyes bulge with fat. Their minds pass the limits of conceit.'),
('PSA', 73, 8, 'PSA.73.8', 'They scoff and speak with malice. In arrogance, they threaten oppression.'),
('PSA', 73, 9, 'PSA.73.9', 'They have set their mouth in the heavens. Their tongue walks through the earth.'),
('PSA', 73, 10, 'PSA.73.10', 'Therefore their people return to them, and they drink up waters of abundance.'),
('PSA', 73, 11, 'PSA.73.11', 'They say, “How does God know? Is there knowledge in the Most High?”'),
('PSA', 73, 12, 'PSA.73.12', 'Behold, these are the wicked. Being always at ease, they increase in riches.'),
('PSA', 73, 13, 'PSA.73.13', 'Surely I have cleansed my heart in vain, and washed my hands in innocence,'),
('PSA', 73, 14, 'PSA.73.14', 'For all day long I have been plagued, and punished every morning.'),
('PSA', 73, 15, 'PSA.73.15', 'If I had said, “I will speak thus”, behold, I would have betrayed the generation of your children.'),
('PSA', 73, 16, 'PSA.73.16', 'When I tried to understand this, it was too painful for me—'),
('PSA', 73, 17, 'PSA.73.17', 'until I entered God’s sanctuary, and considered their latter end.'),
('PSA', 73, 18, 'PSA.73.18', 'Surely you set them in slippery places. You throw them down to destruction.'),
('PSA', 73, 19, 'PSA.73.19', 'How they are suddenly destroyed! They are completely swept away with terrors.'),
('PSA', 73, 20, 'PSA.73.20', 'As a dream when one wakes up, so, Lord, when you awake, you will despise their fantasies.'),
('PSA', 73, 21, 'PSA.73.21', 'For my soul was grieved. I was embittered in my heart.'),
('PSA', 73, 22, 'PSA.73.22', 'I was so senseless and ignorant. I was a brute beast before you.'),
('PSA', 73, 23, 'PSA.73.23', 'Nevertheless, I am continually with you. You have held my right hand.'),
('PSA', 73, 24, 'PSA.73.24', 'You will guide me with your counsel, and afterward receive me to glory.'),
('PSA', 73, 25, 'PSA.73.25', 'Whom do I have in heaven? There is no one on earth whom I desire besides you.'),
('PSA', 73, 26, 'PSA.73.26', 'My flesh and my heart fails, but God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever.'),
('PSA', 73, 27, 'PSA.73.27', 'For, behold, those who are far from you shall perish. You have destroyed all those who are unfaithful to you.'),
('PSA', 73, 28, 'PSA.73.28', 'But it is good for me to come close to God. I have made the Lord GOD my refuge, that I may tell of all your works.'),
('PSA', 74, 1, 'PSA.74.1', 'God, why have you rejected us forever? Why does your anger smolder against the sheep of your pasture?'),
('PSA', 74, 2, 'PSA.74.2', 'Remember your congregation, which you purchased of old, which you have redeemed to be the tribe of your inheritance: Mount Zion, in which you have lived.'),
('PSA', 74, 3, 'PSA.74.3', 'Lift up your feet to the perpetual ruins, all the evil that the enemy has done in the sanctuary.'),
('PSA', 74, 4, 'PSA.74.4', 'Your adversaries have roared in the middle of your assembly. They have set up their standards as signs.'),
('PSA', 74, 5, 'PSA.74.5', 'They behaved like men wielding axes, cutting through a thicket of trees.'),
('PSA', 74, 6, 'PSA.74.6', 'Now they break all its carved work down with hatchet and hammers.'),
('PSA', 74, 7, 'PSA.74.7', 'They have burned your sanctuary to the ground. They have profaned the dwelling place of your Name.'),
('PSA', 74, 8, 'PSA.74.8', 'They said in their heart, “We will crush them completely.” They have burned up all the places in the land where God was worshiped.'),
('PSA', 74, 9, 'PSA.74.9', 'We see no miraculous signs. There is no longer any prophet, neither is there among us anyone who knows how long.'),
('PSA', 74, 10, 'PSA.74.10', 'How long, God, shall the adversary reproach? Shall the enemy blaspheme your name forever?'),
('PSA', 74, 11, 'PSA.74.11', 'Why do you draw back your hand, even your right hand? Take it from your chest and consume them!'),
('PSA', 74, 12, 'PSA.74.12', 'Yet God is my King of old, working salvation throughout the earth.'),
('PSA', 74, 13, 'PSA.74.13', 'You divided the sea by your strength. You broke the heads of the sea monsters in the waters.'),
('PSA', 74, 14, 'PSA.74.14', 'You broke the heads of Leviathan in pieces. You gave him as food to people and desert creatures.'),
('PSA', 74, 15, 'PSA.74.15', 'You opened up spring and stream. You dried up mighty rivers.'),
('PSA', 74, 16, 'PSA.74.16', 'The day is yours, the night is also yours. You have prepared the light and the sun.'),
('PSA', 74, 17, 'PSA.74.17', 'You have set all the boundaries of the earth. You have made summer and winter.'),
('PSA', 74, 18, 'PSA.74.18', 'Remember this, that the enemy has mocked you, LORD. Foolish people have blasphemed your name.'),
('PSA', 74, 19, 'PSA.74.19', 'Don’t deliver the soul of your dove to wild beasts. Don’t forget the life of your poor forever.'),
('PSA', 74, 20, 'PSA.74.20', 'Honor your covenant, for haunts of violence fill the dark places of the earth.'),
('PSA', 74, 21, 'PSA.74.21', 'Don’t let the oppressed return ashamed. Let the poor and needy praise your name.'),
('PSA', 74, 22, 'PSA.74.22', 'Arise, God! Plead your own cause. Remember how the foolish man mocks you all day.'),
('PSA', 74, 23, 'PSA.74.23', 'Don’t forget the voice of your adversaries. The tumult of those who rise up against you ascends continually.'),
('PSA', 75, 1, 'PSA.75.1', 'We give thanks to you, God. We give thanks, for your Name is near. Men tell about your wondrous works.'),
('PSA', 75, 2, 'PSA.75.2', 'When I choose the appointed time, I will judge blamelessly.'),
('PSA', 75, 3, 'PSA.75.3', 'The earth and all its inhabitants quake. I firmly hold its pillars. Selah.'),
('PSA', 75, 4, 'PSA.75.4', 'I said to the arrogant, “Don’t boast!” I said to the wicked, “Don’t lift up the horn.'),
('PSA', 75, 5, 'PSA.75.5', 'Don’t lift up your horn on high. Don’t speak with a stiff neck.”'),
('PSA', 75, 6, 'PSA.75.6', 'For neither from the east, nor from the west, nor yet from the south, comes exaltation.'),
('PSA', 75, 7, 'PSA.75.7', 'But God is the judge. He puts down one, and lifts up another.'),
('PSA', 75, 8, 'PSA.75.8', 'For in the LORD’s hand there is a cup, full of foaming wine mixed with spices. He pours it out. Indeed the wicked of the earth drink and drink it to its very dregs.'),
('PSA', 75, 9, 'PSA.75.9', 'But I will declare this forever: I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.'),
('PSA', 75, 10, 'PSA.75.10', 'I will cut off all the horns of the wicked, but the horns of the righteous shall be lifted up.'),
('PSA', 76, 1, 'PSA.76.1', 'In Judah, God is known. His name is great in Israel.'),
('PSA', 76, 2, 'PSA.76.2', 'His tabernacle is also in Salem. His dwelling place in Zion.'),
('PSA', 76, 3, 'PSA.76.3', 'There he broke the flaming arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the weapons of war. Selah.'),
('PSA', 76, 4, 'PSA.76.4', 'Glorious are you, and excellent, more than mountains of game.'),
('PSA', 76, 5, 'PSA.76.5', 'Valiant men lie plundered, they have slept their last sleep. None of the men of war can lift their hands.'),
('PSA', 76, 6, 'PSA.76.6', 'At your rebuke, God of Jacob, both chariot and horse are cast into a dead sleep.'),
('PSA', 76, 7, 'PSA.76.7', 'You, even you, are to be feared. Who can stand in your sight when you are angry?'),
('PSA', 76, 8, 'PSA.76.8', 'You pronounced judgment from heaven. The earth feared, and was silent,'),
('PSA', 76, 9, 'PSA.76.9', 'when God arose to judgment, to save all the afflicted ones of the earth. Selah.'),
('PSA', 76, 10, 'PSA.76.10', 'Surely the wrath of man praises you. The survivors of your wrath are restrained.'),
('PSA', 76, 11, 'PSA.76.11', 'Make vows to the LORD your God, and fulfill them! Let all of his neighbors bring presents to him who is to be feared.'),
('PSA', 76, 12, 'PSA.76.12', 'He will cut off the spirit of princes. He is feared by the kings of the earth.'),
('PSA', 77, 1, 'PSA.77.1', 'My cry goes to God! Indeed, I cry to God for help, and for him to listen to me.'),
('PSA', 77, 2, 'PSA.77.2', 'In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord. My hand was stretched out in the night, and didn’t get tired. My soul refused to be comforted.'),
('PSA', 77, 3, 'PSA.77.3', 'I remember God, and I groan. I complain, and my spirit is overwhelmed. Selah.'),
('PSA', 77, 4, 'PSA.77.4', 'You hold my eyelids open. I am so troubled that I can’t speak.'),
('PSA', 77, 5, 'PSA.77.5', 'I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times.'),
('PSA', 77, 6, 'PSA.77.6', 'I remember my song in the night. I consider in my own heart; my spirit diligently inquires:'),
('PSA', 77, 7, 'PSA.77.7', '“Will the Lord reject us forever? Will he be favorable no more?'),
('PSA', 77, 8, 'PSA.77.8', 'Has his loving kindness vanished forever? Does his promise fail for generations?'),
('PSA', 77, 9, 'PSA.77.9', 'Has God forgotten to be gracious? Has he, in anger, withheld his compassion?” Selah.'),
('PSA', 77, 10, 'PSA.77.10', 'Then I thought, “I will appeal to this: the years of the right hand of the Most High.”'),
('PSA', 77, 11, 'PSA.77.11', 'I will remember the LORD’s deeds; for I will remember your wonders of old.'),
('PSA', 77, 12, 'PSA.77.12', 'I will also meditate on all your work, and consider your doings.'),
('PSA', 77, 13, 'PSA.77.13', 'Your way, God, is in the sanctuary. What god is great like God?'),
('PSA', 77, 14, 'PSA.77.14', 'You are the God who does wonders. You have made your strength known among the peoples.'),
('PSA', 77, 15, 'PSA.77.15', 'You have redeemed your people with your arm, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah.'),
('PSA', 77, 16, 'PSA.77.16', 'The waters saw you, God. The waters saw you, and they writhed. The depths also convulsed.'),
('PSA', 77, 17, 'PSA.77.17', 'The clouds poured out water. The skies resounded with thunder. Your arrows also flashed around.'),
('PSA', 77, 18, 'PSA.77.18', 'The voice of your thunder was in the whirlwind. The lightnings lit up the world. The earth trembled and shook.'),
('PSA', 77, 19, 'PSA.77.19', 'Your way was through the sea, your paths through the great waters. Your footsteps were not known.'),
('PSA', 77, 20, 'PSA.77.20', 'You led your people like a flock, by the hand of Moses and Aaron.'),
('PSA', 78, 1, 'PSA.78.1', 'Hear my teaching, my people. Turn your ears to the words of my mouth.'),
('PSA', 78, 2, 'PSA.78.2', 'I will open my mouth in a parable. I will utter dark sayings of old,'),
('PSA', 78, 3, 'PSA.78.3', 'which we have heard and known, and our fathers have told us.'),
('PSA', 78, 4, 'PSA.78.4', 'We will not hide them from their children, telling to the generation to come the praises of the LORD, his strength, and his wondrous deeds that he has done.'),
('PSA', 78, 5, 'PSA.78.5', 'For he established a covenant in Jacob, and appointed a teaching in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, that they should make them known to their children;'),
('PSA', 78, 6, 'PSA.78.6', 'that the generation to come might know, even the children who should be born; who should arise and tell their children,'),
('PSA', 78, 7, 'PSA.78.7', 'that they might set their hope in God, and not forget God’s deeds, but keep his commandments,'),
('PSA', 78, 8, 'PSA.78.8', 'and might not be as their fathers— a stubborn and rebellious generation, a generation that didn’t make their hearts loyal, whose spirit was not steadfast with God.'),
('PSA', 78, 9, 'PSA.78.9', 'The children of Ephraim, being armed and carrying bows, turned back in the day of battle.'),
('PSA', 78, 10, 'PSA.78.10', 'They didn’t keep God’s covenant, and refused to walk in his law.'),
('PSA', 78, 11, 'PSA.78.11', 'They forgot his doings, his wondrous deeds that he had shown them.'),
('PSA', 78, 12, 'PSA.78.12', 'He did marvelous things in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the field of Zoan.'),
('PSA', 78, 13, 'PSA.78.13', 'He split the sea, and caused them to pass through. He made the waters stand as a heap.'),
('PSA', 78, 14, 'PSA.78.14', 'In the daytime he also led them with a cloud, and all night with a light of fire.'),
('PSA', 78, 15, 'PSA.78.15', 'He split rocks in the wilderness, and gave them drink abundantly as out of the depths.'),
('PSA', 78, 16, 'PSA.78.16', 'He brought streams also out of the rock, and caused waters to run down like rivers.'),
('PSA', 78, 17, 'PSA.78.17', 'Yet they still went on to sin against him, to rebel against the Most High in the desert.'),
('PSA', 78, 18, 'PSA.78.18', 'They tempted God in their heart by asking food according to their desire.'),
('PSA', 78, 19, 'PSA.78.19', 'Yes, they spoke against God. They said, “Can God prepare a table in the wilderness?'),
('PSA', 78, 20, 'PSA.78.20', 'Behold, he struck the rock, so that waters gushed out, and streams overflowed. Can he give bread also? Will he provide meat for his people?”'),
('PSA', 78, 21, 'PSA.78.21', 'Therefore the LORD heard, and was angry. A fire was kindled against Jacob, anger also went up against Israel,'),
('PSA', 78, 22, 'PSA.78.22', 'because they didn’t believe in God, and didn’t trust in his salvation.'),
('PSA', 78, 23, 'PSA.78.23', 'Yet he commanded the skies above, and opened the doors of heaven.'),
('PSA', 78, 24, 'PSA.78.24', 'He rained down manna on them to eat, and gave them food from the sky.'),
('PSA', 78, 25, 'PSA.78.25', 'Man ate the bread of angels. He sent them food to the full.'),
('PSA', 78, 26, 'PSA.78.26', 'He caused the east wind to blow in the sky. By his power he guided the south wind.'),
('PSA', 78, 27, 'PSA.78.27', 'He also rained meat on them as the dust, winged birds as the sand of the seas.'),
('PSA', 78, 28, 'PSA.78.28', 'He let them fall in the middle of their camp, around their habitations.'),
('PSA', 78, 29, 'PSA.78.29', 'So they ate, and were well filled. He gave them their own desire.'),
('PSA', 78, 30, 'PSA.78.30', 'They didn’t turn from their cravings. Their food was yet in their mouths,'),
('PSA', 78, 31, 'PSA.78.31', 'when the anger of God went up against them, killed some of their strongest, and struck down the young men of Israel.'),
('PSA', 78, 32, 'PSA.78.32', 'For all this they still sinned, and didn’t believe in his wondrous works.'),
('PSA', 78, 33, 'PSA.78.33', 'Therefore he consumed their days in vanity, and their years in terror.'),
('PSA', 78, 34, 'PSA.78.34', 'When he killed them, then they inquired after him. They returned and sought God earnestly.'),
('PSA', 78, 35, 'PSA.78.35', 'They remembered that God was their rock, the Most High God, their redeemer.'),
('PSA', 78, 36, 'PSA.78.36', 'But they flattered him with their mouth, and lied to him with their tongue.'),
('PSA', 78, 37, 'PSA.78.37', 'For their heart was not right with him, neither were they faithful in his covenant.'),
('PSA', 78, 38, 'PSA.78.38', 'But he, being merciful, forgave iniquity, and didn’t destroy them. Yes, many times he turned his anger away, and didn’t stir up all his wrath.'),
('PSA', 78, 39, 'PSA.78.39', 'He remembered that they were but flesh, a wind that passes away, and doesn’t come again.'),
('PSA', 78, 40, 'PSA.78.40', 'How often they rebelled against him in the wilderness, and grieved him in the desert!'),
('PSA', 78, 41, 'PSA.78.41', 'They turned again and tempted God, and provoked the Holy One of Israel.'),
('PSA', 78, 42, 'PSA.78.42', 'They didn’t remember his hand, nor the day when he redeemed them from the adversary;'),
('PSA', 78, 43, 'PSA.78.43', 'how he set his signs in Egypt, his wonders in the field of Zoan,'),
('PSA', 78, 44, 'PSA.78.44', 'he turned their rivers into blood, and their streams, so that they could not drink.'),
('PSA', 78, 45, 'PSA.78.45', 'He sent among them swarms of flies, which devoured them; and frogs, which destroyed them.'),
('PSA', 78, 46, 'PSA.78.46', 'He also gave their increase to the caterpillar, and their labor to the locust.'),
('PSA', 78, 47, 'PSA.78.47', 'He destroyed their vines with hail, their sycamore fig trees with frost.'),
('PSA', 78, 48, 'PSA.78.48', 'He also gave over their livestock to the hail, and their flocks to hot thunderbolts.'),
('PSA', 78, 49, 'PSA.78.49', 'He threw on them the fierceness of his anger, wrath, indignation, and trouble, and a band of angels of evil.'),
('PSA', 78, 50, 'PSA.78.50', 'He made a path for his anger. He didn’t spare their soul from death, but gave their life over to the pestilence,'),
('PSA', 78, 51, 'PSA.78.51', 'and struck all the firstborn in Egypt, the chief of their strength in the tents of Ham.'),
('PSA', 78, 52, 'PSA.78.52', 'But he led out his own people like sheep, and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.'),
('PSA', 78, 53, 'PSA.78.53', 'He led them safely, so that they weren’t afraid, but the sea overwhelmed their enemies.'),
('PSA', 78, 54, 'PSA.78.54', 'He brought them to the border of his sanctuary, to this mountain, which his right hand had taken.'),
('PSA', 78, 55, 'PSA.78.55', 'He also drove out the nations before them, allotted them for an inheritance by line, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.'),
('PSA', 78, 56, 'PSA.78.56', 'Yet they tempted and rebelled against the Most High God, and didn’t keep his testimonies,'),
('PSA', 78, 57, 'PSA.78.57', 'but turned back, and dealt treacherously like their fathers. They were twisted like a deceitful bow.'),
('PSA', 78, 58, 'PSA.78.58', 'For they provoked him to anger with their high places, and moved him to jealousy with their engraved images.'),
('PSA', 78, 59, 'PSA.78.59', 'When God heard this, he was angry, and greatly abhorred Israel,'),
('PSA', 78, 60, 'PSA.78.60', 'so that he abandoned the tent of Shiloh, the tent which he placed among men,'),
('PSA', 78, 61, 'PSA.78.61', 'and delivered his strength into captivity, his glory into the adversary’s hand.'),
('PSA', 78, 62, 'PSA.78.62', 'He also gave his people over to the sword, and was angry with his inheritance.'),
('PSA', 78, 63, 'PSA.78.63', 'Fire devoured their young men. Their virgins had no wedding song.'),
('PSA', 78, 64, 'PSA.78.64', 'Their priests fell by the sword, and their widows couldn’t weep.'),
('PSA', 78, 65, 'PSA.78.65', 'Then the Lord awakened as one out of sleep, like a mighty man who shouts by reason of wine.'),
('PSA', 78, 66, 'PSA.78.66', 'He struck his adversaries backward. He put them to a perpetual reproach.'),
('PSA', 78, 67, 'PSA.78.67', 'Moreover he rejected the tent of Joseph, and didn’t choose the tribe of Ephraim,'),
('PSA', 78, 68, 'PSA.78.68', 'But chose the tribe of Judah, Mount Zion which he loved.'),
('PSA', 78, 69, 'PSA.78.69', 'He built his sanctuary like the heights, like the earth which he has established forever.'),
('PSA', 78, 70, 'PSA.78.70', 'He also chose David his servant, and took him from the sheepfolds;'),
('PSA', 78, 71, 'PSA.78.71', 'from following the ewes that have their young, he brought him to be the shepherd of Jacob, his people, and Israel, his inheritance.'),
('PSA', 78, 72, 'PSA.78.72', 'So he was their shepherd according to the integrity of his heart, and guided them by the skillfulness of his hands.'),
('PSA', 79, 1, 'PSA.79.1', 'God, the nations have come into your inheritance. They have defiled your holy temple. They have laid Jerusalem in heaps.'),
('PSA', 79, 2, 'PSA.79.2', 'They have given the dead bodies of your servants to be food for the birds of the sky, the flesh of your saints to the animals of the earth.'),
('PSA', 79, 3, 'PSA.79.3', 'They have shed their blood like water around Jerusalem. There was no one to bury them.'),
('PSA', 79, 4, 'PSA.79.4', 'We have become a reproach to our neighbors, a scoffing and derision to those who are around us.'),
('PSA', 79, 5, 'PSA.79.5', 'How long, LORD? Will you be angry forever? Will your jealousy burn like fire?'),
('PSA', 79, 6, 'PSA.79.6', 'Pour out your wrath on the nations that don’t know you, on the kingdoms that don’t call on your name,'),
('PSA', 79, 7, 'PSA.79.7', 'for they have devoured Jacob, and destroyed his homeland.'),
('PSA', 79, 8, 'PSA.79.8', 'Don’t hold the iniquities of our forefathers against us. Let your tender mercies speedily meet us, for we are in desperate need.'),
('PSA', 79, 9, 'PSA.79.9', 'Help us, God of our salvation, for the glory of your name. Deliver us, and forgive our sins, for your name’s sake.'),
('PSA', 79, 10, 'PSA.79.10', 'Why should the nations say, “Where is their God?” Let it be known among the nations, before our eyes, that vengeance for your servants’ blood is being poured out.'),
('PSA', 79, 11, 'PSA.79.11', 'Let the sighing of the prisoner come before you. According to the greatness of your power, preserve those who are sentenced to death.'),
('PSA', 79, 12, 'PSA.79.12', 'Pay back to our neighbors seven times into their bosom their reproach with which they have reproached you, Lord.'),
('PSA', 79, 13, 'PSA.79.13', 'So we, your people and sheep of your pasture, will give you thanks forever. We will praise you forever, to all generations.'),
('PSA', 80, 1, 'PSA.80.1', 'Hear us, Shepherd of Israel, you who lead Joseph like a flock, you who sit above the cherubim, shine out.'),
('PSA', 80, 2, 'PSA.80.2', 'Before Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh, stir up your might! Come to save us!'),
('PSA', 80, 3, 'PSA.80.3', 'Turn us again, God. Cause your face to shine, and we will be saved.'),
('PSA', 80, 4, 'PSA.80.4', 'LORD God of Armies, how long will you be angry against the prayer of your people?'),
('PSA', 80, 5, 'PSA.80.5', 'You have fed them with the bread of tears, and given them tears to drink in large measure.'),
('PSA', 80, 6, 'PSA.80.6', 'You make us a source of contention to our neighbors. Our enemies laugh among themselves.'),
('PSA', 80, 7, 'PSA.80.7', 'Turn us again, God of Armies. Cause your face to shine, and we will be saved.'),
('PSA', 80, 8, 'PSA.80.8', 'You brought a vine out of Egypt. You drove out the nations, and planted it.'),
('PSA', 80, 9, 'PSA.80.9', 'You cleared the ground for it. It took deep root, and filled the land.'),
('PSA', 80, 10, 'PSA.80.10', 'The mountains were covered with its shadow. Its boughs were like God’s cedars.'),
('PSA', 80, 11, 'PSA.80.11', 'It sent out its branches to the sea, its shoots to the River.'),
('PSA', 80, 12, 'PSA.80.12', 'Why have you broken down its walls, so that all those who pass by the way pluck it?'),
('PSA', 80, 13, 'PSA.80.13', 'The boar out of the wood ravages it. The wild animals of the field feed on it.'),
('PSA', 80, 14, 'PSA.80.14', 'Turn again, we beg you, God of Armies. Look down from heaven, and see, and visit this vine,'),
('PSA', 80, 15, 'PSA.80.15', 'the stock which your right hand planted, the branch that you made strong for yourself.'),
('PSA', 80, 16, 'PSA.80.16', 'It’s burned with fire. It’s cut down. They perish at your rebuke.'),
('PSA', 80, 17, 'PSA.80.17', 'Let your hand be on the man of your right hand, on the son of man whom you made strong for yourself.'),
('PSA', 80, 18, 'PSA.80.18', 'So we will not turn away from you. Revive us, and we will call on your name.'),
('PSA', 80, 19, 'PSA.80.19', 'Turn us again, LORD God of Armies. Cause your face to shine, and we will be saved.'),
('PSA', 81, 1, 'PSA.81.1', 'Sing aloud to God, our strength! Make a joyful shout to the God of Jacob!'),
('PSA', 81, 2, 'PSA.81.2', 'Raise a song, and bring here the tambourine, the pleasant lyre with the harp.'),
('PSA', 81, 3, 'PSA.81.3', 'Blow the trumpet at the New Moon, at the full moon, on our feast day.'),
('PSA', 81, 4, 'PSA.81.4', 'For it is a statute for Israel, an ordinance of the God of Jacob.'),
('PSA', 81, 5, 'PSA.81.5', 'He appointed it in Joseph for a covenant, when he went out over the land of Egypt, I heard a language that I didn’t know.'),
('PSA', 81, 6, 'PSA.81.6', '“I removed his shoulder from the burden. His hands were freed from the basket.'),
('PSA', 81, 7, 'PSA.81.7', 'You called in trouble, and I delivered you. I answered you in the secret place of thunder. I tested you at the waters of Meribah.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 81, 8, 'PSA.81.8', '“Hear, my people, and I will testify to you, Israel, if you would listen to me!'),
('PSA', 81, 9, 'PSA.81.9', 'There shall be no strange god in you, neither shall you worship any foreign god.'),
('PSA', 81, 10, 'PSA.81.10', 'I am the LORD, your God, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt. Open your mouth wide, and I will fill it.'),
('PSA', 81, 11, 'PSA.81.11', 'But my people didn’t listen to my voice. Israel desired none of me.'),
('PSA', 81, 12, 'PSA.81.12', 'So I let them go after the stubbornness of their hearts, that they might walk in their own counsels.'),
('PSA', 81, 13, 'PSA.81.13', 'Oh that my people would listen to me, that Israel would walk in my ways!'),
('PSA', 81, 14, 'PSA.81.14', 'I would soon subdue their enemies, and turn my hand against their adversaries.'),
('PSA', 81, 15, 'PSA.81.15', 'The haters of the LORD would cringe before him, and their punishment would last forever.'),
('PSA', 81, 16, 'PSA.81.16', 'But he would have also fed them with the finest of the wheat. I will satisfy you with honey out of the rock.”'),
('PSA', 82, 1, 'PSA.82.1', 'God presides in the great assembly. He judges among the gods.'),
('PSA', 82, 2, 'PSA.82.2', '“How long will you judge unjustly, and show partiality to the wicked?” Selah.'),
('PSA', 82, 3, 'PSA.82.3', '“Defend the weak, the poor, and the fatherless. Maintain the rights of the poor and oppressed.'),
('PSA', 82, 4, 'PSA.82.4', 'Rescue the weak and needy. Deliver them out of the hand of the wicked.”'),
('PSA', 82, 5, 'PSA.82.5', 'They don’t know, neither do they understand. They walk back and forth in darkness. All the foundations of the earth are shaken.'),
('PSA', 82, 6, 'PSA.82.6', 'I said, “You are gods, all of you are sons of the Most High.'),
('PSA', 82, 7, 'PSA.82.7', 'Nevertheless you shall die like men, and fall like one of the rulers.”'),
('PSA', 82, 8, 'PSA.82.8', 'Arise, God, judge the earth, for you inherit all of the nations.'),
('PSA', 83, 1, 'PSA.83.1', 'God, don’t keep silent. Don’t keep silent, and don’t be still, God.'),
('PSA', 83, 2, 'PSA.83.2', 'For, behold, your enemies are stirred up. Those who hate you have lifted up their heads.'),
('PSA', 83, 3, 'PSA.83.3', 'They conspire with cunning against your people. They plot against your cherished ones.'),
('PSA', 83, 4, 'PSA.83.4', '“Come,” they say, “let’s destroy them as a nation, that the name of Israel may be remembered no more.”'),
('PSA', 83, 5, 'PSA.83.5', 'For they have conspired together with one mind. They form an alliance against you.'),
('PSA', 83, 6, 'PSA.83.6', 'The tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites; Moab, and the Hagrites;'),
('PSA', 83, 7, 'PSA.83.7', 'Gebal, Ammon, and Amalek; Philistia with the inhabitants of Tyre;'),
('PSA', 83, 8, 'PSA.83.8', 'Assyria also is joined with them. They have helped the children of Lot. Selah.'),
('PSA', 83, 9, 'PSA.83.9', 'Do to them as you did to Midian, as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the river Kishon;'),
('PSA', 83, 10, 'PSA.83.10', 'who perished at Endor, who became as dung for the earth.'),
('PSA', 83, 11, 'PSA.83.11', 'Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb, yes, all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna,'),
('PSA', 83, 12, 'PSA.83.12', 'who said, “Let’s take possession of God’s pasture lands.”'),
('PSA', 83, 13, 'PSA.83.13', 'My God, make them like tumbleweed, like chaff before the wind.'),
('PSA', 83, 14, 'PSA.83.14', 'As the fire that burns the forest, as the flame that sets the mountains on fire,'),
('PSA', 83, 15, 'PSA.83.15', 'so pursue them with your tempest, and terrify them with your storm.'),
('PSA', 83, 16, 'PSA.83.16', 'Fill their faces with confusion, that they may seek your name, LORD.'),
('PSA', 83, 17, 'PSA.83.17', 'Let them be disappointed and dismayed forever. Yes, let them be confounded and perish;'),
('PSA', 83, 18, 'PSA.83.18', 'that they may know that you alone, whose name is the LORD, are the Most High over all the earth.'),
('PSA', 84, 1, 'PSA.84.1', 'How lovely are your dwellings, LORD of Armies!'),
('PSA', 84, 2, 'PSA.84.2', 'My soul longs, and even faints for the courts of the LORD. My heart and my flesh cry out for the living God.'),
('PSA', 84, 3, 'PSA.84.3', 'Yes, the sparrow has found a home, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she may have her young, near your altars, LORD of Armies, my King, and my God.'),
('PSA', 84, 4, 'PSA.84.4', 'Blessed are those who dwell in your house. They are always praising you. Selah.'),
('PSA', 84, 5, 'PSA.84.5', 'Blessed are those whose strength is in you, who have set their hearts on a pilgrimage.'),
('PSA', 84, 6, 'PSA.84.6', 'Passing through the valley of Weeping, they make it a place of springs. Yes, the autumn rain covers it with blessings.'),
('PSA', 84, 7, 'PSA.84.7', 'They go from strength to strength. Every one of them appears before God in Zion.'),
('PSA', 84, 8, 'PSA.84.8', 'LORD, God of Armies, hear my prayer. Listen, God of Jacob. Selah.'),
('PSA', 84, 9, 'PSA.84.9', 'Behold, God our shield, look at the face of your anointed.'),
('PSA', 84, 10, 'PSA.84.10', 'For a day in your courts is better than a thousand. I would rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.'),
('PSA', 84, 11, 'PSA.84.11', 'For the LORD God is a sun and a shield. The LORD will give grace and glory. He withholds no good thing from those who walk blamelessly.'),
('PSA', 84, 12, 'PSA.84.12', 'LORD of Armies, blessed is the man who trusts in you.'),
('PSA', 85, 1, 'PSA.85.1', 'LORD, you have been favorable to your land. You have restored the fortunes of Jacob.'),
('PSA', 85, 2, 'PSA.85.2', 'You have forgiven the iniquity of your people. You have covered all their sin. Selah.'),
('PSA', 85, 3, 'PSA.85.3', 'You have taken away all your wrath. You have turned from the fierceness of your anger.'),
('PSA', 85, 4, 'PSA.85.4', 'Turn us, God of our salvation, and cause your indignation toward us to cease.'),
('PSA', 85, 5, 'PSA.85.5', 'Will you be angry with us forever? Will you draw out your anger to all generations?'),
('PSA', 85, 6, 'PSA.85.6', 'Won’t you revive us again, that your people may rejoice in you?'),
('PSA', 85, 7, 'PSA.85.7', 'Show us your loving kindness, LORD. Grant us your salvation.'),
('PSA', 85, 8, 'PSA.85.8', 'I will hear what God, the LORD, will speak, for he will speak peace to his people, his saints; but let them not turn again to folly.'),
('PSA', 85, 9, 'PSA.85.9', 'Surely his salvation is near those who fear him, that glory may dwell in our land.'),
('PSA', 85, 10, 'PSA.85.10', 'Mercy and truth meet together. Righteousness and peace have kissed each other.'),
('PSA', 85, 11, 'PSA.85.11', 'Truth springs out of the earth. Righteousness has looked down from heaven.'),
('PSA', 85, 12, 'PSA.85.12', 'Yes, the LORD will give that which is good. Our land will yield its increase.'),
('PSA', 85, 13, 'PSA.85.13', 'Righteousness goes before him, and prepares the way for his steps.'),
('PSA', 86, 1, 'PSA.86.1', 'Hear, LORD, and answer me, for I am poor and needy.'),
('PSA', 86, 2, 'PSA.86.2', 'Preserve my soul, for I am godly. You, my God, save your servant who trusts in you.'),
('PSA', 86, 3, 'PSA.86.3', 'Be merciful to me, Lord, for I call to you all day long.'),
('PSA', 86, 4, 'PSA.86.4', 'Bring joy to the soul of your servant, for to you, Lord, do I lift up my soul.'),
('PSA', 86, 5, 'PSA.86.5', 'For you, Lord, are good, and ready to forgive, abundant in loving kindness to all those who call on you.'),
('PSA', 86, 6, 'PSA.86.6', 'Hear, LORD, my prayer. Listen to the voice of my petitions.'),
('PSA', 86, 7, 'PSA.86.7', 'In the day of my trouble I will call on you, for you will answer me.'),
('PSA', 86, 8, 'PSA.86.8', 'There is no one like you among the gods, Lord, nor any deeds like your deeds.'),
('PSA', 86, 9, 'PSA.86.9', 'All nations you have made will come and worship before you, Lord. They shall glorify your name.'),
('PSA', 86, 10, 'PSA.86.10', 'For you are great, and do wondrous things. You are God alone.'),
('PSA', 86, 11, 'PSA.86.11', 'Teach me your way, LORD. I will walk in your truth. Make my heart undivided to fear your name.'),
('PSA', 86, 12, 'PSA.86.12', 'I will praise you, Lord my God, with my whole heart. I will glorify your name forever more.'),
('PSA', 86, 13, 'PSA.86.13', 'For your loving kindness is great toward me. You have delivered my soul from the lowest Sheol.'),
('PSA', 86, 14, 'PSA.86.14', 'God, the proud have risen up against me. A company of violent men have sought after my soul, and they don’t hold regard for you before them.'),
('PSA', 86, 15, 'PSA.86.15', 'But you, Lord, are a merciful and gracious God, slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness and truth.'),
('PSA', 86, 16, 'PSA.86.16', 'Turn to me, and have mercy on me! Give your strength to your servant. Save the son of your servant.'),
('PSA', 86, 17, 'PSA.86.17', 'Show me a sign of your goodness, that those who hate me may see it, and be shamed, because you, LORD, have helped me, and comforted me.'),
('PSA', 87, 1, 'PSA.87.1', 'His foundation is in the holy mountains.'),
('PSA', 87, 2, 'PSA.87.2', 'The LORD loves the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.'),
('PSA', 87, 3, 'PSA.87.3', 'Glorious things are spoken about you, city of God. Selah.'),
('PSA', 87, 4, 'PSA.87.4', 'I will record Rahab and Babylon among those who acknowledge me. Behold, Philistia, Tyre, and also Ethiopia: “This one was born there.”'),
('PSA', 87, 5, 'PSA.87.5', 'Yes, of Zion it will be said, “This one and that one was born in her;” the Most High himself will establish her.'),
('PSA', 87, 6, 'PSA.87.6', 'The LORD will count, when he writes up the peoples, “This one was born there.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 87, 7, 'PSA.87.7', 'Those who sing as well as those who dance say, “All my springs are in you.”'),
('PSA', 88, 1, 'PSA.88.1', 'LORD, the God of my salvation, I have cried day and night before you.'),
('PSA', 88, 2, 'PSA.88.2', 'Let my prayer enter into your presence. Turn your ear to my cry.'),
('PSA', 88, 3, 'PSA.88.3', 'For my soul is full of troubles. My life draws near to Sheol.'),
('PSA', 88, 4, 'PSA.88.4', 'I am counted among those who go down into the pit. I am like a man who has no help,'),
('PSA', 88, 5, 'PSA.88.5', 'set apart among the dead, like the slain who lie in the grave, whom you remember no more. They are cut off from your hand.'),
('PSA', 88, 6, 'PSA.88.6', 'You have laid me in the lowest pit, in the darkest depths.'),
('PSA', 88, 7, 'PSA.88.7', 'Your wrath lies heavily on me. You have afflicted me with all your waves. Selah.'),
('PSA', 88, 8, 'PSA.88.8', 'You have taken my friends from me. You have made me an abomination to them. I am confined, and I can’t escape.'),
('PSA', 88, 9, 'PSA.88.9', 'My eyes are dim from grief. I have called on you daily, LORD. I have spread out my hands to you.'),
('PSA', 88, 10, 'PSA.88.10', 'Do you show wonders to the dead? Do the departed spirits rise up and praise you? Selah.'),
('PSA', 88, 11, 'PSA.88.11', 'Is your loving kindness declared in the grave? Or your faithfulness in Destruction?'),
('PSA', 88, 12, 'PSA.88.12', 'Are your wonders made known in the dark? Or your righteousness in the land of forgetfulness?'),
('PSA', 88, 13, 'PSA.88.13', 'But to you, LORD, I have cried. In the morning, my prayer comes before you.'),
('PSA', 88, 14, 'PSA.88.14', 'LORD, why do you reject my soul? Why do you hide your face from me?'),
('PSA', 88, 15, 'PSA.88.15', 'I am afflicted and ready to die from my youth up. While I suffer your terrors, I am distracted.'),
('PSA', 88, 16, 'PSA.88.16', 'Your fierce wrath has gone over me. Your terrors have cut me off.'),
('PSA', 88, 17, 'PSA.88.17', 'They came around me like water all day long. They completely engulfed me.'),
('PSA', 88, 18, 'PSA.88.18', 'You have put lover and friend far from me, and my friends into darkness.'),
('PSA', 89, 1, 'PSA.89.1', 'I will sing of the loving kindness of the LORD forever. With my mouth, I will make known your faithfulness to all generations.'),
('PSA', 89, 2, 'PSA.89.2', 'I indeed declare, “Love stands firm forever. You established the heavens. Your faithfulness is in them.”'),
('PSA', 89, 3, 'PSA.89.3', '“I have made a covenant with my chosen one, I have sworn to David, my servant,'),
('PSA', 89, 4, 'PSA.89.4', '‘I will establish your offspring forever, and build up your throne to all generations.’” Selah.'),
('PSA', 89, 5, 'PSA.89.5', 'The heavens will praise your wonders, LORD, your faithfulness also in the assembly of the holy ones.'),
('PSA', 89, 6, 'PSA.89.6', 'For who in the skies can be compared to the LORD? Who among the sons of the heavenly beings is like the LORD,'),
('PSA', 89, 7, 'PSA.89.7', 'a very awesome God in the council of the holy ones, to be feared above all those who are around him?'),
('PSA', 89, 8, 'PSA.89.8', 'LORD, God of Armies, who is a mighty one, like you? LORD, your faithfulness is around you.'),
('PSA', 89, 9, 'PSA.89.9', 'You rule the pride of the sea. When its waves rise up, you calm them.'),
('PSA', 89, 10, 'PSA.89.10', 'You have broken Rahab in pieces, like one of the slain. You have scattered your enemies with your mighty arm.'),
('PSA', 89, 11, 'PSA.89.11', 'The heavens are yours. The earth also is yours, the world and its fullness. You have founded them.'),
('PSA', 89, 12, 'PSA.89.12', 'You have created the north and the south. Tabor and Hermon rejoice in your name.'),
('PSA', 89, 13, 'PSA.89.13', 'You have a mighty arm. Your hand is strong, and your right hand is exalted.'),
('PSA', 89, 14, 'PSA.89.14', 'Righteousness and justice are the foundation of your throne. Loving kindness and truth go before your face.'),
('PSA', 89, 15, 'PSA.89.15', 'Blessed are the people who learn to acclaim you. They walk in the light of your presence, LORD.'),
('PSA', 89, 16, 'PSA.89.16', 'In your name they rejoice all day. In your righteousness, they are exalted.'),
('PSA', 89, 17, 'PSA.89.17', 'For you are the glory of their strength. In your favor, our horn will be exalted.'),
('PSA', 89, 18, 'PSA.89.18', 'For our shield belongs to the LORD, our king to the Holy One of Israel.'),
('PSA', 89, 19, 'PSA.89.19', 'Then you spoke in vision to your saints, and said, “I have given strength to the warrior. I have exalted a young man from the people.'),
('PSA', 89, 20, 'PSA.89.20', 'I have found David, my servant. I have anointed him with my holy oil,'),
('PSA', 89, 21, 'PSA.89.21', 'with whom my hand shall be established. My arm will also strengthen him.'),
('PSA', 89, 22, 'PSA.89.22', 'No enemy will tax him. No wicked man will oppress him.'),
('PSA', 89, 23, 'PSA.89.23', 'I will beat down his adversaries before him, and strike those who hate him.'),
('PSA', 89, 24, 'PSA.89.24', 'But my faithfulness and my loving kindness will be with him. In my name, his horn will be exalted.'),
('PSA', 89, 25, 'PSA.89.25', 'I will set his hand also on the sea, and his right hand on the rivers.'),
('PSA', 89, 26, 'PSA.89.26', 'He will call to me, ‘You are my Father, my God, and the rock of my salvation!’'),
('PSA', 89, 27, 'PSA.89.27', 'I will also appoint him my firstborn, the highest of the kings of the earth.'),
('PSA', 89, 28, 'PSA.89.28', 'I will keep my loving kindness for him forever more. My covenant will stand firm with him.'),
('PSA', 89, 29, 'PSA.89.29', 'I will also make his offspring endure forever, and his throne as the days of heaven.'),
('PSA', 89, 30, 'PSA.89.30', 'If his children forsake my law, and don’t walk in my ordinances;'),
('PSA', 89, 31, 'PSA.89.31', 'if they break my statutes, and don’t keep my commandments;'),
('PSA', 89, 32, 'PSA.89.32', 'then I will punish their sin with the rod, and their iniquity with stripes.'),
('PSA', 89, 33, 'PSA.89.33', 'But I will not completely take my loving kindness from him, nor allow my faithfulness to fail.'),
('PSA', 89, 34, 'PSA.89.34', 'I will not break my covenant, nor alter what my lips have uttered.'),
('PSA', 89, 35, 'PSA.89.35', 'Once I have sworn by my holiness, I will not lie to David.'),
('PSA', 89, 36, 'PSA.89.36', 'His offspring will endure forever, his throne like the sun before me.'),
('PSA', 89, 37, 'PSA.89.37', 'It will be established forever like the moon, the faithful witness in the sky.” Selah.'),
('PSA', 89, 38, 'PSA.89.38', 'But you have rejected and spurned. You have been angry with your anointed.'),
('PSA', 89, 39, 'PSA.89.39', 'You have renounced the covenant of your servant. You have defiled his crown in the dust.'),
('PSA', 89, 40, 'PSA.89.40', 'You have broken down all his hedges. You have brought his strongholds to ruin.'),
('PSA', 89, 41, 'PSA.89.41', 'All who pass by the way rob him. He has become a reproach to his neighbors.'),
('PSA', 89, 42, 'PSA.89.42', 'You have exalted the right hand of his adversaries. You have made all of his enemies rejoice.'),
('PSA', 89, 43, 'PSA.89.43', 'Yes, you turn back the edge of his sword, and haven’t supported him in battle.'),
('PSA', 89, 44, 'PSA.89.44', 'You have ended his splendor, and thrown his throne down to the ground.'),
('PSA', 89, 45, 'PSA.89.45', 'You have shortened the days of his youth. You have covered him with shame. Selah.'),
('PSA', 89, 46, 'PSA.89.46', 'How long, LORD? Will you hide yourself forever? Will your wrath burn like fire?'),
('PSA', 89, 47, 'PSA.89.47', 'Remember how short my time is, for what vanity you have created all the children of men!'),
('PSA', 89, 48, 'PSA.89.48', 'What man is he who shall live and not see death, who shall deliver his soul from the power of Sheol? Selah.'),
('PSA', 89, 49, 'PSA.89.49', 'Lord, where are your former loving kindnesses, which you swore to David in your faithfulness?'),
('PSA', 89, 50, 'PSA.89.50', 'Remember, Lord, the reproach of your servants, how I bear in my heart the taunts of all the mighty peoples,'),
('PSA', 89, 51, 'PSA.89.51', 'With which your enemies have mocked, LORD, with which they have mocked the footsteps of your anointed one.'),
('PSA', 89, 52, 'PSA.89.52', 'Blessed be the LORD forever more. Amen, and Amen.'),
('PSA', 90, 1, 'PSA.90.1', 'Lord, you have been our dwelling place for all generations.'),
('PSA', 90, 2, 'PSA.90.2', 'Before the mountains were born, before you had formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, you are God.'),
('PSA', 90, 3, 'PSA.90.3', 'You turn man to destruction, saying, “Return, you children of men.”'),
('PSA', 90, 4, 'PSA.90.4', 'For a thousand years in your sight are just like yesterday when it is past, like a watch in the night.'),
('PSA', 90, 5, 'PSA.90.5', 'You sweep them away as they sleep. In the morning they sprout like new grass.'),
('PSA', 90, 6, 'PSA.90.6', 'In the morning it sprouts and springs up. By evening, it is withered and dry.'),
('PSA', 90, 7, 'PSA.90.7', 'For we are consumed in your anger. We are troubled in your wrath.'),
('PSA', 90, 8, 'PSA.90.8', 'You have set our iniquities before you, our secret sins in the light of your presence.'),
('PSA', 90, 9, 'PSA.90.9', 'For all our days have passed away in your wrath. We bring our years to an end as a sigh.'),
('PSA', 90, 10, 'PSA.90.10', 'The days of our years are seventy, or even by reason of strength eighty years; yet their pride is but labor and sorrow, for it passes quickly, and we fly away.'),
('PSA', 90, 11, 'PSA.90.11', 'Who knows the power of your anger, your wrath according to the fear that is due to you?'),
('PSA', 90, 12, 'PSA.90.12', 'So teach us to count our days, that we may gain a heart of wisdom.'),
('PSA', 90, 13, 'PSA.90.13', 'Relent, LORD! How long? Have compassion on your servants!'),
('PSA', 90, 14, 'PSA.90.14', 'Satisfy us in the morning with your loving kindness, that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.'),
('PSA', 90, 15, 'PSA.90.15', 'Make us glad for as many days as you have afflicted us, for as many years as we have seen evil.'),
('PSA', 90, 16, 'PSA.90.16', 'Let your work appear to your servants, your glory to their children.'),
('PSA', 90, 17, 'PSA.90.17', 'Let the favor of the Lord our God be on us. Establish the work of our hands for us. Yes, establish the work of our hands.'),
('PSA', 91, 1, 'PSA.91.1', 'He who dwells in the secret place of the Most High will rest in the shadow of the Almighty.'),
('PSA', 91, 2, 'PSA.91.2', 'I will say of the LORD, “He is my refuge and my fortress; my God, in whom I trust.”'),
('PSA', 91, 3, 'PSA.91.3', 'For he will deliver you from the snare of the fowler, and from the deadly pestilence.'),
('PSA', 91, 4, 'PSA.91.4', 'He will cover you with his feathers. Under his wings you will take refuge. His faithfulness is your shield and rampart.'),
('PSA', 91, 5, 'PSA.91.5', 'You shall not be afraid of the terror by night, nor of the arrow that flies by day,'),
('PSA', 91, 6, 'PSA.91.6', 'nor of the pestilence that walks in darkness, nor of the destruction that wastes at noonday.'),
('PSA', 91, 7, 'PSA.91.7', 'A thousand may fall at your side, and ten thousand at your right hand; but it will not come near you.'),
('PSA', 91, 8, 'PSA.91.8', 'You will only look with your eyes, and see the recompense of the wicked.'),
('PSA', 91, 9, 'PSA.91.9', 'Because you have made the LORD your refuge, and the Most High your dwelling place,'),
('PSA', 91, 10, 'PSA.91.10', 'no evil shall happen to you, neither shall any plague come near your dwelling.'),
('PSA', 91, 11, 'PSA.91.11', 'For he will put his angels in charge of you, to guard you in all your ways.'),
('PSA', 91, 12, 'PSA.91.12', 'They will bear you up in their hands, so that you won’t dash your foot against a stone.'),
('PSA', 91, 13, 'PSA.91.13', 'You will tread on the lion and cobra. You will trample the young lion and the serpent underfoot.'),
('PSA', 91, 14, 'PSA.91.14', '“Because he has set his love on me, therefore I will deliver him. I will set him on high, because he has known my name.'),
('PSA', 91, 15, 'PSA.91.15', 'He will call on me, and I will answer him. I will be with him in trouble. I will deliver him, and honor him.'),
('PSA', 91, 16, 'PSA.91.16', 'I will satisfy him with long life, and show him my salvation.”'),
('PSA', 92, 1, 'PSA.92.1', 'It is a good thing to give thanks to the LORD, to sing praises to your name, Most High,'),
('PSA', 92, 2, 'PSA.92.2', 'to proclaim your loving kindness in the morning, and your faithfulness every night,'),
('PSA', 92, 3, 'PSA.92.3', 'with the ten-stringed lute, with the harp, and with the melody of the lyre.'),
('PSA', 92, 4, 'PSA.92.4', 'For you, LORD, have made me glad through your work. I will triumph in the works of your hands.'),
('PSA', 92, 5, 'PSA.92.5', 'How great are your works, LORD! Your thoughts are very deep.'),
('PSA', 92, 6, 'PSA.92.6', 'A senseless man doesn’t know, neither does a fool understand this:'),
('PSA', 92, 7, 'PSA.92.7', 'though the wicked spring up as the grass, and all the evildoers flourish, they will be destroyed forever.'),
('PSA', 92, 8, 'PSA.92.8', 'But you, LORD, are on high forever more.'),
('PSA', 92, 9, 'PSA.92.9', 'For behold, your enemies, LORD, for behold, your enemies shall perish. All the evildoers will be scattered.'),
('PSA', 92, 10, 'PSA.92.10', 'But you have exalted my horn like that of the wild ox. I am anointed with fresh oil.'),
('PSA', 92, 11, 'PSA.92.11', 'My eye has also seen my enemies. My ears have heard of the wicked enemies who rise up against me.'),
('PSA', 92, 12, 'PSA.92.12', 'The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree. He will grow like a cedar in Lebanon.'),
('PSA', 92, 13, 'PSA.92.13', 'They are planted in the LORD’s house. They will flourish in our God’s courts.'),
('PSA', 92, 14, 'PSA.92.14', 'They will still produce fruit in old age. They will be full of sap and green,'),
('PSA', 92, 15, 'PSA.92.15', 'to show that the LORD is upright. He is my rock, and there is no unrighteousness in him.'),
('PSA', 93, 1, 'PSA.93.1', 'The LORD reigns! He is clothed with majesty! The LORD is armed with strength. The world also is established. It can’t be moved.'),
('PSA', 93, 2, 'PSA.93.2', 'Your throne is established from long ago. You are from everlasting.'),
('PSA', 93, 3, 'PSA.93.3', 'The floods have lifted up, LORD, the floods have lifted up their voice. The floods lift up their waves.'),
('PSA', 93, 4, 'PSA.93.4', 'Above the voices of many waters, the mighty breakers of the sea, the LORD on high is mighty.'),
('PSA', 93, 5, 'PSA.93.5', 'Your statutes stand firm. Holiness adorns your house, LORD, forever more.'),
('PSA', 94, 1, 'PSA.94.1', 'LORD, you God to whom vengeance belongs, you God to whom vengeance belongs, shine out.'),
('PSA', 94, 2, 'PSA.94.2', 'Rise up, you judge of the earth. Pay back the proud what they deserve.'),
('PSA', 94, 3, 'PSA.94.3', 'LORD, how long will the wicked, how long will the wicked triumph?'),
('PSA', 94, 4, 'PSA.94.4', 'They pour out arrogant words. All the evildoers boast.'),
('PSA', 94, 5, 'PSA.94.5', 'They break your people in pieces, LORD, and afflict your heritage.'),
('PSA', 94, 6, 'PSA.94.6', 'They kill the widow and the alien, and murder the fatherless.'),
('PSA', 94, 7, 'PSA.94.7', 'They say, “The LORD will not see, neither will Jacob’s God consider.”'),
('PSA', 94, 8, 'PSA.94.8', 'Consider, you senseless among the people; you fools, when will you be wise?'),
('PSA', 94, 9, 'PSA.94.9', 'He who implanted the ear, won’t he hear? He who formed the eye, won’t he see?'),
('PSA', 94, 10, 'PSA.94.10', 'He who disciplines the nations, won’t he punish? He who teaches man knows.'),
('PSA', 94, 11, 'PSA.94.11', 'The LORD knows the thoughts of man, that they are futile.'),
('PSA', 94, 12, 'PSA.94.12', 'Blessed is the man whom you discipline, LORD, and teach out of your law,'),
('PSA', 94, 13, 'PSA.94.13', 'that you may give him rest from the days of adversity, until the pit is dug for the wicked.'),
('PSA', 94, 14, 'PSA.94.14', 'For the LORD won’t reject his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance.'),
('PSA', 94, 15, 'PSA.94.15', 'For judgment will return to righteousness. All the upright in heart shall follow it.'),
('PSA', 94, 16, 'PSA.94.16', 'Who will rise up for me against the wicked? Who will stand up for me against the evildoers?'),
('PSA', 94, 17, 'PSA.94.17', 'Unless the LORD had been my help, my soul would have soon lived in silence.'),
('PSA', 94, 18, 'PSA.94.18', 'When I said, “My foot is slipping!” Your loving kindness, LORD, held me up.'),
('PSA', 94, 19, 'PSA.94.19', 'In the multitude of my thoughts within me, your comforts delight my soul.'),
('PSA', 94, 20, 'PSA.94.20', 'Shall the throne of wickedness have fellowship with you, which brings about mischief by statute?'),
('PSA', 94, 21, 'PSA.94.21', 'They gather themselves together against the soul of the righteous, and condemn the innocent blood.'),
('PSA', 94, 22, 'PSA.94.22', 'But the LORD has been my high tower, my God, the rock of my refuge.'),
('PSA', 94, 23, 'PSA.94.23', 'He has brought on them their own iniquity, and will cut them off in their own wickedness. The LORD, our God, will cut them off.'),
('PSA', 95, 1, 'PSA.95.1', 'Oh come, let’s sing to the LORD. Let’s shout aloud to the rock of our salvation!'),
('PSA', 95, 2, 'PSA.95.2', 'Let’s come before his presence with thanksgiving. Let’s extol him with songs!'),
('PSA', 95, 3, 'PSA.95.3', 'For the LORD is a great God, a great King above all gods.'),
('PSA', 95, 4, 'PSA.95.4', 'In his hand are the deep places of the earth. The heights of the mountains are also his.'),
('PSA', 95, 5, 'PSA.95.5', 'The sea is his, and he made it. His hands formed the dry land.'),
('PSA', 95, 6, 'PSA.95.6', 'Oh come, let’s worship and bow down. Let’s kneel before the LORD, our Maker,'),
('PSA', 95, 7, 'PSA.95.7', 'for he is our God. We are the people of his pasture, and the sheep in his care. Today, oh that you would hear his voice!'),
('PSA', 95, 8, 'PSA.95.8', 'Don’t harden your heart, as at Meribah, as in the day of Massah in the wilderness,'),
('PSA', 95, 9, 'PSA.95.9', 'when your fathers tempted me, tested me, and saw my work.'),
('PSA', 95, 10, 'PSA.95.10', 'Forty long years I was grieved with that generation, and said, “They are a people who err in their heart. They have not known my ways.”'),
('PSA', 95, 11, 'PSA.95.11', 'Therefore I swore in my wrath, “They won’t enter into my rest.”'),
('PSA', 96, 1, 'PSA.96.1', 'Sing to the LORD a new song! Sing to the LORD, all the earth.'),
('PSA', 96, 2, 'PSA.96.2', 'Sing to the LORD! Bless his name! Proclaim his salvation from day to day!'),
('PSA', 96, 3, 'PSA.96.3', 'Declare his glory among the nations, his marvelous works among all the peoples.'),
('PSA', 96, 4, 'PSA.96.4', 'For the LORD is great, and greatly to be praised! He is to be feared above all gods.'),
('PSA', 96, 5, 'PSA.96.5', 'For all the gods of the peoples are idols, but the LORD made the heavens.'),
('PSA', 96, 6, 'PSA.96.6', 'Honor and majesty are before him. Strength and beauty are in his sanctuary.'),
('PSA', 96, 7, 'PSA.96.7', 'Ascribe to the LORD, you families of nations, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.'),
('PSA', 96, 8, 'PSA.96.8', 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his name. Bring an offering, and come into his courts.'),
('PSA', 96, 9, 'PSA.96.9', 'Worship the LORD in holy array. Tremble before him, all the earth.'),
('PSA', 96, 10, 'PSA.96.10', 'Say among the nations, “The LORD reigns.” The world is also established. It can’t be moved. He will judge the peoples with equity.'),
('PSA', 96, 11, 'PSA.96.11', 'Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice. Let the sea roar, and its fullness!'),
('PSA', 96, 12, 'PSA.96.12', 'Let the field and all that is in it exult! Then all the trees of the woods shall sing for joy'),
('PSA', 96, 13, 'PSA.96.13', 'before the LORD; for he comes, for he comes to judge the earth. He will judge the world with righteousness, the peoples with his truth.'),
('PSA', 97, 1, 'PSA.97.1', 'The LORD reigns! Let the earth rejoice! Let the multitude of islands be glad!'),
('PSA', 97, 2, 'PSA.97.2', 'Clouds and darkness are around him. Righteousness and justice are the foundation of his throne.'),
('PSA', 97, 3, 'PSA.97.3', 'A fire goes before him, and burns up his adversaries on every side.'),
('PSA', 97, 4, 'PSA.97.4', 'His lightning lights up the world. The earth sees, and trembles.'),
('PSA', 97, 5, 'PSA.97.5', 'The mountains melt like wax at the presence of the LORD, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth.'),
('PSA', 97, 6, 'PSA.97.6', 'The heavens declare his righteousness. All the peoples have seen his glory.'),
('PSA', 97, 7, 'PSA.97.7', 'Let all them be shamed who serve engraved images, who boast in their idols. Worship him, all you gods!'),
('PSA', 97, 8, 'PSA.97.8', 'Zion heard and was glad. The daughters of Judah rejoiced because of your judgments, LORD.'),
('PSA', 97, 9, 'PSA.97.9', 'For you, LORD, are most high above all the earth. You are exalted far above all gods.'),
('PSA', 97, 10, 'PSA.97.10', 'You who love the LORD, hate evil! He preserves the souls of his saints. He delivers them out of the hand of the wicked.'),
('PSA', 97, 11, 'PSA.97.11', 'Light is sown for the righteous, and gladness for the upright in heart.'),
('PSA', 97, 12, 'PSA.97.12', 'Be glad in the LORD, you righteous people! Give thanks to his holy Name.'),
('PSA', 98, 1, 'PSA.98.1', 'Sing to the LORD a new song, for he has done marvelous things! His right hand and his holy arm have worked salvation for him.'),
('PSA', 98, 2, 'PSA.98.2', 'The LORD has made known his salvation. He has openly shown his righteousness in the sight of the nations.'),
('PSA', 98, 3, 'PSA.98.3', 'He has remembered his loving kindness and his faithfulness toward the house of Israel. All the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.'),
('PSA', 98, 4, 'PSA.98.4', 'Make a joyful noise to the LORD, all the earth! Burst out and sing for joy, yes, sing praises!'),
('PSA', 98, 5, 'PSA.98.5', 'Sing praises to the LORD with the harp, with the harp and the voice of melody.'),
('PSA', 98, 6, 'PSA.98.6', 'With trumpets and sound of the ram’s horn, make a joyful noise before the King, the LORD.'),
('PSA', 98, 7, 'PSA.98.7', 'Let the sea roar with its fullness; the world, and those who dwell therein.'),
('PSA', 98, 8, 'PSA.98.8', 'Let the rivers clap their hands. Let the mountains sing for joy together.'),
('PSA', 98, 9, 'PSA.98.9', 'Let them sing before the LORD, for he comes to judge the earth. He will judge the world with righteousness, and the peoples with equity.'),
('PSA', 99, 1, 'PSA.99.1', 'The LORD reigns! Let the peoples tremble. He sits enthroned among the cherubim. Let the earth be moved.'),
('PSA', 99, 2, 'PSA.99.2', 'The LORD is great in Zion. He is high above all the peoples.'),
('PSA', 99, 3, 'PSA.99.3', 'Let them praise your great and awesome name. He is Holy!'),
('PSA', 99, 4, 'PSA.99.4', 'The King’s strength also loves justice. You establish equity. You execute justice and righteousness in Jacob.'),
('PSA', 99, 5, 'PSA.99.5', 'Exalt the LORD our God. Worship at his footstool. He is Holy!'),
('PSA', 99, 6, 'PSA.99.6', 'Moses and Aaron were among his priests, Samuel was among those who call on his name. They called on the LORD, and he answered them.'),
('PSA', 99, 7, 'PSA.99.7', 'He spoke to them in the pillar of cloud. They kept his testimonies, the statute that he gave them.'),
('PSA', 99, 8, 'PSA.99.8', 'You answered them, LORD our God. You are a God who forgave them, although you took vengeance for their doings.'),
('PSA', 99, 9, 'PSA.99.9', 'Exalt the LORD, our God. Worship at his holy hill, for the LORD, our God, is holy!'),
('PSA', 100, 1, 'PSA.100.1', 'Shout for joy to the LORD, all you lands!'),
('PSA', 100, 2, 'PSA.100.2', 'Serve the LORD with gladness. Come before his presence with singing.'),
('PSA', 100, 3, 'PSA.100.3', 'Know that the LORD, he is God. It is he who has made us, and we are his. We are his people, and the sheep of his pasture.'),
('PSA', 100, 4, 'PSA.100.4', 'Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and into his courts with praise. Give thanks to him, and bless his name.'),
('PSA', 100, 5, 'PSA.100.5', 'For the LORD is good. His loving kindness endures forever, his faithfulness to all generations.'),
('PSA', 101, 1, 'PSA.101.1', 'I will sing of loving kindness and justice. To you, LORD, I will sing praises.'),
('PSA', 101, 2, 'PSA.101.2', 'I will be careful to live a blameless life. When will you come to me? I will walk within my house with a blameless heart.'),
('PSA', 101, 3, 'PSA.101.3', 'I will set no vile thing before my eyes. I hate the deeds of faithless men. They will not cling to me.'),
('PSA', 101, 4, 'PSA.101.4', 'A perverse heart will be far from me. I will have nothing to do with evil.'),
('PSA', 101, 5, 'PSA.101.5', 'I will silence whoever secretly slanders his neighbor. I won’t tolerate one who is arrogant and conceited.'),
('PSA', 101, 6, 'PSA.101.6', 'My eyes will be on the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me. He who walks in a perfect way, he will serve me.'),
('PSA', 101, 7, 'PSA.101.7', 'He who practices deceit won’t dwell within my house. He who speaks falsehood won’t be established before my eyes.'),
('PSA', 101, 8, 'PSA.101.8', 'Morning by morning, I will destroy all the wicked of the land, to cut off all the workers of iniquity from the LORD’s city.'),
('PSA', 102, 1, 'PSA.102.1', 'Hear my prayer, LORD! Let my cry come to you.'),
('PSA', 102, 2, 'PSA.102.2', 'Don’t hide your face from me in the day of my distress. Turn your ear to me. Answer me quickly in the day when I call.'),
('PSA', 102, 3, 'PSA.102.3', 'For my days consume away like smoke. My bones are burned as a torch.'),
('PSA', 102, 4, 'PSA.102.4', 'My heart is blighted like grass, and withered, for I forget to eat my bread.'),
('PSA', 102, 5, 'PSA.102.5', 'By reason of the voice of my groaning, my bones stick to my skin.'),
('PSA', 102, 6, 'PSA.102.6', 'I am like a pelican of the wilderness. I have become as an owl of the waste places.'),
('PSA', 102, 7, 'PSA.102.7', 'I watch, and have become like a sparrow that is alone on the housetop.'),
('PSA', 102, 8, 'PSA.102.8', 'My enemies reproach me all day. Those who are mad at me use my name as a curse.'),
('PSA', 102, 9, 'PSA.102.9', 'For I have eaten ashes like bread, and mixed my drink with tears,'),
('PSA', 102, 10, 'PSA.102.10', 'because of your indignation and your wrath; for you have taken me up and thrown me away.'),
('PSA', 102, 11, 'PSA.102.11', 'My days are like a long shadow. I have withered like grass.'),
('PSA', 102, 12, 'PSA.102.12', 'But you, LORD, will remain forever; your renown endures to all generations.'),
('PSA', 102, 13, 'PSA.102.13', 'You will arise and have mercy on Zion, for it is time to have pity on her. Yes, the set time has come.'),
('PSA', 102, 14, 'PSA.102.14', 'For your servants take pleasure in her stones, and have pity on her dust.'),
('PSA', 102, 15, 'PSA.102.15', 'So the nations will fear the LORD’s name, all the kings of the earth your glory.'),
('PSA', 102, 16, 'PSA.102.16', 'For the LORD has built up Zion. He has appeared in his glory.'),
('PSA', 102, 17, 'PSA.102.17', 'He has responded to the prayer of the destitute, and has not despised their prayer.'),
('PSA', 102, 18, 'PSA.102.18', 'This will be written for the generation to come. A people which will be created will praise the LORD,'),
('PSA', 102, 19, 'PSA.102.19', 'for he has looked down from the height of his sanctuary. From heaven, the LORD saw the earth,'),
('PSA', 102, 20, 'PSA.102.20', 'to hear the groans of the prisoner, to free those who are condemned to death,'),
('PSA', 102, 21, 'PSA.102.21', 'that men may declare the LORD’s name in Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem,'),
('PSA', 102, 22, 'PSA.102.22', 'when the peoples are gathered together, the kingdoms, to serve the LORD.'),
('PSA', 102, 23, 'PSA.102.23', 'He weakened my strength along the course. He shortened my days.'),
('PSA', 102, 24, 'PSA.102.24', 'I said, “My God, don’t take me away in the middle of my days. Your years are throughout all generations.'),
('PSA', 102, 25, 'PSA.102.25', 'Of old, you laid the foundation of the earth. The heavens are the work of your hands.'),
('PSA', 102, 26, 'PSA.102.26', 'They will perish, but you will endure. Yes, all of them will wear out like a garment. You will change them like a cloak, and they will be changed.'),
('PSA', 102, 27, 'PSA.102.27', 'But you are the same. Your years will have no end.'),
('PSA', 102, 28, 'PSA.102.28', 'The children of your servants will continue. Their offspring will be established before you.”'),
('PSA', 103, 1, 'PSA.103.1', 'Praise the LORD, my soul! All that is within me, praise his holy name!'),
('PSA', 103, 2, 'PSA.103.2', 'Praise the LORD, my soul, and don’t forget all his benefits,'),
('PSA', 103, 3, 'PSA.103.3', 'who forgives all your sins, who heals all your diseases,'),
('PSA', 103, 4, 'PSA.103.4', 'who redeems your life from destruction, who crowns you with loving kindness and tender mercies,'),
('PSA', 103, 5, 'PSA.103.5', 'who satisfies your desire with good things, so that your youth is renewed like the eagle’s.'),
('PSA', 103, 6, 'PSA.103.6', 'The LORD executes righteous acts, and justice for all who are oppressed.'),
('PSA', 103, 7, 'PSA.103.7', 'He made known his ways to Moses, his deeds to the children of Israel.'),
('PSA', 103, 8, 'PSA.103.8', 'The LORD is merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness.'),
('PSA', 103, 9, 'PSA.103.9', 'He will not always accuse; neither will he stay angry forever.'),
('PSA', 103, 10, 'PSA.103.10', 'He has not dealt with us according to our sins, nor repaid us for our iniquities.'),
('PSA', 103, 11, 'PSA.103.11', 'For as the heavens are high above the earth, so great is his loving kindness toward those who fear him.'),
('PSA', 103, 12, 'PSA.103.12', 'As far as the east is from the west, so far has he removed our transgressions from us.'),
('PSA', 103, 13, 'PSA.103.13', 'Like a father has compassion on his children, so the LORD has compassion on those who fear him.'),
('PSA', 103, 14, 'PSA.103.14', 'For he knows how we are made. He remembers that we are dust.'),
('PSA', 103, 15, 'PSA.103.15', 'As for man, his days are like grass. As a flower of the field, so he flourishes.'),
('PSA', 103, 16, 'PSA.103.16', 'For the wind passes over it, and it is gone. Its place remembers it no more.'),
('PSA', 103, 17, 'PSA.103.17', 'But the LORD’s loving kindness is from everlasting to everlasting with those who fear him, his righteousness to children’s children,'),
('PSA', 103, 18, 'PSA.103.18', 'to those who keep his covenant, to those who remember to obey his precepts.'),
('PSA', 103, 19, 'PSA.103.19', 'The LORD has established his throne in the heavens. His kingdom rules over all.'),
('PSA', 103, 20, 'PSA.103.20', 'Praise the LORD, you angels of his, who are mighty in strength, who fulfill his word, obeying the voice of his word.'),
('PSA', 103, 21, 'PSA.103.21', 'Praise the LORD, all you armies of his, you servants of his, who do his pleasure.'),
('PSA', 103, 22, 'PSA.103.22', 'Praise the LORD, all you works of his, in all places of his dominion. Praise the LORD, my soul!'),
('PSA', 104, 1, 'PSA.104.1', 'Bless the LORD, my soul. The LORD, my God, you are very great. You are clothed with honor and majesty.'),
('PSA', 104, 2, 'PSA.104.2', 'He covers himself with light as with a garment. He stretches out the heavens like a curtain.'),
('PSA', 104, 3, 'PSA.104.3', 'He lays the beams of his rooms in the waters. He makes the clouds his chariot. He walks on the wings of the wind.'),
('PSA', 104, 4, 'PSA.104.4', 'He makes his messengers winds, and his servants flames of fire.'),
('PSA', 104, 5, 'PSA.104.5', 'He laid the foundations of the earth, that it should not be moved forever.'),
('PSA', 104, 6, 'PSA.104.6', 'You covered it with the deep as with a cloak. The waters stood above the mountains.'),
('PSA', 104, 7, 'PSA.104.7', 'At your rebuke they fled. At the voice of your thunder they hurried away.'),
('PSA', 104, 8, 'PSA.104.8', 'The mountains rose, the valleys sank down, to the place which you had assigned to them.'),
('PSA', 104, 9, 'PSA.104.9', 'You have set a boundary that they may not pass over, that they don’t turn again to cover the earth.'),
('PSA', 104, 10, 'PSA.104.10', 'He sends springs into the valleys. They run among the mountains.'),
('PSA', 104, 11, 'PSA.104.11', 'They give drink to every animal of the field. The wild donkeys quench their thirst.'),
('PSA', 104, 12, 'PSA.104.12', 'The birds of the sky nest by them. They sing among the branches.'),
('PSA', 104, 13, 'PSA.104.13', 'He waters the mountains from his rooms. The earth is filled with the fruit of your works.'),
('PSA', 104, 14, 'PSA.104.14', 'He causes the grass to grow for the livestock, and plants for man to cultivate, that he may produce food out of the earth:'),
('PSA', 104, 15, 'PSA.104.15', 'wine that makes the heart of man glad, oil to make his face to shine, and bread that strengthens man’s heart.'),
('PSA', 104, 16, 'PSA.104.16', 'The LORD’s trees are well watered, the cedars of Lebanon, which he has planted,'),
('PSA', 104, 17, 'PSA.104.17', 'where the birds make their nests. The stork makes its home in the cypress trees.'),
('PSA', 104, 18, 'PSA.104.18', 'The high mountains are for the wild goats. The rocks are a refuge for the rock badgers.'),
('PSA', 104, 19, 'PSA.104.19', 'He appointed the moon for seasons. The sun knows when to set.'),
('PSA', 104, 20, 'PSA.104.20', 'You make darkness, and it is night, in which all the animals of the forest prowl.'),
('PSA', 104, 21, 'PSA.104.21', 'The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their food from God.'),
('PSA', 104, 22, 'PSA.104.22', 'The sun rises, and they steal away, and lie down in their dens.'),
('PSA', 104, 23, 'PSA.104.23', 'Man goes out to his work, to his labor until the evening.'),
('PSA', 104, 24, 'PSA.104.24', 'LORD, how many are your works! In wisdom, you have made them all. The earth is full of your riches.'),
('PSA', 104, 25, 'PSA.104.25', 'There is the sea, great and wide, in which are innumerable living things, both small and large animals.'),
('PSA', 104, 26, 'PSA.104.26', 'There the ships go, and leviathan, whom you formed to play there.'),
('PSA', 104, 27, 'PSA.104.27', 'These all wait for you, that you may give them their food in due season.'),
('PSA', 104, 28, 'PSA.104.28', 'You give to them; they gather. You open your hand; they are satisfied with good.'),
('PSA', 104, 29, 'PSA.104.29', 'You hide your face; they are troubled. You take away their breath; they die and return to the dust.'),
('PSA', 104, 30, 'PSA.104.30', 'You send out your Spirit and they are created. You renew the face of the ground.'),
('PSA', 104, 31, 'PSA.104.31', 'Let the LORD’s glory endure forever. Let the LORD rejoice in his works.'),
('PSA', 104, 32, 'PSA.104.32', 'He looks at the earth, and it trembles. He touches the mountains, and they smoke.'),
('PSA', 104, 33, 'PSA.104.33', 'I will sing to the LORD as long as I live. I will sing praise to my God while I have any being.'),
('PSA', 104, 34, 'PSA.104.34', 'Let my meditation be sweet to him. I will rejoice in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 104, 35, 'PSA.104.35', 'Let sinners be consumed out of the earth. Let the wicked be no more. Bless the LORD, my soul. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 105, 1, 'PSA.105.1', 'Give thanks to the LORD! Call on his name! Make his doings known among the peoples.'),
('PSA', 105, 2, 'PSA.105.2', 'Sing to him, sing praises to him! Tell of all his marvelous works.'),
('PSA', 105, 3, 'PSA.105.3', 'Glory in his holy name. Let the heart of those who seek the LORD rejoice.'),
('PSA', 105, 4, 'PSA.105.4', 'Seek the LORD and his strength. Seek his face forever more.'),
('PSA', 105, 5, 'PSA.105.5', 'Remember his marvelous works that he has done: his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth,'),
('PSA', 105, 6, 'PSA.105.6', 'you offspring of Abraham, his servant, you children of Jacob, his chosen ones.'),
('PSA', 105, 7, 'PSA.105.7', 'He is the LORD, our God. His judgments are in all the earth.'),
('PSA', 105, 8, 'PSA.105.8', 'He has remembered his covenant forever, the word which he commanded to a thousand generations,'),
('PSA', 105, 9, 'PSA.105.9', 'the covenant which he made with Abraham, his oath to Isaac,'),
('PSA', 105, 10, 'PSA.105.10', 'and confirmed it to Jacob for a statute; to Israel for an everlasting covenant,'),
('PSA', 105, 11, 'PSA.105.11', 'saying, “To you I will give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance,”'),
('PSA', 105, 12, 'PSA.105.12', 'when they were but a few men in number, yes, very few, and foreigners in it.'),
('PSA', 105, 13, 'PSA.105.13', 'They went about from nation to nation, from one kingdom to another people.'),
('PSA', 105, 14, 'PSA.105.14', 'He allowed no one to do them wrong. Yes, he reproved kings for their sakes,'),
('PSA', 105, 15, 'PSA.105.15', '“Don’t touch my anointed ones! Do my prophets no harm!”'),
('PSA', 105, 16, 'PSA.105.16', 'He called for a famine on the land. He destroyed the food supplies.'),
('PSA', 105, 17, 'PSA.105.17', 'He sent a man before them. Joseph was sold for a slave.'),
('PSA', 105, 18, 'PSA.105.18', 'They bruised his feet with shackles. His neck was locked in irons,'),
('PSA', 105, 19, 'PSA.105.19', 'until the time that his word happened, and the LORD’s word proved him true.'),
('PSA', 105, 20, 'PSA.105.20', 'The king sent and freed him, even the ruler of peoples, and let him go free.'),
('PSA', 105, 21, 'PSA.105.21', 'He made him lord of his house, and ruler of all of his possessions,'),
('PSA', 105, 22, 'PSA.105.22', 'to discipline his princes at his pleasure, and to teach his elders wisdom.'),
('PSA', 105, 23, 'PSA.105.23', 'Israel also came into Egypt. Jacob lived in the land of Ham.'),
('PSA', 105, 24, 'PSA.105.24', 'He increased his people greatly, and made them stronger than their adversaries.'),
('PSA', 105, 25, 'PSA.105.25', 'He turned their heart to hate his people, to conspire against his servants.'),
('PSA', 105, 26, 'PSA.105.26', 'He sent Moses, his servant, and Aaron, whom he had chosen.'),
('PSA', 105, 27, 'PSA.105.27', 'They performed miracles among them, and wonders in the land of Ham.'),
('PSA', 105, 28, 'PSA.105.28', 'He sent darkness, and made it dark. They didn’t rebel against his words.'),
('PSA', 105, 29, 'PSA.105.29', 'He turned their waters into blood, and killed their fish.'),
('PSA', 105, 30, 'PSA.105.30', 'Their land swarmed with frogs, even in the rooms of their kings.'),
('PSA', 105, 31, 'PSA.105.31', 'He spoke, and swarms of flies came, and lice in all their borders.'),
('PSA', 105, 32, 'PSA.105.32', 'He gave them hail for rain, with lightning in their land.'),
('PSA', 105, 33, 'PSA.105.33', 'He struck their vines and also their fig trees, and shattered the trees of their country.'),
('PSA', 105, 34, 'PSA.105.34', 'He spoke, and the locusts came with the grasshoppers, without number.'),
('PSA', 105, 35, 'PSA.105.35', 'They ate up every plant in their land, and ate up the fruit of their ground.'),
('PSA', 105, 36, 'PSA.105.36', 'He struck also all the firstborn in their land, the first fruits of all their manhood.'),
('PSA', 105, 37, 'PSA.105.37', 'He brought them out with silver and gold. There was not one feeble person among his tribes.'),
('PSA', 105, 38, 'PSA.105.38', 'Egypt was glad when they departed, for the fear of them had fallen on them.'),
('PSA', 105, 39, 'PSA.105.39', 'He spread a cloud for a covering, fire to give light in the night.'),
('PSA', 105, 40, 'PSA.105.40', 'They asked, and he brought quails, and satisfied them with the bread of the sky.'),
('PSA', 105, 41, 'PSA.105.41', 'He opened the rock, and waters gushed out. They ran as a river in the dry places.'),
('PSA', 105, 42, 'PSA.105.42', 'For he remembered his holy word, and Abraham, his servant.'),
('PSA', 105, 43, 'PSA.105.43', 'He brought his people out with joy, his chosen with singing.'),
('PSA', 105, 44, 'PSA.105.44', 'He gave them the lands of the nations. They took the labor of the peoples in possession,'),
('PSA', 105, 45, 'PSA.105.45', 'that they might keep his statutes, and observe his laws. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 106, 1, 'PSA.106.1', 'Praise the LORD! Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 106, 2, 'PSA.106.2', 'Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD, or fully declare all his praise?'),
('PSA', 106, 3, 'PSA.106.3', 'Blessed are those who keep justice. Blessed is one who does what is right at all times.'),
('PSA', 106, 4, 'PSA.106.4', 'Remember me, LORD, with the favor that you show to your people. Visit me with your salvation,'),
('PSA', 106, 5, 'PSA.106.5', 'that I may see the prosperity of your chosen, that I may rejoice in the gladness of your nation, that I may glory with your inheritance.'),
('PSA', 106, 6, 'PSA.106.6', 'We have sinned with our fathers. We have committed iniquity. We have done wickedly.'),
('PSA', 106, 7, 'PSA.106.7', 'Our fathers didn’t understand your wonders in Egypt. They didn’t remember the multitude of your loving kindnesses, but were rebellious at the sea, even at the Red Sea.'),
('PSA', 106, 8, 'PSA.106.8', 'Nevertheless he saved them for his name’s sake, that he might make his mighty power known.'),
('PSA', 106, 9, 'PSA.106.9', 'He rebuked the Red Sea also, and it was dried up; so he led them through the depths, as through a desert.'),
('PSA', 106, 10, 'PSA.106.10', 'He saved them from the hand of him who hated them, and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.'),
('PSA', 106, 11, 'PSA.106.11', 'The waters covered their adversaries. There was not one of them left.'),
('PSA', 106, 12, 'PSA.106.12', 'Then they believed his words. They sang his praise.'),
('PSA', 106, 13, 'PSA.106.13', 'They soon forgot his works. They didn’t wait for his counsel,'),
('PSA', 106, 14, 'PSA.106.14', 'but gave in to craving in the desert, and tested God in the wasteland.'),
('PSA', 106, 15, 'PSA.106.15', 'He gave them their request, but sent leanness into their soul.'),
('PSA', 106, 16, 'PSA.106.16', 'They envied Moses also in the camp, and Aaron, the LORD’s saint.'),
('PSA', 106, 17, 'PSA.106.17', 'The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, and covered the company of Abiram.'),
('PSA', 106, 18, 'PSA.106.18', 'A fire was kindled in their company. The flame burned up the wicked.'),
('PSA', 106, 19, 'PSA.106.19', 'They made a calf in Horeb, and worshiped a molten image.'),
('PSA', 106, 20, 'PSA.106.20', 'Thus they exchanged their glory for an image of a bull that eats grass.'),
('PSA', 106, 21, 'PSA.106.21', 'They forgot God, their Savior, who had done great things in Egypt,'),
('PSA', 106, 22, 'PSA.106.22', 'wondrous works in the land of Ham, and awesome things by the Red Sea.'),
('PSA', 106, 23, 'PSA.106.23', 'Therefore he said that he would destroy them, had Moses, his chosen, not stood before him in the breach, to turn away his wrath, so that he wouldn’t destroy them.'),
('PSA', 106, 24, 'PSA.106.24', 'Yes, they despised the pleasant land. They didn’t believe his word,'),
('PSA', 106, 25, 'PSA.106.25', 'but murmured in their tents, and didn’t listen to the LORD’s voice.'),
('PSA', 106, 26, 'PSA.106.26', 'Therefore he swore to them that he would overthrow them in the wilderness,'),
('PSA', 106, 27, 'PSA.106.27', 'that he would overthrow their offspring among the nations, and scatter them in the lands.'),
('PSA', 106, 28, 'PSA.106.28', 'They joined themselves also to Baal Peor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead.'),
('PSA', 106, 29, 'PSA.106.29', 'Thus they provoked him to anger with their deeds. The plague broke in on them.'),
('PSA', 106, 30, 'PSA.106.30', 'Then Phinehas stood up and executed judgment, so the plague was stopped.'),
('PSA', 106, 31, 'PSA.106.31', 'That was credited to him for righteousness, for all generations to come.'),
('PSA', 106, 32, 'PSA.106.32', 'They angered him also at the waters of Meribah, so that Moses was troubled for their sakes;'),
('PSA', 106, 33, 'PSA.106.33', 'because they were rebellious against his spirit, he spoke rashly with his lips.'),
('PSA', 106, 34, 'PSA.106.34', 'They didn’t destroy the peoples, as the LORD commanded them,'),
('PSA', 106, 35, 'PSA.106.35', 'but mixed themselves with the nations, and learned their works.'),
('PSA', 106, 36, 'PSA.106.36', 'They served their idols, which became a snare to them.'),
('PSA', 106, 37, 'PSA.106.37', 'Yes, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters to demons.'),
('PSA', 106, 38, 'PSA.106.38', 'They shed innocent blood, even the blood of their sons and of their daughters, whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan. The land was polluted with blood.'),
('PSA', 106, 39, 'PSA.106.39', 'Thus they were defiled with their works, and prostituted themselves in their deeds.'),
('PSA', 106, 40, 'PSA.106.40', 'Therefore the LORD burned with anger against his people. He abhorred his inheritance.'),
('PSA', 106, 41, 'PSA.106.41', 'He gave them into the hand of the nations. Those who hated them ruled over them.'),
('PSA', 106, 42, 'PSA.106.42', 'Their enemies also oppressed them. They were brought into subjection under their hand.'),
('PSA', 106, 43, 'PSA.106.43', 'He rescued them many times, but they were rebellious in their counsel, and were brought low in their iniquity.'),
('PSA', 106, 44, 'PSA.106.44', 'Nevertheless he regarded their distress, when he heard their cry.'),
('PSA', 106, 45, 'PSA.106.45', 'He remembered for them his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his loving kindnesses.'),
('PSA', 106, 46, 'PSA.106.46', 'He made them also to be pitied by all those who carried them captive.'),
('PSA', 106, 47, 'PSA.106.47', 'Save us, LORD, our God, gather us from among the nations, to give thanks to your holy name, to triumph in your praise!'),
('PSA', 106, 48, 'PSA.106.48', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting even to everlasting! Let all the people say, “Amen.” Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 107, 1, 'PSA.107.1', 'Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 107, 2, 'PSA.107.2', 'Let the redeemed by the LORD say so, whom he has redeemed from the hand of the adversary,'),
('PSA', 107, 3, 'PSA.107.3', 'and gathered out of the lands, from the east and from the west, from the north and from the south.'),
('PSA', 107, 4, 'PSA.107.4', 'They wandered in the wilderness in a desert way. They found no city to live in.'),
('PSA', 107, 5, 'PSA.107.5', 'Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.'),
('PSA', 107, 6, 'PSA.107.6', 'Then they cried to the LORD in their trouble, and he delivered them out of their distresses.'),
('PSA', 107, 7, 'PSA.107.7', 'He led them also by a straight way, that they might go to a city to live in.'),
('PSA', 107, 8, 'PSA.107.8', 'Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness, for his wonderful deeds to the children of men!'),
('PSA', 107, 9, 'PSA.107.9', 'For he satisfies the longing soul. He fills the hungry soul with good.'),
('PSA', 107, 10, 'PSA.107.10', 'Some sat in darkness and in the shadow of death, being bound in affliction and iron,'),
('PSA', 107, 11, 'PSA.107.11', 'because they rebelled against the words of God, and condemned the counsel of the Most High.'),
('PSA', 107, 12, 'PSA.107.12', 'Therefore he brought down their heart with labor. They fell down, and there was no one to help.'),
('PSA', 107, 13, 'PSA.107.13', 'Then they cried to the LORD in their trouble, and he saved them out of their distresses.'),
('PSA', 107, 14, 'PSA.107.14', 'He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and broke away their chains.'),
('PSA', 107, 15, 'PSA.107.15', 'Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness, for his wonderful deeds to the children of men!'),
('PSA', 107, 16, 'PSA.107.16', 'For he has broken the gates of bronze, and cut through bars of iron.'),
('PSA', 107, 17, 'PSA.107.17', 'Fools are afflicted because of their disobedience, and because of their iniquities.'),
('PSA', 107, 18, 'PSA.107.18', 'Their soul abhors all kinds of food. They draw near to the gates of death.'),
('PSA', 107, 19, 'PSA.107.19', 'Then they cry to the LORD in their trouble, and he saves them out of their distresses.'),
('PSA', 107, 20, 'PSA.107.20', 'He sends his word, and heals them, and delivers them from their graves.'),
('PSA', 107, 21, 'PSA.107.21', 'Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness, for his wonderful deeds to the children of men!'),
('PSA', 107, 22, 'PSA.107.22', 'Let them offer the sacrifices of thanksgiving, and declare his deeds with singing.'),
('PSA', 107, 23, 'PSA.107.23', 'Those who go down to the sea in ships, who do business in great waters,'),
('PSA', 107, 24, 'PSA.107.24', 'these see the LORD’s deeds, and his wonders in the deep.'),
('PSA', 107, 25, 'PSA.107.25', 'For he commands, and raises the stormy wind, which lifts up its waves.'),
('PSA', 107, 26, 'PSA.107.26', 'They mount up to the sky; they go down again to the depths. Their soul melts away because of trouble.'),
('PSA', 107, 27, 'PSA.107.27', 'They reel back and forth, and stagger like a drunken man, and are at their wits’ end.'),
('PSA', 107, 28, 'PSA.107.28', 'Then they cry to the LORD in their trouble, and he brings them out of their distress.'),
('PSA', 107, 29, 'PSA.107.29', 'He makes the storm a calm, so that its waves are still.'),
('PSA', 107, 30, 'PSA.107.30', 'Then they are glad because it is calm, so he brings them to their desired haven.'),
('PSA', 107, 31, 'PSA.107.31', 'Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness, for his wonderful deeds for the children of men!'),
('PSA', 107, 32, 'PSA.107.32', 'Let them exalt him also in the assembly of the people, and praise him in the seat of the elders.'),
('PSA', 107, 33, 'PSA.107.33', 'He turns rivers into a desert, water springs into a thirsty ground,'),
('PSA', 107, 34, 'PSA.107.34', 'and a fruitful land into a salt waste, for the wickedness of those who dwell in it.'),
('PSA', 107, 35, 'PSA.107.35', 'He turns a desert into a pool of water, and a dry land into water springs.'),
('PSA', 107, 36, 'PSA.107.36', 'There he makes the hungry live, that they may prepare a city to live in,'),
('PSA', 107, 37, 'PSA.107.37', 'sow fields, plant vineyards, and reap the fruits of increase.'),
('PSA', 107, 38, 'PSA.107.38', 'He blesses them also, so that they are multiplied greatly. He doesn’t allow their livestock to decrease.'),
('PSA', 107, 39, 'PSA.107.39', 'Again, they are diminished and bowed down through oppression, trouble, and sorrow.'),
('PSA', 107, 40, 'PSA.107.40', 'He pours contempt on princes, and causes them to wander in a trackless waste.'),
('PSA', 107, 41, 'PSA.107.41', 'Yet he lifts the needy out of their affliction, and increases their families like a flock.'),
('PSA', 107, 42, 'PSA.107.42', 'The upright will see it, and be glad. All the wicked will shut their mouths.'),
('PSA', 107, 43, 'PSA.107.43', 'Whoever is wise will pay attention to these things. They will consider the loving kindnesses of the LORD.'),
('PSA', 108, 1, 'PSA.108.1', 'My heart is steadfast, God. I will sing and I will make music with my soul.'),
('PSA', 108, 2, 'PSA.108.2', 'Wake up, harp and lyre! I will wake up the dawn.'),
('PSA', 108, 3, 'PSA.108.3', 'I will give thanks to you, LORD, among the nations. I will sing praises to you among the peoples.'),
('PSA', 108, 4, 'PSA.108.4', 'For your loving kindness is great above the heavens. Your faithfulness reaches to the skies.'),
('PSA', 108, 5, 'PSA.108.5', 'Be exalted, God, above the heavens! Let your glory be over all the earth.'),
('PSA', 108, 6, 'PSA.108.6', 'That your beloved may be delivered, save with your right hand, and answer us.'),
('PSA', 108, 7, 'PSA.108.7', 'God has spoken from his sanctuary: “In triumph, I will divide Shechem, and measure out the valley of Succoth.'),
('PSA', 108, 8, 'PSA.108.8', 'Gilead is mine. Manasseh is mine. Ephraim also is my helmet. Judah is my scepter.'),
('PSA', 108, 9, 'PSA.108.9', 'Moab is my wash pot. I will toss my sandal on Edom. I will shout over Philistia.”'),
('PSA', 108, 10, 'PSA.108.10', 'Who will bring me into the fortified city? Who will lead me to Edom?'),
('PSA', 108, 11, 'PSA.108.11', 'Haven’t you rejected us, God? You don’t go out, God, with our armies.'),
('PSA', 108, 12, 'PSA.108.12', 'Give us help against the enemy, for the help of man is vain.'),
('PSA', 108, 13, 'PSA.108.13', 'Through God, we will do valiantly, for it is he who will tread down our enemies.'),
('PSA', 109, 1, 'PSA.109.1', 'God of my praise, don’t remain silent,'),
('PSA', 109, 2, 'PSA.109.2', 'for they have opened the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of deceit against me. They have spoken to me with a lying tongue.'),
('PSA', 109, 3, 'PSA.109.3', 'They have also surrounded me with words of hatred, and fought against me without a cause.'),
('PSA', 109, 4, 'PSA.109.4', 'In return for my love, they are my adversaries; but I am in prayer.'),
('PSA', 109, 5, 'PSA.109.5', 'They have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.'),
('PSA', 109, 6, 'PSA.109.6', 'Set a wicked man over him. Let an adversary stand at his right hand.'),
('PSA', 109, 7, 'PSA.109.7', 'When he is judged, let him come out guilty. Let his prayer be turned into sin.'),
('PSA', 109, 8, 'PSA.109.8', 'Let his days be few. Let another take his office.'),
('PSA', 109, 9, 'PSA.109.9', 'Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.'),
('PSA', 109, 10, 'PSA.109.10', 'Let his children be wandering beggars. Let them be sought from their ruins.'),
('PSA', 109, 11, 'PSA.109.11', 'Let the creditor seize all that he has. Let strangers plunder the fruit of his labor.'),
('PSA', 109, 12, 'PSA.109.12', 'Let there be no one to extend kindness to him, neither let there be anyone to have pity on his fatherless children.'),
('PSA', 109, 13, 'PSA.109.13', 'Let his posterity be cut off. In the generation following let their name be blotted out.'),
('PSA', 109, 14, 'PSA.109.14', 'Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered by the LORD. Don’t let the sin of his mother be blotted out.'),
('PSA', 109, 15, 'PSA.109.15', 'Let them be before the LORD continually, that he may cut off their memory from the earth;'),
('PSA', 109, 16, 'PSA.109.16', 'because he didn’t remember to show kindness, but persecuted the poor and needy man, the broken in heart, to kill them.'),
('PSA', 109, 17, 'PSA.109.17', 'Yes, he loved cursing, and it came to him. He didn’t delight in blessing, and it was far from him.'),
('PSA', 109, 18, 'PSA.109.18', 'He clothed himself also with cursing as with his garment. It came into his inward parts like water, like oil into his bones.'),
('PSA', 109, 19, 'PSA.109.19', 'Let it be to him as the clothing with which he covers himself, for the belt that is always around him.'),
('PSA', 109, 20, 'PSA.109.20', 'This is the reward of my adversaries from the LORD, of those who speak evil against my soul.'),
('PSA', 109, 21, 'PSA.109.21', 'But deal with me, GOD the Lord, for your name’s sake, because your loving kindness is good, deliver me;'),
('PSA', 109, 22, 'PSA.109.22', 'for I am poor and needy. My heart is wounded within me.'),
('PSA', 109, 23, 'PSA.109.23', 'I fade away like an evening shadow. I am shaken off like a locust.'),
('PSA', 109, 24, 'PSA.109.24', 'My knees are weak through fasting. My body is thin and lacks fat.'),
('PSA', 109, 25, 'PSA.109.25', 'I have also become a reproach to them. When they see me, they shake their head.'),
('PSA', 109, 26, 'PSA.109.26', 'Help me, LORD, my God. Save me according to your loving kindness;'),
('PSA', 109, 27, 'PSA.109.27', 'that they may know that this is your hand; that you, LORD, have done it.'),
('PSA', 109, 28, 'PSA.109.28', 'They may curse, but you bless. When they arise, they will be shamed, but your servant shall rejoice.'),
('PSA', 109, 29, 'PSA.109.29', 'Let my adversaries be clothed with dishonor. Let them cover themselves with their own shame as with a robe.'),
('PSA', 109, 30, 'PSA.109.30', 'I will give great thanks to the LORD with my mouth. Yes, I will praise him among the multitude.'),
('PSA', 109, 31, 'PSA.109.31', 'For he will stand at the right hand of the needy, to save him from those who judge his soul.'),
('PSA', 110, 1, 'PSA.110.1', 'The LORD says to my Lord, “Sit at my right hand, until I make your enemies your footstool for your feet.”'),
('PSA', 110, 2, 'PSA.110.2', 'The LORD will send out the rod of your strength out of Zion. Rule among your enemies.'),
('PSA', 110, 3, 'PSA.110.3', 'Your people offer themselves willingly in the day of your power, in holy array. Out of the womb of the morning, you have the dew of your youth.'),
('PSA', 110, 4, 'PSA.110.4', 'The LORD has sworn, and will not change his mind: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”'),
('PSA', 110, 5, 'PSA.110.5', 'The Lord is at your right hand. He will crush kings in the day of his wrath.'),
('PSA', 110, 6, 'PSA.110.6', 'He will judge among the nations. He will heap up dead bodies. He will crush the ruler of the whole earth.'),
('PSA', 110, 7, 'PSA.110.7', 'He will drink of the brook on the way; therefore he will lift up his head.'),
('PSA', 111, 1, 'PSA.111.1', 'Praise the LORD! I will give thanks to the LORD with my whole heart, in the council of the upright, and in the congregation.'),
('PSA', 111, 2, 'PSA.111.2', 'The LORD’s works are great, pondered by all those who delight in them.'),
('PSA', 111, 3, 'PSA.111.3', 'His work is honor and majesty. His righteousness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 111, 4, 'PSA.111.4', 'He has caused his wonderful works to be remembered. The LORD is gracious and merciful.'),
('PSA', 111, 5, 'PSA.111.5', 'He has given food to those who fear him. He always remembers his covenant.'),
('PSA', 111, 6, 'PSA.111.6', 'He has shown his people the power of his works, in giving them the heritage of the nations.'),
('PSA', 111, 7, 'PSA.111.7', 'The works of his hands are truth and justice. All his precepts are sure.'),
('PSA', 111, 8, 'PSA.111.8', 'They are established forever and ever. They are done in truth and uprightness.'),
('PSA', 111, 9, 'PSA.111.9', 'He has sent redemption to his people. He has ordained his covenant forever. His name is holy and awesome!'),
('PSA', 111, 10, 'PSA.111.10', 'The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom. All those who do his work have a good understanding. His praise endures forever!'),
('PSA', 112, 1, 'PSA.112.1', 'Praise the LORD! Blessed is the man who fears the LORD, who delights greatly in his commandments.'),
('PSA', 112, 2, 'PSA.112.2', 'His offspring will be mighty in the land. The generation of the upright will be blessed.'),
('PSA', 112, 3, 'PSA.112.3', 'Wealth and riches are in his house. His righteousness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 112, 4, 'PSA.112.4', 'Light dawns in the darkness for the upright, gracious, merciful, and righteous.'),
('PSA', 112, 5, 'PSA.112.5', 'It is well with the man who deals graciously and lends. He will maintain his cause in judgment.'),
('PSA', 112, 6, 'PSA.112.6', 'For he will never be shaken. The righteous will be remembered forever.'),
('PSA', 112, 7, 'PSA.112.7', 'He will not be afraid of evil news. His heart is steadfast, trusting in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 112, 8, 'PSA.112.8', 'His heart is established. He will not be afraid in the end when he sees his adversaries.'),
('PSA', 112, 9, 'PSA.112.9', 'He has dispersed, he has given to the poor. His righteousness endures forever. His horn will be exalted with honor.'),
('PSA', 112, 10, 'PSA.112.10', 'The wicked will see it, and be grieved. He shall gnash with his teeth, and melt away. The desire of the wicked will perish.'),
('PSA', 113, 1, 'PSA.113.1', 'Praise the LORD! Praise, you servants of the LORD, praise the LORD’s name.'),
('PSA', 113, 2, 'PSA.113.2', 'Blessed be the LORD’s name, from this time forward and forever more.'),
('PSA', 113, 3, 'PSA.113.3', 'From the rising of the sun to its going down, the LORD’s name is to be praised.'),
('PSA', 113, 4, 'PSA.113.4', 'The LORD is high above all nations, his glory above the heavens.'),
('PSA', 113, 5, 'PSA.113.5', 'Who is like the LORD, our God, who has his seat on high,'),
('PSA', 113, 6, 'PSA.113.6', 'who stoops down to see in heaven and on the earth?'),
('PSA', 113, 7, 'PSA.113.7', 'He raises up the poor out of the dust, and lifts up the needy from the ash heap,'),
('PSA', 113, 8, 'PSA.113.8', 'that he may set him with princes, even with the princes of his people.'),
('PSA', 113, 9, 'PSA.113.9', 'He settles the barren woman in her home as a joyful mother of children. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 114, 1, 'PSA.114.1', 'When Israel went out of Egypt, the house of Jacob from a people of foreign language,'),
('PSA', 114, 2, 'PSA.114.2', 'Judah became his sanctuary, Israel his dominion.'),
('PSA', 114, 3, 'PSA.114.3', 'The sea saw it, and fled. The Jordan was driven back.'),
('PSA', 114, 4, 'PSA.114.4', 'The mountains skipped like rams, the little hills like lambs.'),
('PSA', 114, 5, 'PSA.114.5', 'What was it, you sea, that you fled? You Jordan, that you turned back?'),
('PSA', 114, 6, 'PSA.114.6', 'You mountains, that you skipped like rams? You little hills, like lambs?'),
('PSA', 114, 7, 'PSA.114.7', 'Tremble, you earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob,'),
('PSA', 114, 8, 'PSA.114.8', 'who turned the rock into a pool of water, the flint into a spring of waters.'),
('PSA', 115, 1, 'PSA.115.1', 'Not to us, LORD, not to us, but to your name give glory, for your loving kindness, and for your truth’s sake.'),
('PSA', 115, 2, 'PSA.115.2', 'Why should the nations say, “Where is their God, now?”'),
('PSA', 115, 3, 'PSA.115.3', 'But our God is in the heavens. He does whatever he pleases.'),
('PSA', 115, 4, 'PSA.115.4', 'Their idols are silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.'),
('PSA', 115, 5, 'PSA.115.5', 'They have mouths, but they don’t speak. They have eyes, but they don’t see.'),
('PSA', 115, 6, 'PSA.115.6', 'They have ears, but they don’t hear. They have noses, but they don’t smell.'),
('PSA', 115, 7, 'PSA.115.7', 'They have hands, but they don’t feel. They have feet, but they don’t walk, neither do they speak through their throat.'),
('PSA', 115, 8, 'PSA.115.8', 'Those who make them will be like them; yes, everyone who trusts in them.'),
('PSA', 115, 9, 'PSA.115.9', 'Israel, trust in the LORD! He is their help and their shield.'),
('PSA', 115, 10, 'PSA.115.10', 'House of Aaron, trust in the LORD! He is their help and their shield.'),
('PSA', 115, 11, 'PSA.115.11', 'You who fear the LORD, trust in the LORD! He is their help and their shield.'),
('PSA', 115, 12, 'PSA.115.12', 'The LORD remembers us. He will bless us. He will bless the house of Israel. He will bless the house of Aaron.'),
('PSA', 115, 13, 'PSA.115.13', 'He will bless those who fear the LORD, both small and great.'),
('PSA', 115, 14, 'PSA.115.14', 'May the LORD increase you more and more, you and your children.'),
('PSA', 115, 15, 'PSA.115.15', 'Blessed are you by the LORD, who made heaven and earth.'),
('PSA', 115, 16, 'PSA.115.16', 'The heavens are the LORD’s heavens, but he has given the earth to the children of men.'),
('PSA', 115, 17, 'PSA.115.17', 'The dead don’t praise the LORD, nor any who go down into silence,'),
('PSA', 115, 18, 'PSA.115.18', 'but we will bless the LORD, from this time forward and forever more. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 116, 1, 'PSA.116.1', 'I love the LORD, because he listens to my voice, and my cries for mercy.'),
('PSA', 116, 2, 'PSA.116.2', 'Because he has turned his ear to me, therefore I will call on him as long as I live.'),
('PSA', 116, 3, 'PSA.116.3', 'The cords of death surrounded me, the pains of Sheol got a hold of me. I found trouble and sorrow.'),
('PSA', 116, 4, 'PSA.116.4', 'Then I called on the LORD’s name: “LORD, I beg you, deliver my soul.”'),
('PSA', 116, 5, 'PSA.116.5', 'The LORD is gracious and righteous. Yes, our God is merciful.'),
('PSA', 116, 6, 'PSA.116.6', 'The LORD preserves the simple. I was brought low, and he saved me.'),
('PSA', 116, 7, 'PSA.116.7', 'Return to your rest, my soul, for the LORD has dealt bountifully with you.'),
('PSA', 116, 8, 'PSA.116.8', 'For you have delivered my soul from death, my eyes from tears, and my feet from falling.'),
('PSA', 116, 9, 'PSA.116.9', 'I will walk before the LORD in the land of the living.'),
('PSA', 116, 10, 'PSA.116.10', 'I believed, therefore I said, “I was greatly afflicted.”'),
('PSA', 116, 11, 'PSA.116.11', 'I said in my haste, “All people are liars.”'),
('PSA', 116, 12, 'PSA.116.12', 'What will I give to the LORD for all his benefits toward me?'),
('PSA', 116, 13, 'PSA.116.13', 'I will take the cup of salvation, and call on the LORD’s name.'),
('PSA', 116, 14, 'PSA.116.14', 'I will pay my vows to the LORD, yes, in the presence of all his people.'),
('PSA', 116, 15, 'PSA.116.15', 'Precious in the LORD’s sight is the death of his saints.'),
('PSA', 116, 16, 'PSA.116.16', 'LORD, truly I am your servant. I am your servant, the son of your servant girl. You have freed me from my chains.'),
('PSA', 116, 17, 'PSA.116.17', 'I will offer to you the sacrifice of thanksgiving, and will call on the LORD’s name.'),
('PSA', 116, 18, 'PSA.116.18', 'I will pay my vows to the LORD, yes, in the presence of all his people,'),
('PSA', 116, 19, 'PSA.116.19', 'in the courts of the LORD’s house, in the middle of you, Jerusalem. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 117, 1, 'PSA.117.1', 'Praise the LORD, all you nations! Extol him, all you peoples!'),
('PSA', 117, 2, 'PSA.117.2', 'For his loving kindness is great toward us. The LORD’s faithfulness endures forever. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 118, 1, 'PSA.118.1', 'Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 118, 2, 'PSA.118.2', 'Let Israel now say that his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 118, 3, 'PSA.118.3', 'Let the house of Aaron now say that his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 118, 4, 'PSA.118.4', 'Now let those who fear the LORD say that his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 118, 5, 'PSA.118.5', 'Out of my distress, I called on the LORD. The LORD answered me with freedom.'),
('PSA', 118, 6, 'PSA.118.6', 'The LORD is on my side. I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?'),
('PSA', 118, 7, 'PSA.118.7', 'The LORD is on my side among those who help me. Therefore I will look in triumph at those who hate me.'),
('PSA', 118, 8, 'PSA.118.8', 'It is better to take refuge in the LORD, than to put confidence in man.'),
('PSA', 118, 9, 'PSA.118.9', 'It is better to take refuge in the LORD, than to put confidence in princes.'),
('PSA', 118, 10, 'PSA.118.10', 'All the nations surrounded me, but in the LORD’s name I cut them off.'),
('PSA', 118, 11, 'PSA.118.11', 'They surrounded me, yes, they surrounded me. In the LORD’s name I indeed cut them off.'),
('PSA', 118, 12, 'PSA.118.12', 'They surrounded me like bees. They are quenched like the burning thorns. In the LORD’s name I cut them off.'),
('PSA', 118, 13, 'PSA.118.13', 'You pushed me back hard, to make me fall, but the LORD helped me.'),
('PSA', 118, 14, 'PSA.118.14', 'The LORD is my strength and song. He has become my salvation.'),
('PSA', 118, 15, 'PSA.118.15', 'The voice of rejoicing and salvation is in the tents of the righteous. “The right hand of the LORD does valiantly.'),
('PSA', 118, 16, 'PSA.118.16', 'The right hand of the LORD is exalted! The right hand of the LORD does valiantly!”'),
('PSA', 118, 17, 'PSA.118.17', 'I will not die, but live, and declare the LORD’s works.'),
('PSA', 118, 18, 'PSA.118.18', 'The LORD has punished me severely, but he has not given me over to death.'),
('PSA', 118, 19, 'PSA.118.19', 'Open to me the gates of righteousness. I will enter into them. I will give thanks to the LORD.'),
('PSA', 118, 20, 'PSA.118.20', 'This is the gate of the LORD; the righteous will enter into it.'),
('PSA', 118, 21, 'PSA.118.21', 'I will give thanks to you, for you have answered me, and have become my salvation.'),
('PSA', 118, 22, 'PSA.118.22', 'The stone which the builders rejected has become the cornerstone.'),
('PSA', 118, 23, 'PSA.118.23', 'This is the LORD’s doing. It is marvelous in our eyes.'),
('PSA', 118, 24, 'PSA.118.24', 'This is the day that the LORD has made. We will rejoice and be glad in it!'),
('PSA', 118, 25, 'PSA.118.25', 'Save us now, we beg you, LORD! LORD, we beg you, send prosperity now.'),
('PSA', 118, 26, 'PSA.118.26', 'Blessed is he who comes in the LORD’s name! We have blessed you out of the LORD’s house.'),
('PSA', 118, 27, 'PSA.118.27', 'The LORD is God, and he has given us light. Bind the sacrifice with cords, even to the horns of the altar.'),
('PSA', 118, 28, 'PSA.118.28', 'You are my God, and I will give thanks to you. You are my God, I will exalt you.'),
('PSA', 118, 29, 'PSA.118.29', 'Oh give thanks to the LORD, for he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 119, 1, 'PSA.119.1', 'Blessed are those whose ways are blameless, who walk according to the LORD’s law.'),
('PSA', 119, 2, 'PSA.119.2', 'Blessed are those who keep his statutes, who seek him with their whole heart.'),
('PSA', 119, 3, 'PSA.119.3', 'Yes, they do nothing wrong. They walk in his ways.'),
('PSA', 119, 4, 'PSA.119.4', 'You have commanded your precepts, that we should fully obey them.'),
('PSA', 119, 5, 'PSA.119.5', 'Oh that my ways were steadfast to obey your statutes!'),
('PSA', 119, 6, 'PSA.119.6', 'Then I wouldn’t be disappointed, when I consider all of your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 7, 'PSA.119.7', 'I will give thanks to you with uprightness of heart, when I learn your righteous judgments.'),
('PSA', 119, 8, 'PSA.119.8', 'I will observe your statutes. Don’t utterly forsake me.'),
('PSA', 119, 9, 'PSA.119.9', 'How can a young man keep his way pure? By living according to your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 10, 'PSA.119.10', 'With my whole heart I have sought you. Don’t let me wander from your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 11, 'PSA.119.11', 'I have hidden your word in my heart, that I might not sin against you.'),
('PSA', 119, 12, 'PSA.119.12', 'Blessed are you, LORD. Teach me your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 13, 'PSA.119.13', 'With my lips, I have declared all the ordinances of your mouth.'),
('PSA', 119, 14, 'PSA.119.14', 'I have rejoiced in the way of your testimonies, as much as in all riches.'),
('PSA', 119, 15, 'PSA.119.15', 'I will meditate on your precepts, and consider your ways.'),
('PSA', 119, 16, 'PSA.119.16', 'I will delight myself in your statutes. I will not forget your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 17, 'PSA.119.17', 'Do good to your servant. I will live and I will obey your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 18, 'PSA.119.18', 'Open my eyes, that I may see wondrous things out of your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 19, 'PSA.119.19', 'I am a stranger on the earth. Don’t hide your commandments from me.'),
('PSA', 119, 20, 'PSA.119.20', 'My soul is consumed with longing for your ordinances at all times.'),
('PSA', 119, 21, 'PSA.119.21', 'You have rebuked the proud who are cursed, who wander from your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 22, 'PSA.119.22', 'Take reproach and contempt away from me, for I have kept your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 23, 'PSA.119.23', 'Though princes sit and slander me, your servant will meditate on your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 24, 'PSA.119.24', 'Indeed your statutes are my delight, and my counselors.'),
('PSA', 119, 25, 'PSA.119.25', 'My soul is laid low in the dust. Revive me according to your word!'),
('PSA', 119, 26, 'PSA.119.26', 'I declared my ways, and you answered me. Teach me your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 27, 'PSA.119.27', 'Let me understand the teaching of your precepts! Then I will meditate on your wondrous works.'),
('PSA', 119, 28, 'PSA.119.28', 'My soul is weary with sorrow; strengthen me according to your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 29, 'PSA.119.29', 'Keep me from the way of deceit. Grant me your law graciously!'),
('PSA', 119, 30, 'PSA.119.30', 'I have chosen the way of truth. I have set your ordinances before me.'),
('PSA', 119, 31, 'PSA.119.31', 'I cling to your statutes, LORD. Don’t let me be disappointed.'),
('PSA', 119, 32, 'PSA.119.32', 'I run in the path of your commandments, for you have set my heart free.'),
('PSA', 119, 33, 'PSA.119.33', 'Teach me, LORD, the way of your statutes. I will keep them to the end.'),
('PSA', 119, 34, 'PSA.119.34', 'Give me understanding, and I will keep your law. Yes, I will obey it with my whole heart.'),
('PSA', 119, 35, 'PSA.119.35', 'Direct me in the path of your commandments, for I delight in them.'),
('PSA', 119, 36, 'PSA.119.36', 'Turn my heart toward your statutes, not toward selfish gain.'),
('PSA', 119, 37, 'PSA.119.37', 'Turn my eyes away from looking at worthless things. Revive me in your ways.'),
('PSA', 119, 38, 'PSA.119.38', 'Fulfill your promise to your servant, that you may be feared.'),
('PSA', 119, 39, 'PSA.119.39', 'Take away my disgrace that I dread, for your ordinances are good.'),
('PSA', 119, 40, 'PSA.119.40', 'Behold, I long for your precepts! Revive me in your righteousness.'),
('PSA', 119, 41, 'PSA.119.41', 'Let your loving kindness also come to me, LORD, your salvation, according to your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 42, 'PSA.119.42', 'So I will have an answer for him who reproaches me, for I trust in your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 43, 'PSA.119.43', 'Don’t snatch the word of truth out of my mouth, for I put my hope in your ordinances.'),
('PSA', 119, 44, 'PSA.119.44', 'So I will obey your law continually, forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 119, 45, 'PSA.119.45', 'I will walk in liberty, for I have sought your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 46, 'PSA.119.46', 'I will also speak of your statutes before kings, and will not be disappointed.'),
('PSA', 119, 47, 'PSA.119.47', 'I will delight myself in your commandments, because I love them.'),
('PSA', 119, 48, 'PSA.119.48', 'I reach out my hands for your commandments, which I love. I will meditate on your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 49, 'PSA.119.49', 'Remember your word to your servant, because you gave me hope.'),
('PSA', 119, 50, 'PSA.119.50', 'This is my comfort in my affliction, for your word has revived me.'),
('PSA', 119, 51, 'PSA.119.51', 'The arrogant mock me excessively, but I don’t swerve from your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 52, 'PSA.119.52', 'I remember your ordinances of old, LORD, and have comforted myself.'),
('PSA', 119, 53, 'PSA.119.53', 'Indignation has taken hold on me, because of the wicked who forsake your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 54, 'PSA.119.54', 'Your statutes have been my songs in the house where I live.'),
('PSA', 119, 55, 'PSA.119.55', 'I have remembered your name, LORD, in the night, and I obey your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 56, 'PSA.119.56', 'This is my way, that I keep your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 57, 'PSA.119.57', 'The LORD is my portion. I promised to obey your words.'),
('PSA', 119, 58, 'PSA.119.58', 'I sought your favor with my whole heart. Be merciful to me according to your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 59, 'PSA.119.59', 'I considered my ways, and turned my steps to your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 60, 'PSA.119.60', 'I will hurry, and not delay, to obey your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 61, 'PSA.119.61', 'The ropes of the wicked bind me, but I won’t forget your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 62, 'PSA.119.62', 'At midnight I will rise to give thanks to you, because of your righteous ordinances.'),
('PSA', 119, 63, 'PSA.119.63', 'I am a friend of all those who fear you, of those who observe your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 64, 'PSA.119.64', 'The earth is full of your loving kindness, LORD. Teach me your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 65, 'PSA.119.65', 'You have treated your servant well, according to your word, LORD.'),
('PSA', 119, 66, 'PSA.119.66', 'Teach me good judgment and knowledge, for I believe in your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 67, 'PSA.119.67', 'Before I was afflicted, I went astray; but now I observe your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 68, 'PSA.119.68', 'You are good, and do good. Teach me your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 69, 'PSA.119.69', 'The proud have smeared a lie upon me. With my whole heart, I will keep your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 70, 'PSA.119.70', 'Their heart is as callous as the fat, but I delight in your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 71, 'PSA.119.71', 'It is good for me that I have been afflicted, that I may learn your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 72, 'PSA.119.72', 'The law of your mouth is better to me than thousands of pieces of gold and silver.'),
('PSA', 119, 73, 'PSA.119.73', 'Your hands have made me and formed me. Give me understanding, that I may learn your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 74, 'PSA.119.74', 'Those who fear you will see me and be glad, because I have put my hope in your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 75, 'PSA.119.75', 'LORD, I know that your judgments are righteous, that in faithfulness you have afflicted me.'),
('PSA', 119, 76, 'PSA.119.76', 'Please let your loving kindness be for my comfort, according to your word to your servant.'),
('PSA', 119, 77, 'PSA.119.77', 'Let your tender mercies come to me, that I may live; for your law is my delight.'),
('PSA', 119, 78, 'PSA.119.78', 'Let the proud be disappointed, for they have overthrown me wrongfully. I will meditate on your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 79, 'PSA.119.79', 'Let those who fear you turn to me. They will know your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 80, 'PSA.119.80', 'Let my heart be blameless toward your decrees, that I may not be disappointed.'),
('PSA', 119, 81, 'PSA.119.81', 'My soul faints for your salvation. I hope in your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 82, 'PSA.119.82', 'My eyes fail for your word. I say, “When will you comfort me?”'),
('PSA', 119, 83, 'PSA.119.83', 'For I have become like a wineskin in the smoke. I don’t forget your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 84, 'PSA.119.84', 'How many are the days of your servant? When will you execute judgment on those who persecute me?'),
('PSA', 119, 85, 'PSA.119.85', 'The proud have dug pits for me, contrary to your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 86, 'PSA.119.86', 'All of your commandments are faithful. They persecute me wrongfully. Help me!'),
('PSA', 119, 87, 'PSA.119.87', 'They had almost wiped me from the earth, but I didn’t forsake your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 88, 'PSA.119.88', 'Preserve my life according to your loving kindness, so I will obey the statutes of your mouth.'),
('PSA', 119, 89, 'PSA.119.89', 'LORD, your word is settled in heaven forever.'),
('PSA', 119, 90, 'PSA.119.90', 'Your faithfulness is to all generations. You have established the earth, and it remains.'),
('PSA', 119, 91, 'PSA.119.91', 'Your laws remain to this day, for all things serve you.'),
('PSA', 119, 92, 'PSA.119.92', 'Unless your law had been my delight, I would have perished in my affliction.'),
('PSA', 119, 93, 'PSA.119.93', 'I will never forget your precepts, for with them, you have revived me.'),
('PSA', 119, 94, 'PSA.119.94', 'I am yours. Save me, for I have sought your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 95, 'PSA.119.95', 'The wicked have waited for me, to destroy me. I will consider your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 96, 'PSA.119.96', 'I have seen a limit to all perfection, but your commands are boundless.'),
('PSA', 119, 97, 'PSA.119.97', 'How I love your law! It is my meditation all day.'),
('PSA', 119, 98, 'PSA.119.98', 'Your commandments make me wiser than my enemies, for your commandments are always with me.'),
('PSA', 119, 99, 'PSA.119.99', 'I have more understanding than all my teachers, for your testimonies are my meditation.'),
('PSA', 119, 100, 'PSA.119.100', 'I understand more than the aged, because I have kept your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 101, 'PSA.119.101', 'I have kept my feet from every evil way, that I might observe your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 102, 'PSA.119.102', 'I have not turned away from your ordinances, for you have taught me.'),
('PSA', 119, 103, 'PSA.119.103', 'How sweet are your promises to my taste, more than honey to my mouth!'),
('PSA', 119, 104, 'PSA.119.104', 'Through your precepts, I get understanding; therefore I hate every false way.'),
('PSA', 119, 105, 'PSA.119.105', 'Your word is a lamp to my feet, and a light for my path.'),
('PSA', 119, 106, 'PSA.119.106', 'I have sworn, and have confirmed it, that I will obey your righteous ordinances.'),
('PSA', 119, 107, 'PSA.119.107', 'I am afflicted very much. Revive me, LORD, according to your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 108, 'PSA.119.108', 'Accept, I beg you, the willing offerings of my mouth. LORD, teach me your ordinances.'),
('PSA', 119, 109, 'PSA.119.109', 'My soul is continually in my hand, yet I won’t forget your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 110, 'PSA.119.110', 'The wicked have laid a snare for me, yet I haven’t gone astray from your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 111, 'PSA.119.111', 'I have taken your testimonies as a heritage forever, for they are the joy of my heart.'),
('PSA', 119, 112, 'PSA.119.112', 'I have set my heart to perform your statutes forever, even to the end.'),
('PSA', 119, 113, 'PSA.119.113', 'I hate double-minded men, but I love your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 114, 'PSA.119.114', 'You are my hiding place and my shield. I hope in your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 115, 'PSA.119.115', 'Depart from me, you evildoers, that I may keep the commandments of my God.'),
('PSA', 119, 116, 'PSA.119.116', 'Uphold me according to your word, that I may live. Let me not be ashamed of my hope.'),
('PSA', 119, 117, 'PSA.119.117', 'Hold me up, and I will be safe, and will have respect for your statutes continually.'),
('PSA', 119, 118, 'PSA.119.118', 'You reject all those who stray from your statutes, for their deceit is in vain.'),
('PSA', 119, 119, 'PSA.119.119', 'You put away all the wicked of the earth like dross. Therefore I love your testimonies.'),
('PSA', 119, 120, 'PSA.119.120', 'My flesh trembles for fear of you. I am afraid of your judgments.'),
('PSA', 119, 121, 'PSA.119.121', 'I have done what is just and righteous. Don’t leave me to my oppressors.'),
('PSA', 119, 122, 'PSA.119.122', 'Ensure your servant’s well-being. Don’t let the proud oppress me.'),
('PSA', 119, 123, 'PSA.119.123', 'My eyes fail looking for your salvation, for your righteous word.'),
('PSA', 119, 124, 'PSA.119.124', 'Deal with your servant according to your loving kindness. Teach me your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 125, 'PSA.119.125', 'I am your servant. Give me understanding, that I may know your testimonies.'),
('PSA', 119, 126, 'PSA.119.126', 'It is time to act, LORD, for they break your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 127, 'PSA.119.127', 'Therefore I love your commandments more than gold, yes, more than pure gold.'),
('PSA', 119, 128, 'PSA.119.128', 'Therefore I consider all of your precepts to be right. I hate every false way.'),
('PSA', 119, 129, 'PSA.119.129', 'Your testimonies are wonderful, therefore my soul keeps them.'),
('PSA', 119, 130, 'PSA.119.130', 'The entrance of your words gives light. It gives understanding to the simple.'),
('PSA', 119, 131, 'PSA.119.131', 'I opened my mouth wide and panted, for I longed for your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 132, 'PSA.119.132', 'Turn to me, and have mercy on me, as you always do to those who love your name.'),
('PSA', 119, 133, 'PSA.119.133', 'Establish my footsteps in your word. Don’t let any iniquity have dominion over me.'),
('PSA', 119, 134, 'PSA.119.134', 'Redeem me from the oppression of man, so I will observe your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 135, 'PSA.119.135', 'Make your face shine on your servant. Teach me your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 136, 'PSA.119.136', 'Streams of tears run down my eyes, because they don’t observe your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 137, 'PSA.119.137', 'You are righteous, LORD. Your judgments are upright.'),
('PSA', 119, 138, 'PSA.119.138', 'You have commanded your statutes in righteousness. They are fully trustworthy.'),
('PSA', 119, 139, 'PSA.119.139', 'My zeal wears me out, because my enemies ignore your words.'),
('PSA', 119, 140, 'PSA.119.140', 'Your promises have been thoroughly tested, and your servant loves them.'),
('PSA', 119, 141, 'PSA.119.141', 'I am small and despised. I don’t forget your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 142, 'PSA.119.142', 'Your righteousness is an everlasting righteousness. Your law is truth.'),
('PSA', 119, 143, 'PSA.119.143', 'Trouble and anguish have taken hold of me. Your commandments are my delight.'),
('PSA', 119, 144, 'PSA.119.144', 'Your testimonies are righteous forever. Give me understanding, that I may live.'),
('PSA', 119, 145, 'PSA.119.145', 'I have called with my whole heart. Answer me, LORD! I will keep your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 146, 'PSA.119.146', 'I have called to you. Save me! I will obey your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 147, 'PSA.119.147', 'I rise before dawn and cry for help. I put my hope in your words.'),
('PSA', 119, 148, 'PSA.119.148', 'My eyes stay open through the night watches, that I might meditate on your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 149, 'PSA.119.149', 'Hear my voice according to your loving kindness. Revive me, LORD, according to your ordinances.'),
('PSA', 119, 150, 'PSA.119.150', 'They draw near who follow after wickedness. They are far from your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 151, 'PSA.119.151', 'You are near, LORD. All your commandments are truth.'),
('PSA', 119, 152, 'PSA.119.152', 'Of old I have known from your testimonies, that you have founded them forever.'),
('PSA', 119, 153, 'PSA.119.153', 'Consider my affliction, and deliver me, for I don’t forget your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 154, 'PSA.119.154', 'Plead my cause, and redeem me! Revive me according to your promise.'),
('PSA', 119, 155, 'PSA.119.155', 'Salvation is far from the wicked, for they don’t seek your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 156, 'PSA.119.156', 'Great are your tender mercies, LORD. Revive me according to your ordinances.'),
('PSA', 119, 157, 'PSA.119.157', 'Many are my persecutors and my adversaries. I haven’t swerved from your testimonies.'),
('PSA', 119, 158, 'PSA.119.158', 'I look at the faithless with loathing, because they don’t observe your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 159, 'PSA.119.159', 'Consider how I love your precepts. Revive me, LORD, according to your loving kindness.'),
('PSA', 119, 160, 'PSA.119.160', 'All of your words are truth. Every one of your righteous ordinances endures forever.'),
('PSA', 119, 161, 'PSA.119.161', 'Princes have persecuted me without a cause, but my heart stands in awe of your words.'),
('PSA', 119, 162, 'PSA.119.162', 'I rejoice at your word, as one who finds great plunder.'),
('PSA', 119, 163, 'PSA.119.163', 'I hate and abhor falsehood. I love your law.'),
('PSA', 119, 164, 'PSA.119.164', 'Seven times a day, I praise you, because of your righteous ordinances.'),
('PSA', 119, 165, 'PSA.119.165', 'Those who love your law have great peace. Nothing causes them to stumble.'),
('PSA', 119, 166, 'PSA.119.166', 'I have hoped for your salvation, LORD. I have done your commandments.'),
('PSA', 119, 167, 'PSA.119.167', 'My soul has observed your testimonies. I love them exceedingly.'),
('PSA', 119, 168, 'PSA.119.168', 'I have obeyed your precepts and your testimonies, for all my ways are before you.'),
('PSA', 119, 169, 'PSA.119.169', 'Let my cry come before you, LORD. Give me understanding according to your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 170, 'PSA.119.170', 'Let my supplication come before you. Deliver me according to your word.'),
('PSA', 119, 171, 'PSA.119.171', 'Let my lips utter praise, for you teach me your statutes.'),
('PSA', 119, 172, 'PSA.119.172', 'Let my tongue sing of your word, for all your commandments are righteousness.'),
('PSA', 119, 173, 'PSA.119.173', 'Let your hand be ready to help me, for I have chosen your precepts.'),
('PSA', 119, 174, 'PSA.119.174', 'I have longed for your salvation, LORD. Your law is my delight.'),
('PSA', 119, 175, 'PSA.119.175', 'Let my soul live, that I may praise you. Let your ordinances help me.'),
('PSA', 119, 176, 'PSA.119.176', 'I have gone astray like a lost sheep. Seek your servant, for I don’t forget your commandments.'),
('PSA', 120, 1, 'PSA.120.1', 'In my distress, I cried to the LORD. He answered me.'),
('PSA', 120, 2, 'PSA.120.2', 'Deliver my soul, LORD, from lying lips, from a deceitful tongue.'),
('PSA', 120, 3, 'PSA.120.3', 'What will be given to you, and what will be done more to you, you deceitful tongue?'),
('PSA', 120, 4, 'PSA.120.4', 'Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of juniper.'),
('PSA', 120, 5, 'PSA.120.5', 'Woe is me, that I live in Meshech, that I dwell among the tents of Kedar!'),
('PSA', 120, 6, 'PSA.120.6', 'My soul has had her dwelling too long with him who hates peace.'),
('PSA', 120, 7, 'PSA.120.7', 'I am for peace, but when I speak, they are for war.'),
('PSA', 121, 1, 'PSA.121.1', 'I will lift up my eyes to the hills. Where does my help come from?'),
('PSA', 121, 2, 'PSA.121.2', 'My help comes from the LORD, who made heaven and earth.'),
('PSA', 121, 3, 'PSA.121.3', 'He will not allow your foot to be moved. He who keeps you will not slumber.'),
('PSA', 121, 4, 'PSA.121.4', 'Behold, he who keeps Israel will neither slumber nor sleep.'),
('PSA', 121, 5, 'PSA.121.5', 'The LORD is your keeper. The LORD is your shade on your right hand.'),
('PSA', 121, 6, 'PSA.121.6', 'The sun will not harm you by day, nor the moon by night.'),
('PSA', 121, 7, 'PSA.121.7', 'The LORD will keep you from all evil. He will keep your soul.'),
('PSA', 121, 8, 'PSA.121.8', 'The LORD will keep your going out and your coming in, from this time forward, and forever more.'),
('PSA', 122, 1, 'PSA.122.1', 'I was glad when they said to me, “Let’s go to the LORD’s house!”'),
('PSA', 122, 2, 'PSA.122.2', 'Our feet are standing within your gates, Jerusalem!'),
('PSA', 122, 3, 'PSA.122.3', 'Jerusalem is built as a city that is compact together,'),
('PSA', 122, 4, 'PSA.122.4', 'where the tribes go up, even the LORD’s tribes, according to an ordinance for Israel, to give thanks to the LORD’s name.'),
('PSA', 122, 5, 'PSA.122.5', 'For there are set thrones for judgment, the thrones of David’s house.'),
('PSA', 122, 6, 'PSA.122.6', 'Pray for the peace of Jerusalem. Those who love you will prosper.'),
('PSA', 122, 7, 'PSA.122.7', 'Peace be within your walls, and prosperity within your palaces.'),
('PSA', 122, 8, 'PSA.122.8', 'For my brothers’ and companions’ sakes, I will now say, “Peace be within you.”'),
('PSA', 122, 9, 'PSA.122.9', 'For the sake of the house of the LORD our God, I will seek your good.'),
('PSA', 123, 1, 'PSA.123.1', 'I lift up my eyes to you, you who sit in the heavens.'),
('PSA', 123, 2, 'PSA.123.2', 'Behold, as the eyes of servants look to the hand of their master, as the eyes of a maid to the hand of her mistress, so our eyes look to the LORD, our God, until he has mercy on us.'),
('PSA', 123, 3, 'PSA.123.3', 'Have mercy on us, LORD, have mercy on us, for we have endured much contempt.'),
('PSA', 123, 4, 'PSA.123.4', 'Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scoffing of those who are at ease, with the contempt of the proud.'),
('PSA', 124, 1, 'PSA.124.1', 'If it had not been the LORD who was on our side, let Israel now say,'),
('PSA', 124, 2, 'PSA.124.2', 'if it had not been the LORD who was on our side, when men rose up against us,'),
('PSA', 124, 3, 'PSA.124.3', 'then they would have swallowed us up alive, when their wrath was kindled against us,'),
('PSA', 124, 4, 'PSA.124.4', 'then the waters would have overwhelmed us, the stream would have gone over our soul.'),
('PSA', 124, 5, 'PSA.124.5', 'Then the proud waters would have gone over our soul.'),
('PSA', 124, 6, 'PSA.124.6', 'Blessed be the LORD, who has not given us as a prey to their teeth.'),
('PSA', 124, 7, 'PSA.124.7', 'Our soul has escaped like a bird out of the fowler’s snare. The snare is broken, and we have escaped.'),
('PSA', 124, 8, 'PSA.124.8', 'Our help is in the LORD’s name, who made heaven and earth.'),
('PSA', 125, 1, 'PSA.125.1', 'Those who trust in the LORD are as Mount Zion, which can’t be moved, but remains forever.'),
('PSA', 125, 2, 'PSA.125.2', 'As the mountains surround Jerusalem, so the LORD surrounds his people from this time forward and forever more.'),
('PSA', 125, 3, 'PSA.125.3', 'For the scepter of wickedness won’t remain over the allotment of the righteous, so that the righteous won’t use their hands to do evil.'),
('PSA', 125, 4, 'PSA.125.4', 'Do good, LORD, to those who are good, to those who are upright in their hearts.'),
('PSA', 125, 5, 'PSA.125.5', 'But as for those who turn away to their crooked ways, the LORD will lead them away with the workers of iniquity. Peace be on Israel.'),
('PSA', 126, 1, 'PSA.126.1', 'When the LORD brought back those who returned to Zion, we were like those who dream.'),
('PSA', 126, 2, 'PSA.126.2', 'Then our mouth was filled with laughter, and our tongue with singing. Then they said among the nations, “The LORD has done great things for them.”'),
('PSA', 126, 3, 'PSA.126.3', 'The LORD has done great things for us, and we are glad.'),
('PSA', 126, 4, 'PSA.126.4', 'Restore our fortunes again, LORD, like the streams in the Negev.'),
('PSA', 126, 5, 'PSA.126.5', 'Those who sow in tears will reap in joy.'),
('PSA', 126, 6, 'PSA.126.6', 'He who goes out weeping, carrying seed for sowing, will certainly come again with joy, carrying his sheaves.'),
('PSA', 127, 1, 'PSA.127.1', 'Unless the LORD builds the house, they who build it labor in vain. Unless the LORD watches over the city, the watchman guards it in vain.'),
('PSA', 127, 2, 'PSA.127.2', 'It is vain for you to rise up early, to stay up late, eating the bread of toil, for he gives sleep to his loved ones.'),
('PSA', 127, 3, 'PSA.127.3', 'Behold, children are a heritage of the LORD. The fruit of the womb is his reward.'),
('PSA', 127, 4, 'PSA.127.4', 'As arrows in the hand of a mighty man, so are the children of youth.'),
('PSA', 127, 5, 'PSA.127.5', 'Happy is the man who has his quiver full of them. They won’t be disappointed when they speak with their enemies in the gate.'),
('PSA', 128, 1, 'PSA.128.1', 'Blessed is everyone who fears the LORD, who walks in his ways.'),
('PSA', 128, 2, 'PSA.128.2', 'For you will eat the labor of your hands. You will be happy, and it will be well with you.'),
('PSA', 128, 3, 'PSA.128.3', 'Your wife will be as a fruitful vine in the innermost parts of your house, your children like olive shoots around your table.'),
('PSA', 128, 4, 'PSA.128.4', 'Behold, this is how the man who fears the LORD is blessed.'),
('PSA', 128, 5, 'PSA.128.5', 'May the LORD bless you out of Zion, and may you see the good of Jerusalem all the days of your life.'),
('PSA', 128, 6, 'PSA.128.6', 'Yes, may you see your children’s children. Peace be upon Israel.'),
('PSA', 129, 1, 'PSA.129.1', 'Many times they have afflicted me from my youth up. Let Israel now say:'),
('PSA', 129, 2, 'PSA.129.2', 'many times they have afflicted me from my youth up, yet they have not prevailed against me.'),
('PSA', 129, 3, 'PSA.129.3', 'The plowers plowed on my back. They made their furrows long.'),
('PSA', 129, 4, 'PSA.129.4', 'The LORD is righteous. He has cut apart the cords of the wicked.'),
('PSA', 129, 5, 'PSA.129.5', 'Let them be disappointed and turned backward, all those who hate Zion.'),
('PSA', 129, 6, 'PSA.129.6', 'Let them be as the grass on the housetops, which withers before it grows up,'),
('PSA', 129, 7, 'PSA.129.7', 'with which the reaper doesn’t fill his hand, nor he who binds sheaves, his bosom.'),
('PSA', 129, 8, 'PSA.129.8', 'Neither do those who go by say, “The blessing of the LORD be on you. We bless you in the LORD’s name.”'),
('PSA', 130, 1, 'PSA.130.1', 'Out of the depths I have cried to you, LORD.'),
('PSA', 130, 2, 'PSA.130.2', 'Lord, hear my voice. Let your ears be attentive to the voice of my petitions.'),
('PSA', 130, 3, 'PSA.130.3', 'If you, LORD, kept a record of sins, Lord, who could stand?'),
('PSA', 130, 4, 'PSA.130.4', 'But there is forgiveness with you, therefore you are feared.'),
('PSA', 130, 5, 'PSA.130.5', 'I wait for the LORD. My soul waits. I hope in his word.'),
('PSA', 130, 6, 'PSA.130.6', 'My soul longs for the Lord more than watchmen long for the morning, more than watchmen for the morning.'),
('PSA', 130, 7, 'PSA.130.7', 'Israel, hope in the LORD, for there is loving kindness with the LORD. Abundant redemption is with him.'),
('PSA', 130, 8, 'PSA.130.8', 'He will redeem Israel from all their sins.'),
('PSA', 131, 1, 'PSA.131.1', 'LORD, my heart isn’t arrogant, nor my eyes lofty; nor do I concern myself with great matters, or things too wonderful for me.'),
('PSA', 131, 2, 'PSA.131.2', 'Surely I have stilled and quieted my soul, like a weaned child with his mother, like a weaned child is my soul within me.'),
('PSA', 131, 3, 'PSA.131.3', 'Israel, hope in the LORD, from this time forward and forever more.'),
('PSA', 132, 1, 'PSA.132.1', 'LORD, remember David and all his affliction,'),
('PSA', 132, 2, 'PSA.132.2', 'how he swore to the LORD, and vowed to the Mighty One of Jacob:'),
('PSA', 132, 3, 'PSA.132.3', '“Surely I will not come into the structure of my house, nor go up into my bed;'),
('PSA', 132, 4, 'PSA.132.4', 'I will not give sleep to my eyes, or slumber to my eyelids,'),
('PSA', 132, 5, 'PSA.132.5', 'until I find out a place for the LORD, a dwelling for the Mighty One of Jacob.”'),
('PSA', 132, 6, 'PSA.132.6', 'Behold, we heard of it in Ephrathah. We found it in the field of Jaar.'),
('PSA', 132, 7, 'PSA.132.7', '“We will go into his dwelling place. We will worship at his footstool.”'),
('PSA', 132, 8, 'PSA.132.8', 'Arise, LORD, into your resting place, you, and the ark of your strength.'),
('PSA', 132, 9, 'PSA.132.9', 'Let your priests be clothed with righteousness. Let your saints shout for joy!'),
('PSA', 132, 10, 'PSA.132.10', 'For your servant David’s sake, don’t turn away the face of your anointed one.'),
('PSA', 132, 11, 'PSA.132.11', 'The LORD has sworn to David in truth. He will not turn from it: “I will set the fruit of your body on your throne.'),
('PSA', 132, 12, 'PSA.132.12', 'If your children will keep my covenant, my testimony that I will teach them, their children also will sit on your throne forever more.”'),
('PSA', 132, 13, 'PSA.132.13', 'For the LORD has chosen Zion. He has desired it for his habitation.'),
('PSA', 132, 14, 'PSA.132.14', '“This is my resting place forever. I will live here, for I have desired it.'),
('PSA', 132, 15, 'PSA.132.15', 'I will abundantly bless her provision. I will satisfy her poor with bread.'),
('PSA', 132, 16, 'PSA.132.16', 'I will also clothe her priests with salvation. Her saints will shout aloud for joy.'),
('PSA', 132, 17, 'PSA.132.17', 'I will make the horn of David to bud there. I have ordained a lamp for my anointed.'),
('PSA', 132, 18, 'PSA.132.18', 'I will clothe his enemies with shame, but on himself, his crown will shine.”'),
('PSA', 133, 1, 'PSA.133.1', 'See how good and how pleasant it is for brothers to live together in unity!'),
('PSA', 133, 2, 'PSA.133.2', 'It is like the precious oil on the head, that ran down on the beard, even Aaron’s beard, that came down on the edge of his robes,'),
('PSA', 133, 3, 'PSA.133.3', 'like the dew of Hermon, that comes down on the hills of Zion; for there the LORD gives the blessing, even life forever more.'),
('PSA', 134, 1, 'PSA.134.1', 'Look! Praise the LORD, all you servants of the LORD, who stand by night in the LORD’s house!'),
('PSA', 134, 2, 'PSA.134.2', 'Lift up your hands in the sanctuary. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 134, 3, 'PSA.134.3', 'May the LORD bless you from Zion, even he who made heaven and earth.'),
('PSA', 135, 1, 'PSA.135.1', 'Praise the LORD! Praise the LORD’s name! Praise him, you servants of the LORD,'),
('PSA', 135, 2, 'PSA.135.2', 'you who stand in the LORD’s house, in the courts of our God’s house.'),
('PSA', 135, 3, 'PSA.135.3', 'Praise the LORD, for the LORD is good. Sing praises to his name, for that is pleasant.'),
('PSA', 135, 4, 'PSA.135.4', 'For the LORD has chosen Jacob for himself, Israel for his own possession.'),
('PSA', 135, 5, 'PSA.135.5', 'For I know that the LORD is great, that our Lord is above all gods.'),
('PSA', 135, 6, 'PSA.135.6', 'Whatever the LORD pleased, that he has done, in heaven and in earth, in the seas and in all deeps.'),
('PSA', 135, 7, 'PSA.135.7', 'He causes the clouds to rise from the ends of the earth. He makes lightnings with the rain. He brings the wind out of his treasuries.'),
('PSA', 135, 8, 'PSA.135.8', 'He struck the firstborn of Egypt, both of man and animal.'),
('PSA', 135, 9, 'PSA.135.9', 'He sent signs and wonders into the middle of you, Egypt, on Pharaoh, and on all his servants.'),
('PSA', 135, 10, 'PSA.135.10', 'He struck many nations, and killed mighty kings—'),
('PSA', 135, 11, 'PSA.135.11', 'Sihon king of the Amorites, Og king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan—'),
('PSA', 135, 12, 'PSA.135.12', 'and gave their land for a heritage, a heritage to Israel, his people.'),
('PSA', 135, 13, 'PSA.135.13', 'Your name, LORD, endures forever; your renown, LORD, throughout all generations.'),
('PSA', 135, 14, 'PSA.135.14', 'For the LORD will judge his people and have compassion on his servants.'),
('PSA', 135, 15, 'PSA.135.15', 'The idols of the nations are silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.'),
('PSA', 135, 16, 'PSA.135.16', 'They have mouths, but they can’t speak. They have eyes, but they can’t see.'),
('PSA', 135, 17, 'PSA.135.17', 'They have ears, but they can’t hear, neither is there any breath in their mouths.'),
('PSA', 135, 18, 'PSA.135.18', 'Those who make them will be like them, yes, everyone who trusts in them.'),
('PSA', 135, 19, 'PSA.135.19', 'House of Israel, praise the LORD! House of Aaron, praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 135, 20, 'PSA.135.20', 'House of Levi, praise the LORD! You who fear the LORD, praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 135, 21, 'PSA.135.21', 'Blessed be the LORD from Zion, who dwells in Jerusalem. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 136, 1, 'PSA.136.1', 'Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 136, 2, 'PSA.136.2', 'Give thanks to the God of gods, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 136, 3, 'PSA.136.3', 'Give thanks to the Lord of lords, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 4, 'PSA.136.4', 'to him who alone does great wonders, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 5, 'PSA.136.5', 'to him who by understanding made the heavens, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 6, 'PSA.136.6', 'to him who spread out the earth above the waters, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 7, 'PSA.136.7', 'to him who made the great lights, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 8, 'PSA.136.8', 'the sun to rule by day, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 9, 'PSA.136.9', 'the moon and stars to rule by night, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 10, 'PSA.136.10', 'to him who struck down the Egyptian firstborn, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 11, 'PSA.136.11', 'and brought out Israel from among them, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 12, 'PSA.136.12', 'with a strong hand, and with an outstretched arm, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 13, 'PSA.136.13', 'to him who divided the Red Sea apart, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 14, 'PSA.136.14', 'and made Israel to pass through the middle of it, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 15, 'PSA.136.15', 'but overthrew Pharaoh and his army in the Red Sea, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 16, 'PSA.136.16', 'to him who led his people through the wilderness, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 17, 'PSA.136.17', 'to him who struck great kings, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 18, 'PSA.136.18', 'and killed mighty kings, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 19, 'PSA.136.19', 'Sihon king of the Amorites, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 20, 'PSA.136.20', 'Og king of Bashan, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 21, 'PSA.136.21', 'and gave their land as an inheritance, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 22, 'PSA.136.22', 'even a heritage to Israel his servant, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 23, 'PSA.136.23', 'who remembered us in our low estate, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 24, 'PSA.136.24', 'and has delivered us from our adversaries, for his loving kindness endures forever;'),
('PSA', 136, 25, 'PSA.136.25', 'who gives food to every creature, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 136, 26, 'PSA.136.26', 'Oh give thanks to the God of heaven, for his loving kindness endures forever.'),
('PSA', 137, 1, 'PSA.137.1', 'By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down. Yes, we wept, when we remembered Zion.'),
('PSA', 137, 2, 'PSA.137.2', 'On the willows in that land, we hung up our harps.'),
('PSA', 137, 3, 'PSA.137.3', 'For there, those who led us captive asked us for songs. Those who tormented us demanded songs of joy: “Sing us one of the songs of Zion!”'),
('PSA', 137, 4, 'PSA.137.4', 'How can we sing the LORD’s song in a foreign land?'),
('PSA', 137, 5, 'PSA.137.5', 'If I forget you, Jerusalem, let my right hand forget its skill.'),
('PSA', 137, 6, 'PSA.137.6', 'Let my tongue stick to the roof of my mouth if I don’t remember you, if I don’t prefer Jerusalem above my chief joy.'),
('PSA', 137, 7, 'PSA.137.7', 'Remember, LORD, against the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem, who said, “Raze it! Raze it even to its foundation!”'),
('PSA', 137, 8, 'PSA.137.8', 'Daughter of Babylon, doomed to destruction, he will be happy who repays you, as you have done to us.'),
('PSA', 137, 9, 'PSA.137.9', 'Happy shall he be, who takes and dashes your little ones against the rock.'),
('PSA', 138, 1, 'PSA.138.1', 'I will give you thanks with my whole heart. Before the gods, I will sing praises to you.'),
('PSA', 138, 2, 'PSA.138.2', 'I will bow down toward your holy temple, and give thanks to your Name for your loving kindness and for your truth; for you have exalted your Name and your Word above all.'),
('PSA', 138, 3, 'PSA.138.3', 'In the day that I called, you answered me. You encouraged me with strength in my soul.'),
('PSA', 138, 4, 'PSA.138.4', 'All the kings of the earth will give you thanks, LORD, for they have heard the words of your mouth.'),
('PSA', 138, 5, 'PSA.138.5', 'Yes, they will sing of the ways of the LORD, for the LORD’s glory is great!'),
('PSA', 138, 6, 'PSA.138.6', 'For though the LORD is high, yet he looks after the lowly; but he knows the proud from afar.'),
('PSA', 138, 7, 'PSA.138.7', 'Though I walk in the middle of trouble, you will revive me. You will stretch out your hand against the wrath of my enemies. Your right hand will save me.'),
('PSA', 138, 8, 'PSA.138.8', 'The LORD will fulfill that which concerns me. Your loving kindness, LORD, endures forever. Don’t forsake the works of your own hands.'),
('PSA', 139, 1, 'PSA.139.1', 'LORD, you have searched me, and you know me.'),
('PSA', 139, 2, 'PSA.139.2', 'You know my sitting down and my rising up. You perceive my thoughts from afar.'),
('PSA', 139, 3, 'PSA.139.3', 'You search out my path and my lying down, and are acquainted with all my ways.'),
('PSA', 139, 4, 'PSA.139.4', 'For there is not a word on my tongue, but behold, LORD, you know it altogether.'),
('PSA', 139, 5, 'PSA.139.5', 'You hem me in behind and before. You laid your hand on me.'),
('PSA', 139, 6, 'PSA.139.6', 'This knowledge is beyond me. It’s lofty. I can’t attain it.'),
('PSA', 139, 7, 'PSA.139.7', 'Where could I go from your Spirit? Or where could I flee from your presence?'),
('PSA', 139, 8, 'PSA.139.8', 'If I ascend up into heaven, you are there. If I make my bed in Sheol, behold, you are there!'),
('PSA', 139, 9, 'PSA.139.9', 'If I take the wings of the dawn, and settle in the uttermost parts of the sea,'),
('PSA', 139, 10, 'PSA.139.10', 'even there your hand will lead me, and your right hand will hold me.'),
('PSA', 139, 11, 'PSA.139.11', 'If I say, “Surely the darkness will overwhelm me. The light around me will be night,”'),
('PSA', 139, 12, 'PSA.139.12', 'even the darkness doesn’t hide from you, but the night shines as the day. The darkness is like light to you.'),
('PSA', 139, 13, 'PSA.139.13', 'For you formed my inmost being. You knit me together in my mother’s womb.'),
('PSA', 139, 14, 'PSA.139.14', 'I will give thanks to you, for I am fearfully and wonderfully made. Your works are wonderful. My soul knows that very well.'),
('PSA', 139, 15, 'PSA.139.15', 'My frame wasn’t hidden from you, when I was made in secret, woven together in the depths of the earth.'),
('PSA', 139, 16, 'PSA.139.16', 'Your eyes saw my body. In your book they were all written, the days that were ordained for me, when as yet there were none of them.'),
('PSA', 139, 17, 'PSA.139.17', 'How precious to me are your thoughts, God! How vast is their sum!'),
('PSA', 139, 18, 'PSA.139.18', 'If I would count them, they are more in number than the sand. When I wake up, I am still with you.'),
('PSA', 139, 19, 'PSA.139.19', 'If only you, God, would kill the wicked. Get away from me, you bloodthirsty men!'),
('PSA', 139, 20, 'PSA.139.20', 'For they speak against you wickedly. Your enemies take your name in vain.'),
('PSA', 139, 21, 'PSA.139.21', 'LORD, don’t I hate those who hate you? Am I not grieved with those who rise up against you?'),
('PSA', 139, 22, 'PSA.139.22', 'I hate them with perfect hatred. They have become my enemies.'),
('PSA', 139, 23, 'PSA.139.23', 'Search me, God, and know my heart. Try me, and know my thoughts.'),
('PSA', 139, 24, 'PSA.139.24', 'See if there is any wicked way in me, and lead me in the everlasting way.'),
('PSA', 140, 1, 'PSA.140.1', 'Deliver me, LORD, from evil men. Preserve me from violent men:'),
('PSA', 140, 2, 'PSA.140.2', 'those who devise mischief in their hearts. They continually gather themselves together for war.'),
('PSA', 140, 3, 'PSA.140.3', 'They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent. Viper’s poison is under their lips. Selah.'),
('PSA', 140, 4, 'PSA.140.4', 'LORD, keep me from the hands of the wicked. Preserve me from the violent men who have determined to trip my feet.'),
('PSA', 140, 5, 'PSA.140.5', 'The proud have hidden a snare for me, they have spread the cords of a net by the path. They have set traps for me. Selah.'),
('PSA', 140, 6, 'PSA.140.6', 'I said to the LORD, “You are my God.” Listen to the cry of my petitions, LORD.'),
('PSA', 140, 7, 'PSA.140.7', 'LORD, the Lord, the strength of my salvation, you have covered my head in the day of battle.'),
('PSA', 140, 8, 'PSA.140.8', 'LORD, don’t grant the desires of the wicked. Don’t let their evil plans succeed, or they will become proud. Selah.'),
('PSA', 140, 9, 'PSA.140.9', 'As for the head of those who surround me, let the mischief of their own lips cover them.'),
('PSA', 140, 10, 'PSA.140.10', 'Let burning coals fall on them. Let them be thrown into the fire, into miry pits, from where they never rise.'),
('PSA', 140, 11, 'PSA.140.11', 'An evil speaker won’t be established on the earth. Evil will hunt the violent man to overthrow him.'),
('PSA', 140, 12, 'PSA.140.12', 'I know that the LORD will maintain the cause of the afflicted, and justice for the needy.'),
('PSA', 140, 13, 'PSA.140.13', 'Surely the righteous will give thanks to your name. The upright will dwell in your presence.'),
('PSA', 141, 1, 'PSA.141.1', 'LORD, I have called on you. Come to me quickly! Listen to my voice when I call to you.'),
('PSA', 141, 2, 'PSA.141.2', 'Let my prayer be set before you like incense; the lifting up of my hands like the evening sacrifice.'),
('PSA', 141, 3, 'PSA.141.3', 'Set a watch, LORD, before my mouth. Keep the door of my lips.'),
('PSA', 141, 4, 'PSA.141.4', 'Don’t incline my heart to any evil thing, to practice deeds of wickedness with men who work iniquity. Don’t let me eat of their delicacies.'),
('PSA', 141, 5, 'PSA.141.5', 'Let the righteous strike me, it is kindness; let him reprove me, it is like oil on the head; don’t let my head refuse it; Yet my prayer is always against evil deeds.'),
('PSA', 141, 6, 'PSA.141.6', 'Their judges are thrown down by the sides of the rock. They will hear my words, for they are well spoken.'),
('PSA', 141, 7, 'PSA.141.7', '“As when one plows and breaks up the earth, our bones are scattered at the mouth of Sheol.”'),
('PSA', 141, 8, 'PSA.141.8', 'For my eyes are on you, LORD, the Lord. I take refuge in you. Don’t leave my soul destitute.'),
('PSA', 141, 9, 'PSA.141.9', 'Keep me from the snare which they have laid for me, from the traps of the workers of iniquity.'),
('PSA', 141, 10, 'PSA.141.10', 'Let the wicked fall together into their own nets while I pass by.'),
('PSA', 142, 1, 'PSA.142.1', 'I cry with my voice to the LORD. With my voice, I ask the LORD for mercy.'),
('PSA', 142, 2, 'PSA.142.2', 'I pour out my complaint before him. I tell him my troubles.'),
('PSA', 142, 3, 'PSA.142.3', 'When my spirit was overwhelmed within me, you knew my route. On the path in which I walk, they have hidden a snare for me.'),
('PSA', 142, 4, 'PSA.142.4', 'Look on my right, and see; for there is no one who is concerned for me. Refuge has fled from me. No one cares for my soul.'),
('PSA', 142, 5, 'PSA.142.5', 'I cried to you, LORD. I said, “You are my refuge, my portion in the land of the living.”'),
('PSA', 142, 6, 'PSA.142.6', 'Listen to my cry, for I am in desperate need. Deliver me from my persecutors, for they are too strong for me.'),
('PSA', 142, 7, 'PSA.142.7', 'Bring my soul out of prison, that I may give thanks to your name. The righteous will surround me, for you will be good to me.'),
('PSA', 143, 1, 'PSA.143.1', 'Hear my prayer, LORD. Listen to my petitions. In your faithfulness and righteousness, relieve me.'),
('PSA', 143, 2, 'PSA.143.2', 'Don’t enter into judgment with your servant, for in your sight no man living is righteous.'),
('PSA', 143, 3, 'PSA.143.3', 'For the enemy pursues my soul. He has struck my life down to the ground. He has made me live in dark places, as those who have been long dead.'),
('PSA', 143, 4, 'PSA.143.4', 'Therefore my spirit is overwhelmed within me. My heart within me is desolate.'),
('PSA', 143, 5, 'PSA.143.5', 'I remember the days of old. I meditate on all your doings. I contemplate the work of your hands.'),
('PSA', 143, 6, 'PSA.143.6', 'I spread out my hands to you. My soul thirsts for you, like a parched land. Selah.'),
('PSA', 143, 7, 'PSA.143.7', 'Hurry to answer me, LORD. My spirit fails. Don’t hide your face from me, so that I don’t become like those who go down into the pit.'),
('PSA', 143, 8, 'PSA.143.8', 'Cause me to hear your loving kindness in the morning, for I trust in you. Cause me to know the way in which I should walk, for I lift up my soul to you.'),
('PSA', 143, 9, 'PSA.143.9', 'Deliver me, LORD, from my enemies. I flee to you to hide me.'),
('PSA', 143, 10, 'PSA.143.10', 'Teach me to do your will, for you are my God. Your Spirit is good. Lead me in the land of uprightness.'),
('PSA', 143, 11, 'PSA.143.11', 'Revive me, LORD, for your name’s sake. In your righteousness, bring my soul out of trouble.'),
('PSA', 143, 12, 'PSA.143.12', 'In your loving kindness, cut off my enemies, and destroy all those who afflict my soul, for I am your servant.'),
('PSA', 144, 1, 'PSA.144.1', 'Blessed be the LORD, my rock, who trains my hands to war, and my fingers to battle—'),
('PSA', 144, 2, 'PSA.144.2', 'my loving kindness, my fortress, my high tower, my deliverer, my shield, and he in whom I take refuge, who subdues my people under me.'),
('PSA', 144, 3, 'PSA.144.3', 'LORD, what is man, that you care for him? Or the son of man, that you think of him?'),
('PSA', 144, 4, 'PSA.144.4', 'Man is like a breath. His days are like a shadow that passes away.'),
('PSA', 144, 5, 'PSA.144.5', 'Part your heavens, LORD, and come down. Touch the mountains, and they will smoke.'),
('PSA', 144, 6, 'PSA.144.6', 'Throw out lightning, and scatter them. Send out your arrows, and rout them.'),
('PSA', 144, 7, 'PSA.144.7', 'Stretch out your hand from above, rescue me, and deliver me out of great waters, out of the hands of foreigners,'),
('PSA', 144, 8, 'PSA.144.8', 'whose mouths speak deceit, whose right hand is a right hand of falsehood.'),
('PSA', 144, 9, 'PSA.144.9', 'I will sing a new song to you, God. On a ten-stringed lyre, I will sing praises to you.'),
('PSA', 144, 10, 'PSA.144.10', 'You are he who gives salvation to kings, who rescues David, his servant, from the deadly sword.'),
('PSA', 144, 11, 'PSA.144.11', 'Rescue me, and deliver me out of the hands of foreigners, whose mouths speak deceit, whose right hand is a right hand of falsehood.'),
('PSA', 144, 12, 'PSA.144.12', 'Then our sons will be like well-nurtured plants, our daughters like pillars carved to adorn a palace.'),
('PSA', 144, 13, 'PSA.144.13', 'Our barns are full, filled with all kinds of provision. Our sheep produce thousands and ten thousands in our fields.'),
('PSA', 144, 14, 'PSA.144.14', 'Our oxen will pull heavy loads. There is no breaking in, and no going away, and no outcry in our streets.'),
('PSA', 144, 15, 'PSA.144.15', 'Happy are the people who are in such a situation. Happy are the people whose God is the LORD.'),
('PSA', 145, 1, 'PSA.145.1', 'I will exalt you, my God, the King. I will praise your name forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 145, 2, 'PSA.145.2', 'Every day I will praise you. I will extol your name forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 145, 3, 'PSA.145.3', 'Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised! His greatness is unsearchable.'),
('PSA', 145, 4, 'PSA.145.4', 'One generation will commend your works to another, and will declare your mighty acts.'),
('PSA', 145, 5, 'PSA.145.5', 'I will meditate on the glorious majesty of your honor, on your wondrous works.'),
('PSA', 145, 6, 'PSA.145.6', 'Men will speak of the might of your awesome acts. I will declare your greatness.'),
('PSA', 145, 7, 'PSA.145.7', 'They will utter the memory of your great goodness, and will sing of your righteousness.'),
('PSA', 145, 8, 'PSA.145.8', 'The LORD is gracious, merciful, slow to anger, and of great loving kindness.'),
('PSA', 145, 9, 'PSA.145.9', 'The LORD is good to all. His tender mercies are over all his works.'),
('PSA', 145, 10, 'PSA.145.10', 'All your works will give thanks to you, LORD. Your saints will extol you.'),
('PSA', 145, 11, 'PSA.145.11', 'They will speak of the glory of your kingdom, and talk about your power,'),
('PSA', 145, 12, 'PSA.145.12', 'to make known to the sons of men his mighty acts, the glory of the majesty of his kingdom.'),
('PSA', 145, 13, 'PSA.145.13', 'Your kingdom is an everlasting kingdom. Your dominion endures throughout all generations. The LORD is faithful in all his words, and loving in all his deeds.'),
('PSA', 145, 14, 'PSA.145.14', 'The LORD upholds all who fall, and raises up all those who are bowed down.'),
('PSA', 145, 15, 'PSA.145.15', 'The eyes of all wait for you. You give them their food in due season.'),
('PSA', 145, 16, 'PSA.145.16', 'You open your hand, and satisfy the desire of every living thing.'),
('PSA', 145, 17, 'PSA.145.17', 'The LORD is righteous in all his ways, and gracious in all his works.'),
('PSA', 145, 18, 'PSA.145.18', 'The LORD is near to all those who call on him, to all who call on him in truth.'),
('PSA', 145, 19, 'PSA.145.19', 'He will fulfill the desire of those who fear him. He also will hear their cry, and will save them.'),
('PSA', 145, 20, 'PSA.145.20', 'The LORD preserves all those who love him, but he will destroy all the wicked.'),
('PSA', 145, 21, 'PSA.145.21', 'My mouth will speak the praise of the LORD. Let all flesh bless his holy name forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 146, 1, 'PSA.146.1', 'Praise the LORD! Praise the LORD, my soul.'),
('PSA', 146, 2, 'PSA.146.2', 'While I live, I will praise the LORD. I will sing praises to my God as long as I exist.'),
('PSA', 146, 3, 'PSA.146.3', 'Don’t put your trust in princes, in a son of man in whom there is no help.'),
('PSA', 146, 4, 'PSA.146.4', 'His spirit departs, and he returns to the earth. In that very day, his thoughts perish.'),
('PSA', 146, 5, 'PSA.146.5', 'Happy is he who has the God of Jacob for his help, whose hope is in the LORD, his God,'),
('PSA', 146, 6, 'PSA.146.6', 'who made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that is in them; who keeps truth forever;'),
('PSA', 146, 7, 'PSA.146.7', 'who executes justice for the oppressed; who gives food to the hungry. The LORD frees the prisoners.'),
('PSA', 146, 8, 'PSA.146.8', 'The LORD opens the eyes of the blind. The LORD raises up those who are bowed down. The LORD loves the righteous.'),
('PSA', 146, 9, 'PSA.146.9', 'The LORD preserves the foreigners. He upholds the fatherless and widow, but he turns the way of the wicked upside down.'),
('PSA', 146, 10, 'PSA.146.10', 'The LORD will reign forever; your God, O Zion, to all generations. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 147, 1, 'PSA.147.1', 'Praise the LORD, for it is good to sing praises to our God; for it is pleasant and fitting to praise him.'),
('PSA', 147, 2, 'PSA.147.2', 'The LORD builds up Jerusalem. He gathers together the outcasts of Israel.'),
('PSA', 147, 3, 'PSA.147.3', 'He heals the broken in heart, and binds up their wounds.'),
('PSA', 147, 4, 'PSA.147.4', 'He counts the number of the stars. He calls them all by their names.'),
('PSA', 147, 5, 'PSA.147.5', 'Great is our Lord, and mighty in power. His understanding is infinite.'),
('PSA', 147, 6, 'PSA.147.6', 'The LORD upholds the humble. He brings the wicked down to the ground.'),
('PSA', 147, 7, 'PSA.147.7', 'Sing to the LORD with thanksgiving. Sing praises on the harp to our God,'),
('PSA', 147, 8, 'PSA.147.8', 'who covers the sky with clouds, who prepares rain for the earth, who makes grass grow on the mountains.'),
('PSA', 147, 9, 'PSA.147.9', 'He provides food for the livestock, and for the young ravens when they call.'),
('PSA', 147, 10, 'PSA.147.10', 'He doesn’t delight in the strength of the horse. He takes no pleasure in the legs of a man.'),
('PSA', 147, 11, 'PSA.147.11', 'The LORD takes pleasure in those who fear him, in those who hope in his loving kindness.'),
('PSA', 147, 12, 'PSA.147.12', 'Praise the LORD, Jerusalem! Praise your God, Zion!'),
('PSA', 147, 13, 'PSA.147.13', 'For he has strengthened the bars of your gates. He has blessed your children within you.'),
('PSA', 147, 14, 'PSA.147.14', 'He makes peace in your borders. He fills you with the finest of the wheat.'),
('PSA', 147, 15, 'PSA.147.15', 'He sends out his commandment to the earth. His word runs very swiftly.'),
('PSA', 147, 16, 'PSA.147.16', 'He gives snow like wool, and scatters frost like ashes.'),
('PSA', 147, 17, 'PSA.147.17', 'He hurls down his hail like pebbles. Who can stand before his cold?'),
('PSA', 147, 18, 'PSA.147.18', 'He sends out his word, and melts them. He causes his wind to blow, and the waters flow.'),
('PSA', 147, 19, 'PSA.147.19', 'He shows his word to Jacob, his statutes and his ordinances to Israel.'),
('PSA', 147, 20, 'PSA.147.20', 'He has not done this for just any nation. They don’t know his ordinances. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 148, 1, 'PSA.148.1', 'Praise the LORD! Praise the LORD from the heavens! Praise him in the heights!'),
('PSA', 148, 2, 'PSA.148.2', 'Praise him, all his angels! Praise him, all his army!'),
('PSA', 148, 3, 'PSA.148.3', 'Praise him, sun and moon! Praise him, all you shining stars!'),
('PSA', 148, 4, 'PSA.148.4', 'Praise him, you heavens of heavens, you waters that are above the heavens.'),
('PSA', 148, 5, 'PSA.148.5', 'Let them praise the LORD’s name, for he commanded, and they were created.'),
('PSA', 148, 6, 'PSA.148.6', 'He has also established them forever and ever. He has made a decree which will not pass away.'),
('PSA', 148, 7, 'PSA.148.7', 'Praise the LORD from the earth, you great sea creatures, and all depths,'),
('PSA', 148, 8, 'PSA.148.8', 'lightning and hail, snow and clouds, stormy wind, fulfilling his word,'),
('PSA', 148, 9, 'PSA.148.9', 'mountains and all hills, fruit trees and all cedars,'),
('PSA', 148, 10, 'PSA.148.10', 'wild animals and all livestock, small creatures and flying birds,'),
('PSA', 148, 11, 'PSA.148.11', 'kings of the earth and all peoples, princes and all judges of the earth,'),
('PSA', 148, 12, 'PSA.148.12', 'both young men and maidens, old men and children.'),
('PSA', 148, 13, 'PSA.148.13', 'Let them praise the LORD’s name, for his name alone is exalted. His glory is above the earth and the heavens.'),
('PSA', 148, 14, 'PSA.148.14', 'He has lifted up the horn of his people, the praise of all his saints, even of the children of Israel, a people near to him. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 149, 1, 'PSA.149.1', 'Praise the LORD! Sing to the LORD a new song, his praise in the assembly of the saints.'),
('PSA', 149, 2, 'PSA.149.2', 'Let Israel rejoice in him who made them. Let the children of Zion be joyful in their King.'),
('PSA', 149, 3, 'PSA.149.3', 'Let them praise his name in the dance! Let them sing praises to him with tambourine and harp!'),
('PSA', 149, 4, 'PSA.149.4', 'For the LORD takes pleasure in his people. He crowns the humble with salvation.'),
('PSA', 149, 5, 'PSA.149.5', 'Let the saints rejoice in honor. Let them sing for joy on their beds.'),
('PSA', 149, 6, 'PSA.149.6', 'May the high praises of God be in their mouths, and a two-edged sword in their hand,'),
('PSA', 149, 7, 'PSA.149.7', 'to execute vengeance on the nations, and punishments on the peoples;'),
('PSA', 149, 8, 'PSA.149.8', 'to bind their kings with chains, and their nobles with fetters of iron;'),
('PSA', 149, 9, 'PSA.149.9', 'to execute on them the written judgment. All his saints have this honor. Praise the LORD!'),
('PSA', 150, 1, 'PSA.150.1', 'Praise the LORD! Praise God in his sanctuary! Praise him in his heavens for his acts of power!'),
('PSA', 150, 2, 'PSA.150.2', 'Praise him for his mighty acts! Praise him according to his excellent greatness!'),
('PSA', 150, 3, 'PSA.150.3', 'Praise him with the sounding of the trumpet! Praise him with harp and lyre!'),
('PSA', 150, 4, 'PSA.150.4', 'Praise him with tambourine and dancing! Praise him with stringed instruments and flute!'),
('PSA', 150, 5, 'PSA.150.5', 'Praise him with loud cymbals! Praise him with resounding cymbals!'),
('PSA', 150, 6, 'PSA.150.6', 'Let everything that has breath praise the LORD! Praise the LORD!'),
('PRO', 1, 1, 'PRO.1.1', 'The proverbs of Solomon, the son of David, king of Israel:'),
('PRO', 1, 2, 'PRO.1.2', 'to know wisdom and instruction; to discern the words of understanding;'),
('PRO', 1, 3, 'PRO.1.3', 'to receive instruction in wise dealing, in righteousness, justice, and equity;'),
('PRO', 1, 4, 'PRO.1.4', 'to give prudence to the simple, knowledge and discretion to the young man—'),
('PRO', 1, 5, 'PRO.1.5', 'that the wise man may hear, and increase in learning; that the man of understanding may attain to sound counsel;'),
('PRO', 1, 6, 'PRO.1.6', 'to understand a proverb and parables, the words and riddles of the wise.'),
('PRO', 1, 7, 'PRO.1.7', 'The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge, but the foolish despise wisdom and instruction.'),
('PRO', 1, 8, 'PRO.1.8', 'My son, listen to your father’s instruction, and don’t forsake your mother’s teaching;'),
('PRO', 1, 9, 'PRO.1.9', 'for they will be a garland to grace your head, and chains around your neck.'),
('PRO', 1, 10, 'PRO.1.10', 'My son, if sinners entice you, don’t consent.'),
('PRO', 1, 11, 'PRO.1.11', 'If they say, “Come with us. Let’s lie in wait for blood. Let’s lurk secretly for the innocent without cause.'),
('PRO', 1, 12, 'PRO.1.12', 'Let’s swallow them up alive like Sheol, and whole, like those who go down into the pit.'),
('PRO', 1, 13, 'PRO.1.13', 'We’ll find all valuable wealth. We’ll fill our houses with plunder.'),
('PRO', 1, 14, 'PRO.1.14', 'You shall cast your lot among us. We’ll all have one purse”—'),
('PRO', 1, 15, 'PRO.1.15', 'my son, don’t walk on the path with them. Keep your foot from their path,'),
('PRO', 1, 16, 'PRO.1.16', 'for their feet run to evil. They hurry to shed blood.'),
('PRO', 1, 17, 'PRO.1.17', 'For the net is spread in vain in the sight of any bird;'),
('PRO', 1, 18, 'PRO.1.18', 'but these lay in wait for their own blood. They lurk secretly for their own lives.'),
('PRO', 1, 19, 'PRO.1.19', 'So are the ways of everyone who is greedy for gain. It takes away the life of its owners.'),
('PRO', 1, 20, 'PRO.1.20', 'Wisdom calls aloud in the street. She utters her voice in the public squares.'),
('PRO', 1, 21, 'PRO.1.21', 'She calls at the head of noisy places. At the entrance of the city gates, she utters her words:'),
('PRO', 1, 22, 'PRO.1.22', '“How long, you simple ones, will you love simplicity? How long will mockers delight themselves in mockery, and fools hate knowledge?'),
('PRO', 1, 23, 'PRO.1.23', 'Turn at my reproof. Behold, I will pour out my spirit on you. I will make known my words to you.'),
('PRO', 1, 24, 'PRO.1.24', 'Because I have called, and you have refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no one has paid attention;'),
('PRO', 1, 25, 'PRO.1.25', 'but you have ignored all my counsel, and wanted none of my reproof;'),
('PRO', 1, 26, 'PRO.1.26', 'I also will laugh at your disaster. I will mock when calamity overtakes you,'),
('PRO', 1, 27, 'PRO.1.27', 'when calamity overtakes you like a storm, when your disaster comes on like a whirlwind, when distress and anguish come on you.'),
('PRO', 1, 28, 'PRO.1.28', 'Then they will call on me, but I will not answer. They will seek me diligently, but they will not find me,'),
('PRO', 1, 29, 'PRO.1.29', 'because they hated knowledge, and didn’t choose the fear of the LORD.'),
('PRO', 1, 30, 'PRO.1.30', 'They wanted none of my counsel. They despised all my reproof.'),
('PRO', 1, 31, 'PRO.1.31', 'Therefore they will eat of the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own schemes.'),
('PRO', 1, 32, 'PRO.1.32', 'For the backsliding of the simple will kill them. The careless ease of fools will destroy them.'),
('PRO', 1, 33, 'PRO.1.33', 'But whoever listens to me will dwell securely, and will be at ease, without fear of harm.”'),
('PRO', 2, 1, 'PRO.2.1', 'My son, if you will receive my words, and store up my commandments within you,'),
('PRO', 2, 2, 'PRO.2.2', 'so as to turn your ear to wisdom, and apply your heart to understanding;'),
('PRO', 2, 3, 'PRO.2.3', 'yes, if you call out for discernment, and lift up your voice for understanding;'),
('PRO', 2, 4, 'PRO.2.4', 'if you seek her as silver, and search for her as for hidden treasures;'),
('PRO', 2, 5, 'PRO.2.5', 'then you will understand the fear of the LORD, and find the knowledge of God.'),
('PRO', 2, 6, 'PRO.2.6', 'For the LORD gives wisdom. Out of his mouth comes knowledge and understanding.'),
('PRO', 2, 7, 'PRO.2.7', 'He lays up sound wisdom for the upright. He is a shield to those who walk in integrity,'),
('PRO', 2, 8, 'PRO.2.8', 'that he may guard the paths of justice, and preserve the way of his saints.'),
('PRO', 2, 9, 'PRO.2.9', 'Then you will understand righteousness and justice, equity and every good path.'),
('PRO', 2, 10, 'PRO.2.10', 'For wisdom will enter into your heart. Knowledge will be pleasant to your soul.'),
('PRO', 2, 11, 'PRO.2.11', 'Discretion will watch over you. Understanding will keep you,'),
('PRO', 2, 12, 'PRO.2.12', 'to deliver you from the way of evil, from the men who speak perverse things,'),
('PRO', 2, 13, 'PRO.2.13', 'who forsake the paths of uprightness, to walk in the ways of darkness,'),
('PRO', 2, 14, 'PRO.2.14', 'who rejoice to do evil, and delight in the perverseness of evil,'),
('PRO', 2, 15, 'PRO.2.15', 'who are crooked in their ways, and wayward in their paths,'),
('PRO', 2, 16, 'PRO.2.16', 'to deliver you from the strange woman, even from the foreigner who flatters with her words,'),
('PRO', 2, 17, 'PRO.2.17', 'who forsakes the friend of her youth, and forgets the covenant of her God;'),
('PRO', 2, 18, 'PRO.2.18', 'for her house leads down to death, her paths to the departed spirits.'),
('PRO', 2, 19, 'PRO.2.19', 'None who go to her return again, neither do they attain to the paths of life.'),
('PRO', 2, 20, 'PRO.2.20', 'Therefore walk in the way of good men, and keep the paths of the righteous.'),
('PRO', 2, 21, 'PRO.2.21', 'For the upright will dwell in the land. The perfect will remain in it.'),
('PRO', 2, 22, 'PRO.2.22', 'But the wicked will be cut off from the land. The treacherous will be rooted out of it.'),
('PRO', 3, 1, 'PRO.3.1', 'My son, don’t forget my teaching, but let your heart keep my commandments,'),
('PRO', 3, 2, 'PRO.3.2', 'for they will add to you length of days, years of life, and peace.'),
('PRO', 3, 3, 'PRO.3.3', 'Don’t let kindness and truth forsake you. Bind them around your neck. Write them on the tablet of your heart.'),
('PRO', 3, 4, 'PRO.3.4', 'So you will find favor, and good understanding in the sight of God and man.'),
('PRO', 3, 5, 'PRO.3.5', 'Trust in the LORD with all your heart, and don’t lean on your own understanding.'),
('PRO', 3, 6, 'PRO.3.6', 'In all your ways acknowledge him, and he will make your paths straight.'),
('PRO', 3, 7, 'PRO.3.7', 'Don’t be wise in your own eyes. Fear the LORD, and depart from evil.'),
('PRO', 3, 8, 'PRO.3.8', 'It will be health to your body, and nourishment to your bones.'),
('PRO', 3, 9, 'PRO.3.9', 'Honor the LORD with your substance, with the first fruits of all your increase;'),
('PRO', 3, 10, 'PRO.3.10', 'so your barns will be filled with plenty, and your vats will overflow with new wine.'),
('PRO', 3, 11, 'PRO.3.11', 'My son, don’t despise the LORD’s discipline, neither be weary of his correction;'),
('PRO', 3, 12, 'PRO.3.12', 'for whom the LORD loves, he corrects, even as a father reproves the son in whom he delights.'),
('PRO', 3, 13, 'PRO.3.13', 'Happy is the man who finds wisdom, the man who gets understanding.'),
('PRO', 3, 14, 'PRO.3.14', 'For her good profit is better than getting silver, and her return is better than fine gold.'),
('PRO', 3, 15, 'PRO.3.15', 'She is more precious than rubies. None of the things you can desire are to be compared to her.'),
('PRO', 3, 16, 'PRO.3.16', 'Length of days is in her right hand. In her left hand are riches and honor.'),
('PRO', 3, 17, 'PRO.3.17', 'Her ways are ways of pleasantness. All her paths are peace.'),
('PRO', 3, 18, 'PRO.3.18', 'She is a tree of life to those who lay hold of her. Happy is everyone who retains her.'),
('PRO', 3, 19, 'PRO.3.19', 'By wisdom the LORD founded the earth. By understanding, he established the heavens.'),
('PRO', 3, 20, 'PRO.3.20', 'By his knowledge, the depths were broken up, and the skies drop down the dew.'),
('PRO', 3, 21, 'PRO.3.21', 'My son, let them not depart from your eyes. Keep sound wisdom and discretion,'),
('PRO', 3, 22, 'PRO.3.22', 'so they will be life to your soul, and grace for your neck.'),
('PRO', 3, 23, 'PRO.3.23', 'Then you shall walk in your way securely. Your foot won’t stumble.'),
('PRO', 3, 24, 'PRO.3.24', 'When you lie down, you will not be afraid. Yes, you will lie down, and your sleep will be sweet.'),
('PRO', 3, 25, 'PRO.3.25', 'Don’t be afraid of sudden fear, neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it comes;'),
('PRO', 3, 26, 'PRO.3.26', 'for the LORD will be your confidence, and will keep your foot from being taken.'),
('PRO', 3, 27, 'PRO.3.27', 'Don’t withhold good from those to whom it is due, when it is in the power of your hand to do it.'),
('PRO', 3, 28, 'PRO.3.28', 'Don’t say to your neighbor, “Go, and come again; tomorrow I will give it to you,” when you have it by you.'),
('PRO', 3, 29, 'PRO.3.29', 'Don’t devise evil against your neighbor, since he dwells securely by you.'),
('PRO', 3, 30, 'PRO.3.30', 'Don’t strive with a man without cause, if he has done you no harm.'),
('PRO', 3, 31, 'PRO.3.31', 'Don’t envy the man of violence. Choose none of his ways.'),
('PRO', 3, 32, 'PRO.3.32', 'For the perverse is an abomination to the LORD, but his friendship is with the upright.'),
('PRO', 3, 33, 'PRO.3.33', 'The LORD’s curse is in the house of the wicked, but he blesses the habitation of the righteous.'),
('PRO', 3, 34, 'PRO.3.34', 'Surely he mocks the mockers, but he gives grace to the humble.'),
('PRO', 3, 35, 'PRO.3.35', 'The wise will inherit glory, but shame will be the promotion of fools.'),
('PRO', 4, 1, 'PRO.4.1', 'Listen, sons, to a father’s instruction. Pay attention and know understanding;'),
('PRO', 4, 2, 'PRO.4.2', 'for I give you sound learning. Don’t forsake my law.'),
('PRO', 4, 3, 'PRO.4.3', 'For I was a son to my father, tender and an only child in the sight of my mother.'),
('PRO', 4, 4, 'PRO.4.4', 'He taught me, and said to me: “Let your heart retain my words. Keep my commandments, and live.'),
('PRO', 4, 5, 'PRO.4.5', 'Get wisdom. Get understanding. Don’t forget, and don’t deviate from the words of my mouth.'),
('PRO', 4, 6, 'PRO.4.6', 'Don’t forsake her, and she will preserve you. Love her, and she will keep you.'),
('PRO', 4, 7, 'PRO.4.7', 'Wisdom is supreme. Get wisdom. Yes, though it costs all your possessions, get understanding.'),
('PRO', 4, 8, 'PRO.4.8', 'Esteem her, and she will exalt you. She will bring you to honor when you embrace her.'),
('PRO', 4, 9, 'PRO.4.9', 'She will give to your head a garland of grace. She will deliver a crown of splendor to you.”'),
('PRO', 4, 10, 'PRO.4.10', 'Listen, my son, and receive my sayings. The years of your life will be many.'),
('PRO', 4, 11, 'PRO.4.11', 'I have taught you in the way of wisdom. I have led you in straight paths.'),
('PRO', 4, 12, 'PRO.4.12', 'When you go, your steps will not be hampered. When you run, you will not stumble.'),
('PRO', 4, 13, 'PRO.4.13', 'Take firm hold of instruction. Don’t let her go. Keep her, for she is your life.'),
('PRO', 4, 14, 'PRO.4.14', 'Don’t enter into the path of the wicked. Don’t walk in the way of evil men.'),
('PRO', 4, 15, 'PRO.4.15', 'Avoid it, and don’t pass by it. Turn from it, and pass on.'),
('PRO', 4, 16, 'PRO.4.16', 'For they don’t sleep unless they do evil. Their sleep is taken away, unless they make someone fall.'),
('PRO', 4, 17, 'PRO.4.17', 'For they eat the bread of wickedness and drink the wine of violence.'),
('PRO', 4, 18, 'PRO.4.18', 'But the path of the righteous is like the dawning light that shines more and more until the perfect day.'),
('PRO', 4, 19, 'PRO.4.19', 'The way of the wicked is like darkness. They don’t know what they stumble over.'),
('PRO', 4, 20, 'PRO.4.20', 'My son, attend to my words. Turn your ear to my sayings.'),
('PRO', 4, 21, 'PRO.4.21', 'Let them not depart from your eyes. Keep them in the center of your heart.'),
('PRO', 4, 22, 'PRO.4.22', 'For they are life to those who find them, and health to their whole body.'),
('PRO', 4, 23, 'PRO.4.23', 'Keep your heart with all diligence, for out of it is the wellspring of life.'),
('PRO', 4, 24, 'PRO.4.24', 'Put away from yourself a perverse mouth. Put corrupt lips far from you.'),
('PRO', 4, 25, 'PRO.4.25', 'Let your eyes look straight ahead. Fix your gaze directly before you.'),
('PRO', 4, 26, 'PRO.4.26', 'Make the path of your feet level. Let all of your ways be established.'),
('PRO', 4, 27, 'PRO.4.27', 'Don’t turn to the right hand nor to the left. Remove your foot from evil.'),
('PRO', 5, 1, 'PRO.5.1', 'My son, pay attention to my wisdom. Turn your ear to my understanding,'),
('PRO', 5, 2, 'PRO.5.2', 'that you may maintain discretion, that your lips may preserve knowledge.'),
('PRO', 5, 3, 'PRO.5.3', 'For the lips of an adulteress drip honey. Her mouth is smoother than oil,'),
('PRO', 5, 4, 'PRO.5.4', 'but in the end she is as bitter as wormwood, and as sharp as a two-edged sword.'),
('PRO', 5, 5, 'PRO.5.5', 'Her feet go down to death. Her steps lead straight to Sheol.'),
('PRO', 5, 6, 'PRO.5.6', 'She gives no thought to the way of life. Her ways are crooked, and she doesn’t know it.'),
('PRO', 5, 7, 'PRO.5.7', 'Now therefore, my sons, listen to me. Don’t depart from the words of my mouth.'),
('PRO', 5, 8, 'PRO.5.8', 'Remove your way far from her. Don’t come near the door of her house,'),
('PRO', 5, 9, 'PRO.5.9', 'lest you give your honor to others, and your years to the cruel one;'),
('PRO', 5, 10, 'PRO.5.10', 'lest strangers feast on your wealth, and your labors enrich another man’s house.'),
('PRO', 5, 11, 'PRO.5.11', 'You will groan at your latter end, when your flesh and your body are consumed,'),
('PRO', 5, 12, 'PRO.5.12', 'and say, “How I have hated instruction, and my heart despised reproof.'),
('PRO', 5, 13, 'PRO.5.13', 'I haven’t obeyed the voice of my teachers, nor turned my ear to those who instructed me!'),
('PRO', 5, 14, 'PRO.5.14', 'I have come to the brink of utter ruin, among the gathered assembly.”'),
('PRO', 5, 15, 'PRO.5.15', 'Drink water out of your own cistern, running water out of your own well.'),
('PRO', 5, 16, 'PRO.5.16', 'Should your springs overflow in the streets, streams of water in the public squares?'),
('PRO', 5, 17, 'PRO.5.17', 'Let them be for yourself alone, not for strangers with you.'),
('PRO', 5, 18, 'PRO.5.18', 'Let your spring be blessed. Rejoice in the wife of your youth.'),
('PRO', 5, 19, 'PRO.5.19', 'A loving doe and a graceful deer— let her breasts satisfy you at all times. Be captivated always with her love.'),
('PRO', 5, 20, 'PRO.5.20', 'For why should you, my son, be captivated with an adulteress? Why embrace the bosom of another?'),
('PRO', 5, 21, 'PRO.5.21', 'For the ways of man are before the LORD’s eyes. He examines all his paths.'),
('PRO', 5, 22, 'PRO.5.22', 'The evil deeds of the wicked ensnare him. The cords of his sin hold him firmly.'),
('PRO', 5, 23, 'PRO.5.23', 'He will die for lack of instruction. In the greatness of his folly, he will go astray.'),
('PRO', 6, 1, 'PRO.6.1', 'My son, if you have become collateral for your neighbor, if you have struck your hands in pledge for a stranger,'),
('PRO', 6, 2, 'PRO.6.2', 'you are trapped by the words of your mouth; you are ensnared with the words of your mouth.'),
('PRO', 6, 3, 'PRO.6.3', 'Do this now, my son, and deliver yourself, since you have come into the hand of your neighbor. Go, humble yourself. Press your plea with your neighbor.'),
('PRO', 6, 4, 'PRO.6.4', 'Give no sleep to your eyes, nor slumber to your eyelids.'),
('PRO', 6, 5, 'PRO.6.5', 'Free yourself, like a gazelle from the hand of the hunter, like a bird from the snare of the fowler.'),
('PRO', 6, 6, 'PRO.6.6', 'Go to the ant, you sluggard. Consider her ways, and be wise;'),
('PRO', 6, 7, 'PRO.6.7', 'which having no chief, overseer, or ruler,'),
('PRO', 6, 8, 'PRO.6.8', 'provides her bread in the summer, and gathers her food in the harvest.'),
('PRO', 6, 9, 'PRO.6.9', 'How long will you sleep, sluggard? When will you arise out of your sleep?'),
('PRO', 6, 10, 'PRO.6.10', 'A little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep—'),
('PRO', 6, 11, 'PRO.6.11', 'so your poverty will come as a robber, and your scarcity as an armed man.'),
('PRO', 6, 12, 'PRO.6.12', 'A worthless person, a man of iniquity, is he who walks with a perverse mouth,'),
('PRO', 6, 13, 'PRO.6.13', 'who winks with his eyes, who signals with his feet, who motions with his fingers,'),
('PRO', 6, 14, 'PRO.6.14', 'in whose heart is perverseness, who devises evil continually, who always sows discord.'),
('PRO', 6, 15, 'PRO.6.15', 'Therefore his calamity will come suddenly. He will be broken suddenly, and that without remedy.'),
('PRO', 6, 16, 'PRO.6.16', 'There are six things which the LORD hates; yes, seven which are an abomination to him:'),
('PRO', 6, 17, 'PRO.6.17', 'arrogant eyes, a lying tongue, hands that shed innocent blood,'),
('PRO', 6, 18, 'PRO.6.18', 'a heart that devises wicked schemes, feet that are swift in running to mischief,'),
('PRO', 6, 19, 'PRO.6.19', 'a false witness who utters lies, and he who sows discord among brothers.'),
('PRO', 6, 20, 'PRO.6.20', 'My son, keep your father’s commandment, and don’t forsake your mother’s teaching.'),
('PRO', 6, 21, 'PRO.6.21', 'Bind them continually on your heart. Tie them around your neck.'),
('PRO', 6, 22, 'PRO.6.22', 'When you walk, it will lead you. When you sleep, it will watch over you. When you awake, it will talk with you.'),
('PRO', 6, 23, 'PRO.6.23', 'For the commandment is a lamp, and the law is light. Reproofs of instruction are the way of life,'),
('PRO', 6, 24, 'PRO.6.24', 'to keep you from the immoral woman, from the flattery of the wayward wife’s tongue.'),
('PRO', 6, 25, 'PRO.6.25', 'Don’t lust after her beauty in your heart, neither let her captivate you with her eyelids.'),
('PRO', 6, 26, 'PRO.6.26', 'For a prostitute reduces you to a piece of bread. The adulteress hunts for your precious life.'),
('PRO', 6, 27, 'PRO.6.27', 'Can a man scoop fire into his lap, and his clothes not be burned?'),
('PRO', 6, 28, 'PRO.6.28', 'Or can one walk on hot coals, and his feet not be scorched?'),
('PRO', 6, 29, 'PRO.6.29', 'So is he who goes in to his neighbor’s wife. Whoever touches her will not be unpunished.'),
('PRO', 6, 30, 'PRO.6.30', 'Men don’t despise a thief if he steals to satisfy himself when he is hungry,'),
('PRO', 6, 31, 'PRO.6.31', 'but if he is found, he shall restore seven times. He shall give all the wealth of his house.'),
('PRO', 6, 32, 'PRO.6.32', 'He who commits adultery with a woman is void of understanding. He who does it destroys his own soul.'),
('PRO', 6, 33, 'PRO.6.33', 'He will get wounds and dishonor. His reproach will not be wiped away.'),
('PRO', 6, 34, 'PRO.6.34', 'For jealousy arouses the fury of the husband. He won’t spare in the day of vengeance.'),
('PRO', 6, 35, 'PRO.6.35', 'He won’t regard any ransom, neither will he rest content, though you give many gifts.'),
('PRO', 7, 1, 'PRO.7.1', 'My son, keep my words. Lay up my commandments within you.'),
('PRO', 7, 2, 'PRO.7.2', 'Keep my commandments and live! Guard my teaching as the apple of your eye.'),
('PRO', 7, 3, 'PRO.7.3', 'Bind them on your fingers. Write them on the tablet of your heart.'),
('PRO', 7, 4, 'PRO.7.4', 'Tell wisdom, “You are my sister.” Call understanding your relative,'),
('PRO', 7, 5, 'PRO.7.5', 'that they may keep you from the strange woman, from the foreigner who flatters with her words.'),
('PRO', 7, 6, 'PRO.7.6', 'For at the window of my house, I looked out through my lattice.'),
('PRO', 7, 7, 'PRO.7.7', 'I saw among the simple ones. I discerned among the youths a young man void of understanding,'),
('PRO', 7, 8, 'PRO.7.8', 'passing through the street near her corner, he went the way to her house,'),
('PRO', 7, 9, 'PRO.7.9', 'in the twilight, in the evening of the day, in the middle of the night and in the darkness.'),
('PRO', 7, 10, 'PRO.7.10', 'Behold, there a woman met him with the attire of a prostitute, and with crafty intent.'),
('PRO', 7, 11, 'PRO.7.11', 'She is loud and defiant. Her feet don’t stay in her house.'),
('PRO', 7, 12, 'PRO.7.12', 'Now she is in the streets, now in the squares, and lurking at every corner.'),
('PRO', 7, 13, 'PRO.7.13', 'So she caught him, and kissed him. With an impudent face she said to him:'),
('PRO', 7, 14, 'PRO.7.14', '“Sacrifices of peace offerings are with me. Today I have paid my vows.'),
('PRO', 7, 15, 'PRO.7.15', 'Therefore I came out to meet you, to diligently seek your face, and I have found you.'),
('PRO', 7, 16, 'PRO.7.16', 'I have spread my couch with carpets of tapestry, with striped cloths of the yarn of Egypt.'),
('PRO', 7, 17, 'PRO.7.17', 'I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.'),
('PRO', 7, 18, 'PRO.7.18', 'Come, let’s take our fill of loving until the morning. Let’s solace ourselves with loving.'),
('PRO', 7, 19, 'PRO.7.19', 'For my husband isn’t at home. He has gone on a long journey.'),
('PRO', 7, 20, 'PRO.7.20', 'He has taken a bag of money with him. He will come home at the full moon.”'),
('PRO', 7, 21, 'PRO.7.21', 'With persuasive words, she led him astray. With the flattering of her lips, she seduced him.'),
('PRO', 7, 22, 'PRO.7.22', 'He followed her immediately, as an ox goes to the slaughter, as a fool stepping into a noose.'),
('PRO', 7, 23, 'PRO.7.23', 'Until an arrow strikes through his liver, as a bird hurries to the snare, and doesn’t know that it will cost his life.'),
('PRO', 7, 24, 'PRO.7.24', 'Now therefore, sons, listen to me. Pay attention to the words of my mouth.'),
('PRO', 7, 25, 'PRO.7.25', 'Don’t let your heart turn to her ways. Don’t go astray in her paths,'),
('PRO', 7, 26, 'PRO.7.26', 'for she has thrown down many wounded. Yes, all her slain are a mighty army.'),
('PRO', 7, 27, 'PRO.7.27', 'Her house is the way to Sheol, going down to the rooms of death.'),
('PRO', 8, 1, 'PRO.8.1', 'Doesn’t wisdom cry out? Doesn’t understanding raise her voice?'),
('PRO', 8, 2, 'PRO.8.2', 'On the top of high places by the way, where the paths meet, she stands.'),
('PRO', 8, 3, 'PRO.8.3', 'Beside the gates, at the entry of the city, at the entry doors, she cries aloud:'),
('PRO', 8, 4, 'PRO.8.4', '“I call to you men! I send my voice to the sons of mankind.'),
('PRO', 8, 5, 'PRO.8.5', 'You simple, understand prudence! You fools, be of an understanding heart!'),
('PRO', 8, 6, 'PRO.8.6', 'Hear, for I will speak excellent things. The opening of my lips is for right things.'),
('PRO', 8, 7, 'PRO.8.7', 'For my mouth speaks truth. Wickedness is an abomination to my lips.'),
('PRO', 8, 8, 'PRO.8.8', 'All the words of my mouth are in righteousness. There is nothing crooked or perverse in them.'),
('PRO', 8, 9, 'PRO.8.9', 'They are all plain to him who understands, right to those who find knowledge.'),
('PRO', 8, 10, 'PRO.8.10', 'Receive my instruction rather than silver, knowledge rather than choice gold.'),
('PRO', 8, 11, 'PRO.8.11', 'For wisdom is better than rubies. All the things that may be desired can’t be compared to it.'),
('PRO', 8, 12, 'PRO.8.12', '“I, wisdom, have made prudence my dwelling. Find out knowledge and discretion.'),
('PRO', 8, 13, 'PRO.8.13', 'The fear of the LORD is to hate evil. I hate pride, arrogance, the evil way, and the perverse mouth.'),
('PRO', 8, 14, 'PRO.8.14', 'Counsel and sound knowledge are mine. I have understanding and power.'),
('PRO', 8, 15, 'PRO.8.15', 'By me kings reign, and princes decree justice.'),
('PRO', 8, 16, 'PRO.8.16', 'By me princes rule, nobles, and all the righteous rulers of the earth.'),
('PRO', 8, 17, 'PRO.8.17', 'I love those who love me. Those who seek me diligently will find me.'),
('PRO', 8, 18, 'PRO.8.18', 'With me are riches, honor, enduring wealth, and prosperity.'),
('PRO', 8, 19, 'PRO.8.19', 'My fruit is better than gold, yes, than fine gold, my yield than choice silver.'),
('PRO', 8, 20, 'PRO.8.20', 'I walk in the way of righteousness, in the middle of the paths of justice,'),
('PRO', 8, 21, 'PRO.8.21', 'that I may give wealth to those who love me. I fill their treasuries.'),
('PRO', 8, 22, 'PRO.8.22', '“The LORD possessed me in the beginning of his work, before his deeds of old.'),
('PRO', 8, 23, 'PRO.8.23', 'I was set up from everlasting, from the beginning, before the earth existed.'),
('PRO', 8, 24, 'PRO.8.24', 'When there were no depths, I was born, when there were no springs abounding with water.'),
('PRO', 8, 25, 'PRO.8.25', 'Before the mountains were settled in place, before the hills, I was born;'),
('PRO', 8, 26, 'PRO.8.26', 'while as yet he had not made the earth, nor the fields, nor the beginning of the dust of the world.'),
('PRO', 8, 27, 'PRO.8.27', 'When he established the heavens, I was there. When he set a circle on the surface of the deep,'),
('PRO', 8, 28, 'PRO.8.28', 'when he established the clouds above, when the springs of the deep became strong,'),
('PRO', 8, 29, 'PRO.8.29', 'when he gave to the sea its boundary, that the waters should not violate his commandment, when he marked out the foundations of the earth,'),
('PRO', 8, 30, 'PRO.8.30', 'then I was the craftsman by his side. I was a delight day by day, always rejoicing before him,'),
('PRO', 8, 31, 'PRO.8.31', 'rejoicing in his whole world. My delight was with the sons of men.'),
('PRO', 8, 32, 'PRO.8.32', '“Now therefore, my sons, listen to me, for blessed are those who keep my ways.'),
('PRO', 8, 33, 'PRO.8.33', 'Hear instruction, and be wise. Don’t refuse it.'),
('PRO', 8, 34, 'PRO.8.34', 'Blessed is the man who hears me, watching daily at my gates, waiting at my door posts.'),
('PRO', 8, 35, 'PRO.8.35', 'For whoever finds me finds life, and will obtain favor from the LORD.'),
('PRO', 8, 36, 'PRO.8.36', 'But he who sins against me wrongs his own soul. All those who hate me love death.”'),
('PRO', 9, 1, 'PRO.9.1', 'Wisdom has built her house. She has carved out her seven pillars.'),
('PRO', 9, 2, 'PRO.9.2', 'She has prepared her meat. She has mixed her wine. She has also set her table.'),
('PRO', 9, 3, 'PRO.9.3', 'She has sent out her maidens. She cries from the highest places of the city:'),
('PRO', 9, 4, 'PRO.9.4', '“Whoever is simple, let him turn in here!” As for him who is void of understanding, she says to him,'),
('PRO', 9, 5, 'PRO.9.5', '“Come, eat some of my bread, Drink some of the wine which I have mixed!'),
('PRO', 9, 6, 'PRO.9.6', 'Leave your simple ways, and live. Walk in the way of understanding.”'),
('PRO', 9, 7, 'PRO.9.7', 'One who corrects a mocker invites insult. One who reproves a wicked man invites abuse.'),
('PRO', 9, 8, 'PRO.9.8', 'Don’t reprove a scoffer, lest he hate you. Reprove a wise person, and he will love you.'),
('PRO', 9, 9, 'PRO.9.9', 'Instruct a wise person, and he will be still wiser. Teach a righteous person, and he will increase in learning.'),
('PRO', 9, 10, 'PRO.9.10', 'The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom. The knowledge of the Holy One is understanding.'),
('PRO', 9, 11, 'PRO.9.11', 'For by me your days will be multiplied. The years of your life will be increased.'),
('PRO', 9, 12, 'PRO.9.12', 'If you are wise, you are wise for yourself. If you mock, you alone will bear it.'),
('PRO', 9, 13, 'PRO.9.13', 'The foolish woman is loud, undisciplined, and knows nothing.'),
('PRO', 9, 14, 'PRO.9.14', 'She sits at the door of her house, on a seat in the high places of the city,'),
('PRO', 9, 15, 'PRO.9.15', 'to call to those who pass by, who go straight on their ways,'),
('PRO', 9, 16, 'PRO.9.16', '“Whoever is simple, let him turn in here.” As for him who is void of understanding, she says to him,'),
('PRO', 9, 17, 'PRO.9.17', '“Stolen water is sweet. Food eaten in secret is pleasant.”'),
('PRO', 9, 18, 'PRO.9.18', 'But he doesn’t know that the departed spirits are there, that her guests are in the depths of Sheol.'),
('PRO', 10, 1, 'PRO.10.1', 'The proverbs of Solomon. A wise son makes a glad father; but a foolish son brings grief to his mother.'),
('PRO', 10, 2, 'PRO.10.2', 'Treasures of wickedness profit nothing, but righteousness delivers from death.'),
('PRO', 10, 3, 'PRO.10.3', 'The LORD will not allow the soul of the righteous to go hungry, but he thrusts away the desire of the wicked.'),
('PRO', 10, 4, 'PRO.10.4', 'He becomes poor who works with a lazy hand, but the hand of the diligent brings wealth.'),
('PRO', 10, 5, 'PRO.10.5', 'He who gathers in summer is a wise son, but he who sleeps during the harvest is a son who causes shame.'),
('PRO', 10, 6, 'PRO.10.6', 'Blessings are on the head of the righteous, but violence covers the mouth of the wicked.'),
('PRO', 10, 7, 'PRO.10.7', 'The memory of the righteous is blessed, but the name of the wicked will rot.'),
('PRO', 10, 8, 'PRO.10.8', 'The wise in heart accept commandments, but a chattering fool will fall.'),
('PRO', 10, 9, 'PRO.10.9', 'He who walks blamelessly walks surely, but he who perverts his ways will be found out.'),
('PRO', 10, 10, 'PRO.10.10', 'One who winks with the eye causes sorrow, but a chattering fool will fall.'),
('PRO', 10, 11, 'PRO.10.11', 'The mouth of the righteous is a spring of life, but violence covers the mouth of the wicked.'),
('PRO', 10, 12, 'PRO.10.12', 'Hatred stirs up strife, but love covers all wrongs.'),
('PRO', 10, 13, 'PRO.10.13', 'Wisdom is found on the lips of him who has discernment, but a rod is for the back of him who is void of understanding.'),
('PRO', 10, 14, 'PRO.10.14', 'Wise men lay up knowledge, but the mouth of the foolish is near ruin.'),
('PRO', 10, 15, 'PRO.10.15', 'The rich man’s wealth is his strong city. The destruction of the poor is their poverty.'),
('PRO', 10, 16, 'PRO.10.16', 'The labor of the righteous leads to life. The increase of the wicked leads to sin.'),
('PRO', 10, 17, 'PRO.10.17', 'He is in the way of life who heeds correction, but he who forsakes reproof leads others astray.'),
('PRO', 10, 18, 'PRO.10.18', 'He who hides hatred has lying lips. He who utters a slander is a fool.'),
('PRO', 10, 19, 'PRO.10.19', 'In the multitude of words there is no lack of disobedience, but he who restrains his lips does wisely.'),
('PRO', 10, 20, 'PRO.10.20', 'The tongue of the righteous is like choice silver. The heart of the wicked is of little worth.'),
('PRO', 10, 21, 'PRO.10.21', 'The lips of the righteous feed many, but the foolish die for lack of understanding.'),
('PRO', 10, 22, 'PRO.10.22', 'The LORD’s blessing brings wealth, and he adds no trouble to it.'),
('PRO', 10, 23, 'PRO.10.23', 'It is a fool’s pleasure to do wickedness, but wisdom is a man of understanding’s pleasure.'),
('PRO', 10, 24, 'PRO.10.24', 'What the wicked fear will overtake them, but the desire of the righteous will be granted.'),
('PRO', 10, 25, 'PRO.10.25', 'When the whirlwind passes, the wicked is no more; but the righteous stand firm forever.'),
('PRO', 10, 26, 'PRO.10.26', 'As vinegar to the teeth, and as smoke to the eyes, so is the sluggard to those who send him.'),
('PRO', 10, 27, 'PRO.10.27', 'The fear of the LORD prolongs days, but the years of the wicked shall be shortened.'),
('PRO', 10, 28, 'PRO.10.28', 'The prospect of the righteous is joy, but the hope of the wicked will perish.'),
('PRO', 10, 29, 'PRO.10.29', 'The way of the LORD is a stronghold to the upright, but it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity.'),
('PRO', 10, 30, 'PRO.10.30', 'The righteous will never be removed, but the wicked will not dwell in the land.'),
('PRO', 10, 31, 'PRO.10.31', 'The mouth of the righteous produces wisdom, but the perverse tongue will be cut off.'),
('PRO', 10, 32, 'PRO.10.32', 'The lips of the righteous know what is acceptable, but the mouth of the wicked is perverse.'),
('PRO', 11, 1, 'PRO.11.1', 'A false balance is an abomination to the LORD, but accurate weights are his delight.'),
('PRO', 11, 2, 'PRO.11.2', 'When pride comes, then comes shame, but with humility comes wisdom.'),
('PRO', 11, 3, 'PRO.11.3', 'The integrity of the upright shall guide them, but the perverseness of the treacherous shall destroy them.'),
('PRO', 11, 4, 'PRO.11.4', 'Riches don’t profit in the day of wrath, but righteousness delivers from death.'),
('PRO', 11, 5, 'PRO.11.5', 'The righteousness of the blameless will direct his way, but the wicked shall fall by his own wickedness.'),
('PRO', 11, 6, 'PRO.11.6', 'The righteousness of the upright shall deliver them, but the unfaithful will be trapped by evil desires.'),
('PRO', 11, 7, 'PRO.11.7', 'When a wicked man dies, hope perishes, and expectation of power comes to nothing.'),
('PRO', 11, 8, 'PRO.11.8', 'A righteous person is delivered out of trouble, and the wicked takes his place.'),
('PRO', 11, 9, 'PRO.11.9', 'With his mouth the godless man destroys his neighbor, but the righteous will be delivered through knowledge.'),
('PRO', 11, 10, 'PRO.11.10', 'When it goes well with the righteous, the city rejoices. When the wicked perish, there is shouting.'),
('PRO', 11, 11, 'PRO.11.11', 'By the blessing of the upright, the city is exalted, but it is overthrown by the mouth of the wicked.'),
('PRO', 11, 12, 'PRO.11.12', 'One who despises his neighbor is void of wisdom, but a man of understanding holds his peace.'),
('PRO', 11, 13, 'PRO.11.13', 'One who brings gossip betrays a confidence, but one who is of a trustworthy spirit is one who keeps a secret.'),
('PRO', 11, 14, 'PRO.11.14', 'Where there is no wise guidance, the nation falls, but in the multitude of counselors there is victory.'),
('PRO', 11, 15, 'PRO.11.15', 'He who is collateral for a stranger will suffer for it, but he who refuses pledges of collateral is secure.'),
('PRO', 11, 16, 'PRO.11.16', 'A gracious woman obtains honor, but violent men obtain riches.'),
('PRO', 11, 17, 'PRO.11.17', 'The merciful man does good to his own soul, but he who is cruel troubles his own flesh.'),
('PRO', 11, 18, 'PRO.11.18', 'Wicked people earn deceitful wages, but one who sows righteousness reaps a sure reward.'),
('PRO', 11, 19, 'PRO.11.19', 'He who is truly righteous gets life. He who pursues evil gets death.'),
('PRO', 11, 20, 'PRO.11.20', 'Those who are perverse in heart are an abomination to the LORD, but those whose ways are blameless are his delight.'),
('PRO', 11, 21, 'PRO.11.21', 'Most certainly, the evil man will not be unpunished, but the offspring of the righteous will be delivered.'),
('PRO', 11, 22, 'PRO.11.22', 'Like a gold ring in a pig’s snout, is a beautiful woman who lacks discretion.'),
('PRO', 11, 23, 'PRO.11.23', 'The desire of the righteous is only good. The expectation of the wicked is wrath.'),
('PRO', 11, 24, 'PRO.11.24', 'There is one who scatters, and increases yet more. There is one who withholds more than is appropriate, but gains poverty.'),
('PRO', 11, 25, 'PRO.11.25', 'The liberal soul shall be made fat. He who waters shall be watered also himself.'),
('PRO', 11, 26, 'PRO.11.26', 'People curse someone who withholds grain, but blessing will be on the head of him who sells it.'),
('PRO', 11, 27, 'PRO.11.27', 'He who diligently seeks good seeks favor, but he who searches after evil, it shall come to him.'),
('PRO', 11, 28, 'PRO.11.28', 'He who trusts in his riches will fall, but the righteous shall flourish as the green leaf.'),
('PRO', 11, 29, 'PRO.11.29', 'He who troubles his own house shall inherit the wind. The foolish shall be servant to the wise of heart.'),
('PRO', 11, 30, 'PRO.11.30', 'The fruit of the righteous is a tree of life. He who is wise wins souls.'),
('PRO', 11, 31, 'PRO.11.31', 'Behold, the righteous shall be repaid on the earth, how much more the wicked and the sinner!'),
('PRO', 12, 1, 'PRO.12.1', 'Whoever loves correction loves knowledge, but he who hates reproof is stupid.'),
('PRO', 12, 2, 'PRO.12.2', 'A good man shall obtain favor from the LORD, but he will condemn a man of wicked plans.'),
('PRO', 12, 3, 'PRO.12.3', 'A man shall not be established by wickedness, but the root of the righteous shall not be moved.'),
('PRO', 12, 4, 'PRO.12.4', 'A worthy woman is the crown of her husband, but a disgraceful wife is as rottenness in his bones.'),
('PRO', 12, 5, 'PRO.12.5', 'The thoughts of the righteous are just, but the advice of the wicked is deceitful.'),
('PRO', 12, 6, 'PRO.12.6', 'The words of the wicked are about lying in wait for blood, but the speech of the upright rescues them.'),
('PRO', 12, 7, 'PRO.12.7', 'The wicked are overthrown, and are no more, but the house of the righteous shall stand.'),
('PRO', 12, 8, 'PRO.12.8', 'A man shall be commended according to his wisdom, but he who has a warped mind shall be despised.'),
('PRO', 12, 9, 'PRO.12.9', 'Better is he who is little known, and has a servant, than he who honors himself and lacks bread.'),
('PRO', 12, 10, 'PRO.12.10', 'A righteous man respects the life of his animal, but the tender mercies of the wicked are cruel.'),
('PRO', 12, 11, 'PRO.12.11', 'He who tills his land shall have plenty of bread, but he who chases fantasies is void of understanding.'),
('PRO', 12, 12, 'PRO.12.12', 'The wicked desires the plunder of evil men, but the root of the righteous flourishes.'),
('PRO', 12, 13, 'PRO.12.13', 'An evil man is trapped by sinfulness of lips, but the righteous shall come out of trouble.'),
('PRO', 12, 14, 'PRO.12.14', 'A man shall be satisfied with good by the fruit of his mouth. The work of a man’s hands shall be rewarded to him.'),
('PRO', 12, 15, 'PRO.12.15', 'The way of a fool is right in his own eyes, but he who is wise listens to counsel.'),
('PRO', 12, 16, 'PRO.12.16', 'A fool shows his annoyance the same day, but one who overlooks an insult is prudent.'),
('PRO', 12, 17, 'PRO.12.17', 'He who is truthful testifies honestly, but a false witness lies.'),
('PRO', 12, 18, 'PRO.12.18', 'There is one who speaks rashly like the piercing of a sword, but the tongue of the wise heals.'),
('PRO', 12, 19, 'PRO.12.19', 'Truth’s lips will be established forever, but a lying tongue is only momentary.'),
('PRO', 12, 20, 'PRO.12.20', 'Deceit is in the heart of those who plot evil, but joy comes to the promoters of peace.'),
('PRO', 12, 21, 'PRO.12.21', 'No mischief shall happen to the righteous, but the wicked shall be filled with evil.'),
('PRO', 12, 22, 'PRO.12.22', 'Lying lips are an abomination to the LORD, but those who do the truth are his delight.'),
('PRO', 12, 23, 'PRO.12.23', 'A prudent man keeps his knowledge, but the hearts of fools proclaim foolishness.'),
('PRO', 12, 24, 'PRO.12.24', 'The hands of the diligent ones shall rule, but laziness ends in slave labor.'),
('PRO', 12, 25, 'PRO.12.25', 'Anxiety in a man’s heart weighs it down, but a kind word makes it glad.'),
('PRO', 12, 26, 'PRO.12.26', 'A righteous person is cautious in friendship, but the way of the wicked leads them astray.'),
('PRO', 12, 27, 'PRO.12.27', 'The slothful man doesn’t roast his game, but the possessions of diligent men are prized.'),
('PRO', 12, 28, 'PRO.12.28', 'In the way of righteousness is life; in its path there is no death.'),
('PRO', 13, 1, 'PRO.13.1', 'A wise son listens to his father’s instruction, but a scoffer doesn’t listen to rebuke.'),
('PRO', 13, 2, 'PRO.13.2', 'By the fruit of his lips, a man enjoys good things, but the unfaithful crave violence.'),
('PRO', 13, 3, 'PRO.13.3', 'He who guards his mouth guards his soul. One who opens wide his lips comes to ruin.'),
('PRO', 13, 4, 'PRO.13.4', 'The soul of the sluggard desires, and has nothing, but the desire of the diligent shall be fully satisfied.'),
('PRO', 13, 5, 'PRO.13.5', 'A righteous man hates lies, but a wicked man brings shame and disgrace.'),
('PRO', 13, 6, 'PRO.13.6', 'Righteousness guards the way of integrity, but wickedness overthrows the sinner.'),
('PRO', 13, 7, 'PRO.13.7', 'There are some who pretend to be rich, yet have nothing. There are some who pretend to be poor, yet have great wealth.'),
('PRO', 13, 8, 'PRO.13.8', 'The ransom of a man’s life is his riches, but the poor hear no threats.'),
('PRO', 13, 9, 'PRO.13.9', 'The light of the righteous shines brightly, but the lamp of the wicked is snuffed out.'),
('PRO', 13, 10, 'PRO.13.10', 'Pride only breeds quarrels, but wisdom is with people who take advice.'),
('PRO', 13, 11, 'PRO.13.11', 'Wealth gained dishonestly dwindles away, but he who gathers by hand makes it grow.'),
('PRO', 13, 12, 'PRO.13.12', 'Hope deferred makes the heart sick, but when longing is fulfilled, it is a tree of life.'),
('PRO', 13, 13, 'PRO.13.13', 'Whoever despises instruction will pay for it, but he who respects a command will be rewarded.'),
('PRO', 13, 14, 'PRO.13.14', 'The teaching of the wise is a spring of life, to turn from the snares of death.'),
('PRO', 13, 15, 'PRO.13.15', 'Good understanding wins favor, but the way of the unfaithful is hard.'),
('PRO', 13, 16, 'PRO.13.16', 'Every prudent man acts from knowledge, but a fool exposes folly.'),
('PRO', 13, 17, 'PRO.13.17', 'A wicked messenger falls into trouble, but a trustworthy envoy gains healing.'),
('PRO', 13, 18, 'PRO.13.18', 'Poverty and shame come to him who refuses discipline, but he who heeds correction shall be honored.'),
('PRO', 13, 19, 'PRO.13.19', 'Longing fulfilled is sweet to the soul, but fools detest turning from evil.'),
('PRO', 13, 20, 'PRO.13.20', 'One who walks with wise men grows wise, but a companion of fools suffers harm.'),
('PRO', 13, 21, 'PRO.13.21', 'Misfortune pursues sinners, but prosperity rewards the righteous.'),
('PRO', 13, 22, 'PRO.13.22', 'A good man leaves an inheritance to his children’s children, but the wealth of the sinner is stored for the righteous.'),
('PRO', 13, 23, 'PRO.13.23', 'An abundance of food is in poor people’s fields, but injustice sweeps it away.'),
('PRO', 13, 24, 'PRO.13.24', 'One who spares the rod hates his son, but one who loves him is careful to discipline him.'),
('PRO', 13, 25, 'PRO.13.25', 'The righteous one eats to the satisfying of his soul, but the belly of the wicked goes hungry.'),
('PRO', 14, 1, 'PRO.14.1', 'Every wise woman builds her house, but the foolish one tears it down with her own hands.'),
('PRO', 14, 2, 'PRO.14.2', 'He who walks in his uprightness fears the LORD, but he who is perverse in his ways despises him.'),
('PRO', 14, 3, 'PRO.14.3', 'The fool’s talk brings a rod to his back, but the lips of the wise protect them.'),
('PRO', 14, 4, 'PRO.14.4', 'Where no oxen are, the crib is clean, but much increase is by the strength of the ox.'),
('PRO', 14, 5, 'PRO.14.5', 'A truthful witness will not lie, but a false witness pours out lies.'),
('PRO', 14, 6, 'PRO.14.6', 'A scoffer seeks wisdom, and doesn’t find it, but knowledge comes easily to a discerning person.'),
('PRO', 14, 7, 'PRO.14.7', 'Stay away from a foolish man, for you won’t find knowledge on his lips.'),
('PRO', 14, 8, 'PRO.14.8', 'The wisdom of the prudent is to think about his way, but the folly of fools is deceit.'),
('PRO', 14, 9, 'PRO.14.9', 'Fools mock at making atonement for sins, but among the upright there is good will.'),
('PRO', 14, 10, 'PRO.14.10', 'The heart knows its own bitterness and joy; he will not share these with a stranger.'),
('PRO', 14, 11, 'PRO.14.11', 'The house of the wicked will be overthrown, but the tent of the upright will flourish.'),
('PRO', 14, 12, 'PRO.14.12', 'There is a way which seems right to a man, but in the end it leads to death.'),
('PRO', 14, 13, 'PRO.14.13', 'Even in laughter the heart may be sorrowful, and mirth may end in heaviness.'),
('PRO', 14, 14, 'PRO.14.14', 'The unfaithful will be repaid for his own ways; likewise a good man will be rewarded for his ways.'),
('PRO', 14, 15, 'PRO.14.15', 'A simple man believes everything, but the prudent man carefully considers his ways.'),
('PRO', 14, 16, 'PRO.14.16', 'A wise man fears and shuns evil, but the fool is hot headed and reckless.'),
('PRO', 14, 17, 'PRO.14.17', 'He who is quick to become angry will commit folly, and a crafty man is hated.'),
('PRO', 14, 18, 'PRO.14.18', 'The simple inherit folly, but the prudent are crowned with knowledge.'),
('PRO', 14, 19, 'PRO.14.19', 'The evil bow down before the good, and the wicked at the gates of the righteous.'),
('PRO', 14, 20, 'PRO.14.20', 'The poor person is shunned even by his own neighbor, but the rich person has many friends.'),
('PRO', 14, 21, 'PRO.14.21', 'He who despises his neighbor sins, but he who has pity on the poor is blessed.'),
('PRO', 14, 22, 'PRO.14.22', 'Don’t they go astray who plot evil? But love and faithfulness belong to those who plan good.'),
('PRO', 14, 23, 'PRO.14.23', 'In all hard work there is profit, but the talk of the lips leads only to poverty.'),
('PRO', 14, 24, 'PRO.14.24', 'The crown of the wise is their riches, but the folly of fools crowns them with folly.'),
('PRO', 14, 25, 'PRO.14.25', 'A truthful witness saves souls, but a false witness is deceitful.'),
('PRO', 14, 26, 'PRO.14.26', 'In the fear of the LORD is a secure fortress, and he will be a refuge for his children.'),
('PRO', 14, 27, 'PRO.14.27', 'The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life, turning people from the snares of death.'),
('PRO', 14, 28, 'PRO.14.28', 'In the multitude of people is the king’s glory, but in the lack of people is the destruction of the prince.'),
('PRO', 14, 29, 'PRO.14.29', 'He who is slow to anger has great understanding, but he who has a quick temper displays folly.'),
('PRO', 14, 30, 'PRO.14.30', 'The life of the body is a heart at peace, but envy rots the bones.'),
('PRO', 14, 31, 'PRO.14.31', 'He who oppresses the poor shows contempt for his Maker, but he who is kind to the needy honors him.'),
('PRO', 14, 32, 'PRO.14.32', 'The wicked is brought down in his calamity, but in death, the righteous has a refuge.'),
('PRO', 14, 33, 'PRO.14.33', 'Wisdom rests in the heart of one who has understanding, and is even made known in the inward part of fools.'),
('PRO', 14, 34, 'PRO.14.34', 'Righteousness exalts a nation, but sin is a disgrace to any people.'),
('PRO', 14, 35, 'PRO.14.35', 'The king’s favor is toward a servant who deals wisely, but his wrath is toward one who causes shame.'),
('PRO', 15, 1, 'PRO.15.1', 'A gentle answer turns away wrath, but a harsh word stirs up anger.'),
('PRO', 15, 2, 'PRO.15.2', 'The tongue of the wise commends knowledge, but the mouths of fools gush out folly.'),
('PRO', 15, 3, 'PRO.15.3', 'The LORD’s eyes are everywhere, keeping watch on the evil and the good.'),
('PRO', 15, 4, 'PRO.15.4', 'A gentle tongue is a tree of life, but deceit in it crushes the spirit.'),
('PRO', 15, 5, 'PRO.15.5', 'A fool despises his father’s correction, but he who heeds reproof shows prudence.'),
('PRO', 15, 6, 'PRO.15.6', 'In the house of the righteous is much treasure, but the income of the wicked brings trouble.'),
('PRO', 15, 7, 'PRO.15.7', 'The lips of the wise spread knowledge; not so with the heart of fools.'),
('PRO', 15, 8, 'PRO.15.8', 'The sacrifice made by the wicked is an abomination to the LORD, but the prayer of the upright is his delight.'),
('PRO', 15, 9, 'PRO.15.9', 'The way of the wicked is an abomination to the LORD, but he loves him who follows after righteousness.'),
('PRO', 15, 10, 'PRO.15.10', 'There is stern discipline for one who forsakes the way. Whoever hates reproof shall die.'),
('PRO', 15, 11, 'PRO.15.11', 'Sheol and Abaddon are before the LORD— how much more then the hearts of the children of men!'),
('PRO', 15, 12, 'PRO.15.12', 'A scoffer doesn’t love to be reproved; he will not go to the wise.'),
('PRO', 15, 13, 'PRO.15.13', 'A glad heart makes a cheerful face, but an aching heart breaks the spirit.'),
('PRO', 15, 14, 'PRO.15.14', 'The heart of one who has understanding seeks knowledge, but the mouths of fools feed on folly.'),
('PRO', 15, 15, 'PRO.15.15', 'All the days of the afflicted are wretched, but one who has a cheerful heart enjoys a continual feast.'),
('PRO', 15, 16, 'PRO.15.16', 'Better is little, with the fear of the LORD, than great treasure with trouble.'),
('PRO', 15, 17, 'PRO.15.17', 'Better is a dinner of herbs, where love is, than a fattened calf with hatred.'),
('PRO', 15, 18, 'PRO.15.18', 'A wrathful man stirs up contention, but one who is slow to anger appeases strife.'),
('PRO', 15, 19, 'PRO.15.19', 'The way of the sluggard is like a thorn patch, but the path of the upright is a highway.'),
('PRO', 15, 20, 'PRO.15.20', 'A wise son makes a father glad, but a foolish man despises his mother.'),
('PRO', 15, 21, 'PRO.15.21', 'Folly is joy to one who is void of wisdom, but a man of understanding keeps his way straight.'),
('PRO', 15, 22, 'PRO.15.22', 'Where there is no counsel, plans fail; but in a multitude of counselors they are established.'),
('PRO', 15, 23, 'PRO.15.23', 'Joy comes to a man with the reply of his mouth. How good is a word at the right time!'),
('PRO', 15, 24, 'PRO.15.24', 'The path of life leads upward for the wise, to keep him from going downward to Sheol.'),
('PRO', 15, 25, 'PRO.15.25', 'The LORD will uproot the house of the proud, but he will keep the widow’s borders intact.'),
('PRO', 15, 26, 'PRO.15.26', 'The LORD detests the thoughts of the wicked, but the thoughts of the pure are pleasing.'),
('PRO', 15, 27, 'PRO.15.27', 'He who is greedy for gain troubles his own house, but he who hates bribes will live.'),
('PRO', 15, 28, 'PRO.15.28', 'The heart of the righteous weighs answers, but the mouth of the wicked gushes out evil.'),
('PRO', 15, 29, 'PRO.15.29', 'The LORD is far from the wicked, but he hears the prayer of the righteous.'),
('PRO', 15, 30, 'PRO.15.30', 'The light of the eyes rejoices the heart. Good news gives health to the bones.'),
('PRO', 15, 31, 'PRO.15.31', 'The ear that listens to reproof lives, and will be at home among the wise.'),
('PRO', 15, 32, 'PRO.15.32', 'He who refuses correction despises his own soul, but he who listens to reproof gets understanding.'),
('PRO', 15, 33, 'PRO.15.33', 'The fear of the LORD teaches wisdom. Before honor is humility.'),
('PRO', 16, 1, 'PRO.16.1', 'The plans of the heart belong to man, but the answer of the tongue is from the LORD.'),
('PRO', 16, 2, 'PRO.16.2', 'All the ways of a man are clean in his own eyes, but the LORD weighs the motives.'),
('PRO', 16, 3, 'PRO.16.3', 'Commit your deeds to the LORD, and your plans shall succeed.'),
('PRO', 16, 4, 'PRO.16.4', 'The LORD has made everything for its own end— yes, even the wicked for the day of evil.'),
('PRO', 16, 5, 'PRO.16.5', 'Everyone who is proud in heart is an abomination to the LORD; they shall certainly not be unpunished.'),
('PRO', 16, 6, 'PRO.16.6', 'By mercy and truth iniquity is atoned for. By the fear of the LORD men depart from evil.'),
('PRO', 16, 7, 'PRO.16.7', 'When a man’s ways please the LORD, he makes even his enemies to be at peace with him.'),
('PRO', 16, 8, 'PRO.16.8', 'Better is a little with righteousness, than great revenues with injustice.'),
('PRO', 16, 9, 'PRO.16.9', 'A man’s heart plans his course, but the LORD directs his steps.'),
('PRO', 16, 10, 'PRO.16.10', 'Inspired judgments are on the lips of the king. He shall not betray his mouth.'),
('PRO', 16, 11, 'PRO.16.11', 'Honest balances and scales are the LORD’s; all the weights in the bag are his work.'),
('PRO', 16, 12, 'PRO.16.12', 'It is an abomination for kings to do wrong, for the throne is established by righteousness.'),
('PRO', 16, 13, 'PRO.16.13', 'Righteous lips are the delight of kings. They value one who speaks the truth.'),
('PRO', 16, 14, 'PRO.16.14', 'The king’s wrath is a messenger of death, but a wise man will pacify it.'),
('PRO', 16, 15, 'PRO.16.15', 'In the light of the king’s face is life. His favor is like a cloud of the spring rain.'),
('PRO', 16, 16, 'PRO.16.16', 'How much better it is to get wisdom than gold! Yes, to get understanding is to be chosen rather than silver.'),
('PRO', 16, 17, 'PRO.16.17', 'The highway of the upright is to depart from evil. He who keeps his way preserves his soul.'),
('PRO', 16, 18, 'PRO.16.18', 'Pride goes before destruction, and an arrogant spirit before a fall.'),
('PRO', 16, 19, 'PRO.16.19', 'It is better to be of a lowly spirit with the poor, than to divide the plunder with the proud.'),
('PRO', 16, 20, 'PRO.16.20', 'He who heeds the Word finds prosperity. Whoever trusts in the LORD is blessed.'),
('PRO', 16, 21, 'PRO.16.21', 'The wise in heart shall be called prudent. Pleasantness of the lips promotes instruction.'),
('PRO', 16, 22, 'PRO.16.22', 'Understanding is a fountain of life to one who has it, but the punishment of fools is their folly.'),
('PRO', 16, 23, 'PRO.16.23', 'The heart of the wise instructs his mouth, and adds learning to his lips.'),
('PRO', 16, 24, 'PRO.16.24', 'Pleasant words are a honeycomb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.'),
('PRO', 16, 25, 'PRO.16.25', 'There is a way which seems right to a man, but in the end it leads to death.'),
('PRO', 16, 26, 'PRO.16.26', 'The appetite of the laboring man labors for him, for his mouth urges him on.'),
('PRO', 16, 27, 'PRO.16.27', 'A worthless man devises mischief. His speech is like a scorching fire.'),
('PRO', 16, 28, 'PRO.16.28', 'A perverse man stirs up strife. A whisperer separates close friends.'),
('PRO', 16, 29, 'PRO.16.29', 'A man of violence entices his neighbor, and leads him in a way that is not good.'),
('PRO', 16, 30, 'PRO.16.30', 'One who winks his eyes to plot perversities, one who compresses his lips, is bent on evil.'),
('PRO', 16, 31, 'PRO.16.31', 'Gray hair is a crown of glory. It is attained by a life of righteousness.'),
('PRO', 16, 32, 'PRO.16.32', 'One who is slow to anger is better than the mighty; one who rules his spirit, than he who takes a city.'),
('PRO', 16, 33, 'PRO.16.33', 'The lot is cast into the lap, but its every decision is from the LORD.'),
('PRO', 17, 1, 'PRO.17.1', 'Better is a dry morsel with quietness, than a house full of feasting with strife.'),
('PRO', 17, 2, 'PRO.17.2', 'A servant who deals wisely will rule over a son who causes shame, and shall have a part in the inheritance among the brothers.'),
('PRO', 17, 3, 'PRO.17.3', 'The refining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold, but the LORD tests the hearts.'),
('PRO', 17, 4, 'PRO.17.4', 'An evildoer heeds wicked lips. A liar gives ear to a mischievous tongue.'),
('PRO', 17, 5, 'PRO.17.5', 'Whoever mocks the poor reproaches his Maker. He who is glad at calamity shall not be unpunished.'),
('PRO', 17, 6, 'PRO.17.6', 'Children’s children are the crown of old men; the glory of children is their parents.'),
('PRO', 17, 7, 'PRO.17.7', 'Excellent speech isn’t fitting for a fool, much less do lying lips fit a prince.'),
('PRO', 17, 8, 'PRO.17.8', 'A bribe is a precious stone in the eyes of him who gives it; wherever he turns, he prospers.'),
('PRO', 17, 9, 'PRO.17.9', 'He who covers an offense promotes love; but he who repeats a matter separates best friends.'),
('PRO', 17, 10, 'PRO.17.10', 'A rebuke enters deeper into one who has understanding than a hundred lashes into a fool.'),
('PRO', 17, 11, 'PRO.17.11', 'An evil man seeks only rebellion; therefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.'),
('PRO', 17, 12, 'PRO.17.12', 'Let a bear robbed of her cubs meet a man, rather than a fool in his folly.'),
('PRO', 17, 13, 'PRO.17.13', 'Whoever rewards evil for good, evil shall not depart from his house.'),
('PRO', 17, 14, 'PRO.17.14', 'The beginning of strife is like breaching a dam, therefore stop contention before quarreling breaks out.'),
('PRO', 17, 15, 'PRO.17.15', 'He who justifies the wicked, and he who condemns the righteous, both of them alike are an abomination to the LORD.'),
('PRO', 17, 16, 'PRO.17.16', 'Why is there money in the hand of a fool to buy wisdom, since he has no understanding?'),
('PRO', 17, 17, 'PRO.17.17', 'A friend loves at all times; and a brother is born for adversity.'),
('PRO', 17, 18, 'PRO.17.18', 'A man void of understanding strikes hands, and becomes collateral in the presence of his neighbor.'),
('PRO', 17, 19, 'PRO.17.19', 'He who loves disobedience loves strife. One who builds a high gate seeks destruction.'),
('PRO', 17, 20, 'PRO.17.20', 'One who has a perverse heart doesn’t find prosperity, and one who has a deceitful tongue falls into trouble.'),
('PRO', 17, 21, 'PRO.17.21', 'He who becomes the father of a fool grieves. The father of a fool has no joy.'),
('PRO', 17, 22, 'PRO.17.22', 'A cheerful heart makes good medicine, but a crushed spirit dries up the bones.'),
('PRO', 17, 23, 'PRO.17.23', 'A wicked man receives a bribe in secret, to pervert the ways of justice.'),
('PRO', 17, 24, 'PRO.17.24', 'Wisdom is before the face of one who has understanding, but the eyes of a fool wander to the ends of the earth.'),
('PRO', 17, 25, 'PRO.17.25', 'A foolish son brings grief to his father, and bitterness to her who bore him.'),
('PRO', 17, 26, 'PRO.17.26', 'Also to punish the righteous is not good, nor to flog officials for their integrity.'),
('PRO', 17, 27, 'PRO.17.27', 'He who spares his words has knowledge. He who is even tempered is a man of understanding.'),
('PRO', 17, 28, 'PRO.17.28', 'Even a fool, when he keeps silent, is counted wise. When he shuts his lips, he is thought to be discerning.'),
('PRO', 18, 1, 'PRO.18.1', 'A man who isolates himself pursues selfishness, and defies all sound judgment.'),
('PRO', 18, 2, 'PRO.18.2', 'A fool has no delight in understanding, but only in revealing his own opinion.'),
('PRO', 18, 3, 'PRO.18.3', 'When wickedness comes, contempt also comes, and with shame comes disgrace.'),
('PRO', 18, 4, 'PRO.18.4', 'The words of a man’s mouth are like deep waters. The fountain of wisdom is like a flowing brook.'),
('PRO', 18, 5, 'PRO.18.5', 'To be partial to the faces of the wicked is not good, nor to deprive the innocent of justice.'),
('PRO', 18, 6, 'PRO.18.6', 'A fool’s lips come into strife, and his mouth invites beatings.'),
('PRO', 18, 7, 'PRO.18.7', 'A fool’s mouth is his destruction, and his lips are a snare to his soul.'),
('PRO', 18, 8, 'PRO.18.8', 'The words of a gossip are like dainty morsels: they go down into a person’s innermost parts.'),
('PRO', 18, 9, 'PRO.18.9', 'One who is slack in his work is brother to him who is a master of destruction.'),
('PRO', 18, 10, 'PRO.18.10', 'The LORD’s name is a strong tower: the righteous run to him, and are safe.'),
('PRO', 18, 11, 'PRO.18.11', 'The rich man’s wealth is his strong city, like an unscalable wall in his own imagination.'),
('PRO', 18, 12, 'PRO.18.12', 'Before destruction the heart of man is proud, but before honor is humility.'),
('PRO', 18, 13, 'PRO.18.13', 'He who answers before he hears, that is folly and shame to him.'),
('PRO', 18, 14, 'PRO.18.14', 'A man’s spirit will sustain him in sickness, but a crushed spirit, who can bear?'),
('PRO', 18, 15, 'PRO.18.15', 'The heart of the discerning gets knowledge. The ear of the wise seeks knowledge.'),
('PRO', 18, 16, 'PRO.18.16', 'A man’s gift makes room for him, and brings him before great men.'),
('PRO', 18, 17, 'PRO.18.17', 'He who pleads his cause first seems right— until another comes and questions him.'),
('PRO', 18, 18, 'PRO.18.18', 'The lot settles disputes, and keeps strong ones apart.'),
('PRO', 18, 19, 'PRO.18.19', 'A brother offended is more difficult than a fortified city. Disputes are like the bars of a fortress.'),
('PRO', 18, 20, 'PRO.18.20', 'A man’s stomach is filled with the fruit of his mouth. With the harvest of his lips he is satisfied.'),
('PRO', 18, 21, 'PRO.18.21', 'Death and life are in the power of the tongue; those who love it will eat its fruit.'),
('PRO', 18, 22, 'PRO.18.22', 'Whoever finds a wife finds a good thing, and obtains favor of the LORD.'),
('PRO', 18, 23, 'PRO.18.23', 'The poor plead for mercy, but the rich answer harshly.'),
('PRO', 18, 24, 'PRO.18.24', 'A man of many companions may be ruined, but there is a friend who sticks closer than a brother.'),
('PRO', 19, 1, 'PRO.19.1', 'Better is the poor who walks in his integrity than he who is perverse in his lips and is a fool.'),
('PRO', 19, 2, 'PRO.19.2', 'It isn’t good to have zeal without knowledge, nor to be hasty with one’s feet and miss the way.'),
('PRO', 19, 3, 'PRO.19.3', 'The foolishness of man subverts his way; his heart rages against the LORD.'),
('PRO', 19, 4, 'PRO.19.4', 'Wealth adds many friends, but the poor is separated from his friend.'),
('PRO', 19, 5, 'PRO.19.5', 'A false witness shall not be unpunished. He who pours out lies shall not go free.'),
('PRO', 19, 6, 'PRO.19.6', 'Many will entreat the favor of a ruler, and everyone is a friend to a man who gives gifts.'),
('PRO', 19, 7, 'PRO.19.7', 'All the relatives of the poor shun him; how much more do his friends avoid him! He pursues them with pleas, but they are gone.'),
('PRO', 19, 8, 'PRO.19.8', 'He who gets wisdom loves his own soul. He who keeps understanding shall find good.'),
('PRO', 19, 9, 'PRO.19.9', 'A false witness shall not be unpunished. He who utters lies shall perish.'),
('PRO', 19, 10, 'PRO.19.10', 'Delicate living is not appropriate for a fool, much less for a servant to have rule over princes.'),
('PRO', 19, 11, 'PRO.19.11', 'The discretion of a man makes him slow to anger. It is his glory to overlook an offense.'),
('PRO', 19, 12, 'PRO.19.12', 'The king’s wrath is like the roaring of a lion, but his favor is like dew on the grass.'),
('PRO', 19, 13, 'PRO.19.13', 'A foolish son is the calamity of his father. A wife’s quarrels are a continual dripping.'),
('PRO', 19, 14, 'PRO.19.14', 'House and riches are an inheritance from fathers, but a prudent wife is from the LORD.'),
('PRO', 19, 15, 'PRO.19.15', 'Slothfulness casts into a deep sleep. The idle soul shall suffer hunger.'),
('PRO', 19, 16, 'PRO.19.16', 'He who keeps the commandment keeps his soul, but he who is contemptuous in his ways shall die.'),
('PRO', 19, 17, 'PRO.19.17', 'He who has pity on the poor lends to the LORD; he will reward him.'),
('PRO', 19, 18, 'PRO.19.18', 'Discipline your son, for there is hope; don’t be a willing party to his death.'),
('PRO', 19, 19, 'PRO.19.19', 'A hot-tempered man must pay the penalty, for if you rescue him, you must do it again.'),
('PRO', 19, 20, 'PRO.19.20', 'Listen to counsel and receive instruction, that you may be wise in your latter end.'),
('PRO', 19, 21, 'PRO.19.21', 'There are many plans in a man’s heart, but the LORD’s counsel will prevail.'),
('PRO', 19, 22, 'PRO.19.22', 'That which makes a man to be desired is his kindness. A poor man is better than a liar.'),
('PRO', 19, 23, 'PRO.19.23', 'The fear of the LORD leads to life, then contentment; he rests and will not be touched by trouble.'),
('PRO', 19, 24, 'PRO.19.24', 'The sluggard buries his hand in the dish; he will not so much as bring it to his mouth again.'),
('PRO', 19, 25, 'PRO.19.25', 'Flog a scoffer, and the simple will learn prudence; rebuke one who has understanding, and he will gain knowledge.'),
('PRO', 19, 26, 'PRO.19.26', 'He who robs his father and drives away his mother is a son who causes shame and brings reproach.'),
('PRO', 19, 27, 'PRO.19.27', 'If you stop listening to instruction, my son, you will stray from the words of knowledge.'),
('PRO', 19, 28, 'PRO.19.28', 'A corrupt witness mocks justice, and the mouth of the wicked gulps down iniquity.'),
('PRO', 19, 29, 'PRO.19.29', 'Penalties are prepared for scoffers, and beatings for the backs of fools.'),
('PRO', 20, 1, 'PRO.20.1', 'Wine is a mocker and beer is a brawler. Whoever is led astray by them is not wise.'),
('PRO', 20, 2, 'PRO.20.2', 'The terror of a king is like the roaring of a lion. He who provokes him to anger forfeits his own life.'),
('PRO', 20, 3, 'PRO.20.3', 'It is an honor for a man to keep aloof from strife, but every fool will be quarreling.'),
('PRO', 20, 4, 'PRO.20.4', 'The sluggard will not plow by reason of the winter; therefore he shall beg in harvest, and have nothing.'),
('PRO', 20, 5, 'PRO.20.5', 'Counsel in the heart of man is like deep water, but a man of understanding will draw it out.'),
('PRO', 20, 6, 'PRO.20.6', 'Many men claim to be men of unfailing love, but who can find a faithful man?'),
('PRO', 20, 7, 'PRO.20.7', 'A righteous man walks in integrity. Blessed are his children after him.'),
('PRO', 20, 8, 'PRO.20.8', 'A king who sits on the throne of judgment scatters away all evil with his eyes.'),
('PRO', 20, 9, 'PRO.20.9', 'Who can say, “I have made my heart pure. I am clean and without sin”?'),
('PRO', 20, 10, 'PRO.20.10', 'Differing weights and differing measures, both of them alike are an abomination to the LORD.'),
('PRO', 20, 11, 'PRO.20.11', 'Even a child makes himself known by his doings, whether his work is pure, and whether it is right.'),
('PRO', 20, 12, 'PRO.20.12', 'The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the LORD has made even both of them.'),
('PRO', 20, 13, 'PRO.20.13', 'Don’t love sleep, lest you come to poverty. Open your eyes, and you shall be satisfied with bread.'),
('PRO', 20, 14, 'PRO.20.14', '“It’s no good, it’s no good,” says the buyer; but when he is gone his way, then he boasts.'),
('PRO', 20, 15, 'PRO.20.15', 'There is gold and abundance of rubies, but the lips of knowledge are a rare jewel.'),
('PRO', 20, 16, 'PRO.20.16', 'Take the garment of one who puts up collateral for a stranger; and hold him in pledge for a wayward woman.'),
('PRO', 20, 17, 'PRO.20.17', 'Fraudulent food is sweet to a man, but afterwards his mouth is filled with gravel.'),
('PRO', 20, 18, 'PRO.20.18', 'Plans are established by advice; by wise guidance you wage war!'),
('PRO', 20, 19, 'PRO.20.19', 'He who goes about as a tale-bearer reveals secrets; therefore don’t keep company with him who opens wide his lips.'),
('PRO', 20, 20, 'PRO.20.20', 'Whoever curses his father or his mother, his lamp shall be put out in blackness of darkness.'),
('PRO', 20, 21, 'PRO.20.21', 'An inheritance quickly gained at the beginning won’t be blessed in the end.'),
('PRO', 20, 22, 'PRO.20.22', 'Don’t say, “I will pay back evil.” Wait for the LORD, and he will save you.'),
('PRO', 20, 23, 'PRO.20.23', 'The LORD detests differing weights, and dishonest scales are not pleasing.'),
('PRO', 20, 24, 'PRO.20.24', 'A man’s steps are from the LORD; how then can man understand his way?'),
('PRO', 20, 25, 'PRO.20.25', 'It is a snare to a man to make a rash dedication, then later to consider his vows.'),
('PRO', 20, 26, 'PRO.20.26', 'A wise king winnows out the wicked, and drives the threshing wheel over them.'),
('PRO', 20, 27, 'PRO.20.27', 'The spirit of man is the LORD’s lamp, searching all his innermost parts.'),
('PRO', 20, 28, 'PRO.20.28', 'Love and faithfulness keep the king safe. His throne is sustained by love.'),
('PRO', 20, 29, 'PRO.20.29', 'The glory of young men is their strength. The splendor of old men is their gray hair.'),
('PRO', 20, 30, 'PRO.20.30', 'Wounding blows cleanse away evil, and beatings purge the innermost parts.'),
('PRO', 21, 1, 'PRO.21.1', 'The king’s heart is in the LORD’s hand like the watercourses. He turns it wherever he desires.'),
('PRO', 21, 2, 'PRO.21.2', 'Every way of a man is right in his own eyes, but the LORD weighs the hearts.'),
('PRO', 21, 3, 'PRO.21.3', 'To do righteousness and justice is more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.'),
('PRO', 21, 4, 'PRO.21.4', 'A high look and a proud heart, the lamp of the wicked, is sin.'),
('PRO', 21, 5, 'PRO.21.5', 'The plans of the diligent surely lead to profit; and everyone who is hasty surely rushes to poverty.'),
('PRO', 21, 6, 'PRO.21.6', 'Getting treasures by a lying tongue is a fleeting vapor for those who seek death.'),
('PRO', 21, 7, 'PRO.21.7', 'The violence of the wicked will drive them away, because they refuse to do what is right.'),
('PRO', 21, 8, 'PRO.21.8', 'The way of the guilty is devious, but the conduct of the innocent is upright.'),
('PRO', 21, 9, 'PRO.21.9', 'It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop than to share a house with a contentious woman.'),
('PRO', 21, 10, 'PRO.21.10', 'The soul of the wicked desires evil; his neighbor finds no mercy in his eyes.'),
('PRO', 21, 11, 'PRO.21.11', 'When the mocker is punished, the simple gains wisdom. When the wise is instructed, he receives knowledge.'),
('PRO', 21, 12, 'PRO.21.12', 'The Righteous One considers the house of the wicked, and brings the wicked to ruin.'),
('PRO', 21, 13, 'PRO.21.13', 'Whoever stops his ears at the cry of the poor, he will also cry out, but shall not be heard.'),
('PRO', 21, 14, 'PRO.21.14', 'A gift in secret pacifies anger, and a bribe in the cloak, strong wrath.'),
('PRO', 21, 15, 'PRO.21.15', 'It is joy to the righteous to do justice; but it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity.'),
('PRO', 21, 16, 'PRO.21.16', 'The man who wanders out of the way of understanding shall rest in the assembly of the departed spirits.'),
('PRO', 21, 17, 'PRO.21.17', 'He who loves pleasure will be a poor man. He who loves wine and oil won’t be rich.'),
('PRO', 21, 18, 'PRO.21.18', 'The wicked is a ransom for the righteous, the treacherous for the upright.'),
('PRO', 21, 19, 'PRO.21.19', 'It is better to dwell in a desert land, than with a contentious and fretful woman.'),
('PRO', 21, 20, 'PRO.21.20', 'There is precious treasure and oil in the dwelling of the wise, but a foolish man swallows it up.'),
('PRO', 21, 21, 'PRO.21.21', 'He who follows after righteousness and kindness finds life, righteousness, and honor.'),
('PRO', 21, 22, 'PRO.21.22', 'A wise man scales the city of the mighty, and brings down the strength of its confidence.'),
('PRO', 21, 23, 'PRO.21.23', 'Whoever guards his mouth and his tongue keeps his soul from troubles.'),
('PRO', 21, 24, 'PRO.21.24', 'The proud and arrogant man—“Scoffer” is his name— he works in the arrogance of pride.'),
('PRO', 21, 25, 'PRO.21.25', 'The desire of the sluggard kills him, for his hands refuse to labor.'),
('PRO', 21, 26, 'PRO.21.26', 'There are those who covet greedily all day long; but the righteous give and don’t withhold.'),
('PRO', 21, 27, 'PRO.21.27', 'The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination— how much more, when he brings it with a wicked mind!'),
('PRO', 21, 28, 'PRO.21.28', 'A false witness will perish. A man who listens speaks to eternity.'),
('PRO', 21, 29, 'PRO.21.29', 'A wicked man hardens his face; but as for the upright, he establishes his ways.'),
('PRO', 21, 30, 'PRO.21.30', 'There is no wisdom nor understanding nor counsel against the LORD.'),
('PRO', 21, 31, 'PRO.21.31', 'The horse is prepared for the day of battle; but victory is with the LORD.'),
('PRO', 22, 1, 'PRO.22.1', 'A good name is more desirable than great riches, and loving favor is better than silver and gold.'),
('PRO', 22, 2, 'PRO.22.2', 'The rich and the poor have this in common: The LORD is the maker of them all.'),
('PRO', 22, 3, 'PRO.22.3', 'A prudent man sees danger and hides himself; but the simple pass on, and suffer for it.'),
('PRO', 22, 4, 'PRO.22.4', 'The result of humility and the fear of the LORD is wealth, honor, and life.'),
('PRO', 22, 5, 'PRO.22.5', 'Thorns and snares are in the path of the wicked; whoever guards his soul stays far from them.'),
('PRO', 22, 6, 'PRO.22.6', 'Train up a child in the way he should go, and when he is old he will not depart from it.'),
('PRO', 22, 7, 'PRO.22.7', 'The rich rule over the poor. The borrower is servant to the lender.'),
('PRO', 22, 8, 'PRO.22.8', 'He who sows wickedness reaps trouble, and the rod of his fury will be destroyed.'),
('PRO', 22, 9, 'PRO.22.9', 'He who has a generous eye will be blessed, for he shares his food with the poor.'),
('PRO', 22, 10, 'PRO.22.10', 'Drive out the mocker, and strife will go out; yes, quarrels and insults will stop.'),
('PRO', 22, 11, 'PRO.22.11', 'He who loves purity of heart and speaks gracefully is the king’s friend.'),
('PRO', 22, 12, 'PRO.22.12', 'The LORD’s eyes watch over knowledge, but he frustrates the words of the unfaithful.'),
('PRO', 22, 13, 'PRO.22.13', 'The sluggard says, “There is a lion outside! I will be killed in the streets!”'),
('PRO', 22, 14, 'PRO.22.14', 'The mouth of an adulteress is a deep pit. He who is under the LORD’s wrath will fall into it.'),
('PRO', 22, 15, 'PRO.22.15', 'Folly is bound up in the heart of a child; the rod of discipline drives it far from him.'),
('PRO', 22, 16, 'PRO.22.16', 'Whoever oppresses the poor for his own increase and whoever gives to the rich, both come to poverty.'),
('PRO', 22, 17, 'PRO.22.17', 'Turn your ear, and listen to the words of the wise. Apply your heart to my teaching.'),
('PRO', 22, 18, 'PRO.22.18', 'For it is a pleasant thing if you keep them within you, if all of them are ready on your lips.'),
('PRO', 22, 19, 'PRO.22.19', 'I teach you today, even you, so that your trust may be in the LORD.'),
('PRO', 22, 20, 'PRO.22.20', 'Haven’t I written to you thirty excellent things of counsel and knowledge,'),
('PRO', 22, 21, 'PRO.22.21', 'To teach you truth, reliable words, to give sound answers to the ones who sent you?'),
('PRO', 22, 22, 'PRO.22.22', 'Don’t exploit the poor because he is poor; and don’t crush the needy in court;'),
('PRO', 22, 23, 'PRO.22.23', 'for the LORD will plead their case, and plunder the life of those who plunder them.'),
('PRO', 22, 24, 'PRO.22.24', 'Don’t befriend a hot-tempered man. Don’t associate with one who harbors anger,'),
('PRO', 22, 25, 'PRO.22.25', 'lest you learn his ways and ensnare your soul.'),
('PRO', 22, 26, 'PRO.22.26', 'Don’t you be one of those who strike hands, of those who are collateral for debts.'),
('PRO', 22, 27, 'PRO.22.27', 'If you don’t have means to pay, why should he take away your bed from under you?'),
('PRO', 22, 28, 'PRO.22.28', 'Don’t move the ancient boundary stone which your fathers have set up.'),
('PRO', 22, 29, 'PRO.22.29', 'Do you see a man skilled in his work? He will serve kings. He won’t serve obscure men.'),
('PRO', 23, 1, 'PRO.23.1', 'When you sit to eat with a ruler, consider diligently what is before you;'),
('PRO', 23, 2, 'PRO.23.2', 'put a knife to your throat if you are a man given to appetite.'),
('PRO', 23, 3, 'PRO.23.3', 'Don’t be desirous of his dainties, since they are deceitful food.'),
('PRO', 23, 4, 'PRO.23.4', 'Don’t weary yourself to be rich. In your wisdom, show restraint.'),
('PRO', 23, 5, 'PRO.23.5', 'Why do you set your eyes on that which is not? For it certainly sprouts wings like an eagle and flies in the sky.'),
('PRO', 23, 6, 'PRO.23.6', 'Don’t eat the food of him who has a stingy eye, and don’t crave his delicacies,'),
('PRO', 23, 7, 'PRO.23.7', 'for as he thinks about the cost, so he is. “Eat and drink!” he says to you, but his heart is not with you.'),
('PRO', 23, 8, 'PRO.23.8', 'You will vomit up the morsel which you have eaten and waste your pleasant words.'),
('PRO', 23, 9, 'PRO.23.9', 'Don’t speak in the ears of a fool, for he will despise the wisdom of your words.'),
('PRO', 23, 10, 'PRO.23.10', 'Don’t move the ancient boundary stone. Don’t encroach on the fields of the fatherless,'),
('PRO', 23, 11, 'PRO.23.11', 'for their Defender is strong. He will plead their case against you.'),
('PRO', 23, 12, 'PRO.23.12', 'Apply your heart to instruction, and your ears to the words of knowledge.'),
('PRO', 23, 13, 'PRO.23.13', 'Don’t withhold correction from a child. If you punish him with the rod, he will not die.'),
('PRO', 23, 14, 'PRO.23.14', 'Punish him with the rod, and save his soul from Sheol.'),
('PRO', 23, 15, 'PRO.23.15', 'My son, if your heart is wise, then my heart will be glad, even mine.'),
('PRO', 23, 16, 'PRO.23.16', 'Yes, my heart will rejoice when your lips speak what is right.'),
('PRO', 23, 17, 'PRO.23.17', 'Don’t let your heart envy sinners, but rather fear the LORD all day long.'),
('PRO', 23, 18, 'PRO.23.18', 'Indeed surely there is a future hope, and your hope will not be cut off.'),
('PRO', 23, 19, 'PRO.23.19', 'Listen, my son, and be wise, and keep your heart on the right path!'),
('PRO', 23, 20, 'PRO.23.20', 'Don’t be among ones drinking too much wine, or those who gorge themselves on meat;'),
('PRO', 23, 21, 'PRO.23.21', 'for the drunkard and the glutton shall become poor; and drowsiness clothes them in rags.'),
('PRO', 23, 22, 'PRO.23.22', 'Listen to your father who gave you life, and don’t despise your mother when she is old.'),
('PRO', 23, 23, 'PRO.23.23', 'Buy the truth, and don’t sell it. Get wisdom, discipline, and understanding.'),
('PRO', 23, 24, 'PRO.23.24', 'The father of the righteous has great joy. Whoever fathers a wise child delights in him.'),
('PRO', 23, 25, 'PRO.23.25', 'Let your father and your mother be glad! Let her who bore you rejoice!'),
('PRO', 23, 26, 'PRO.23.26', 'My son, give me your heart; and let your eyes keep in my ways.'),
('PRO', 23, 27, 'PRO.23.27', 'For a prostitute is a deep pit; and a wayward wife is a narrow well.'),
('PRO', 23, 28, 'PRO.23.28', 'Yes, she lies in wait like a robber, and increases the unfaithful among men.'),
('PRO', 23, 29, 'PRO.23.29', 'Who has woe? Who has sorrow? Who has strife? Who has complaints? Who has needless bruises? Who has bloodshot eyes?'),
('PRO', 23, 30, 'PRO.23.30', 'Those who stay long at the wine; those who go to seek out mixed wine.'),
('PRO', 23, 31, 'PRO.23.31', 'Don’t look at the wine when it is red, when it sparkles in the cup, when it goes down smoothly.'),
('PRO', 23, 32, 'PRO.23.32', 'In the end, it bites like a snake, and poisons like a viper.'),
('PRO', 23, 33, 'PRO.23.33', 'Your eyes will see strange things, and your mind will imagine confusing things.'),
('PRO', 23, 34, 'PRO.23.34', 'Yes, you will be as he who lies down in the middle of the sea, or as he who lies on top of the rigging:'),
('PRO', 23, 35, 'PRO.23.35', '“They hit me, and I was not hurt! They beat me, and I don’t feel it! When will I wake up? I can do it again. I will look for more.”'),
('PRO', 24, 1, 'PRO.24.1', 'Don’t be envious of evil men, neither desire to be with them;'),
('PRO', 24, 2, 'PRO.24.2', 'for their hearts plot violence and their lips talk about mischief.'),
('PRO', 24, 3, 'PRO.24.3', 'Through wisdom a house is built; by understanding it is established;'),
('PRO', 24, 4, 'PRO.24.4', 'by knowledge the rooms are filled with all rare and beautiful treasure.'),
('PRO', 24, 5, 'PRO.24.5', 'A wise man has great power. A knowledgeable man increases strength,'),
('PRO', 24, 6, 'PRO.24.6', 'for by wise guidance you wage your war, and victory is in many advisors.'),
('PRO', 24, 7, 'PRO.24.7', 'Wisdom is too high for a fool. He doesn’t open his mouth in the gate.'),
('PRO', 24, 8, 'PRO.24.8', 'One who plots to do evil will be called a schemer.'),
('PRO', 24, 9, 'PRO.24.9', 'The schemes of folly are sin. The mocker is detested by men.'),
('PRO', 24, 10, 'PRO.24.10', 'If you falter in the time of trouble, your strength is small.'),
('PRO', 24, 11, 'PRO.24.11', 'Rescue those who are being led away to death! Indeed, hold back those who are staggering to the slaughter!'),
('PRO', 24, 12, 'PRO.24.12', 'If you say, “Behold, we didn’t know this,” doesn’t he who weighs the hearts consider it? He who keeps your soul, doesn’t he know it? Shall he not give to every man according to his work?'),
('PRO', 24, 13, 'PRO.24.13', 'My son, eat honey, for it is good, the droppings of the honeycomb, which are sweet to your taste;'),
('PRO', 24, 14, 'PRO.24.14', 'so you shall know wisdom to be to your soul. If you have found it, then there will be a reward: Your hope will not be cut off.'),
('PRO', 24, 15, 'PRO.24.15', 'Don’t lay in wait, wicked man, against the habitation of the righteous. Don’t destroy his resting place;'),
('PRO', 24, 16, 'PRO.24.16', 'for a righteous man falls seven times and rises up again, but the wicked are overthrown by calamity.'),
('PRO', 24, 17, 'PRO.24.17', 'Don’t rejoice when your enemy falls. Don’t let your heart be glad when he is overthrown,'),
('PRO', 24, 18, 'PRO.24.18', 'lest the LORD see it, and it displease him, and he turn away his wrath from him.'),
('PRO', 24, 19, 'PRO.24.19', 'Don’t fret yourself because of evildoers, neither be envious of the wicked;'),
('PRO', 24, 20, 'PRO.24.20', 'for there will be no reward to the evil man. The lamp of the wicked will be snuffed out.'),
('PRO', 24, 21, 'PRO.24.21', 'My son, fear the LORD and the king. Don’t join those who are rebellious,'),
('PRO', 24, 22, 'PRO.24.22', 'for their calamity will rise suddenly. Who knows what destruction may come from them both?'),
('PRO', 24, 23, 'PRO.24.23', 'These also are sayings of the wise: To show partiality in judgment is not good.'),
('PRO', 24, 24, 'PRO.24.24', 'He who says to the wicked, “You are righteous,” peoples will curse him, and nations will abhor him—'),
('PRO', 24, 25, 'PRO.24.25', 'but it will go well with those who convict the guilty, and a rich blessing will come on them.'),
('PRO', 24, 26, 'PRO.24.26', 'An honest answer is like a kiss on the lips.'),
('PRO', 24, 27, 'PRO.24.27', 'Prepare your work outside, and get your fields ready. Afterwards, build your house.'),
('PRO', 24, 28, 'PRO.24.28', 'Don’t be a witness against your neighbor without cause. Don’t deceive with your lips.'),
('PRO', 24, 29, 'PRO.24.29', 'Don’t say, “I will do to him as he has done to me; I will repay the man according to his work.”'),
('PRO', 24, 30, 'PRO.24.30', 'I went by the field of the sluggard, by the vineyard of the man void of understanding.'),
('PRO', 24, 31, 'PRO.24.31', 'Behold, it was all grown over with thorns. Its surface was covered with nettles, and its stone wall was broken down.'),
('PRO', 24, 32, 'PRO.24.32', 'Then I saw, and considered well. I saw, and received instruction:'),
('PRO', 24, 33, 'PRO.24.33', 'a little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep,'),
('PRO', 24, 34, 'PRO.24.34', 'so your poverty will come as a robber and your want as an armed man.'),
('PRO', 25, 1, 'PRO.25.1', 'These also are proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out.'),
('PRO', 25, 2, 'PRO.25.2', 'It is the glory of God to conceal a thing, but the glory of kings is to search out a matter.'),
('PRO', 25, 3, 'PRO.25.3', 'As the heavens for height, and the earth for depth, so the hearts of kings are unsearchable.'),
('PRO', 25, 4, 'PRO.25.4', 'Take away the dross from the silver, and material comes out for the refiner.'),
('PRO', 25, 5, 'PRO.25.5', 'Take away the wicked from the king’s presence, and his throne will be established in righteousness.'),
('PRO', 25, 6, 'PRO.25.6', 'Don’t exalt yourself in the presence of the king, or claim a place among great men;'),
('PRO', 25, 7, 'PRO.25.7', 'for it is better that it be said to you, “Come up here,” than that you should be put lower in the presence of the prince, whom your eyes have seen.'),
('PRO', 25, 8, 'PRO.25.8', 'Don’t be hasty in bringing charges to court. What will you do in the end when your neighbor shames you?'),
('PRO', 25, 9, 'PRO.25.9', 'Debate your case with your neighbor, and don’t betray the confidence of another,'),
('PRO', 25, 10, 'PRO.25.10', 'lest one who hears it put you to shame, and your bad reputation never depart.'),
('PRO', 25, 11, 'PRO.25.11', 'A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in settings of silver.'),
('PRO', 25, 12, 'PRO.25.12', 'As an earring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold, so is a wise reprover to an obedient ear.'),
('PRO', 25, 13, 'PRO.25.13', 'As the cold of snow in the time of harvest, so is a faithful messenger to those who send him; for he refreshes the soul of his masters.'),
('PRO', 25, 14, 'PRO.25.14', 'As clouds and wind without rain, so is he who boasts of gifts deceptively.'),
('PRO', 25, 15, 'PRO.25.15', 'By patience a ruler is persuaded. A soft tongue breaks the bone.'),
('PRO', 25, 16, 'PRO.25.16', 'Have you found honey? Eat as much as is sufficient for you, lest you eat too much, and vomit it.'),
('PRO', 25, 17, 'PRO.25.17', 'Let your foot be seldom in your neighbor’s house, lest he be weary of you, and hate you.'),
('PRO', 25, 18, 'PRO.25.18', 'A man who gives false testimony against his neighbor is like a club, a sword, or a sharp arrow.'),
('PRO', 25, 19, 'PRO.25.19', 'Confidence in someone unfaithful in time of trouble is like a bad tooth or a lame foot.'),
('PRO', 25, 20, 'PRO.25.20', 'As one who takes away a garment in cold weather, or vinegar on soda, so is one who sings songs to a heavy heart.'),
('PRO', 25, 21, 'PRO.25.21', 'If your enemy is hungry, give him food to eat. If he is thirsty, give him water to drink;'),
('PRO', 25, 22, 'PRO.25.22', 'for you will heap coals of fire on his head, and the LORD will reward you.'),
('PRO', 25, 23, 'PRO.25.23', 'The north wind produces rain; so a backbiting tongue brings an angry face.'),
('PRO', 25, 24, 'PRO.25.24', 'It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop than to share a house with a contentious woman.'),
('PRO', 25, 25, 'PRO.25.25', 'Like cold water to a thirsty soul, so is good news from a far country.'),
('PRO', 25, 26, 'PRO.25.26', 'Like a muddied spring and a polluted well, so is a righteous man who gives way before the wicked.'),
('PRO', 25, 27, 'PRO.25.27', 'It is not good to eat much honey, nor is it honorable to seek one’s own honor.'),
('PRO', 25, 28, 'PRO.25.28', 'Like a city that is broken down and without walls is a man whose spirit is without restraint.'),
('PRO', 26, 1, 'PRO.26.1', 'Like snow in summer, and as rain in harvest, so honor is not fitting for a fool.'),
('PRO', 26, 2, 'PRO.26.2', 'Like a fluttering sparrow, like a darting swallow, so the undeserved curse doesn’t come to rest.'),
('PRO', 26, 3, 'PRO.26.3', 'A whip is for the horse, a bridle for the donkey, and a rod for the back of fools!'),
('PRO', 26, 4, 'PRO.26.4', 'Don’t answer a fool according to his folly, lest you also be like him.'),
('PRO', 26, 5, 'PRO.26.5', 'Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he be wise in his own eyes.'),
('PRO', 26, 6, 'PRO.26.6', 'One who sends a message by the hand of a fool is cutting off feet and drinking violence.'),
('PRO', 26, 7, 'PRO.26.7', 'Like the legs of the lame that hang loose, so is a parable in the mouth of fools.'),
('PRO', 26, 8, 'PRO.26.8', 'As one who binds a stone in a sling, so is he who gives honor to a fool.'),
('PRO', 26, 9, 'PRO.26.9', 'Like a thorn bush that goes into the hand of a drunkard, so is a parable in the mouth of fools.'),
('PRO', 26, 10, 'PRO.26.10', 'As an archer who wounds all, so is he who hires a fool or he who hires those who pass by.'),
('PRO', 26, 11, 'PRO.26.11', 'As a dog that returns to his vomit, so is a fool who repeats his folly.'),
('PRO', 26, 12, 'PRO.26.12', 'Do you see a man wise in his own eyes? There is more hope for a fool than for him.'),
('PRO', 26, 13, 'PRO.26.13', 'The sluggard says, “There is a lion in the road! A fierce lion roams the streets!”'),
('PRO', 26, 14, 'PRO.26.14', 'As the door turns on its hinges, so does the sluggard on his bed.'),
('PRO', 26, 15, 'PRO.26.15', 'The sluggard buries his hand in the dish. He is too lazy to bring it back to his mouth.'),
('PRO', 26, 16, 'PRO.26.16', 'The sluggard is wiser in his own eyes than seven men who answer with discretion.'),
('PRO', 26, 17, 'PRO.26.17', 'Like one who grabs a dog’s ears is one who passes by and meddles in a quarrel not his own.'),
('PRO', 26, 18, 'PRO.26.18', 'Like a madman who shoots torches, arrows, and death,'),
('PRO', 26, 19, 'PRO.26.19', 'is the man who deceives his neighbor and says, “Am I not joking?”'),
('PRO', 26, 20, 'PRO.26.20', 'For lack of wood a fire goes out. Without gossip, a quarrel dies down.'),
('PRO', 26, 21, 'PRO.26.21', 'As coals are to hot embers, and wood to fire, so is a contentious man to kindling strife.'),
('PRO', 26, 22, 'PRO.26.22', 'The words of a whisperer are as dainty morsels, they go down into the innermost parts.'),
('PRO', 26, 23, 'PRO.26.23', 'Like silver dross on an earthen vessel are the lips of a fervent one with an evil heart.'),
('PRO', 26, 24, 'PRO.26.24', 'A malicious man disguises himself with his lips, but he harbors evil in his heart.'),
('PRO', 26, 25, 'PRO.26.25', 'When his speech is charming, don’t believe him, for there are seven abominations in his heart.'),
('PRO', 26, 26, 'PRO.26.26', 'His malice may be concealed by deception, but his wickedness will be exposed in the assembly.'),
('PRO', 26, 27, 'PRO.26.27', 'Whoever digs a pit shall fall into it. Whoever rolls a stone, it will come back on him.'),
('PRO', 26, 28, 'PRO.26.28', 'A lying tongue hates those it hurts; and a flattering mouth works ruin.'),
('PRO', 27, 1, 'PRO.27.1', 'Don’t boast about tomorrow; for you don’t know what a day may bring.'),
('PRO', 27, 2, 'PRO.27.2', 'Let another man praise you, and not your own mouth; a stranger, and not your own lips.'),
('PRO', 27, 3, 'PRO.27.3', 'A stone is heavy, and sand is a burden; but a fool’s provocation is heavier than both.'),
('PRO', 27, 4, 'PRO.27.4', 'Wrath is cruel, and anger is overwhelming; but who is able to stand before jealousy?'),
('PRO', 27, 5, 'PRO.27.5', 'Better is open rebuke than hidden love.'),
('PRO', 27, 6, 'PRO.27.6', 'The wounds of a friend are faithful, although the kisses of an enemy are profuse.'),
('PRO', 27, 7, 'PRO.27.7', 'A full soul loathes a honeycomb; but to a hungry soul, every bitter thing is sweet.'),
('PRO', 27, 8, 'PRO.27.8', 'As a bird that wanders from her nest, so is a man who wanders from his home.'),
('PRO', 27, 9, 'PRO.27.9', 'Perfume and incense bring joy to the heart; so does earnest counsel from a man’s friend.'),
('PRO', 27, 10, 'PRO.27.10', 'Don’t forsake your friend and your father’s friend. Don’t go to your brother’s house in the day of your disaster. A neighbor who is near is better than a distant brother.'),
('PRO', 27, 11, 'PRO.27.11', 'Be wise, my son, and bring joy to my heart, then I can answer my tormentor.'),
('PRO', 27, 12, 'PRO.27.12', 'A prudent man sees danger and takes refuge; but the simple pass on, and suffer for it.'),
('PRO', 27, 13, 'PRO.27.13', 'Take his garment when he puts up collateral for a stranger. Hold it for a wayward woman!'),
('PRO', 27, 14, 'PRO.27.14', 'He who blesses his neighbor with a loud voice early in the morning, it will be taken as a curse by him.'),
('PRO', 27, 15, 'PRO.27.15', 'A continual dropping on a rainy day and a contentious wife are alike:'),
('PRO', 27, 16, 'PRO.27.16', 'restraining her is like restraining the wind, or like grasping oil in his right hand.'),
('PRO', 27, 17, 'PRO.27.17', 'Iron sharpens iron; so a man sharpens his friend’s countenance.'),
('PRO', 27, 18, 'PRO.27.18', 'Whoever tends the fig tree shall eat its fruit. He who looks after his master shall be honored.'),
('PRO', 27, 19, 'PRO.27.19', 'Like water reflects a face, so a man’s heart reflects the man.'),
('PRO', 27, 20, 'PRO.27.20', 'Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied; and a man’s eyes are never satisfied.'),
('PRO', 27, 21, 'PRO.27.21', 'The crucible is for silver, and the furnace for gold; but man is refined by his praise.'),
('PRO', 27, 22, 'PRO.27.22', 'Though you grind a fool in a mortar with a pestle along with grain, yet his foolishness will not be removed from him.'),
('PRO', 27, 23, 'PRO.27.23', 'Know well the state of your flocks, and pay attention to your herds,'),
('PRO', 27, 24, 'PRO.27.24', 'for riches are not forever, nor does the crown endure to all generations.'),
('PRO', 27, 25, 'PRO.27.25', 'The hay is removed, and the new growth appears, the grasses of the hills are gathered in.'),
('PRO', 27, 26, 'PRO.27.26', 'The lambs are for your clothing, and the goats are the price of a field.'),
('PRO', 27, 27, 'PRO.27.27', 'There will be plenty of goats’ milk for your food, for your family’s food, and for the nourishment of your servant girls.'),
('PRO', 28, 1, 'PRO.28.1', 'The wicked flee when no one pursues; but the righteous are as bold as a lion.'),
('PRO', 28, 2, 'PRO.28.2', 'In rebellion, a land has many rulers, but order is maintained by a man of understanding and knowledge.'),
('PRO', 28, 3, 'PRO.28.3', 'A needy man who oppresses the poor is like a driving rain which leaves no crops.'),
('PRO', 28, 4, 'PRO.28.4', 'Those who forsake the law praise the wicked; but those who keep the law contend with them.'),
('PRO', 28, 5, 'PRO.28.5', 'Evil men don’t understand justice; but those who seek the LORD understand it fully.'),
('PRO', 28, 6, 'PRO.28.6', 'Better is the poor who walks in his integrity than he who is perverse in his ways, and he is rich.'),
('PRO', 28, 7, 'PRO.28.7', 'Whoever keeps the law is a wise son; but he who is a companion of gluttons shames his father.'),
('PRO', 28, 8, 'PRO.28.8', 'He who increases his wealth by excessive interest gathers it for one who has pity on the poor.'),
('PRO', 28, 9, 'PRO.28.9', 'He who turns away his ear from hearing the law, even his prayer is an abomination.'),
('PRO', 28, 10, 'PRO.28.10', 'Whoever causes the upright to go astray in an evil way, he will fall into his own trap; but the blameless will inherit good.'),
('PRO', 28, 11, 'PRO.28.11', 'The rich man is wise in his own eyes; but the poor who has understanding sees through him.'),
('PRO', 28, 12, 'PRO.28.12', 'When the righteous triumph, there is great glory; but when the wicked rise, men hide themselves.'),
('PRO', 28, 13, 'PRO.28.13', 'He who conceals his sins doesn’t prosper, but whoever confesses and renounces them finds mercy.'),
('PRO', 28, 14, 'PRO.28.14', 'Blessed is the man who always fears; but one who hardens his heart falls into trouble.'),
('PRO', 28, 15, 'PRO.28.15', 'As a roaring lion or a charging bear, so is a wicked ruler over helpless people.'),
('PRO', 28, 16, 'PRO.28.16', 'A tyrannical ruler lacks judgment. One who hates ill-gotten gain will have long days.'),
('PRO', 28, 17, 'PRO.28.17', 'A man who is tormented by blood guilt will be a fugitive until death. No one will support him.'),
('PRO', 28, 18, 'PRO.28.18', 'Whoever walks blamelessly is kept safe; but one with perverse ways will fall suddenly.'),
('PRO', 28, 19, 'PRO.28.19', 'One who works his land will have an abundance of food; but one who chases fantasies will have his fill of poverty.'),
('PRO', 28, 20, 'PRO.28.20', 'A faithful man is rich with blessings; but one who is eager to be rich will not go unpunished.'),
('PRO', 28, 21, 'PRO.28.21', 'To show partiality is not good, yet a man will do wrong for a piece of bread.'),
('PRO', 28, 22, 'PRO.28.22', 'A stingy man hurries after riches, and doesn’t know that poverty waits for him.'),
('PRO', 28, 23, 'PRO.28.23', 'One who rebukes a man will afterward find more favor than one who flatters with the tongue.'),
('PRO', 28, 24, 'PRO.28.24', 'Whoever robs his father or his mother and says, “It’s not wrong,” is a partner with a destroyer.'),
('PRO', 28, 25, 'PRO.28.25', 'One who is greedy stirs up strife; but one who trusts in the LORD will prosper.'),
('PRO', 28, 26, 'PRO.28.26', 'One who trusts in himself is a fool; but one who walks in wisdom is kept safe.'),
('PRO', 28, 27, 'PRO.28.27', 'One who gives to the poor has no lack; but one who closes his eyes will have many curses.'),
('PRO', 28, 28, 'PRO.28.28', 'When the wicked rise, men hide themselves; but when they perish, the righteous thrive.'),
('PRO', 29, 1, 'PRO.29.1', 'He who is often rebuked and stiffens his neck will be destroyed suddenly, with no remedy.'),
('PRO', 29, 2, 'PRO.29.2', 'When the righteous thrive, the people rejoice; but when the wicked rule, the people groan.'),
('PRO', 29, 3, 'PRO.29.3', 'Whoever loves wisdom brings joy to his father; but a companion of prostitutes squanders his wealth.'),
('PRO', 29, 4, 'PRO.29.4', 'The king by justice makes the land stable, but he who takes bribes tears it down.'),
('PRO', 29, 5, 'PRO.29.5', 'A man who flatters his neighbor spreads a net for his feet.'),
('PRO', 29, 6, 'PRO.29.6', 'An evil man is snared by his sin, but the righteous can sing and be glad.'),
('PRO', 29, 7, 'PRO.29.7', 'The righteous care about justice for the poor. The wicked aren’t concerned about knowledge.'),
('PRO', 29, 8, 'PRO.29.8', 'Mockers stir up a city, but wise men turn away anger.'),
('PRO', 29, 9, 'PRO.29.9', 'If a wise man goes to court with a foolish man, the fool rages or scoffs, and there is no peace.'),
('PRO', 29, 10, 'PRO.29.10', 'The bloodthirsty hate a man of integrity; and they seek the life of the upright.'),
('PRO', 29, 11, 'PRO.29.11', 'A fool vents all of his anger, but a wise man brings himself under control.'),
('PRO', 29, 12, 'PRO.29.12', 'If a ruler listens to lies, all of his officials are wicked.'),
('PRO', 29, 13, 'PRO.29.13', 'The poor man and the oppressor have this in common: The LORD gives sight to the eyes of both.'),
('PRO', 29, 14, 'PRO.29.14', 'The king who fairly judges the poor, his throne shall be established forever.'),
('PRO', 29, 15, 'PRO.29.15', 'The rod of correction gives wisdom, but a child left to himself causes shame to his mother.'),
('PRO', 29, 16, 'PRO.29.16', 'When the wicked increase, sin increases; but the righteous will see their downfall.'),
('PRO', 29, 17, 'PRO.29.17', 'Correct your son, and he will give you peace; yes, he will bring delight to your soul.'),
('PRO', 29, 18, 'PRO.29.18', 'Where there is no revelation, the people cast off restraint; but one who keeps the law is blessed.'),
('PRO', 29, 19, 'PRO.29.19', 'A servant can’t be corrected by words. Though he understands, yet he will not respond.'),
('PRO', 29, 20, 'PRO.29.20', 'Do you see a man who is hasty in his words? There is more hope for a fool than for him.'),
('PRO', 29, 21, 'PRO.29.21', 'He who pampers his servant from youth will have him become a son in the end.'),
('PRO', 29, 22, 'PRO.29.22', 'An angry man stirs up strife, and a wrathful man abounds in sin.'),
('PRO', 29, 23, 'PRO.29.23', 'A man’s pride brings him low, but one of lowly spirit gains honor.'),
('PRO', 29, 24, 'PRO.29.24', 'Whoever is an accomplice of a thief is an enemy of his own soul. He takes an oath, but dares not testify.'),
('PRO', 29, 25, 'PRO.29.25', 'The fear of man proves to be a snare, but whoever puts his trust in the LORD is kept safe.'),
('PRO', 29, 26, 'PRO.29.26', 'Many seek the ruler’s favor, but a man’s justice comes from the LORD.'),
('PRO', 29, 27, 'PRO.29.27', 'A dishonest man detests the righteous, and the upright in their ways detest the wicked.'),
('PRO', 30, 1, 'PRO.30.1', 'The words of Agur the son of Jakeh, the revelation: the man says to Ithiel, to Ithiel and Ucal:'),
('PRO', 30, 2, 'PRO.30.2', '“Surely I am the most ignorant man, and don’t have a man’s understanding.'),
('PRO', 30, 3, 'PRO.30.3', 'I have not learned wisdom, neither do I have the knowledge of the Holy One.'),
('PRO', 30, 4, 'PRO.30.4', 'Who has ascended up into heaven, and descended? Who has gathered the wind in his fists? Who has bound the waters in his garment? Who has established all the ends of the earth? What is his name, and what is his son’s name, if you know?'),
('PRO', 30, 5, 'PRO.30.5', '“Every word of God is flawless. He is a shield to those who take refuge in him.'),
('PRO', 30, 6, 'PRO.30.6', 'Don’t you add to his words, lest he reprove you, and you be found a liar.'),
('PRO', 30, 7, 'PRO.30.7', '“Two things I have asked of you. Don’t deny me before I die.'),
('PRO', 30, 8, 'PRO.30.8', 'Remove far from me falsehood and lies. Give me neither poverty nor riches. Feed me with the food that is needful for me,'),
('PRO', 30, 9, 'PRO.30.9', 'lest I be full, deny you, and say, ‘Who is the LORD?’ or lest I be poor, and steal, and so dishonor the name of my God.'),
('PRO', 30, 10, 'PRO.30.10', '“Don’t slander a servant to his master, lest he curse you, and you be held guilty.'),
('PRO', 30, 11, 'PRO.30.11', 'There is a generation that curses their father, and doesn’t bless their mother.'),
('PRO', 30, 12, 'PRO.30.12', 'There is a generation that is pure in their own eyes, yet are not washed from their filthiness.'),
('PRO', 30, 13, 'PRO.30.13', 'There is a generation, oh how lofty are their eyes! Their eyelids are lifted up.'),
('PRO', 30, 14, 'PRO.30.14', 'There is a generation whose teeth are like swords, and their jaws like knives, to devour the poor from the earth, and the needy from among men.'),
('PRO', 30, 15, 'PRO.30.15', '“The leech has two daughters: ‘Give, give.’ “There are three things that are never satisfied; four that don’t say, ‘Enough!’:'),
('PRO', 30, 16, 'PRO.30.16', 'Sheol, the barren womb, the earth that is not satisfied with water, and the fire that doesn’t say, ‘Enough!’'),
('PRO', 30, 17, 'PRO.30.17', '“The eye that mocks at his father, and scorns obedience to his mother, the ravens of the valley shall pick it out, the young eagles shall eat it.'),
('PRO', 30, 18, 'PRO.30.18', '“There are three things which are too amazing for me, four which I don’t understand:'),
('PRO', 30, 19, 'PRO.30.19', 'The way of an eagle in the air, the way of a serpent on a rock, the way of a ship in the middle of the sea, and the way of a man with a maiden.'),
('PRO', 30, 20, 'PRO.30.20', '“So is the way of an adulterous woman: She eats and wipes her mouth, and says, ‘I have done nothing wrong.’'),
('PRO', 30, 21, 'PRO.30.21', '“For three things the earth trembles, and under four, it can’t bear up:'),
('PRO', 30, 22, 'PRO.30.22', 'For a servant when he is king, a fool when he is filled with food,'),
('PRO', 30, 23, 'PRO.30.23', 'for an unloved woman when she is married, and a servant who is heir to her mistress.'),
('PRO', 30, 24, 'PRO.30.24', '“There are four things which are little on the earth, but they are exceedingly wise:'),
('PRO', 30, 25, 'PRO.30.25', 'The ants are not a strong people, yet they provide their food in the summer.'),
('PRO', 30, 26, 'PRO.30.26', 'The hyraxes are but a feeble folk, yet make they their houses in the rocks.'),
('PRO', 30, 27, 'PRO.30.27', 'The locusts have no king, yet they advance in ranks.'),
('PRO', 30, 28, 'PRO.30.28', 'You can catch a lizard with your hands, yet it is in kings’ palaces.'),
('PRO', 30, 29, 'PRO.30.29', '“There are three things which are stately in their march, four which are stately in going:'),
('PRO', 30, 30, 'PRO.30.30', 'The lion, which is mightiest among animals, and doesn’t turn away for any;'),
('PRO', 30, 31, 'PRO.30.31', 'the greyhound; the male goat; and the king against whom there is no rising up.'),
('PRO', 30, 32, 'PRO.30.32', '“If you have done foolishly in lifting up yourself, or if you have thought evil, put your hand over your mouth.'),
('PRO', 30, 33, 'PRO.30.33', 'For as the churning of milk produces butter, and the wringing of the nose produces blood, so the forcing of wrath produces strife.”'),
('PRO', 31, 1, 'PRO.31.1', 'The words of King Lemuel—the revelation which his mother taught him:'),
('PRO', 31, 2, 'PRO.31.2', '“Oh, my son! Oh, son of my womb! Oh, son of my vows!'),
('PRO', 31, 3, 'PRO.31.3', 'Don’t give your strength to women, nor your ways to that which destroys kings.'),
('PRO', 31, 4, 'PRO.31.4', 'It is not for kings, Lemuel, it is not for kings to drink wine, nor for princes to say, ‘Where is strong drink?’'),
('PRO', 31, 5, 'PRO.31.5', 'lest they drink, and forget the law, and pervert the justice due to anyone who is afflicted.'),
('PRO', 31, 6, 'PRO.31.6', 'Give strong drink to him who is ready to perish, and wine to the bitter in soul.'),
('PRO', 31, 7, 'PRO.31.7', 'Let him drink, and forget his poverty, and remember his misery no more.'),
('PRO', 31, 8, 'PRO.31.8', 'Open your mouth for the mute, in the cause of all who are left desolate.'),
('PRO', 31, 9, 'PRO.31.9', 'Open your mouth, judge righteously, and serve justice to the poor and needy.”'),
('PRO', 31, 10, 'PRO.31.10', 'Who can find a worthy woman? For her value is far above rubies.'),
('PRO', 31, 11, 'PRO.31.11', 'The heart of her husband trusts in her. He shall have no lack of gain.'),
('PRO', 31, 12, 'PRO.31.12', 'She does him good, and not harm, all the days of her life.'),
('PRO', 31, 13, 'PRO.31.13', 'She seeks wool and flax, and works eagerly with her hands.'),
('PRO', 31, 14, 'PRO.31.14', 'She is like the merchant ships. She brings her bread from afar.'),
('PRO', 31, 15, 'PRO.31.15', 'She rises also while it is yet night, gives food to her household, and portions for her servant girls.'),
('PRO', 31, 16, 'PRO.31.16', 'She considers a field, and buys it. With the fruit of her hands, she plants a vineyard.'),
('PRO', 31, 17, 'PRO.31.17', 'She arms her waist with strength, and makes her arms strong.'),
('PRO', 31, 18, 'PRO.31.18', 'She perceives that her merchandise is profitable. Her lamp doesn’t go out by night.'),
('PRO', 31, 19, 'PRO.31.19', 'She lays her hands to the distaff, and her hands hold the spindle.'),
('PRO', 31, 20, 'PRO.31.20', 'She opens her arms to the poor; yes, she extends her hands to the needy.'),
('PRO', 31, 21, 'PRO.31.21', 'She is not afraid of the snow for her household, for all her household are clothed with scarlet.'),
('PRO', 31, 22, 'PRO.31.22', 'She makes for herself carpets of tapestry. Her clothing is fine linen and purple.'),
('PRO', 31, 23, 'PRO.31.23', 'Her husband is respected in the gates, when he sits among the elders of the land.'),
('PRO', 31, 24, 'PRO.31.24', 'She makes linen garments and sells them, and delivers sashes to the merchant.'),
('PRO', 31, 25, 'PRO.31.25', 'Strength and dignity are her clothing. She laughs at the time to come.'),
('PRO', 31, 26, 'PRO.31.26', 'She opens her mouth with wisdom. Kind instruction is on her tongue.'),
('PRO', 31, 27, 'PRO.31.27', 'She looks well to the ways of her household, and doesn’t eat the bread of idleness.'),
('PRO', 31, 28, 'PRO.31.28', 'Her children rise up and call her blessed. Her husband also praises her:'),
('PRO', 31, 29, 'PRO.31.29', '“Many women do noble things, but you excel them all.”'),
('PRO', 31, 30, 'PRO.31.30', 'Charm is deceitful, and beauty is vain; but a woman who fears the LORD, she shall be praised.'),
('PRO', 31, 31, 'PRO.31.31', 'Give her of the fruit of her hands! Let her works praise her in the gates!'),
('ECC', 1, 1, 'ECC.1.1', 'The words of the Preacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem:'),
('ECC', 1, 2, 'ECC.1.2', '“Vanity of vanities,” says the Preacher; “Vanity of vanities, all is vanity.”'),
('ECC', 1, 3, 'ECC.1.3', 'What does man gain from all his labor in which he labors under the sun?'),
('ECC', 1, 4, 'ECC.1.4', 'One generation goes, and another generation comes; but the earth remains forever.'),
('ECC', 1, 5, 'ECC.1.5', 'The sun also rises, and the sun goes down, and hurries to its place where it rises.'),
('ECC', 1, 6, 'ECC.1.6', 'The wind goes toward the south, and turns around to the north. It turns around continually as it goes, and the wind returns again to its courses.'),
('ECC', 1, 7, 'ECC.1.7', 'All the rivers run into the sea, yet the sea is not full. To the place where the rivers flow, there they flow again.'),
('ECC', 1, 8, 'ECC.1.8', 'All things are full of weariness beyond uttering. The eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.'),
('ECC', 1, 9, 'ECC.1.9', 'That which has been is that which shall be, and that which has been done is that which shall be done; and there is no new thing under the sun.'),
('ECC', 1, 10, 'ECC.1.10', 'Is there a thing of which it may be said, “Behold, this is new”? It has been long ago, in the ages which were before us.'),
('ECC', 1, 11, 'ECC.1.11', 'There is no memory of the former; neither shall there be any memory of the latter that are to come, among those that shall come after.'),
('ECC', 1, 12, 'ECC.1.12', 'I, the Preacher, was king over Israel in Jerusalem.'),
('ECC', 1, 13, 'ECC.1.13', 'I applied my heart to seek and to search out by wisdom concerning all that is done under the sky. It is a heavy burden that God has given to the sons of men to be afflicted with.'),
('ECC', 1, 14, 'ECC.1.14', 'I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and behold, all is vanity and a chasing after wind.'),
('ECC', 1, 15, 'ECC.1.15', 'That which is crooked can’t be made straight; and that which is lacking can’t be counted.'),
('ECC', 1, 16, 'ECC.1.16', 'I said to myself, “Behold, I have obtained for myself great wisdom above all who were before me in Jerusalem. Yes, my heart has had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.”'),
('ECC', 1, 17, 'ECC.1.17', 'I applied my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly. I perceived that this also was a chasing after wind.'),
('ECC', 1, 18, 'ECC.1.18', 'For in much wisdom is much grief; and he who increases knowledge increases sorrow.'),
('ECC', 2, 1, 'ECC.2.1', 'I said in my heart, “Come now, I will test you with mirth; therefore enjoy pleasure;” and behold, this also was vanity.'),
('ECC', 2, 2, 'ECC.2.2', 'I said of laughter, “It is foolishness;” and of mirth, “What does it accomplish?”'),
('ECC', 2, 3, 'ECC.2.3', 'I searched in my heart how to cheer my flesh with wine, my heart yet guiding me with wisdom, and how to lay hold of folly, until I might see what it was good for the sons of men that they should do under heaven all the days of their lives.'),
('ECC', 2, 4, 'ECC.2.4', 'I made myself great works. I built myself houses. I planted myself vineyards.'),
('ECC', 2, 5, 'ECC.2.5', 'I made myself gardens and parks, and I planted trees in them of all kinds of fruit.'),
('ECC', 2, 6, 'ECC.2.6', 'I made myself pools of water, to water the forest where trees were grown.'),
('ECC', 2, 7, 'ECC.2.7', 'I bought male servants and female servants, and had servants born in my house. I also had great possessions of herds and flocks, above all who were before me in Jerusalem.'),
('ECC', 2, 8, 'ECC.2.8', 'I also gathered silver and gold for myself, and the treasure of kings and of the provinces. I got myself male and female singers, and the delights of the sons of men: musical instruments of all sorts.'),
('ECC', 2, 9, 'ECC.2.9', 'So I was great, and increased more than all who were before me in Jerusalem. My wisdom also remained with me.'),
('ECC', 2, 10, 'ECC.2.10', 'Whatever my eyes desired, I didn’t keep from them. I didn’t withhold my heart from any joy, for my heart rejoiced because of all my labor, and this was my portion from all my labor.'),
('ECC', 2, 11, 'ECC.2.11', 'Then I looked at all the works that my hands had worked, and at the labor that I had labored to do; and behold, all was vanity and a chasing after wind, and there was no profit under the sun.'),
('ECC', 2, 12, 'ECC.2.12', 'I turned myself to consider wisdom, madness, and folly; for what can the king’s successor do? Just that which has been done long ago.'),
('ECC', 2, 13, 'ECC.2.13', 'Then I saw that wisdom excels folly, as far as light excels darkness.'),
('ECC', 2, 14, 'ECC.2.14', 'The wise man’s eyes are in his head, and the fool walks in darkness—and yet I perceived that one event happens to them all.'),
('ECC', 2, 15, 'ECC.2.15', 'Then I said in my heart, “As it happens to the fool, so will it happen even to me; and why was I then more wise?” Then I said in my heart that this also is vanity.'),
('ECC', 2, 16, 'ECC.2.16', 'For of the wise man, even as of the fool, there is no memory forever, since in the days to come all will have been long forgotten. Indeed, the wise man must die just like the fool!'),
('ECC', 2, 17, 'ECC.2.17', 'So I hated life, because the work that is worked under the sun was grievous to me; for all is vanity and a chasing after wind.'),
('ECC', 2, 18, 'ECC.2.18', 'I hated all my labor in which I labored under the sun, because I must leave it to the man who comes after me.'),
('ECC', 2, 19, 'ECC.2.19', 'Who knows whether he will be a wise man or a fool? Yet he will have rule over all of my labor in which I have labored, and in which I have shown myself wise under the sun. This also is vanity.'),
('ECC', 2, 20, 'ECC.2.20', 'Therefore I began to cause my heart to despair concerning all the labor in which I had labored under the sun.'),
('ECC', 2, 21, 'ECC.2.21', 'For there is a man whose labor is with wisdom, with knowledge, and with skillfulness; yet he shall leave it for his portion to a man who has not labored for it. This also is vanity and a great evil.'),
('ECC', 2, 22, 'ECC.2.22', 'For what does a man have of all his labor and of the striving of his heart, in which he labors under the sun?'),
('ECC', 2, 23, 'ECC.2.23', 'For all his days are sorrows, and his travail is grief; yes, even in the night his heart takes no rest. This also is vanity.'),
('ECC', 2, 24, 'ECC.2.24', 'There is nothing better for a man than that he should eat and drink, and make his soul enjoy good in his labor. This also I saw, that it is from the hand of God.'),
('ECC', 2, 25, 'ECC.2.25', 'For who can eat, or who can have enjoyment, more than I?'),
('ECC', 2, 26, 'ECC.2.26', 'For to the man who pleases him, God gives wisdom, knowledge, and joy; but to the sinner he gives travail, to gather and to heap up, that he may give to him who pleases God. This also is vanity and a chasing after wind.'),
('ECC', 3, 1, 'ECC.3.1', 'For everything there is a season, and a time for every purpose under heaven:'),
('ECC', 3, 2, 'ECC.3.2', 'a time to be born, and a time to die; a time to plant, and a time to pluck up that which is planted;'),
('ECC', 3, 3, 'ECC.3.3', 'a time to kill, and a time to heal; a time to break down, and a time to build up;'),
('ECC', 3, 4, 'ECC.3.4', 'a time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;'),
('ECC', 3, 5, 'ECC.3.5', 'a time to cast away stones, and a time to gather stones together; a time to embrace, and a time to refrain from embracing;'),
('ECC', 3, 6, 'ECC.3.6', 'a time to seek, and a time to lose; a time to keep, and a time to cast away;'),
('ECC', 3, 7, 'ECC.3.7', 'a time to tear, and a time to sew; a time to keep silence, and a time to speak;'),
('ECC', 3, 8, 'ECC.3.8', 'a time to love, and a time to hate; a time for war, and a time for peace.'),
('ECC', 3, 9, 'ECC.3.9', 'What profit has he who works in that in which he labors?'),
('ECC', 3, 10, 'ECC.3.10', 'I have seen the burden which God has given to the sons of men to be afflicted with.'),
('ECC', 3, 11, 'ECC.3.11', 'He has made everything beautiful in its time. He has also set eternity in their hearts, yet so that man can’t find out the work that God has done from the beginning even to the end.'),
('ECC', 3, 12, 'ECC.3.12', 'I know that there is nothing better for them than to rejoice, and to do good as long as they live.'),
('ECC', 3, 13, 'ECC.3.13', 'Also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy good in all his labor, is the gift of God.'),
('ECC', 3, 14, 'ECC.3.14', 'I know that whatever God does, it shall be forever. Nothing can be added to it, nor anything taken from it; and God has done it, that men should fear before him.'),
('ECC', 3, 15, 'ECC.3.15', 'That which is has been long ago, and that which is to be has been long ago. God seeks again that which is passed away.'),
('ECC', 3, 16, 'ECC.3.16', 'Moreover I saw under the sun, in the place of justice, that wickedness was there; and in the place of righteousness, that wickedness was there.'),
('ECC', 3, 17, 'ECC.3.17', 'I said in my heart, “God will judge the righteous and the wicked; for there is a time there for every purpose and for every work.”'),
('ECC', 3, 18, 'ECC.3.18', 'I said in my heart, “As for the sons of men, God tests them, so that they may see that they themselves are like animals.'),
('ECC', 3, 19, 'ECC.3.19', 'For that which happens to the sons of men happens to animals. Even one thing happens to them. As the one dies, so the other dies. Yes, they have all one breath; and man has no advantage over the animals, for all is vanity.'),
('ECC', 3, 20, 'ECC.3.20', 'All go to one place. All are from the dust, and all turn to dust again.'),
('ECC', 3, 21, 'ECC.3.21', 'Who knows the spirit of man, whether it goes upward, and the spirit of the animal, whether it goes downward to the earth?”'),
('ECC', 3, 22, 'ECC.3.22', 'Therefore I saw that there is nothing better than that a man should rejoice in his works, for that is his portion; for who can bring him to see what will be after him?'),
('ECC', 4, 1, 'ECC.4.1', 'Then I returned and saw all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and behold, the tears of those who were oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors there was power; but they had no comforter.'),
('ECC', 4, 2, 'ECC.4.2', 'Therefore I praised the dead who have been long dead more than the living who are yet alive.'),
('ECC', 4, 3, 'ECC.4.3', 'Yes, better than them both is him who has not yet been, who has not seen the evil work that is done under the sun.'),
('ECC', 4, 4, 'ECC.4.4', 'Then I saw all the labor and achievement that is the envy of a man’s neighbor. This also is vanity and a striving after wind.'),
('ECC', 4, 5, 'ECC.4.5', 'The fool folds his hands together and ruins himself.'),
('ECC', 4, 6, 'ECC.4.6', 'Better is a handful, with quietness, than two handfuls with labor and chasing after wind.'),
('ECC', 4, 7, 'ECC.4.7', 'Then I returned and saw vanity under the sun.'),
('ECC', 4, 8, 'ECC.4.8', 'There is one who is alone, and he has neither son nor brother. There is no end to all of his labor, neither are his eyes satisfied with wealth. “For whom then do I labor and deprive my soul of enjoyment?” This also is vanity. Yes, it is a miserable business.'),
('ECC', 4, 9, 'ECC.4.9', 'Two are better than one, because they have a good reward for their labor.'),
('ECC', 4, 10, 'ECC.4.10', 'For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow; but woe to him who is alone when he falls, and doesn’t have another to lift him up.'),
('ECC', 4, 11, 'ECC.4.11', 'Again, if two lie together, then they have warmth; but how can one keep warm alone?'),
('ECC', 4, 12, 'ECC.4.12', 'If a man prevails against one who is alone, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken.'),
('ECC', 4, 13, 'ECC.4.13', 'Better is a poor and wise youth than an old and foolish king who doesn’t know how to receive admonition any more.'),
('ECC', 4, 14, 'ECC.4.14', 'For out of prison he came out to be king; yes, even in his kingdom he was born poor.'),
('ECC', 4, 15, 'ECC.4.15', 'I saw all the living who walk under the sun, that they were with the youth, the other, who succeeded him.'),
('ECC', 4, 16, 'ECC.4.16', 'There was no end of all the people, even of all them over whom he was—yet those who come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also is vanity and a chasing after wind.'),
('ECC', 5, 1, 'ECC.5.1', 'Guard your steps when you go to God’s house; for to draw near to listen is better than to give the sacrifice of fools, for they don’t know that they do evil.'),
('ECC', 5, 2, 'ECC.5.2', 'Don’t be rash with your mouth, and don’t let your heart be hasty to utter anything before God; for God is in heaven, and you on earth. Therefore let your words be few.'),
('ECC', 5, 3, 'ECC.5.3', 'For as a dream comes with a multitude of cares, so a fool’s speech with a multitude of words.'),
('ECC', 5, 4, 'ECC.5.4', 'When you vow a vow to God, don’t defer to pay it; for he has no pleasure in fools. Pay that which you vow.'),
('ECC', 5, 5, 'ECC.5.5', 'It is better that you should not vow, than that you should vow and not pay.'),
('ECC', 5, 6, 'ECC.5.6', 'Don’t allow your mouth to lead you into sin. Don’t protest before the messenger that this was a mistake. Why should God be angry at your voice, and destroy the work of your hands?'),
('ECC', 5, 7, 'ECC.5.7', 'For in the multitude of dreams there are vanities, as well as in many words; but you must fear God.'),
('ECC', 5, 8, 'ECC.5.8', 'If you see the oppression of the poor, and the violent taking away of justice and righteousness in a district, don’t marvel at the matter, for one official is eyed by a higher one, and there are officials over them.'),
('ECC', 5, 9, 'ECC.5.9', 'Moreover the profit of the earth is for all. The king profits from the field.'),
('ECC', 5, 10, 'ECC.5.10', 'He who loves silver shall not be satisfied with silver, nor he who loves abundance, with increase. This also is vanity.'),
('ECC', 5, 11, 'ECC.5.11', 'When goods increase, those who eat them are increased; and what advantage is there to its owner, except to feast on them with his eyes?'),
('ECC', 5, 12, 'ECC.5.12', 'The sleep of a laboring man is sweet, whether he eats little or much; but the abundance of the rich will not allow him to sleep.'),
('ECC', 5, 13, 'ECC.5.13', 'There is a grievous evil which I have seen under the sun: wealth kept by its owner to his harm.'),
('ECC', 5, 14, 'ECC.5.14', 'Those riches perish by misfortune, and if he has fathered a son, there is nothing in his hand.'),
('ECC', 5, 15, 'ECC.5.15', 'As he came out of his mother’s womb, naked shall he go again as he came, and shall take nothing for his labor, which he may carry away in his hand.'),
('ECC', 5, 16, 'ECC.5.16', 'This also is a grievous evil, that in all points as he came, so shall he go. And what profit does he have who labors for the wind?'),
('ECC', 5, 17, 'ECC.5.17', 'All his days he also eats in darkness, he is frustrated, and has sickness and wrath.'),
('ECC', 5, 18, 'ECC.5.18', 'Behold, that which I have seen to be good and proper is for one to eat and to drink, and to enjoy good in all his labor, in which he labors under the sun, all the days of his life which God has given him; for this is his portion.'),
('ECC', 5, 19, 'ECC.5.19', 'Every man also to whom God has given riches and wealth, and has given him power to eat of it, and to take his portion, and to rejoice in his labor—this is the gift of God.'),
('ECC', 5, 20, 'ECC.5.20', 'For he shall not often reflect on the days of his life, because God occupies him with the joy of his heart.'),
('ECC', 6, 1, 'ECC.6.1', 'There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, and it is heavy on men:'),
('ECC', 6, 2, 'ECC.6.2', 'a man to whom God gives riches, wealth, and honor, so that he lacks nothing for his soul of all that he desires, yet God gives him no power to eat of it, but an alien eats it. This is vanity, and it is an evil disease.'),
('ECC', 6, 3, 'ECC.6.3', 'If a man fathers a hundred children, and lives many years, so that the days of his years are many, but his soul is not filled with good, and moreover he has no burial, I say that a stillborn child is better than he;'),
('ECC', 6, 4, 'ECC.6.4', 'for it comes in vanity, and departs in darkness, and its name is covered with darkness.'),
('ECC', 6, 5, 'ECC.6.5', 'Moreover it has not seen the sun nor known it. This has rest rather than the other.'),
('ECC', 6, 6, 'ECC.6.6', 'Yes, though he live a thousand years twice told, and yet fails to enjoy good, don’t all go to one place?'),
('ECC', 6, 7, 'ECC.6.7', 'All the labor of man is for his mouth, and yet the appetite is not filled.'),
('ECC', 6, 8, 'ECC.6.8', 'For what advantage has the wise more than the fool? What has the poor man, that knows how to walk before the living?'),
('ECC', 6, 9, 'ECC.6.9', 'Better is the sight of the eyes than the wandering of the desire. This also is vanity and a chasing after wind.'),
('ECC', 6, 10, 'ECC.6.10', 'Whatever has been, its name was given long ago; and it is known what man is; neither can he contend with him who is mightier than he.'),
('ECC', 6, 11, 'ECC.6.11', 'For there are many words that create vanity. What does that profit man?'),
('ECC', 6, 12, 'ECC.6.12', 'For who knows what is good for man in life, all the days of his vain life which he spends like a shadow? For who can tell a man what will be after him under the sun?'),
('ECC', 7, 1, 'ECC.7.1', 'A good name is better than fine perfume; and the day of death better than the day of one’s birth.'),
('ECC', 7, 2, 'ECC.7.2', 'It is better to go to the house of mourning than to go to the house of feasting; for that is the end of all men, and the living should take this to heart.'),
('ECC', 7, 3, 'ECC.7.3', 'Sorrow is better than laughter; for by the sadness of the face the heart is made good.'),
('ECC', 7, 4, 'ECC.7.4', 'The heart of the wise is in the house of mourning; but the heart of fools is in the house of mirth.'),
('ECC', 7, 5, 'ECC.7.5', 'It is better to hear the rebuke of the wise than for a man to hear the song of fools.'),
('ECC', 7, 6, 'ECC.7.6', 'For as the crackling of thorns under a pot, so is the laughter of the fool. This also is vanity.'),
('ECC', 7, 7, 'ECC.7.7', 'Surely extortion makes the wise man foolish; and a bribe destroys the understanding.'),
('ECC', 7, 8, 'ECC.7.8', 'Better is the end of a thing than its beginning. The patient in spirit is better than the proud in spirit.'),
('ECC', 7, 9, 'ECC.7.9', 'Don’t be hasty in your spirit to be angry, for anger rests in the bosom of fools.'),
('ECC', 7, 10, 'ECC.7.10', 'Don’t say, “Why were the former days better than these?” For you do not ask wisely about this.'),
('ECC', 7, 11, 'ECC.7.11', 'Wisdom is as good as an inheritance. Yes, it is more excellent for those who see the sun.'),
('ECC', 7, 12, 'ECC.7.12', 'For wisdom is a defense, even as money is a defense; but the excellency of knowledge is that wisdom preserves the life of him who has it.'),
('ECC', 7, 13, 'ECC.7.13', 'Consider the work of God, for who can make that straight which he has made crooked?'),
('ECC', 7, 14, 'ECC.7.14', 'In the day of prosperity be joyful, and in the day of adversity consider; yes, God has made the one side by side with the other, to the end that man should not find out anything after him.'),
('ECC', 7, 15, 'ECC.7.15', 'All this I have seen in my days of vanity: there is a righteous man who perishes in his righteousness, and there is a wicked man who lives long in his evildoing.'),
('ECC', 7, 16, 'ECC.7.16', 'Don’t be overly righteous, neither make yourself overly wise. Why should you destroy yourself?'),
('ECC', 7, 17, 'ECC.7.17', 'Don’t be too wicked, neither be foolish. Why should you die before your time?'),
('ECC', 7, 18, 'ECC.7.18', 'It is good that you should take hold of this. Yes, also don’t withdraw your hand from that; for he who fears God will come out of them all.'),
('ECC', 7, 19, 'ECC.7.19', 'Wisdom is a strength to the wise man more than ten rulers who are in a city.'),
('ECC', 7, 20, 'ECC.7.20', 'Surely there is not a righteous man on earth who does good and doesn’t sin.'),
('ECC', 7, 21, 'ECC.7.21', 'Also don’t take heed to all words that are spoken, lest you hear your servant curse you;'),
('ECC', 7, 22, 'ECC.7.22', 'for often your own heart knows that you yourself have likewise cursed others.'),
('ECC', 7, 23, 'ECC.7.23', 'All this I have proved in wisdom. I said, “I will be wise;” but it was far from me.'),
('ECC', 7, 24, 'ECC.7.24', 'That which is, is far off and exceedingly deep. Who can find it out?'),
('ECC', 7, 25, 'ECC.7.25', 'I turned around, and my heart sought to know and to search out, and to seek wisdom and the scheme of things, and to know that wickedness is stupidity, and that foolishness is madness.'),
('ECC', 7, 26, 'ECC.7.26', 'I find more bitter than death the woman whose heart is snares and traps, whose hands are chains. Whoever pleases God shall escape from her; but the sinner will be ensnared by her.'),
('ECC', 7, 27, 'ECC.7.27', '“Behold, I have found this,” says the Preacher, “to one another, to find an explanation'),
('ECC', 7, 28, 'ECC.7.28', 'which my soul still seeks, but I have not found. I have found one man among a thousand, but I have not found a woman among all those.'),
('ECC', 7, 29, 'ECC.7.29', 'Behold, I have only found this: that God made mankind upright; but they search for many inventions.”'),
('ECC', 8, 1, 'ECC.8.1', 'Who is like the wise man? And who knows the interpretation of a thing? A man’s wisdom makes his face shine, and the hardness of his face is changed.'),
('ECC', 8, 2, 'ECC.8.2', 'I say, “Keep the king’s command!” because of the oath to God.'),
('ECC', 8, 3, 'ECC.8.3', 'Don’t be hasty to go out of his presence. Don’t persist in an evil thing, for he does whatever pleases him,'),
('ECC', 8, 4, 'ECC.8.4', 'for the king’s word is supreme. Who can say to him, “What are you doing?”'),
('ECC', 8, 5, 'ECC.8.5', 'Whoever keeps the commandment shall not come to harm, and his wise heart will know the time and procedure.'),
('ECC', 8, 6, 'ECC.8.6', 'For there is a time and procedure for every purpose, although the misery of man is heavy on him.'),
('ECC', 8, 7, 'ECC.8.7', 'For he doesn’t know that which will be; for who can tell him how it will be?'),
('ECC', 8, 8, 'ECC.8.8', 'There is no man who has power over the spirit to contain the spirit; neither does he have power over the day of death. There is no discharge in war; neither shall wickedness deliver those who practice it.'),
('ECC', 8, 9, 'ECC.8.9', 'All this I have seen, and applied my mind to every work that is done under the sun. There is a time in which one man has power over another to his hurt.'),
('ECC', 8, 10, 'ECC.8.10', 'So I saw the wicked buried. Indeed they came also from holiness. They went and were forgotten in the city where they did this. This also is vanity.'),
('ECC', 8, 11, 'ECC.8.11', 'Because sentence against an evil work is not executed speedily, therefore the heart of the sons of men is fully set in them to do evil.'),
('ECC', 8, 12, 'ECC.8.12', 'Though a sinner commits crimes a hundred times, and lives long, yet surely I know that it will be better with those who fear God, who are reverent before him.'),
('ECC', 8, 13, 'ECC.8.13', 'But it shall not be well with the wicked, neither shall he lengthen days like a shadow, because he doesn’t fear God.'),
('ECC', 8, 14, 'ECC.8.14', 'There is a vanity which is done on the earth, that there are righteous men to whom it happens according to the work of the wicked. Again, there are wicked men to whom it happens according to the work of the righteous. I said that this also is vanity.'),
('ECC', 8, 15, 'ECC.8.15', 'Then I commended mirth, because a man has no better thing under the sun than to eat, to drink, and to be joyful: for that will accompany him in his labor all the days of his life which God has given him under the sun.'),
('ECC', 8, 16, 'ECC.8.16', 'When I applied my heart to know wisdom, and to see the business that is done on the earth (even though eyes see no sleep day or night),'),
('ECC', 8, 17, 'ECC.8.17', 'then I saw all the work of God, that man can’t find out the work that is done under the sun, because however much a man labors to seek it out, yet he won’t find it. Yes even though a wise man thinks he can comprehend it, he won’t be able to find it.'),
('ECC', 9, 1, 'ECC.9.1', 'For all this I laid to my heart, even to explore all this: that the righteous, and the wise, and their works, are in the hand of God; whether it is love or hatred, man doesn’t know it; all is before them.'),
('ECC', 9, 2, 'ECC.9.2', 'All things come alike to all. There is one event to the righteous and to the wicked; to the good, to the clean, to the unclean, to him who sacrifices, and to him who doesn’t sacrifice. As is the good, so is the sinner; he who takes an oath, as he who fears an oath.'),
('ECC', 9, 3, 'ECC.9.3', 'This is an evil in all that is done under the sun, that there is one event to all. Yes also, the heart of the sons of men is full of evil, and madness is in their heart while they live, and after that they go to the dead.'),
('ECC', 9, 4, 'ECC.9.4', 'For to him who is joined with all the living there is hope; for a living dog is better than a dead lion.'),
('ECC', 9, 5, 'ECC.9.5', 'For the living know that they will die, but the dead don’t know anything, neither do they have any more a reward; for their memory is forgotten.'),
('ECC', 9, 6, 'ECC.9.6', 'Also their love, their hatred, and their envy has perished long ago; neither do they any longer have a portion forever in anything that is done under the sun.'),
('ECC', 9, 7, 'ECC.9.7', 'Go your way—eat your bread with joy, and drink your wine with a merry heart; for God has already accepted your works.'),
('ECC', 9, 8, 'ECC.9.8', 'Let your garments be always white, and don’t let your head lack oil.'),
('ECC', 9, 9, 'ECC.9.9', 'Live joyfully with the wife whom you love all the days of your life of vanity, which he has given you under the sun, all your days of vanity, for that is your portion in life, and in your labor in which you labor under the sun.'),
('ECC', 9, 10, 'ECC.9.10', 'Whatever your hand finds to do, do it with your might; for there is no work, nor plan, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in Sheol, where you are going.'),
('ECC', 9, 11, 'ECC.9.11', 'I returned and saw under the sun that the race is not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong, neither yet bread to the wise, nor yet riches to men of understanding, nor yet favor to men of skill; but time and chance happen to them all.'),
('ECC', 9, 12, 'ECC.9.12', 'For man also doesn’t know his time. As the fish that are taken in an evil net, and as the birds that are caught in the snare, even so are the sons of men snared in an evil time, when it falls suddenly on them.'),
('ECC', 9, 13, 'ECC.9.13', 'I have also seen wisdom under the sun in this way, and it seemed great to me.'),
('ECC', 9, 14, 'ECC.9.14', 'There was a little city, and few men within it; and a great king came against it, besieged it, and built great bulwarks against it.'),
('ECC', 9, 15, 'ECC.9.15', 'Now a poor wise man was found in it, and he by his wisdom delivered the city; yet no man remembered that same poor man.'),
('ECC', 9, 16, 'ECC.9.16', 'Then I said, “Wisdom is better than strength.” Nevertheless the poor man’s wisdom is despised, and his words are not heard.'),
('ECC', 9, 17, 'ECC.9.17', 'The words of the wise heard in quiet are better than the cry of him who rules among fools.'),
('ECC', 9, 18, 'ECC.9.18', 'Wisdom is better than weapons of war; but one sinner destroys much good.'),
('ECC', 10, 1, 'ECC.10.1', 'Dead flies cause the oil of the perfumer to produce an evil odor; so does a little folly outweigh wisdom and honor.'),
('ECC', 10, 2, 'ECC.10.2', 'A wise man’s heart is at his right hand, but a fool’s heart at his left.'),
('ECC', 10, 3, 'ECC.10.3', 'Yes also when the fool walks by the way, his understanding fails him, and he says to everyone that he is a fool.'),
('ECC', 10, 4, 'ECC.10.4', 'If the spirit of the ruler rises up against you, don’t leave your place; for gentleness lays great offenses to rest.'),
('ECC', 10, 5, 'ECC.10.5', 'There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, the sort of error which proceeds from the ruler.'),
('ECC', 10, 6, 'ECC.10.6', 'Folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in a low place.'),
('ECC', 10, 7, 'ECC.10.7', 'I have seen servants on horses, and princes walking like servants on the earth.'),
('ECC', 10, 8, 'ECC.10.8', 'He who digs a pit may fall into it; and whoever breaks through a wall may be bitten by a snake.'),
('ECC', 10, 9, 'ECC.10.9', 'Whoever carves out stones may be injured by them. Whoever splits wood may be endangered by it.'),
('ECC', 10, 10, 'ECC.10.10', 'If the ax is blunt, and one doesn’t sharpen the edge, then he must use more strength; but skill brings success.'),
('ECC', 10, 11, 'ECC.10.11', 'If the snake bites before it is charmed, then is there no profit for the charmer’s tongue.'),
('ECC', 10, 12, 'ECC.10.12', 'The words of a wise man’s mouth are gracious; but a fool is swallowed by his own lips.'),
('ECC', 10, 13, 'ECC.10.13', 'The beginning of the words of his mouth is foolishness; and the end of his talk is mischievous madness.'),
('ECC', 10, 14, 'ECC.10.14', 'A fool also multiplies words. Man doesn’t know what will be; and that which will be after him, who can tell him?'),
('ECC', 10, 15, 'ECC.10.15', 'The labor of fools wearies every one of them; for he doesn’t know how to go to the city.'),
('ECC', 10, 16, 'ECC.10.16', 'Woe to you, land, when your king is a child, and your princes eat in the morning!'),
('ECC', 10, 17, 'ECC.10.17', 'Happy are you, land, when your king is the son of nobles, and your princes eat in due season, for strength, and not for drunkenness!'),
('ECC', 10, 18, 'ECC.10.18', 'By slothfulness the roof sinks in; and through idleness of the hands the house leaks.'),
('ECC', 10, 19, 'ECC.10.19', 'A feast is made for laughter, and wine makes the life glad; and money is the answer for all things.'),
('ECC', 10, 20, 'ECC.10.20', 'Don’t curse the king, no, not in your thoughts; and don’t curse the rich in your bedroom, for a bird of the sky may carry your voice, and that which has wings may tell the matter.'),
('ECC', 11, 1, 'ECC.11.1', 'Cast your bread on the waters; for you shall find it after many days.'),
('ECC', 11, 2, 'ECC.11.2', 'Give a portion to seven, yes, even to eight; for you don’t know what evil will be on the earth.'),
('ECC', 11, 3, 'ECC.11.3', 'If the clouds are full of rain, they empty themselves on the earth; and if a tree falls toward the south, or toward the north, in the place where the tree falls, there shall it be.'),
('ECC', 11, 4, 'ECC.11.4', 'He who observes the wind won’t sow; and he who regards the clouds won’t reap.'),
('ECC', 11, 5, 'ECC.11.5', 'As you don’t know what is the way of the wind, nor how the bones grow in the womb of her who is with child; even so you don’t know the work of God who does all.'),
('ECC', 11, 6, 'ECC.11.6', 'In the morning sow your seed, and in the evening don’t withhold your hand; for you don’t know which will prosper, whether this or that, or whether they both will be equally good.'),
('ECC', 11, 7, 'ECC.11.7', 'Truly the light is sweet, and it is a pleasant thing for the eyes to see the sun.'),
('ECC', 11, 8, 'ECC.11.8', 'Yes, if a man lives many years, let him rejoice in them all; but let him remember the days of darkness, for they shall be many. All that comes is vanity.'),
('ECC', 11, 9, 'ECC.11.9', 'Rejoice, young man, in your youth, and let your heart cheer you in the days of your youth, and walk in the ways of your heart, and in the sight of your eyes; but know that for all these things God will bring you into judgment.'),
('ECC', 11, 10, 'ECC.11.10', 'Therefore remove sorrow from your heart, and put away evil from your flesh; for youth and the dawn of life are vanity.'),
('ECC', 12, 1, 'ECC.12.1', 'Remember also your Creator in the days of your youth, before the evil days come, and the years draw near, when you will say, “I have no pleasure in them;”'),
('ECC', 12, 2, 'ECC.12.2', 'Before the sun, the light, the moon, and the stars are darkened, and the clouds return after the rain;'),
('ECC', 12, 3, 'ECC.12.3', 'in the day when the keepers of the house shall tremble, and the strong men shall bow themselves, and the grinders cease because they are few, and those who look out of the windows are darkened,'),
('ECC', 12, 4, 'ECC.12.4', 'and the doors shall be shut in the street; when the sound of the grinding is low, and one shall rise up at the voice of a bird, and all the daughters of music shall be brought low;'),
('ECC', 12, 5, 'ECC.12.5', 'yes, they shall be afraid of heights, and terrors will be on the way; and the almond tree shall blossom, and the grasshopper shall be a burden, and desire shall fail; because man goes to his everlasting home, and the mourners go about the streets;'),
('ECC', 12, 6, 'ECC.12.6', 'before the silver cord is severed, or the golden bowl is broken, or the pitcher is broken at the spring, or the wheel broken at the cistern,'),
('ECC', 12, 7, 'ECC.12.7', 'and the dust returns to the earth as it was, and the spirit returns to God who gave it.'),
('ECC', 12, 8, 'ECC.12.8', '“Vanity of vanities,” says the Preacher. “All is vanity!”'),
('ECC', 12, 9, 'ECC.12.9', 'Further, because the Preacher was wise, he still taught the people knowledge. Yes, he pondered, sought out, and set in order many proverbs.'),
('ECC', 12, 10, 'ECC.12.10', 'The Preacher sought to find out acceptable words, and that which was written blamelessly, words of truth.'),
('ECC', 12, 11, 'ECC.12.11', 'The words of the wise are like goads; and like nails well fastened are words from the masters of assemblies, which are given from one shepherd.'),
('ECC', 12, 12, 'ECC.12.12', 'Furthermore, my son, be admonished: of making many books there is no end; and much study is a weariness of the flesh.'),
('ECC', 12, 13, 'ECC.12.13', 'This is the end of the matter. All has been heard. Fear God and keep his commandments; for this is the whole duty of man.'),
('ECC', 12, 14, 'ECC.12.14', 'For God will bring every work into judgment, with every hidden thing, whether it is good, or whether it is evil.'),
('SNG', 1, 1, 'SNG.1.1', 'The Song of songs, which is Solomon’s.'),
('SNG', 1, 2, 'SNG.1.2', 'Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth; for your love is better than wine.'),
('SNG', 1, 3, 'SNG.1.3', 'Your oils have a pleasing fragrance. Your name is oil poured out, therefore the virgins love you.'),
('SNG', 1, 4, 'SNG.1.4', 'Take me away with you. Let’s hurry. The king has brought me into his rooms. We will be glad and rejoice in you. We will praise your love more than wine! They are right to love you.'),
('SNG', 1, 5, 'SNG.1.5', 'I am dark, but lovely, you daughters of Jerusalem, like Kedar’s tents, like Solomon’s curtains.'),
('SNG', 1, 6, 'SNG.1.6', 'Don’t stare at me because I am dark, because the sun has scorched me. My mother’s sons were angry with me. They made me keeper of the vineyards. I haven’t kept my own vineyard.'),
('SNG', 1, 7, 'SNG.1.7', 'Tell me, you whom my soul loves, where you graze your flock, where you rest them at noon; for why should I be as one who is veiled beside the flocks of your companions?'),
('SNG', 1, 8, 'SNG.1.8', 'If you don’t know, most beautiful among women, follow the tracks of the sheep. Graze your young goats beside the shepherds’ tents.'),
('SNG', 1, 9, 'SNG.1.9', 'I have compared you, my love, to a steed in Pharaoh’s chariots.'),
('SNG', 1, 10, 'SNG.1.10', 'Your cheeks are beautiful with earrings, your neck with strings of jewels.'),
('SNG', 1, 11, 'SNG.1.11', 'We will make you earrings of gold, with studs of silver.'),
('SNG', 1, 12, 'SNG.1.12', 'While the king sat at his table, my perfume spread its fragrance.'),
('SNG', 1, 13, 'SNG.1.13', 'My beloved is to me a sachet of myrrh, that lies between my breasts.'),
('SNG', 1, 14, 'SNG.1.14', 'My beloved is to me a cluster of henna blossoms from the vineyards of En Gedi.'),
('SNG', 1, 15, 'SNG.1.15', 'Behold, you are beautiful, my love. Behold, you are beautiful. Your eyes are like doves.'),
('SNG', 1, 16, 'SNG.1.16', 'Behold, you are beautiful, my beloved, yes, pleasant; and our couch is verdant.'),
('SNG', 1, 17, 'SNG.1.17', 'The beams of our house are cedars. Our rafters are firs.'),
('SNG', 2, 1, 'SNG.2.1', 'I am a rose of Sharon, a lily of the valleys.'),
('SNG', 2, 2, 'SNG.2.2', 'As a lily among thorns, so is my love among the daughters.'),
('SNG', 2, 3, 'SNG.2.3', 'As the apple tree among the trees of the wood, so is my beloved among the sons. I sat down under his shadow with great delight, his fruit was sweet to my taste.'),
('SNG', 2, 4, 'SNG.2.4', 'He brought me to the banquet hall. His banner over me is love.'),
('SNG', 2, 5, 'SNG.2.5', 'Strengthen me with raisins, refresh me with apples; for I am faint with love.'),
('SNG', 2, 6, 'SNG.2.6', 'His left hand is under my head. His right hand embraces me.'),
('SNG', 2, 7, 'SNG.2.7', 'I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, or by the hinds of the field, that you not stir up, nor awaken love, until it so desires.'),
('SNG', 2, 8, 'SNG.2.8', 'The voice of my beloved! Behold, he comes, leaping on the mountains, skipping on the hills.'),
('SNG', 2, 9, 'SNG.2.9', 'My beloved is like a roe or a young deer. Behold, he stands behind our wall! He looks in at the windows. He glances through the lattice.'),
('SNG', 2, 10, 'SNG.2.10', 'My beloved spoke, and said to me, “Rise up, my love, my beautiful one, and come away.'),
('SNG', 2, 11, 'SNG.2.11', 'For behold, the winter is past. The rain is over and gone.'),
('SNG', 2, 12, 'SNG.2.12', 'The flowers appear on the earth. The time of the singing has come, and the voice of the turtledove is heard in our land.'),
('SNG', 2, 13, 'SNG.2.13', 'The fig tree ripens her green figs. The vines are in blossom. They give out their fragrance. Arise, my love, my beautiful one, and come away.”'),
('SNG', 2, 14, 'SNG.2.14', 'My dove in the clefts of the rock, in the hiding places of the mountainside, let me see your face. Let me hear your voice; for your voice is sweet and your face is lovely.'),
('SNG', 2, 15, 'SNG.2.15', 'Catch for us the foxes, the little foxes that plunder the vineyards; for our vineyards are in blossom.'),
('SNG', 2, 16, 'SNG.2.16', 'My beloved is mine, and I am his. He browses among the lilies.'),
('SNG', 2, 17, 'SNG.2.17', 'Until the day is cool, and the shadows flee away, turn, my beloved, and be like a roe or a young deer on the mountains of Bether.'),
('SNG', 3, 1, 'SNG.3.1', 'By night on my bed, I sought him whom my soul loves. I sought him, but I didn’t find him.'),
('SNG', 3, 2, 'SNG.3.2', 'I will get up now, and go about the city; in the streets and in the squares I will seek him whom my soul loves. I sought him, but I didn’t find him.'),
('SNG', 3, 3, 'SNG.3.3', 'The watchmen who go about the city found me; “Have you seen him whom my soul loves?”'),
('SNG', 3, 4, 'SNG.3.4', 'I had scarcely passed from them, when I found him whom my soul loves. I held him, and would not let him go, until I had brought him into my mother’s house, into the room of her who conceived me.'),
('SNG', 3, 5, 'SNG.3.5', 'I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, or by the hinds of the field, that you not stir up nor awaken love, until it so desires.'),
('SNG', 3, 6, 'SNG.3.6', 'Who is this who comes up from the wilderness like pillars of smoke, perfumed with myrrh and frankincense, with all spices of the merchant?'),
('SNG', 3, 7, 'SNG.3.7', 'Behold, it is Solomon’s carriage! Sixty mighty men are around it, of the mighty men of Israel.'),
('SNG', 3, 8, 'SNG.3.8', 'They all handle the sword, and are expert in war. Every man has his sword on his thigh, because of fear in the night.'),
('SNG', 3, 9, 'SNG.3.9', 'King Solomon made himself a carriage of the wood of Lebanon.'),
('SNG', 3, 10, 'SNG.3.10', 'He made its pillars of silver, its bottom of gold, its seat of purple, the middle of it being paved with love, from the daughters of Jerusalem.'),
('SNG', 3, 11, 'SNG.3.11', 'Go out, you daughters of Zion, and see King Solomon, with the crown with which his mother has crowned him, in the day of his weddings, in the day of the gladness of his heart.'),
('SNG', 4, 1, 'SNG.4.1', 'Behold, you are beautiful, my love. Behold, you are beautiful. Your eyes are like doves behind your veil. Your hair is as a flock of goats, that descend from Mount Gilead.'),
('SNG', 4, 2, 'SNG.4.2', 'Your teeth are like a newly shorn flock, which have come up from the washing, where every one of them has twins. None is bereaved among them.'),
('SNG', 4, 3, 'SNG.4.3', 'Your lips are like scarlet thread. Your mouth is lovely. Your temples are like a piece of a pomegranate behind your veil.'),
('SNG', 4, 4, 'SNG.4.4', 'Your neck is like David’s tower built for an armory, on which a thousand shields hang, all the shields of the mighty men.'),
('SNG', 4, 5, 'SNG.4.5', 'Your two breasts are like two fawns that are twins of a roe, which feed among the lilies.'),
('SNG', 4, 6, 'SNG.4.6', 'Until the day is cool, and the shadows flee away, I will go to the mountain of myrrh, to the hill of frankincense.'),
('SNG', 4, 7, 'SNG.4.7', 'You are all beautiful, my love. There is no spot in you.'),
('SNG', 4, 8, 'SNG.4.8', 'Come with me from Lebanon, my bride, with me from Lebanon. Look from the top of Amana, from the top of Senir and Hermon, from the lions’ dens, from the mountains of the leopards.'),
('SNG', 4, 9, 'SNG.4.9', 'You have ravished my heart, my sister, my bride. You have ravished my heart with one of your eyes, with one chain of your neck.'),
('SNG', 4, 10, 'SNG.4.10', 'How beautiful is your love, my sister, my bride! How much better is your love than wine, the fragrance of your perfumes than all kinds of spices!'),
('SNG', 4, 11, 'SNG.4.11', 'Your lips, my bride, drip like the honeycomb. Honey and milk are under your tongue. The smell of your garments is like the smell of Lebanon.'),
('SNG', 4, 12, 'SNG.4.12', 'My sister, my bride, is a locked up garden; a locked up spring, a sealed fountain.'),
('SNG', 4, 13, 'SNG.4.13', 'Your shoots are an orchard of pomegranates, with precious fruits, henna with spikenard plants,'),
('SNG', 4, 14, 'SNG.4.14', 'spikenard and saffron, calamus and cinnamon, with every kind of incense tree; myrrh and aloes, with all the best spices,'),
('SNG', 4, 15, 'SNG.4.15', 'a fountain of gardens, a well of living waters, flowing streams from Lebanon.'),
('SNG', 4, 16, 'SNG.4.16', 'Awake, north wind, and come, you south! Blow on my garden, that its spices may flow out. Let my beloved come into his garden, and taste his precious fruits.'),
('SNG', 5, 1, 'SNG.5.1', 'I have come into my garden, my sister, my bride. I have gathered my myrrh with my spice; I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk my wine with my milk. Eat, friends! Drink, yes, drink abundantly, beloved.'),
('SNG', 5, 2, 'SNG.5.2', 'I was asleep, but my heart was awake. It is the voice of my beloved who knocks: “Open to me, my sister, my love, my dove, my undefiled; for my head is filled with dew, and my hair with the dampness of the night.”'),
('SNG', 5, 3, 'SNG.5.3', 'I have taken off my robe. Indeed, must I put it on? I have washed my feet. Indeed, must I soil them?'),
('SNG', 5, 4, 'SNG.5.4', 'My beloved thrust his hand in through the latch opening. My heart pounded for him.'),
('SNG', 5, 5, 'SNG.5.5', 'I rose up to open for my beloved. My hands dripped with myrrh, my fingers with liquid myrrh, on the handles of the lock.'),
('SNG', 5, 6, 'SNG.5.6', 'I opened to my beloved; but my beloved left, and had gone away. My heart went out when he spoke. I looked for him, but I didn’t find him. I called him, but he didn’t answer.'),
('SNG', 5, 7, 'SNG.5.7', 'The watchmen who go about the city found me. They beat me. They bruised me. The keepers of the walls took my cloak away from me.'),
('SNG', 5, 8, 'SNG.5.8', 'I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem, If you find my beloved, that you tell him that I am faint with love.'),
('SNG', 5, 9, 'SNG.5.9', 'How is your beloved better than another beloved, you fairest among women? How is your beloved better than another beloved, that you do so adjure us?'),
('SNG', 5, 10, 'SNG.5.10', 'My beloved is white and ruddy. The best among ten thousand.'),
('SNG', 5, 11, 'SNG.5.11', 'His head is like the purest gold. His hair is bushy, black as a raven.'),
('SNG', 5, 12, 'SNG.5.12', 'His eyes are like doves beside the water brooks, washed with milk, mounted like jewels.'),
('SNG', 5, 13, 'SNG.5.13', 'His cheeks are like a bed of spices with towers of perfumes. His lips are like lilies, dropping liquid myrrh.'),
('SNG', 5, 14, 'SNG.5.14', 'His hands are like rings of gold set with beryl. His body is like ivory work overlaid with sapphires.'),
('SNG', 5, 15, 'SNG.5.15', 'His legs are like pillars of marble set on sockets of fine gold. His appearance is like Lebanon, excellent as the cedars.'),
('SNG', 5, 16, 'SNG.5.16', 'His mouth is sweetness; yes, he is altogether lovely. This is my beloved, and this is my friend, daughters of Jerusalem.'),
('SNG', 6, 1, 'SNG.6.1', 'Where has your beloved gone, you fairest among women? Where has your beloved turned, that we may seek him with you?'),
('SNG', 6, 2, 'SNG.6.2', 'My beloved has gone down to his garden, to the beds of spices, to pasture his flock in the gardens, and to gather lilies.'),
('SNG', 6, 3, 'SNG.6.3', 'I am my beloved’s, and my beloved is mine. He browses among the lilies.'),
('SNG', 6, 4, 'SNG.6.4', 'You are beautiful, my love, as Tirzah, lovely as Jerusalem, awesome as an army with banners.'),
('SNG', 6, 5, 'SNG.6.5', 'Turn away your eyes from me, for they have overcome me. Your hair is like a flock of goats, that lie along the side of Gilead.'),
('SNG', 6, 6, 'SNG.6.6', 'Your teeth are like a flock of ewes, which have come up from the washing, of which every one has twins; not one is bereaved among them.'),
('SNG', 6, 7, 'SNG.6.7', 'Your temples are like a piece of a pomegranate behind your veil.'),
('SNG', 6, 8, 'SNG.6.8', 'There are sixty queens, eighty concubines, and virgins without number.'),
('SNG', 6, 9, 'SNG.6.9', 'My dove, my perfect one, is unique. She is her mother’s only daughter. She is the favorite one of her who bore her. The daughters saw her, and called her blessed. The queens and the concubines saw her, and they praised her.'),
('SNG', 6, 10, 'SNG.6.10', 'Who is she who looks out as the morning, beautiful as the moon, clear as the sun, and awesome as an army with banners?'),
('SNG', 6, 11, 'SNG.6.11', 'I went down into the nut tree grove, to see the green plants of the valley, to see whether the vine budded, and the pomegranates were in flower.'),
('SNG', 6, 12, 'SNG.6.12', 'Without realizing it, my desire set me with my royal people’s chariots.'),
('SNG', 6, 13, 'SNG.6.13', 'Return, return, Shulammite! Return, return, that we may gaze at you. Why do you desire to gaze at the Shulammite, as at the dance of Mahanaim?'),
('SNG', 7, 1, 'SNG.7.1', 'How beautiful are your feet in sandals, prince’s daughter! Your rounded thighs are like jewels, the work of the hands of a skillful workman.'),
('SNG', 7, 2, 'SNG.7.2', 'Your body is like a round goblet, no mixed wine is wanting. Your waist is like a heap of wheat, set about with lilies.'),
('SNG', 7, 3, 'SNG.7.3', 'Your two breasts are like two fawns, that are twins of a roe.'),
('SNG', 7, 4, 'SNG.7.4', 'Your neck is like an ivory tower. Your eyes are like the pools in Heshbon by the gate of Bathrabbim. Your nose is like the tower of Lebanon which looks toward Damascus.'),
('SNG', 7, 5, 'SNG.7.5', 'Your head on you is like Carmel. The hair of your head like purple. The king is held captive in its tresses.'),
('SNG', 7, 6, 'SNG.7.6', 'How beautiful and how pleasant you are, love, for delights!'),
('SNG', 7, 7, 'SNG.7.7', 'This, your stature, is like a palm tree, your breasts like its fruit.'),
('SNG', 7, 8, 'SNG.7.8', 'I said, “I will climb up into the palm tree. I will take hold of its fruit.” Let your breasts be like clusters of the vine, the smell of your breath like apples.'),
('SNG', 7, 9, 'SNG.7.9', 'Your mouth is like the best wine, that goes down smoothly for my beloved, gliding through the lips of those who are asleep.'),
('SNG', 7, 10, 'SNG.7.10', 'I am my beloved’s. His desire is toward me.'),
('SNG', 7, 11, 'SNG.7.11', 'Come, my beloved! Let’s go out into the field. Let’s lodge in the villages.'),
('SNG', 7, 12, 'SNG.7.12', 'Let’s go early up to the vineyards. Let’s see whether the vine has budded, its blossom is open, and the pomegranates are in flower. There I will give you my love.'),
('SNG', 7, 13, 'SNG.7.13', 'The mandrakes produce fragrance. At our doors are all kinds of precious fruits, new and old, which I have stored up for you, my beloved.'),
('SNG', 8, 1, 'SNG.8.1', 'Oh that you were like my brother, who nursed from the breasts of my mother! If I found you outside, I would kiss you; yes, and no one would despise me.'),
('SNG', 8, 2, 'SNG.8.2', 'I would lead you, bringing you into the house of my mother, who would instruct me. I would have you drink spiced wine, of the juice of my pomegranate.'),
('SNG', 8, 3, 'SNG.8.3', 'His left hand would be under my head. His right hand would embrace me.'),
('SNG', 8, 4, 'SNG.8.4', 'I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem, that you not stir up, nor awaken love, until it so desires.'),
('SNG', 8, 5, 'SNG.8.5', 'Who is this who comes up from the wilderness, leaning on her beloved? Under the apple tree I awakened you. There your mother conceived you. There she was in labor and bore you.'),
('SNG', 8, 6, 'SNG.8.6', 'Set me as a seal on your heart, as a seal on your arm; for love is strong as death. Jealousy is as cruel as Sheol. Its flashes are flashes of fire, a very flame of the LORD.'),
('SNG', 8, 7, 'SNG.8.7', 'Many waters can’t quench love, neither can floods drown it. If a man would give all the wealth of his house for love, he would be utterly scorned.'),
('SNG', 8, 8, 'SNG.8.8', 'We have a little sister. She has no breasts. What shall we do for our sister in the day when she is to be spoken for?'),
('SNG', 8, 9, 'SNG.8.9', 'If she is a wall, we will build on her a turret of silver. If she is a door, we will enclose her with boards of cedar.'),
('SNG', 8, 10, 'SNG.8.10', 'I am a wall, and my breasts like towers, then I was in his eyes like one who found peace.'),
('SNG', 8, 11, 'SNG.8.11', 'Solomon had a vineyard at Baal Hamon. He leased out the vineyard to keepers. Each was to bring a thousand shekels of silver for its fruit.'),
('SNG', 8, 12, 'SNG.8.12', 'My own vineyard is before me. The thousand are for you, Solomon, two hundred for those who tend its fruit.'),
('SNG', 8, 13, 'SNG.8.13', 'You who dwell in the gardens, with friends in attendance, let me hear your voice!'),
('SNG', 8, 14, 'SNG.8.14', 'Come away, my beloved! Be like a gazelle or a young stag on the mountains of spices!'),
('ISA', 1, 1, 'ISA.1.1', 'The vision of Isaiah the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem, in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah.'),
('ISA', 1, 2, 'ISA.1.2', 'Hear, heavens, and listen, earth; for the LORD has spoken: “I have nourished and brought up children and they have rebelled against me.'),
('ISA', 1, 3, 'ISA.1.3', 'The ox knows his owner, and the donkey his master’s crib; but Israel doesn’t know. My people don’t consider.”'),
('ISA', 1, 4, 'ISA.1.4', 'Ah sinful nation, a people loaded with iniquity, offspring of evildoers, children who deal corruptly! They have forsaken the LORD. They have despised the Holy One of Israel. They are estranged and backward.'),
('ISA', 1, 5, 'ISA.1.5', 'Why should you be beaten more, that you revolt more and more? The whole head is sick, and the whole heart faint.'),
('ISA', 1, 6, 'ISA.1.6', 'From the sole of the foot even to the head there is no soundness in it, but wounds, welts, and open sores. They haven’t been closed, bandaged, or soothed with oil.'),
('ISA', 1, 7, 'ISA.1.7', 'Your country is desolate. Your cities are burned with fire. Strangers devour your land in your presence and it is desolate, as overthrown by strangers.'),
('ISA', 1, 8, 'ISA.1.8', 'The daughter of Zion is left like a shelter in a vineyard, like a hut in a field of melons, like a besieged city.'),
('ISA', 1, 9, 'ISA.1.9', 'Unless the LORD of Armies had left to us a very small remnant, we would have been as Sodom. We would have been like Gomorrah.'),
('ISA', 1, 10, 'ISA.1.10', 'Hear the LORD’s word, you rulers of Sodom! Listen to the law of our God, you people of Gomorrah!'),
('ISA', 1, 11, 'ISA.1.11', '“What are the multitude of your sacrifices to me?” says the LORD. “I have had enough of the burnt offerings of rams and the fat of fed animals. I don’t delight in the blood of bulls, or of lambs, or of male goats.'),
('ISA', 1, 12, 'ISA.1.12', 'When you come to appear before me, who has required this at your hand, to trample my courts?'),
('ISA', 1, 13, 'ISA.1.13', 'Bring no more vain offerings. Incense is an abomination to me. New moons, Sabbaths, and convocations— I can’t stand evil assemblies.'),
('ISA', 1, 14, 'ISA.1.14', 'My soul hates your New Moons and your appointed feasts. They are a burden to me. I am weary of bearing them.'),
('ISA', 1, 15, 'ISA.1.15', 'When you spread out your hands, I will hide my eyes from you. Yes, when you make many prayers, I will not hear. Your hands are full of blood.'),
('ISA', 1, 16, 'ISA.1.16', 'Wash yourselves. Make yourself clean. Put away the evil of your doings from before my eyes. Cease to do evil.'),
('ISA', 1, 17, 'ISA.1.17', 'Learn to do well. Seek justice. Relieve the oppressed. Defend the fatherless. Plead for the widow.”'),
('ISA', 1, 18, 'ISA.1.18', '“Come now, and let’s reason together,” says the LORD: “Though your sins are as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow. Though they are red like crimson, they shall be as wool.'),
('ISA', 1, 19, 'ISA.1.19', 'If you are willing and obedient, you will eat the good of the land;'),
('ISA', 1, 20, 'ISA.1.20', 'but if you refuse and rebel, you will be devoured with the sword; for the LORD’s mouth has spoken it.”'),
('ISA', 1, 21, 'ISA.1.21', 'How the faithful city has become a prostitute! She was full of justice. Righteousness lodged in her, but now there are murderers.'),
('ISA', 1, 22, 'ISA.1.22', 'Your silver has become dross, your wine mixed with water.'),
('ISA', 1, 23, 'ISA.1.23', 'Your princes are rebellious and companions of thieves. Everyone loves bribes and follows after rewards. They don’t defend the fatherless, neither does the cause of the widow come to them.'),
('ISA', 1, 24, 'ISA.1.24', 'Therefore the Lord, GOD of Armies, the Mighty One of Israel, says: “Ah, I will get relief from my adversaries, and avenge myself on my enemies.'),
('ISA', 1, 25, 'ISA.1.25', 'I will turn my hand on you, thoroughly purge away your dross, and will take away all your tin.'),
('ISA', 1, 26, 'ISA.1.26', 'I will restore your judges as at the first, and your counselors as at the beginning. Afterward you shall be called ‘The city of righteousness, a faithful town.’'),
('ISA', 1, 27, 'ISA.1.27', 'Zion shall be redeemed with justice, and her converts with righteousness.'),
('ISA', 1, 28, 'ISA.1.28', 'But the destruction of transgressors and sinners shall be together, and those who forsake the LORD shall be consumed.'),
('ISA', 1, 29, 'ISA.1.29', 'For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which you have desired, and you shall be confounded for the gardens that you have chosen.'),
('ISA', 1, 30, 'ISA.1.30', 'For you shall be as an oak whose leaf fades, and as a garden that has no water.'),
('ISA', 1, 31, 'ISA.1.31', 'The strong will be like tinder, and his work like a spark. They will both burn together, and no one will quench them.”'),
('ISA', 2, 1, 'ISA.2.1', 'This is what Isaiah the son of Amoz saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('ISA', 2, 2, 'ISA.2.2', 'It shall happen in the latter days, that the mountain of the LORD’s house shall be established on the top of the mountains, and shall be raised above the hills; and all nations shall flow to it.'),
('ISA', 2, 3, 'ISA.2.3', 'Many peoples shall go and say, “Come, let’s go up to the mountain of the LORD, to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths.” For the law shall go out of Zion, and the LORD’s word from Jerusalem.'),
('ISA', 2, 4, 'ISA.2.4', 'He will judge between the nations, and will decide concerning many peoples. They shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruning hooks. Nation shall not lift up sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.'),
('ISA', 2, 5, 'ISA.2.5', 'House of Jacob, come, and let’s walk in the light of the LORD.'),
('ISA', 2, 6, 'ISA.2.6', 'For you have forsaken your people, the house of Jacob, because they are filled from the east, with those who practice divination like the Philistines, and they clasp hands with the children of foreigners.'),
('ISA', 2, 7, 'ISA.2.7', 'Their land is full of silver and gold, neither is there any end of their treasures. Their land also is full of horses, neither is there any end of their chariots.'),
('ISA', 2, 8, 'ISA.2.8', 'Their land also is full of idols. They worship the work of their own hands, that which their own fingers have made.'),
('ISA', 2, 9, 'ISA.2.9', 'Man is brought low, and mankind is humbled; therefore don’t forgive them.'),
('ISA', 2, 10, 'ISA.2.10', 'Enter into the rock, and hide in the dust, from before the terror of the LORD, and from the glory of his majesty.'),
('ISA', 2, 11, 'ISA.2.11', 'The lofty looks of man will be brought low, the arrogance of men will be bowed down, and the LORD alone will be exalted in that day.'),
('ISA', 2, 12, 'ISA.2.12', 'For there will be a day of the LORD of Armies for all that is proud and arrogant, and for all that is lifted up, and it shall be brought low—'),
('ISA', 2, 13, 'ISA.2.13', 'for all the cedars of Lebanon, that are high and lifted up, for all the oaks of Bashan,'),
('ISA', 2, 14, 'ISA.2.14', 'for all the high mountains, for all the hills that are lifted up,'),
('ISA', 2, 15, 'ISA.2.15', 'for every lofty tower, for every fortified wall,'),
('ISA', 2, 16, 'ISA.2.16', 'for all the ships of Tarshish, and for all pleasant imagery.'),
('ISA', 2, 17, 'ISA.2.17', 'The loftiness of man shall be bowed down, and the arrogance of men shall be brought low; and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day.'),
('ISA', 2, 18, 'ISA.2.18', 'The idols shall utterly pass away.'),
('ISA', 2, 19, 'ISA.2.19', 'Men shall go into the caves of the rocks, and into the holes of the earth, from before the terror of the LORD, and from the glory of his majesty, when he arises to shake the earth mightily.'),
('ISA', 2, 20, 'ISA.2.20', 'In that day, men shall cast away their idols of silver and their idols of gold, which have been made for themselves to worship, to the moles and to the bats,'),
('ISA', 2, 21, 'ISA.2.21', 'to go into the caverns of the rocks, and into the clefts of the ragged rocks, from before the terror of the LORD, and from the glory of his majesty, when he arises to shake the earth mightily.'),
('ISA', 2, 22, 'ISA.2.22', 'Stop trusting in man, whose breath is in his nostrils; for of what account is he?'),
('ISA', 3, 1, 'ISA.3.1', 'For, behold, the Lord, GOD of Armies, takes away from Jerusalem and from Judah supply and support, the whole supply of bread, and the whole supply of water;'),
('ISA', 3, 2, 'ISA.3.2', 'the mighty man, the man of war, the judge, the prophet, the diviner, the elder,'),
('ISA', 3, 3, 'ISA.3.3', 'the captain of fifty, the honorable man, the counselor, the skilled craftsman, and the clever enchanter.'),
('ISA', 3, 4, 'ISA.3.4', 'I will give boys to be their princes, and children shall rule over them.'),
('ISA', 3, 5, 'ISA.3.5', 'The people will be oppressed, everyone by another, and everyone by his neighbor. The child will behave himself proudly against the old man, and the wicked against the honorable.'),
('ISA', 3, 6, 'ISA.3.6', 'Indeed a man shall take hold of his brother in the house of his father, saying, “You have clothing, you be our ruler, and let this ruin be under your hand.”'),
('ISA', 3, 7, 'ISA.3.7', 'In that day he will cry out, saying, “I will not be a healer; for in my house is neither bread nor clothing. You shall not make me ruler of the people.”'),
('ISA', 3, 8, 'ISA.3.8', 'For Jerusalem is ruined, and Judah is fallen; because their tongue and their doings are against the LORD, to provoke the eyes of his glory.'),
('ISA', 3, 9, 'ISA.3.9', 'The look of their faces testify against them. They parade their sin like Sodom. They don’t hide it. Woe to their soul! For they have brought disaster upon themselves.'),
('ISA', 3, 10, 'ISA.3.10', 'Tell the righteous that it will be well with them, for they will eat the fruit of their deeds.'),
('ISA', 3, 11, 'ISA.3.11', 'Woe to the wicked! Disaster is upon them, for the deeds of their hands will be paid back to them.'),
('ISA', 3, 12, 'ISA.3.12', 'As for my people, children are their oppressors, and women rule over them. My people, those who lead you cause you to err, and destroy the way of your paths.'),
('ISA', 3, 13, 'ISA.3.13', 'The LORD stands up to contend, and stands to judge the peoples.'),
('ISA', 3, 14, 'ISA.3.14', 'The LORD will enter into judgment with the elders of his people and their leaders: “It is you who have eaten up the vineyard. The plunder of the poor is in your houses.'),
('ISA', 3, 15, 'ISA.3.15', 'What do you mean that you crush my people, and grind the face of the poor?” says the Lord, GOD of Armies.'),
('ISA', 3, 16, 'ISA.3.16', 'Moreover the LORD said, “Because the daughters of Zion are arrogant, and walk with outstretched necks and flirting eyes, walking daintily as they go, jingling ornaments on their feet;'),
('ISA', 3, 17, 'ISA.3.17', 'therefore the Lord brings sores on the crown of the head of the women of Zion, and the LORD will make their scalps bald.”'),
('ISA', 3, 18, 'ISA.3.18', 'In that day the Lord will take away the beauty of their anklets, the headbands, the crescent necklaces,'),
('ISA', 3, 19, 'ISA.3.19', 'the earrings, the bracelets, the veils,'),
('ISA', 3, 20, 'ISA.3.20', 'the headdresses, the ankle chains, the sashes, the perfume containers, the charms,'),
('ISA', 3, 21, 'ISA.3.21', 'the signet rings, the nose rings,'),
('ISA', 3, 22, 'ISA.3.22', 'the fine robes, the capes, the cloaks, the purses,'),
('ISA', 3, 23, 'ISA.3.23', 'the hand mirrors, the fine linen garments, the tiaras, and the shawls.'),
('ISA', 3, 24, 'ISA.3.24', 'It shall happen that instead of sweet spices, there shall be rottenness; instead of a belt, a rope; instead of well set hair, baldness; instead of a robe, a wearing of sackcloth; and branding instead of beauty.'),
('ISA', 3, 25, 'ISA.3.25', 'Your men shall fall by the sword, and your mighty in the war.'),
('ISA', 3, 26, 'ISA.3.26', 'Her gates shall lament and mourn. She shall be desolate and sit on the ground.'),
('ISA', 4, 1, 'ISA.4.1', 'Seven women shall take hold of one man in that day, saying, “We will eat our own bread, and wear our own clothing. Just let us be called by your name. Take away our reproach.”'),
('ISA', 4, 2, 'ISA.4.2', 'In that day, the LORD’s branch will be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the land will be the beauty and glory of the survivors of Israel.'),
('ISA', 4, 3, 'ISA.4.3', 'It will happen that he who is left in Zion and he who remains in Jerusalem shall be called holy, even everyone who is written among the living in Jerusalem,'),
('ISA', 4, 4, 'ISA.4.4', 'when the Lord shall have washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion, and shall have purged the blood of Jerusalem from within it, by the spirit of justice and by the spirit of burning.'),
('ISA', 4, 5, 'ISA.4.5', 'The LORD will create over the whole habitation of Mount Zion and over her assemblies, a cloud and smoke by day, and the shining of a flaming fire by night, for over all the glory will be a canopy.'),
('ISA', 4, 6, 'ISA.4.6', 'There will be a pavilion for a shade in the daytime from the heat, and for a refuge and for a shelter from storm and from rain.'),
('ISA', 5, 1, 'ISA.5.1', 'Let me sing for my well beloved a song of my beloved about his vineyard. My beloved had a vineyard on a very fruitful hill.'),
('ISA', 5, 2, 'ISA.5.2', 'He dug it up, gathered out its stones, planted it with the choicest vine, built a tower in the middle of it, and also cut out a wine press in it. He looked for it to yield grapes, but it yielded wild grapes.'),
('ISA', 5, 3, 'ISA.5.3', '“Now, inhabitants of Jerusalem and men of Judah, please judge between me and my vineyard.'),
('ISA', 5, 4, 'ISA.5.4', 'What could have been done more to my vineyard, that I have not done in it? Why, when I looked for it to yield grapes, did it yield wild grapes?'),
('ISA', 5, 5, 'ISA.5.5', 'Now I will tell you what I will do to my vineyard. I will take away its hedge, and it will be eaten up. I will break down its wall, and it will be trampled down.'),
('ISA', 5, 6, 'ISA.5.6', 'I will lay it a wasteland. It won’t be pruned or hoed, but it will grow briers and thorns. I will also command the clouds that they rain no rain on it.”'),
('ISA', 5, 7, 'ISA.5.7', 'For the vineyard of the LORD of Armies is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah his pleasant plant. He looked for justice, but behold, oppression, for righteousness, but behold, a cry of distress.'),
('ISA', 5, 8, 'ISA.5.8', 'Woe to those who join house to house, who lay field to field, until there is no room, and you are made to dwell alone in the middle of the land!'),
('ISA', 5, 9, 'ISA.5.9', 'In my ears, the LORD of Armies says: “Surely many houses will be desolate, even great and beautiful, unoccupied.'),
('ISA', 5, 10, 'ISA.5.10', 'For ten acres of vineyard shall yield one bath, and a homer of seed shall yield an ephah.”'),
('ISA', 5, 11, 'ISA.5.11', 'Woe to those who rise up early in the morning, that they may follow strong drink, who stay late into the night, until wine inflames them!'),
('ISA', 5, 12, 'ISA.5.12', 'The harp, lyre, tambourine, and flute, with wine, are at their feasts; but they don’t respect the work of the LORD, neither have they considered the operation of his hands.'),
('ISA', 5, 13, 'ISA.5.13', 'Therefore my people go into captivity for lack of knowledge. Their honorable men are famished, and their multitudes are parched with thirst.'),
('ISA', 5, 14, 'ISA.5.14', 'Therefore Sheol has enlarged its desire, and opened its mouth without measure; and their glory, their multitude, their pomp, and he who rejoices among them, descend into it.'),
('ISA', 5, 15, 'ISA.5.15', 'So man is brought low, mankind is humbled, and the eyes of the arrogant ones are humbled;'),
('ISA', 5, 16, 'ISA.5.16', 'but the LORD of Armies is exalted in justice, and God the Holy One is sanctified in righteousness.'),
('ISA', 5, 17, 'ISA.5.17', 'Then the lambs will graze as in their pasture, and strangers will eat the ruins of the rich.'),
('ISA', 5, 18, 'ISA.5.18', 'Woe to those who draw iniquity with cords of falsehood, and wickedness as with cart rope,'),
('ISA', 5, 19, 'ISA.5.19', 'who say, “Let him make haste, let him hasten his work, that we may see it; let the counsel of the Holy One of Israel draw near and come, that we may know it!”'),
('ISA', 5, 20, 'ISA.5.20', 'Woe to those who call evil good, and good evil; who put darkness for light, and light for darkness; who put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!'),
('ISA', 5, 21, 'ISA.5.21', 'Woe to those who are wise in their own eyes, and prudent in their own sight!'),
('ISA', 5, 22, 'ISA.5.22', 'Woe to those who are mighty to drink wine, and champions at mixing strong drink;'),
('ISA', 5, 23, 'ISA.5.23', 'who acquit the guilty for a bribe, but deny justice for the innocent!'),
('ISA', 5, 24, 'ISA.5.24', 'Therefore as the tongue of fire devours the stubble, and as the dry grass sinks down in the flame, so their root shall be as rottenness, and their blossom shall go up as dust, because they have rejected the law of the LORD of Armies, and despised the word of the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 5, 25, 'ISA.5.25', 'Therefore the LORD’s anger burns against his people, and he has stretched out his hand against them and has struck them. The mountains tremble, and their dead bodies are as refuse in the middle of the streets. For all this, his anger is not turned away, but his hand is still stretched out.'),
('ISA', 5, 26, 'ISA.5.26', 'He will lift up a banner to the nations from far away, and he will whistle for them from the end of the earth. Behold, they will come speedily and swiftly.'),
('ISA', 5, 27, 'ISA.5.27', 'No one shall be weary nor stumble among them; no one shall slumber nor sleep, neither shall the belt of their waist be untied, nor the strap of their sandals be broken,'),
('ISA', 5, 28, 'ISA.5.28', 'whose arrows are sharp, and all their bows bent. Their horses’ hoofs will be like flint, and their wheels like a whirlwind.'),
('ISA', 5, 29, 'ISA.5.29', 'Their roaring will be like a lioness. They will roar like young lions. Yes, they shall roar, and seize their prey and carry it off, and there will be no one to deliver.'),
('ISA', 5, 30, 'ISA.5.30', 'They will roar against them in that day like the roaring of the sea. If one looks to the land, behold, darkness and distress. The light is darkened in its clouds.'),
('ISA', 6, 1, 'ISA.6.1', 'In the year that King Uzziah died, I saw the Lord sitting on a throne, high and lifted up; and his train filled the temple.'),
('ISA', 6, 2, 'ISA.6.2', 'Above him stood the seraphim. Each one had six wings. With two he covered his face. With two he covered his feet. With two he flew.'),
('ISA', 6, 3, 'ISA.6.3', 'One called to another, and said, “Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of Armies! The whole earth is full of his glory!”'),
('ISA', 6, 4, 'ISA.6.4', 'The foundations of the thresholds shook at the voice of him who called, and the house was filled with smoke.'),
('ISA', 6, 5, 'ISA.6.5', 'Then I said, “Woe is me! For I am undone, because I am a man of unclean lips and I live among a people of unclean lips, for my eyes have seen the King, the LORD of Armies!”'),
('ISA', 6, 6, 'ISA.6.6', 'Then one of the seraphim flew to me, having a live coal in his hand, which he had taken with the tongs from off the altar.'),
('ISA', 6, 7, 'ISA.6.7', 'He touched my mouth with it, and said, “Behold, this has touched your lips; and your iniquity is taken away, and your sin forgiven.”'),
('ISA', 6, 8, 'ISA.6.8', 'I heard the Lord’s voice, saying, “Whom shall I send, and who will go for us?” Then I said, “Here I am. Send me!”'),
('ISA', 6, 9, 'ISA.6.9', 'He said, “Go, and tell this people, ‘You hear indeed, but don’t understand. You see indeed, but don’t perceive.’'),
('ISA', 6, 10, 'ISA.6.10', 'Make the heart of this people fat. Make their ears heavy, and shut their eyes; lest they see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their heart, and turn again, and be healed.”'),
('ISA', 6, 11, 'ISA.6.11', 'Then I said, “Lord, how long?” He answered, “Until cities are waste without inhabitant, houses without man, the land becomes utterly waste,'),
('ISA', 6, 12, 'ISA.6.12', 'and the LORD has removed men far away, and the forsaken places are many within the land.'),
('ISA', 6, 13, 'ISA.6.13', 'If there is a tenth left in it, that also will in turn be consumed, as a terebinth, and as an oak whose stump remains when they are cut down, so the holy seed is its stump.”'),
('ISA', 7, 1, 'ISA.7.1', 'In the days of Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, king of Judah, Rezin the king of Syria and Pekah the son of Remaliah, king of Israel, went up to Jerusalem to war against it, but could not prevail against it.'),
('ISA', 7, 2, 'ISA.7.2', 'David’s house was told, “Syria is allied with Ephraim.” His heart trembled, and the heart of his people, as the trees of the forest tremble with the wind.'),
('ISA', 7, 3, 'ISA.7.3', 'Then the LORD said to Isaiah, “Go out now to meet Ahaz, you, and Shearjashub your son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool, on the highway of the fuller’s field.'),
('ISA', 7, 4, 'ISA.7.4', 'Tell him, ‘Be careful, and keep calm. Don’t be afraid, neither let your heart be faint because of these two tails of smoking torches, for the fierce anger of Rezin and Syria, and of the son of Remaliah.'),
('ISA', 7, 5, 'ISA.7.5', 'Because Syria, Ephraim, and the son of Remaliah, have plotted evil against you, saying,'),
('ISA', 7, 6, 'ISA.7.6', '“Let’s go up against Judah, and tear it apart, and let’s divide it among ourselves, and set up a king within it, even the son of Tabeel.”'),
('ISA', 7, 7, 'ISA.7.7', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: “It shall not stand, neither shall it happen.”'),
('ISA', 7, 8, 'ISA.7.8', 'For the head of Syria is Damascus, and the head of Damascus is Rezin. Within sixty-five years Ephraim shall be broken in pieces, so that it shall not be a people.'),
('ISA', 7, 9, 'ISA.7.9', 'The head of Ephraim is Samaria, and the head of Samaria is Remaliah’s son. If you will not believe, surely you shall not be established.’”'),
('ISA', 7, 10, 'ISA.7.10', 'The LORD spoke again to Ahaz, saying,'),
('ISA', 7, 11, 'ISA.7.11', '“Ask a sign of the LORD your God; ask it either in the depth, or in the height above.”'),
('ISA', 7, 12, 'ISA.7.12', 'But Ahaz said, “I won’t ask. I won’t tempt the LORD.”'),
('ISA', 7, 13, 'ISA.7.13', 'He said, “Listen now, house of David. Is it not enough for you to try the patience of men, that you will try the patience of my God also?'),
('ISA', 7, 14, 'ISA.7.14', 'Therefore the Lord himself will give you a sign. Behold, the virgin will conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.'),
('ISA', 7, 15, 'ISA.7.15', 'He shall eat butter and honey when he knows to refuse the evil and choose the good.'),
('ISA', 7, 16, 'ISA.7.16', 'For before the child knows to refuse the evil and choose the good, the land whose two kings you abhor shall be forsaken.'),
('ISA', 7, 17, 'ISA.7.17', 'The LORD will bring on you, on your people, and on your father’s house days that have not come, from the day that Ephraim departed from Judah, even the king of Assyria.'),
('ISA', 7, 18, 'ISA.7.18', 'It will happen in that day that the LORD will whistle for the fly that is in the uttermost part of the rivers of Egypt, and for the bee that is in the land of Assyria.'),
('ISA', 7, 19, 'ISA.7.19', 'They shall come, and shall all rest in the desolate valleys, in the clefts of the rocks, on all thorn hedges, and on all pastures.'),
('ISA', 7, 20, 'ISA.7.20', 'In that day the Lord will shave with a razor that is hired in the parts beyond the River, even with the king of Assyria, the head and the hair of the feet; and it shall also consume the beard.'),
('ISA', 7, 21, 'ISA.7.21', 'It shall happen in that day that a man shall keep alive a young cow, and two sheep.'),
('ISA', 7, 22, 'ISA.7.22', 'It shall happen, that because of the abundance of milk which they shall give he shall eat butter, for everyone will eat butter and honey that is left within the land.'),
('ISA', 7, 23, 'ISA.7.23', 'It will happen in that day that every place where there were a thousand vines worth a thousand silver shekels, will be for briers and thorns.'),
('ISA', 7, 24, 'ISA.7.24', 'People will go there with arrows and with bow, because all the land will be briers and thorns.'),
('ISA', 7, 25, 'ISA.7.25', 'All the hills that were cultivated with the hoe, you shall not come there for fear of briers and thorns; but it shall be for the sending out of oxen, and for sheep to tread on.”'),
('ISA', 8, 1, 'ISA.8.1', 'The LORD said to me, “Take a large tablet, and write on it with a man’s pen, ‘For Maher Shalal Hash Baz’;'),
('ISA', 8, 2, 'ISA.8.2', 'and I will take for myself faithful witnesses to testify: Uriah the priest, and Zechariah the son of Jeberechiah.”'),
('ISA', 8, 3, 'ISA.8.3', 'I went to the prophetess, and she conceived, and bore a son. Then the LORD said to me, “Call his name ‘Maher Shalal Hash Baz.’'),
('ISA', 8, 4, 'ISA.8.4', 'For before the child knows how to say, ‘My father’ and ‘My mother,’ the riches of Damascus and the plunder of Samaria will be carried away by the king of Assyria.”'),
('ISA', 8, 5, 'ISA.8.5', 'The LORD spoke to me yet again, saying,'),
('ISA', 8, 6, 'ISA.8.6', '“Because this people has refused the waters of Shiloah that go softly, and rejoice in Rezin and Remaliah’s son;'),
('ISA', 8, 7, 'ISA.8.7', 'now therefore, behold, the Lord brings upon them the mighty flood waters of the River: the king of Assyria and all his glory. It will come up over all its channels, and go over all its banks.'),
('ISA', 8, 8, 'ISA.8.8', 'It will sweep onward into Judah. It will overflow and pass through. It will reach even to the neck. The stretching out of its wings will fill the width of your land, O Immanuel.'),
('ISA', 8, 9, 'ISA.8.9', 'Make an uproar, you peoples, and be broken in pieces! Listen, all you from far countries: dress for battle, and be shattered! Dress for battle, and be shattered!'),
('ISA', 8, 10, 'ISA.8.10', 'Take counsel together, and it will be brought to nothing; speak the word, and it will not stand, for God is with us.”'),
('ISA', 8, 11, 'ISA.8.11', 'For the LORD spoke this to me with a strong hand, and instructed me not to walk in the way of this people, saying,'),
('ISA', 8, 12, 'ISA.8.12', '“Don’t call a conspiracy all that this people call a conspiracy. Don’t fear their threats or be terrorized.'),
('ISA', 8, 13, 'ISA.8.13', 'The LORD of Armies is who you must respect as holy. He is the one you must fear. He is the one you must dread.'),
('ISA', 8, 14, 'ISA.8.14', 'He will be a sanctuary, but for both houses of Israel, he will be a stumbling stone and a rock that makes them fall. For the people of Jerusalem, he will be a trap and a snare.'),
('ISA', 8, 15, 'ISA.8.15', 'Many will stumble over it, fall, be broken, be snared, and be captured.”'),
('ISA', 8, 16, 'ISA.8.16', 'Wrap up the covenant. Seal the law among my disciples.'),
('ISA', 8, 17, 'ISA.8.17', 'I will wait for the LORD, who hides his face from the house of Jacob, and I will look for him.'),
('ISA', 8, 18, 'ISA.8.18', 'Behold, I and the children whom the LORD has given me are for signs and for wonders in Israel from the LORD of Armies, who dwells in Mount Zion.'),
('ISA', 8, 19, 'ISA.8.19', 'When they tell you, “Consult with those who have familiar spirits and with the wizards, who chirp and who mutter,” shouldn’t a people consult with their God? Should they consult the dead on behalf of the living?'),
('ISA', 8, 20, 'ISA.8.20', 'Turn to the law and to the covenant! If they don’t speak according to this word, surely there is no morning for them.'),
('ISA', 8, 21, 'ISA.8.21', 'They will pass through it, very distressed and hungry. It will happen that when they are hungry, they will worry, and curse their king and their God. They will turn their faces upward,'),
('ISA', 8, 22, 'ISA.8.22', 'then look to the earth and see distress, darkness, and the gloom of anguish. They will be driven into thick darkness.'),
('ISA', 9, 1, 'ISA.9.1', 'But there shall be no more gloom for her who was in anguish. In the former time, he brought into contempt the land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali; but in the latter time he has made it glorious, by the way of the sea, beyond the Jordan, Galilee of the nations.'),
('ISA', 9, 2, 'ISA.9.2', 'The people who walked in darkness have seen a great light. The light has shined on those who lived in the land of the shadow of death.'),
('ISA', 9, 3, 'ISA.9.3', 'You have multiplied the nation. You have increased their joy. They rejoice before you according to the joy in harvest, as men rejoice when they divide the plunder.'),
('ISA', 9, 4, 'ISA.9.4', 'For the yoke of his burden, and the staff of his shoulder, the rod of his oppressor, you have broken as in the day of Midian.'),
('ISA', 9, 5, 'ISA.9.5', 'For all the armor of the armed man in the noisy battle, and the garments rolled in blood, will be for burning, fuel for the fire.'),
('ISA', 9, 6, 'ISA.9.6', 'For a child is born to us. A son is given to us; and the government will be on his shoulders. His name will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.'),
('ISA', 9, 7, 'ISA.9.7', 'Of the increase of his government and of peace there shall be no end, on David’s throne, and on his kingdom, to establish it, and to uphold it with justice and with righteousness from that time on, even forever. The zeal of the LORD of Armies will perform this.'),
('ISA', 9, 8, 'ISA.9.8', 'The Lord sent a word into Jacob, and it falls on Israel.'),
('ISA', 9, 9, 'ISA.9.9', 'All the people will know, including Ephraim and the inhabitants of Samaria, who say in pride and in arrogance of heart,'),
('ISA', 9, 10, 'ISA.9.10', '“The bricks have fallen, but we will build with cut stone. The sycamore fig trees have been cut down, but we will put cedars in their place.”'),
('ISA', 9, 11, 'ISA.9.11', 'Therefore the LORD will set up on high against him the adversaries of Rezin, and will stir up his enemies,'),
('ISA', 9, 12, 'ISA.9.12', 'The Syrians in front, and the Philistines behind; and they will devour Israel with open mouth. For all this, his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.'),
('ISA', 9, 13, 'ISA.9.13', 'Yet the people have not turned to him who struck them, neither have they sought the LORD of Armies.'),
('ISA', 9, 14, 'ISA.9.14', 'Therefore the LORD will cut off from Israel head and tail, palm branch and reed, in one day.'),
('ISA', 9, 15, 'ISA.9.15', 'The elder and the honorable man is the head, and the prophet who teaches lies is the tail.'),
('ISA', 9, 16, 'ISA.9.16', 'For those who lead this people lead them astray; and those who are led by them are destroyed.'),
('ISA', 9, 17, 'ISA.9.17', 'Therefore the Lord will not rejoice over their young men, neither will he have compassion on their fatherless and widows; for everyone is profane and an evildoer, and every mouth speaks folly. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.'),
('ISA', 9, 18, 'ISA.9.18', 'For wickedness burns like a fire. It devours the briers and thorns; yes, it kindles in the thickets of the forest, and they roll upward in a column of smoke.'),
('ISA', 9, 19, 'ISA.9.19', 'Through the LORD of Armies’ wrath, the land is burned up; and the people are the fuel for the fire. No one spares his brother.'),
('ISA', 9, 20, 'ISA.9.20', 'One will devour on the right hand, and be hungry; and he will eat on the left hand, and they will not be satisfied. Everyone will eat the flesh of his own arm:'),
('ISA', 9, 21, 'ISA.9.21', 'Manasseh eating Ephraim and Ephraim eating Manasseh, and they together will be against Judah. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.'),
('ISA', 10, 1, 'ISA.10.1', 'Woe to those who decree unrighteous decrees, and to the writers who write oppressive decrees'),
('ISA', 10, 2, 'ISA.10.2', 'to deprive the needy of justice, and to rob the poor among my people of their rights, that widows may be their plunder, and that they may make the fatherless their prey!'),
('ISA', 10, 3, 'ISA.10.3', 'What will you do in the day of visitation, and in the desolation which will come from afar? To whom will you flee for help? Where will you leave your wealth?'),
('ISA', 10, 4, 'ISA.10.4', 'They will only bow down under the prisoners, and will fall under the slain. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.'),
('ISA', 10, 5, 'ISA.10.5', 'Alas Assyrian, the rod of my anger, the staff in whose hand is my indignation!'),
('ISA', 10, 6, 'ISA.10.6', 'I will send him against a profane nation, and against the people who anger me I will give him a command to take the plunder and to take the prey, and to tread them down like the mire of the streets.'),
('ISA', 10, 7, 'ISA.10.7', 'However, he doesn’t mean so, neither does his heart think so; but it is in his heart to destroy, and to cut off not a few nations.'),
('ISA', 10, 8, 'ISA.10.8', 'For he says, “Aren’t all of my princes kings?'),
('ISA', 10, 9, 'ISA.10.9', 'Isn’t Calno like Carchemish? Isn’t Hamath like Arpad? Isn’t Samaria like Damascus?”'),
('ISA', 10, 10, 'ISA.10.10', 'As my hand has found the kingdoms of the idols, whose engraved images exceeded those of Jerusalem and of Samaria,'),
('ISA', 10, 11, 'ISA.10.11', 'shall I not, as I have done to Samaria and her idols, so do to Jerusalem and her idols?'),
('ISA', 10, 12, 'ISA.10.12', 'Therefore it will happen that when the Lord has performed his whole work on Mount Zion and on Jerusalem, I will punish the fruit of the willful proud heart of the king of Assyria, and the insolence of his arrogant looks.'),
('ISA', 10, 13, 'ISA.10.13', 'For he has said, “By the strength of my hand I have done it, and by my wisdom, for I have understanding. I have removed the boundaries of the peoples, and have robbed their treasures. Like a valiant man I have brought down their rulers.'),
('ISA', 10, 14, 'ISA.10.14', 'My hand has found the riches of the peoples like a nest, and like one gathers eggs that are abandoned, I have gathered all the earth. There was no one who moved their wing, or that opened their mouth, or chirped.”'),
('ISA', 10, 15, 'ISA.10.15', 'Should an ax brag against him who chops with it? Should a saw exalt itself above him who saws with it? As if a rod should lift those who lift it up, or as if a staff should lift up someone who is not wood.'),
('ISA', 10, 16, 'ISA.10.16', 'Therefore the Lord, GOD of Armies, will send among his fat ones leanness; and under his glory a burning will be kindled like the burning of fire.'),
('ISA', 10, 17, 'ISA.10.17', 'The light of Israel will be for a fire, and his Holy One for a flame; and it will burn and devour his thorns and his briers in one day.'),
('ISA', 10, 18, 'ISA.10.18', 'He will consume the glory of his forest and of his fruitful field, both soul and body. It will be as when a standard bearer faints.'),
('ISA', 10, 19, 'ISA.10.19', 'The remnant of the trees of his forest shall be few, so that a child could write their number.'),
('ISA', 10, 20, 'ISA.10.20', 'It will come to pass in that day that the remnant of Israel, and those who have escaped from the house of Jacob will no more again lean on him who struck them, but shall lean on the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, in truth.'),
('ISA', 10, 21, 'ISA.10.21', 'A remnant will return, even the remnant of Jacob, to the mighty God.'),
('ISA', 10, 22, 'ISA.10.22', 'For though your people, Israel, are like the sand of the sea, only a remnant of them will return. A destruction is determined, overflowing with righteousness.'),
('ISA', 10, 23, 'ISA.10.23', 'For the Lord, GOD of Armies, will make a full end, and that determined, throughout all the earth.'),
('ISA', 10, 24, 'ISA.10.24', 'Therefore the Lord, GOD of Armies, says, “My people who dwell in Zion, don’t be afraid of the Assyrian, though he strike you with the rod, and lift up his staff against you, as Egypt did.'),
('ISA', 10, 25, 'ISA.10.25', 'For yet a very little while, and the indignation against you will be accomplished, and my anger will be directed to his destruction.”'),
('ISA', 10, 26, 'ISA.10.26', 'The LORD of Armies will stir up a scourge against him, as in the slaughter of Midian at the rock of Oreb. His rod will be over the sea, and he will lift it up like he did against Egypt.'),
('ISA', 10, 27, 'ISA.10.27', 'It will happen in that day that his burden will depart from off your shoulder, and his yoke from off your neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing oil.'),
('ISA', 10, 28, 'ISA.10.28', 'He has come to Aiath. He has passed through Migron. At Michmash he stores his baggage.'),
('ISA', 10, 29, 'ISA.10.29', 'They have gone over the pass. They have taken up their lodging at Geba. Ramah trembles. Gibeah of Saul has fled.'),
('ISA', 10, 30, 'ISA.10.30', 'Cry aloud with your voice, daughter of Gallim! Listen, Laishah! You poor Anathoth!'),
('ISA', 10, 31, 'ISA.10.31', 'Madmenah is a fugitive. The inhabitants of Gebim flee for safety.'),
('ISA', 10, 32, 'ISA.10.32', 'This very day he will halt at Nob. He shakes his hand at the mountain of the daughter of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem.'),
('ISA', 10, 33, 'ISA.10.33', 'Behold, the Lord, GOD of Armies, will lop the boughs with terror. The tall will be cut down, and the lofty will be brought low.'),
('ISA', 10, 34, 'ISA.10.34', 'He will cut down the thickets of the forest with iron, and Lebanon will fall by the Mighty One.'),
('ISA', 11, 1, 'ISA.11.1', 'A shoot will come out of the stock of Jesse, and a branch out of his roots will bear fruit.'),
('ISA', 11, 2, 'ISA.11.2', 'The LORD’s Spirit will rest on him: the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the LORD.'),
('ISA', 11, 3, 'ISA.11.3', 'His delight will be in the fear of the LORD. He will not judge by the sight of his eyes, neither decide by the hearing of his ears;'),
('ISA', 11, 4, 'ISA.11.4', 'but he will judge the poor with righteousness, and decide with equity for the humble of the earth. He will strike the earth with the rod of his mouth; and with the breath of his lips he will kill the wicked.'),
('ISA', 11, 5, 'ISA.11.5', 'Righteousness will be the belt around his waist, and faithfulness the belt around his waist.'),
('ISA', 11, 6, 'ISA.11.6', 'The wolf will live with the lamb, and the leopard will lie down with the young goat, the calf, the young lion, and the fattened calf together; and a little child will lead them.'),
('ISA', 11, 7, 'ISA.11.7', 'The cow and the bear will graze. Their young ones will lie down together. The lion will eat straw like the ox.'),
('ISA', 11, 8, 'ISA.11.8', 'The nursing child will play near a cobra’s hole, and the weaned child will put his hand on the viper’s den.'),
('ISA', 11, 9, 'ISA.11.9', 'They will not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain; for the earth will be full of the knowledge of the LORD, as the waters cover the sea.'),
('ISA', 11, 10, 'ISA.11.10', 'It will happen in that day that the nations will seek the root of Jesse, who stands as a banner of the peoples; and his resting place will be glorious.'),
('ISA', 11, 11, 'ISA.11.11', 'It will happen in that day that the Lord will set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant that is left of his people from Assyria, from Egypt, from Pathros, from Cush, from Elam, from Shinar, from Hamath, and from the islands of the sea.'),
('ISA', 11, 12, 'ISA.11.12', 'He will set up a banner for the nations, and will assemble the outcasts of Israel, and gather together the dispersed of Judah from the four corners of the earth.'),
('ISA', 11, 13, 'ISA.11.13', 'The envy also of Ephraim will depart, and those who persecute Judah will be cut off. Ephraim won’t envy Judah, and Judah won’t persecute Ephraim.'),
('ISA', 11, 14, 'ISA.11.14', 'They will fly down on the shoulders of the Philistines on the west. Together they will plunder the children of the east. They will extend their power over Edom and Moab, and the children of Ammon will obey them.'),
('ISA', 11, 15, 'ISA.11.15', 'The LORD will utterly destroy the tongue of the Egyptian sea; and with his scorching wind he will wave his hand over the River, and will split it into seven streams, and cause men to march over in sandals.'),
('ISA', 11, 16, 'ISA.11.16', 'There will be a highway for the remnant that is left of his people from Assyria, like there was for Israel in the day that he came up out of the land of Egypt.'),
('ISA', 12, 1, 'ISA.12.1', 'In that day you will say, “I will give thanks to you, the LORD; for though you were angry with me, your anger has turned away and you comfort me.'),
('ISA', 12, 2, 'ISA.12.2', 'Behold, God is my salvation. I will trust, and will not be afraid; for the LORD, the LORD, is my strength and song; and he has become my salvation.”'),
('ISA', 12, 3, 'ISA.12.3', 'Therefore with joy you will draw water out of the wells of salvation.'),
('ISA', 12, 4, 'ISA.12.4', 'In that day you will say, “Give thanks to the LORD! Call on his name! Declare his doings among the peoples! Proclaim that his name is exalted!'),
('ISA', 12, 5, 'ISA.12.5', 'Sing to the LORD, for he has done excellent things! Let this be known in all the earth!'),
('ISA', 12, 6, 'ISA.12.6', 'Cry aloud and shout, you inhabitant of Zion, for the Holy One of Israel is great among you!”'),
('ISA', 13, 1, 'ISA.13.1', 'The burden of Babylon, which Isaiah the son of Amoz saw.'),
('ISA', 13, 2, 'ISA.13.2', 'Set up a banner on the bare mountain! Lift up your voice to them! Wave your hand, that they may go into the gates of the nobles.'),
('ISA', 13, 3, 'ISA.13.3', 'I have commanded my consecrated ones; yes, I have called my mighty men for my anger, even my proudly exulting ones.'),
('ISA', 13, 4, 'ISA.13.4', 'The noise of a multitude is in the mountains, as of a great people; the noise of an uproar of the kingdoms of the nations gathered together! The LORD of Armies is mustering the army for the battle.'),
('ISA', 13, 5, 'ISA.13.5', 'They come from a far country, from the uttermost part of heaven, even the LORD, and the weapons of his indignation, to destroy the whole land.'),
('ISA', 13, 6, 'ISA.13.6', 'Wail, for the LORD’s day is at hand! It will come as destruction from the Almighty.'),
('ISA', 13, 7, 'ISA.13.7', 'Therefore all hands will be feeble, and everyone’s heart will melt.'),
('ISA', 13, 8, 'ISA.13.8', 'They will be dismayed. Pangs and sorrows will seize them. They will be in pain like a woman in labor. They will look in amazement one at another. Their faces will be faces of flame.'),
('ISA', 13, 9, 'ISA.13.9', 'Behold, the day of the LORD comes, cruel, with wrath and fierce anger; to make the land a desolation, and to destroy its sinners out of it.'),
('ISA', 13, 10, 'ISA.13.10', 'For the stars of the sky and its constellations will not give their light. The sun will be darkened in its going out, and the moon will not cause its light to shine.'),
('ISA', 13, 11, 'ISA.13.11', 'I will punish the world for their evil, and the wicked for their iniquity. I will cause the arrogance of the proud to cease, and will humble the arrogance of the terrible.'),
('ISA', 13, 12, 'ISA.13.12', 'I will make people more rare than fine gold, even a person than the pure gold of Ophir.'),
('ISA', 13, 13, 'ISA.13.13', 'Therefore I will make the heavens tremble, and the earth will be shaken out of its place in the LORD of Armies’ wrath, and in the day of his fierce anger.'),
('ISA', 13, 14, 'ISA.13.14', 'It will happen that like a hunted gazelle and like sheep that no one gathers, they will each turn to their own people, and will each flee to their own land.'),
('ISA', 13, 15, 'ISA.13.15', 'Everyone who is found will be thrust through. Everyone who is captured will fall by the sword.'),
('ISA', 13, 16, 'ISA.13.16', 'Their infants also will be dashed in pieces before their eyes. Their houses will be ransacked, and their wives raped.'),
('ISA', 13, 17, 'ISA.13.17', 'Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them, who will not value silver, and as for gold, they will not delight in it.'),
('ISA', 13, 18, 'ISA.13.18', 'Their bows will dash the young men in pieces; and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb. Their eyes will not spare children.'),
('ISA', 13, 19, 'ISA.13.19', 'Babylon, the glory of kingdoms, the beauty of the Chaldeans’ pride, will be like when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah.'),
('ISA', 13, 20, 'ISA.13.20', 'It will never be inhabited, neither will it be lived in from generation to generation. The Arabian will not pitch a tent there, neither will shepherds make their flocks lie down there.'),
('ISA', 13, 21, 'ISA.13.21', 'But wild animals of the desert will lie there, and their houses will be full of jackals. Ostriches will dwell there, and wild goats will frolic there.'),
('ISA', 13, 22, 'ISA.13.22', 'Hyenas will cry in their fortresses, and jackals in the pleasant palaces. Her time is near to come, and her days will not be prolonged.'),
('ISA', 14, 1, 'ISA.14.1', 'For the LORD will have compassion on Jacob, and will yet choose Israel, and set them in their own land. The foreigner will join himself with them, and they will unite with the house of Jacob.'),
('ISA', 14, 2, 'ISA.14.2', 'The peoples will take them, and bring them to their place. The house of Israel will possess them in the LORD’s land for servants and for handmaids. They will take as captives those whose captives they were; and they shall rule over their oppressors.'),
('ISA', 14, 3, 'ISA.14.3', 'It will happen in the day that the LORD will give you rest from your sorrow, from your trouble, and from the hard service in which you were made to serve,'),
('ISA', 14, 4, 'ISA.14.4', 'that you will take up this parable against the king of Babylon, and say, “How the oppressor has ceased! The golden city has ceased!”'),
('ISA', 14, 5, 'ISA.14.5', 'The LORD has broken the staff of the wicked, the scepter of the rulers,'),
('ISA', 14, 6, 'ISA.14.6', 'who struck the peoples in wrath with a continual stroke, who ruled the nations in anger, with a persecution that no one restrained.'),
('ISA', 14, 7, 'ISA.14.7', 'The whole earth is at rest, and is quiet. They break out in song.'),
('ISA', 14, 8, 'ISA.14.8', 'Yes, the cypress trees rejoice with you, with the cedars of Lebanon, saying, “Since you are humbled, no lumberjack has come up against us.”'),
('ISA', 14, 9, 'ISA.14.9', 'Sheol from beneath has moved for you to meet you at your coming. It stirs up the departed spirits for you, even all the rulers of the earth. It has raised up from their thrones all the kings of the nations.'),
('ISA', 14, 10, 'ISA.14.10', 'They all will answer and ask you, “Have you also become as weak as we are? Have you become like us?”'),
('ISA', 14, 11, 'ISA.14.11', 'Your pomp is brought down to Sheol, with the sound of your stringed instruments. Maggots are spread out under you, and worms cover you.'),
('ISA', 14, 12, 'ISA.14.12', 'How you have fallen from heaven, shining one, son of the dawn! How you are cut down to the ground, who laid the nations low!'),
('ISA', 14, 13, 'ISA.14.13', 'You said in your heart, “I will ascend into heaven! I will exalt my throne above the stars of God! I will sit on the mountain of assembly, in the far north!'),
('ISA', 14, 14, 'ISA.14.14', 'I will ascend above the heights of the clouds! I will make myself like the Most High!”'),
('ISA', 14, 15, 'ISA.14.15', 'Yet you shall be brought down to Sheol, to the depths of the pit.'),
('ISA', 14, 16, 'ISA.14.16', 'Those who see you will stare at you. They will ponder you, saying, “Is this the man who made the earth to tremble, who shook kingdoms,'),
('ISA', 14, 17, 'ISA.14.17', 'who made the world like a wilderness, and overthrew its cities, who didn’t release his prisoners to their home?”'),
('ISA', 14, 18, 'ISA.14.18', 'All the kings of the nations sleep in glory, everyone in his own house.'),
('ISA', 14, 19, 'ISA.14.19', 'But you are cast away from your tomb like an abominable branch, clothed with the slain who are thrust through with the sword, who go down to the stones of the pit; like a dead body trodden under foot.'),
('ISA', 14, 20, 'ISA.14.20', 'You will not join them in burial, because you have destroyed your land. You have killed your people. The offspring of evildoers will not be named forever.'),
('ISA', 14, 21, 'ISA.14.21', 'Prepare for slaughter of his children because of the iniquity of their fathers, that they not rise up and possess the earth, and fill the surface of the world with cities.'),
('ISA', 14, 22, 'ISA.14.22', '“I will rise up against them,” says the LORD of Armies, “and cut off from Babylon name and remnant, and son and son’s son,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 14, 23, 'ISA.14.23', '“I will also make it a possession for the porcupine, and pools of water. I will sweep it with the broom of destruction,” says the LORD of Armies.'),
('ISA', 14, 24, 'ISA.14.24', 'The LORD of Armies has sworn, saying, “Surely, as I have thought, so shall it happen; and as I have purposed, so shall it stand:'),
('ISA', 14, 25, 'ISA.14.25', 'that I will break the Assyrian in my land, and tread him under foot on my mountains. Then his yoke will leave them, and his burden leave their shoulders.'),
('ISA', 14, 26, 'ISA.14.26', 'This is the plan that is determined for the whole earth. This is the hand that is stretched out over all the nations.'),
('ISA', 14, 27, 'ISA.14.27', 'For the LORD of Armies has planned, and who can stop it? His hand is stretched out, and who can turn it back?”'),
('ISA', 14, 28, 'ISA.14.28', 'This burden was in the year that King Ahaz died.'),
('ISA', 14, 29, 'ISA.14.29', 'Don’t rejoice, O Philistia, all of you, because the rod that struck you is broken; for out of the serpent’s root an adder will emerge, and his fruit will be a fiery flying serpent.'),
('ISA', 14, 30, 'ISA.14.30', 'The firstborn of the poor will eat, and the needy will lie down in safety; and I will kill your root with famine, and your remnant will be killed.'),
('ISA', 14, 31, 'ISA.14.31', 'Howl, gate! Cry, city! You are melted away, Philistia, all of you; for smoke comes out of the north, and there is no straggler in his ranks.'),
('ISA', 14, 32, 'ISA.14.32', 'What will they answer the messengers of the nation? That the LORD has founded Zion, and in her the afflicted of his people will take refuge.'),
('ISA', 15, 1, 'ISA.15.1', 'The burden of Moab. For in a night, Ar of Moab is laid waste, and brought to nothing. For in a night Kir of Moab is laid waste, and brought to nothing.'),
('ISA', 15, 2, 'ISA.15.2', 'They have gone up to Bayith, and to Dibon, to the high places, to weep. Moab wails over Nebo and over Medeba. Baldness is on all of their heads. Every beard is cut off.'),
('ISA', 15, 3, 'ISA.15.3', 'In their streets, they clothe themselves in sackcloth. In their streets and on their housetops, everyone wails, weeping abundantly.'),
('ISA', 15, 4, 'ISA.15.4', 'Heshbon cries out with Elealeh. Their voice is heard even to Jahaz. Therefore the armed men of Moab cry aloud. Their souls tremble within them.'),
('ISA', 15, 5, 'ISA.15.5', 'My heart cries out for Moab! Her nobles flee to Zoar, to Eglath Shelishiyah; for they go up by the ascent of Luhith with weeping; for on the way to Horonaim, they raise up a cry of destruction.'),
('ISA', 15, 6, 'ISA.15.6', 'For the waters of Nimrim will be desolate; for the grass has withered away, the tender grass fails, there is no green thing.'),
('ISA', 15, 7, 'ISA.15.7', 'Therefore they will carry away the abundance they have gotten, and that which they have stored up, over the brook of the willows.'),
('ISA', 15, 8, 'ISA.15.8', 'For the cry has gone around the borders of Moab, its wailing to Eglaim, and its wailing to Beer Elim.'),
('ISA', 15, 9, 'ISA.15.9', 'For the waters of Dimon are full of blood; for I will bring yet more on Dimon, a lion on those of Moab who escape, and on the remnant of the land.'),
('ISA', 16, 1, 'ISA.16.1', 'Send the lambs for the ruler of the land from Selah to the wilderness, to the mountain of the daughter of Zion.'),
('ISA', 16, 2, 'ISA.16.2', 'For it will be that as wandering birds, as a scattered nest, so will the daughters of Moab be at the fords of the Arnon.'),
('ISA', 16, 3, 'ISA.16.3', 'Give counsel! Execute justice! Make your shade like the night in the middle of the noonday! Hide the outcasts! Don’t betray the fugitive!'),
('ISA', 16, 4, 'ISA.16.4', 'Let my outcasts dwell with you! As for Moab, be a hiding place for him from the face of the destroyer. For the extortionist is brought to nothing. Destruction ceases. The oppressors are consumed out of the land.'),
('ISA', 16, 5, 'ISA.16.5', 'A throne will be established in loving kindness. One will sit on it in truth, in the tent of David, judging, seeking justice, and swift to do righteousness.'),
('ISA', 16, 6, 'ISA.16.6', 'We have heard of the pride of Moab, that he is very proud; even of his arrogance, his pride, and his wrath. His boastings are nothing.'),
('ISA', 16, 7, 'ISA.16.7', 'Therefore Moab will wail for Moab. Everyone will wail. You will mourn for the raisin cakes of Kir Hareseth, utterly stricken.'),
('ISA', 16, 8, 'ISA.16.8', 'For the fields of Heshbon languish with the vine of Sibmah. The lords of the nations have broken down its choice branches, which reached even to Jazer, which wandered into the wilderness. Its shoots were spread abroad. They passed over the sea.'),
('ISA', 16, 9, 'ISA.16.9', 'Therefore I will weep with the weeping of Jazer for the vine of Sibmah. I will water you with my tears, Heshbon, and Elealeh: for on your summer fruits and on your harvest the battle shout has fallen.'),
('ISA', 16, 10, 'ISA.16.10', 'Gladness is taken away, and joy out of the fruitful field; and in the vineyards there will be no singing, neither joyful noise. Nobody will tread out wine in the presses. I have made the shouting stop.'),
('ISA', 16, 11, 'ISA.16.11', 'Therefore my heart sounds like a harp for Moab, and my inward parts for Kir Heres.'),
('ISA', 16, 12, 'ISA.16.12', 'It will happen that when Moab presents himself, when he wearies himself on the high place, and comes to his sanctuary to pray, that he will not prevail.'),
('ISA', 16, 13, 'ISA.16.13', 'This is the word that the LORD spoke concerning Moab in time past.'),
('ISA', 16, 14, 'ISA.16.14', 'But now the LORD has spoken, saying, “Within three years, as a worker bound by contract would count them, the glory of Moab shall be brought into contempt, with all his great multitude; and the remnant will be very small and feeble.”'),
('ISA', 17, 1, 'ISA.17.1', 'The burden of Damascus. “Behold, Damascus is taken away from being a city, and it will be a ruinous heap.'),
('ISA', 17, 2, 'ISA.17.2', 'The cities of Aroer are forsaken. They will be for flocks, which shall lie down, and no one shall make them afraid.'),
('ISA', 17, 3, 'ISA.17.3', 'The fortress shall cease from Ephraim, and the kingdom from Damascus, and the remnant of Syria. They will be as the glory of the children of Israel,” says the LORD of Armies.'),
('ISA', 17, 4, 'ISA.17.4', '“It will happen in that day that the glory of Jacob will be made thin, and the fatness of his flesh will become lean.'),
('ISA', 17, 5, 'ISA.17.5', 'It will be like when the harvester gathers the wheat, and his arm reaps the grain. Yes, it will be like when one gleans grain in the valley of Rephaim.'),
('ISA', 17, 6, 'ISA.17.6', 'Yet gleanings will be left there, like the shaking of an olive tree, two or three olives in the top of the uppermost bough, four or five in the outermost branches of a fruitful tree,” says the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('ISA', 17, 7, 'ISA.17.7', 'In that day, people will look to their Maker, and their eyes will have respect for the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 17, 8, 'ISA.17.8', 'They will not look to the altars, the work of their hands; neither shall they respect that which their fingers have made, either the Asherah poles or the incense altars.'),
('ISA', 17, 9, 'ISA.17.9', 'In that day, their strong cities will be like the forsaken places in the woods and on the mountain top, which were forsaken from before the children of Israel; and it will be a desolation.'),
('ISA', 17, 10, 'ISA.17.10', 'For you have forgotten the God of your salvation, and have not remembered the rock of your strength. Therefore you plant pleasant plants, and set out foreign seedlings.'),
('ISA', 17, 11, 'ISA.17.11', 'In the day of your planting, you hedge it in. In the morning, you make your seed blossom, but the harvest flees away in the day of grief and of desperate sorrow.'),
('ISA', 17, 12, 'ISA.17.12', 'Ah, the uproar of many peoples who roar like the roaring of the seas; and the rushing of nations that rush like the rushing of mighty waters!'),
('ISA', 17, 13, 'ISA.17.13', 'The nations will rush like the rushing of many waters, but he will rebuke them, and they will flee far off, and will be chased like the chaff of the mountains before the wind, and like the whirling dust before the storm.'),
('ISA', 17, 14, 'ISA.17.14', 'At evening, behold, terror! Before the morning, they are no more. This is the portion of those who plunder us, and the lot of those who rob us.'),
('ISA', 18, 1, 'ISA.18.1', 'Ah, the land of the rustling of wings, which is beyond the rivers of Ethiopia;'),
('ISA', 18, 2, 'ISA.18.2', 'that sends ambassadors by the sea, even in vessels of papyrus on the waters, saying, “Go, you swift messengers, to a nation tall and smooth, to a people awesome from their beginning onward, a nation that measures out and treads down, whose land the rivers divide!”'),
('ISA', 18, 3, 'ISA.18.3', 'All you inhabitants of the world, and you dwellers on the earth, when a banner is lifted up on the mountains, look! When the trumpet is blown, listen!'),
('ISA', 18, 4, 'ISA.18.4', 'For the LORD said to me, “I will be still, and I will see in my dwelling place, like clear heat in sunshine, like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest.”'),
('ISA', 18, 5, 'ISA.18.5', 'For before the harvest, when the blossom is over, and the flower becomes a ripening grape, he will cut off the sprigs with pruning hooks, and he will cut down and take away the spreading branches.'),
('ISA', 18, 6, 'ISA.18.6', 'They will be left together for the ravenous birds of the mountains, and for the animals of the earth. The ravenous birds will eat them in the summer, and all the animals of the earth will eat them in the winter.'),
('ISA', 18, 7, 'ISA.18.7', 'In that time, a present will be brought to the LORD of Armies from a people tall and smooth, even from a people awesome from their beginning onward, a nation that measures out and treads down, whose land the rivers divide, to the place of the name of the LORD of Armies, Mount Zion.'),
('ISA', 19, 1, 'ISA.19.1', 'The burden of Egypt. “Behold, the LORD rides on a swift cloud, and comes to Egypt. The idols of Egypt will tremble at his presence; and the heart of Egypt will melt within it.'),
('ISA', 19, 2, 'ISA.19.2', 'I will stir up the Egyptians against the Egyptians, and they will fight everyone against his brother, and everyone against his neighbor; city against city, and kingdom against kingdom.'),
('ISA', 19, 3, 'ISA.19.3', 'The spirit of the Egyptians will fail within them. I will destroy their counsel. They will seek the idols, the charmers, those who have familiar spirits, and the wizards.'),
('ISA', 19, 4, 'ISA.19.4', 'I will give over the Egyptians into the hand of a cruel lord. A fierce king will rule over them,” says the Lord, GOD of Armies.'),
('ISA', 19, 5, 'ISA.19.5', 'The waters will fail from the sea, and the river will be wasted and become dry.'),
('ISA', 19, 6, 'ISA.19.6', 'The rivers will become foul. The streams of Egypt will be diminished and dried up. The reeds and flags will wither away.'),
('ISA', 19, 7, 'ISA.19.7', 'The meadows by the Nile, by the brink of the Nile, and all the sown fields of the Nile, will become dry, be driven away, and be no more.'),
('ISA', 19, 8, 'ISA.19.8', 'The fishermen will lament, and all those who fish in the Nile will mourn, and those who spread nets on the waters will languish.'),
('ISA', 19, 9, 'ISA.19.9', 'Moreover those who work in combed flax, and those who weave white cloth, will be confounded.'),
('ISA', 19, 10, 'ISA.19.10', 'The pillars will be broken in pieces. All those who work for hire will be grieved in soul.'),
('ISA', 19, 11, 'ISA.19.11', 'The princes of Zoan are utterly foolish. The counsel of the wisest counselors of Pharaoh has become stupid. How do you say to Pharaoh, “I am the son of the wise, the son of ancient kings”?'),
('ISA', 19, 12, 'ISA.19.12', 'Where then are your wise men? Let them tell you now; and let them know what the LORD of Armies has purposed concerning Egypt.'),
('ISA', 19, 13, 'ISA.19.13', 'The princes of Zoan have become fools. The princes of Memphis are deceived. They have caused Egypt to go astray, those who are the cornerstone of her tribes.'),
('ISA', 19, 14, 'ISA.19.14', 'The LORD has mixed a spirit of perverseness in the middle of her; and they have caused Egypt to go astray in all of its works, like a drunken man staggers in his vomit.'),
('ISA', 19, 15, 'ISA.19.15', 'Neither shall there be any work for Egypt, which head or tail, palm branch or rush, may do.'),
('ISA', 19, 16, 'ISA.19.16', 'In that day the Egyptians will be like women. They will tremble and fear because of the shaking of the LORD of Armies’s hand, which he shakes over them.'),
('ISA', 19, 17, 'ISA.19.17', 'The land of Judah will become a terror to Egypt. Everyone to whom mention is made of it will be afraid, because of the plans of the LORD of Armies, which he determines against it.'),
('ISA', 19, 18, 'ISA.19.18', 'In that day, there will be five cities in the land of Egypt that speak the language of Canaan, and swear to the LORD of Armies. One will be called “The city of destruction.”'),
('ISA', 19, 19, 'ISA.19.19', 'In that day, there will be an altar to the LORD in the middle of the land of Egypt, and a pillar to the LORD at its border.'),
('ISA', 19, 20, 'ISA.19.20', 'It will be for a sign and for a witness to the LORD of Armies in the land of Egypt; for they will cry to the LORD because of oppressors, and he will send them a savior and a defender, and he will deliver them.'),
('ISA', 19, 21, 'ISA.19.21', 'The LORD will be known to Egypt, and the Egyptians will know the LORD in that day. Yes, they will worship with sacrifice and offering, and will vow a vow to the LORD, and will perform it.'),
('ISA', 19, 22, 'ISA.19.22', 'The LORD will strike Egypt, striking and healing. They will return to the LORD, and he will be entreated by them, and will heal them.'),
('ISA', 19, 23, 'ISA.19.23', 'In that day there will be a highway out of Egypt to Assyria, and the Assyrian shall come into Egypt, and the Egyptian into Assyria; and the Egyptians will worship with the Assyrians.'),
('ISA', 19, 24, 'ISA.19.24', 'In that day, Israel will be the third with Egypt and with Assyria, a blessing within the earth;'),
('ISA', 19, 25, 'ISA.19.25', 'because the LORD of Armies has blessed them, saying, “Blessed be Egypt my people, Assyria the work of my hands, and Israel my inheritance.”'),
('ISA', 20, 1, 'ISA.20.1', 'In the year that Tartan came to Ashdod, when Sargon the king of Assyria sent him, and he fought against Ashdod and took it;'),
('ISA', 20, 2, 'ISA.20.2', 'at that time the LORD spoke by Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, “Go, and loosen the sackcloth from off your waist, and take your sandals from off your feet.” He did so, walking naked and barefoot.'),
('ISA', 20, 3, 'ISA.20.3', 'The LORD said, “As my servant Isaiah has walked naked and barefoot three years for a sign and a wonder concerning Egypt and concerning Ethiopia,'),
('ISA', 20, 4, 'ISA.20.4', 'so the king of Assyria will lead away the captives of Egypt and the exiles of Ethiopia, young and old, naked and barefoot, and with buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt.'),
('ISA', 20, 5, 'ISA.20.5', 'They will be dismayed and confounded, because of Ethiopia their expectation, and of Egypt their glory.'),
('ISA', 20, 6, 'ISA.20.6', 'The inhabitants of this coast land will say in that day, ‘Behold, this is our expectation, where we fled for help to be delivered from the king of Assyria. And we, how will we escape?’”'),
('ISA', 21, 1, 'ISA.21.1', 'The burden of the wilderness of the sea. As whirlwinds in the South sweep through, it comes from the wilderness, from an awesome land.'),
('ISA', 21, 2, 'ISA.21.2', 'A grievous vision is declared to me. The treacherous man deals treacherously, and the destroyer destroys. Go up, Elam; attack! I have stopped all of Media’s sighing.'),
('ISA', 21, 3, 'ISA.21.3', 'Therefore my thighs are filled with anguish. Pains have seized me, like the pains of a woman in labor. I am in so much pain that I can’t hear. I am so dismayed that I can’t see.'),
('ISA', 21, 4, 'ISA.21.4', 'My heart flutters. Horror has frightened me. The twilight that I desired has been turned into trembling for me.'),
('ISA', 21, 5, 'ISA.21.5', 'They prepare the table. They set the watch. They eat. They drink. Rise up, you princes, oil the shield!'),
('ISA', 21, 6, 'ISA.21.6', 'For the Lord said to me, “Go, set a watchman. Let him declare what he sees.'),
('ISA', 21, 7, 'ISA.21.7', 'When he sees a troop, horsemen in pairs, a troop of donkeys, a troop of camels, he shall listen diligently with great attentiveness.”'),
('ISA', 21, 8, 'ISA.21.8', 'He cried like a lion: “Lord, I stand continually on the watchtower in the daytime, and every night I stay at my post.'),
('ISA', 21, 9, 'ISA.21.9', 'Behold, here comes a troop of men, horsemen in pairs.” He answered, “Fallen, fallen is Babylon; and all the engraved images of her gods are broken to the ground.'),
('ISA', 21, 10, 'ISA.21.10', 'You are my threshing, and the grain of my floor!” That which I have heard from the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, I have declared to you.'),
('ISA', 21, 11, 'ISA.21.11', 'The burden of Dumah. One calls to me out of Seir, “Watchman, what of the night? Watchman, what of the night?”'),
('ISA', 21, 12, 'ISA.21.12', 'The watchman said, “The morning comes, and also the night. If you will inquire, inquire. Come back again.”'),
('ISA', 21, 13, 'ISA.21.13', 'The burden on Arabia. You will lodge in the thickets in Arabia, you caravans of Dedanites.'),
('ISA', 21, 14, 'ISA.21.14', 'They brought water to him who was thirsty. The inhabitants of the land of Tema met the fugitives with their bread.'),
('ISA', 21, 15, 'ISA.21.15', 'For they fled away from the swords, from the drawn sword, from the bent bow, and from the heat of battle.'),
('ISA', 21, 16, 'ISA.21.16', 'For the Lord said to me, “Within a year, as a worker bound by contract would count it, all the glory of Kedar will fail,'),
('ISA', 21, 17, 'ISA.21.17', 'and the residue of the number of the archers, the mighty men of the children of Kedar, will be few; for the LORD, the God of Israel, has spoken it.”'),
('ISA', 22, 1, 'ISA.22.1', 'The burden of the valley of vision. What ails you now, that you have all gone up to the housetops?'),
('ISA', 22, 2, 'ISA.22.2', 'You that are full of shouting, a tumultuous city, a joyous town, your slain are not slain with the sword, neither are they dead in battle.'),
('ISA', 22, 3, 'ISA.22.3', 'All your rulers fled away together. They were bound by the archers. All who were found by you were bound together. They fled far away.'),
('ISA', 22, 4, 'ISA.22.4', 'Therefore I said, “Look away from me. I will weep bitterly. Don’t labor to comfort me for the destruction of the daughter of my people.'),
('ISA', 22, 5, 'ISA.22.5', 'For it is a day of confusion, and of treading down, and of perplexity from the Lord, GOD of Armies, in the valley of vision, a breaking down of the walls, and a crying to the mountains.”'),
('ISA', 22, 6, 'ISA.22.6', 'Elam carried his quiver, with chariots of men and horsemen; and Kir uncovered the shield.'),
('ISA', 22, 7, 'ISA.22.7', 'Your choicest valleys were full of chariots, and the horsemen set themselves in array at the gate.'),
('ISA', 22, 8, 'ISA.22.8', 'He took away the covering of Judah; and you looked in that day to the armor in the house of the forest.'),
('ISA', 22, 9, 'ISA.22.9', 'You saw the breaches of David’s city, that they were many; and you gathered together the waters of the lower pool.'),
('ISA', 22, 10, 'ISA.22.10', 'You counted the houses of Jerusalem, and you broke down the houses to fortify the wall.'),
('ISA', 22, 11, 'ISA.22.11', 'You also made a reservoir between the two walls for the water of the old pool. But you didn’t look to him who had done this, neither did you have respect for him who planned it long ago.'),
('ISA', 22, 12, 'ISA.22.12', 'In that day, the Lord, GOD of Armies, called to weeping, to mourning, to baldness, and to dressing in sackcloth;'),
('ISA', 22, 13, 'ISA.22.13', 'and behold, there is joy and gladness, killing cattle and killing sheep, eating meat and drinking wine: “Let’s eat and drink, for tomorrow we will die.”'),
('ISA', 22, 14, 'ISA.22.14', 'The LORD of Armies revealed himself in my ears, “Surely this iniquity will not be forgiven you until you die,” says the Lord, GOD of Armies.'),
('ISA', 22, 15, 'ISA.22.15', 'The Lord, GOD of Armies says, “Go, get yourself to this treasurer, even to Shebna, who is over the house, and say,'),
('ISA', 22, 16, 'ISA.22.16', '‘What are you doing here? Who has you here, that you have dug out a tomb here?’ Cutting himself out a tomb on high, chiseling a habitation for himself in the rock!”'),
('ISA', 22, 17, 'ISA.22.17', 'Behold, the LORD will overcome you and hurl you away violently. Yes, he will grasp you firmly.'),
('ISA', 22, 18, 'ISA.22.18', 'He will surely wind you around and around, and throw you like a ball into a large country. There you will die, and there the chariots of your glory will be, you disgrace of your lord’s house.'),
('ISA', 22, 19, 'ISA.22.19', 'I will thrust you from your office. You will be pulled down from your station.'),
('ISA', 22, 20, 'ISA.22.20', 'It will happen in that day that I will call my servant Eliakim the son of Hilkiah,'),
('ISA', 22, 21, 'ISA.22.21', 'and I will clothe him with your robe, and strengthen him with your belt. I will commit your government into his hand; and he will be a father to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and to the house of Judah.'),
('ISA', 22, 22, 'ISA.22.22', 'I will lay the key of David’s house on his shoulder. He will open, and no one will shut. He will shut, and no one will open.'),
('ISA', 22, 23, 'ISA.22.23', 'I will fasten him like a nail in a sure place. He will be for a throne of glory to his father’s house.'),
('ISA', 22, 24, 'ISA.22.24', 'They will hang on him all the glory of his father’s house, the offspring and the issue, every small vessel, from the cups even to all the pitchers.'),
('ISA', 22, 25, 'ISA.22.25', '“In that day,” says the LORD of Armies, “the nail that was fastened in a sure place will give way. It will be cut down and fall. The burden that was on it will be cut off, for the LORD has spoken it.”'),
('ISA', 23, 1, 'ISA.23.1', 'The burden of Tyre. Howl, you ships of Tarshish! For it is laid waste, so that there is no house, no entering in. From the land of Kittim it is revealed to them.'),
('ISA', 23, 2, 'ISA.23.2', 'Be still, you inhabitants of the coast, you whom the merchants of Sidon that pass over the sea have replenished.'),
('ISA', 23, 3, 'ISA.23.3', 'On great waters, the seed of the Shihor, the harvest of the Nile, was her revenue. She was the market of nations.'),
('ISA', 23, 4, 'ISA.23.4', 'Be ashamed, Sidon; for the sea has spoken, the stronghold of the sea, saying, “I have not travailed, nor given birth, neither have I nourished young men, nor brought up virgins.”'),
('ISA', 23, 5, 'ISA.23.5', 'When the report comes to Egypt, they will be in anguish at the report of Tyre.'),
('ISA', 23, 6, 'ISA.23.6', 'Pass over to Tarshish! Wail, you inhabitants of the coast!'),
('ISA', 23, 7, 'ISA.23.7', 'Is this your joyous city, whose antiquity is of ancient days, whose feet carried her far away to travel?'),
('ISA', 23, 8, 'ISA.23.8', 'Who has planned this against Tyre, the giver of crowns, whose merchants are princes, whose traders are the honorable of the earth?'),
('ISA', 23, 9, 'ISA.23.9', 'The LORD of Armies has planned it, to stain the pride of all glory, to bring into contempt all the honorable of the earth.'),
('ISA', 23, 10, 'ISA.23.10', 'Pass through your land like the Nile, daughter of Tarshish. There is no restraint any more.'),
('ISA', 23, 11, 'ISA.23.11', 'He has stretched out his hand over the sea. He has shaken the kingdoms. The LORD has ordered the destruction of Canaan’s strongholds.'),
('ISA', 23, 12, 'ISA.23.12', 'He said, “You shall rejoice no more, you oppressed virgin daughter of Sidon. Arise, pass over to Kittim. Even there you will have no rest.”'),
('ISA', 23, 13, 'ISA.23.13', 'Behold, the land of the Chaldeans. This people didn’t exist. The Assyrians founded it for those who dwell in the wilderness. They set up their towers. They overthrew its palaces. They made it a ruin.'),
('ISA', 23, 14, 'ISA.23.14', 'Howl, you ships of Tarshish, for your stronghold is laid waste!'),
('ISA', 23, 15, 'ISA.23.15', 'It will come to pass in that day that Tyre will be forgotten seventy years, according to the days of one king. After the end of seventy years it will be to Tyre like in the song of the prostitute.'),
('ISA', 23, 16, 'ISA.23.16', 'Take a harp; go about the city, you prostitute that has been forgotten. Make sweet melody. Sing many songs, that you may be remembered.'),
('ISA', 23, 17, 'ISA.23.17', 'It will happen after the end of seventy years that the LORD will visit Tyre. She will return to her wages, and will play the prostitute with all the kingdoms of the world on the surface of the earth.'),
('ISA', 23, 18, 'ISA.23.18', 'Her merchandise and her wages will be holiness to the LORD. It will not be treasured nor laid up; for her merchandise will be for those who dwell before the LORD, to eat sufficiently, and for durable clothing.'),
('ISA', 24, 1, 'ISA.24.1', 'Behold, the LORD makes the earth empty, makes it waste, turns it upside down, and scatters its inhabitants.'),
('ISA', 24, 2, 'ISA.24.2', 'It will be as with the people, so with the priest; as with the servant, so with his master; as with the maid, so with her mistress; as with the buyer, so with the seller; as with the creditor, so with the debtor; as with the taker of interest, so with the giver of interest.'),
('ISA', 24, 3, 'ISA.24.3', 'The earth will be utterly emptied and utterly laid waste; for the LORD has spoken this word.'),
('ISA', 24, 4, 'ISA.24.4', 'The earth mourns and fades away. The world languishes and fades away. The lofty people of the earth languish.'),
('ISA', 24, 5, 'ISA.24.5', 'The earth also is polluted under its inhabitants, because they have transgressed the laws, violated the statutes, and broken the everlasting covenant.'),
('ISA', 24, 6, 'ISA.24.6', 'Therefore the curse has devoured the earth, and those who dwell therein are found guilty. Therefore the inhabitants of the earth are burned, and few men are left.'),
('ISA', 24, 7, 'ISA.24.7', 'The new wine mourns. The vine languishes. All the merry-hearted sigh.'),
('ISA', 24, 8, 'ISA.24.8', 'The mirth of tambourines ceases. The sound of those who rejoice ends. The joy of the harp ceases.'),
('ISA', 24, 9, 'ISA.24.9', 'They will not drink wine with a song. Strong drink will be bitter to those who drink it.'),
('ISA', 24, 10, 'ISA.24.10', 'The confused city is broken down. Every house is shut up, that no man may come in.'),
('ISA', 24, 11, 'ISA.24.11', 'There is a crying in the streets because of the wine. All joy is darkened. The mirth of the land is gone.'),
('ISA', 24, 12, 'ISA.24.12', 'The city is left in desolation, and the gate is struck with destruction.'),
('ISA', 24, 13, 'ISA.24.13', 'For it will be so within the earth among the peoples, as the shaking of an olive tree, as the gleanings when the vintage is done.'),
('ISA', 24, 14, 'ISA.24.14', 'These shall lift up their voice. They will shout for the majesty of the LORD. They cry aloud from the sea.'),
('ISA', 24, 15, 'ISA.24.15', 'Therefore glorify the LORD in the east, even the name of the LORD, the God of Israel, in the islands of the sea!'),
('ISA', 24, 16, 'ISA.24.16', 'From the uttermost part of the earth have we heard songs. Glory to the righteous! But I said, “I pine away! I pine away! woe is me!” The treacherous have dealt treacherously. Yes, the treacherous have dealt very treacherously.'),
('ISA', 24, 17, 'ISA.24.17', 'Fear, the pit, and the snare are on you who inhabit the earth.'),
('ISA', 24, 18, 'ISA.24.18', 'It will happen that he who flees from the noise of the fear will fall into the pit; and he who comes up out of the middle of the pit will be taken in the snare; for the windows on high are opened, and the foundations of the earth tremble.'),
('ISA', 24, 19, 'ISA.24.19', 'The earth is utterly broken. The earth is torn apart. The earth is shaken violently.'),
('ISA', 24, 20, 'ISA.24.20', 'The earth will stagger like a drunken man, and will sway back and forth like a hammock. Its disobedience will be heavy on it, and it will fall and not rise again.'),
('ISA', 24, 21, 'ISA.24.21', 'It will happen in that day that the LORD will punish the army of the high ones on high, and the kings of the earth on the earth.'),
('ISA', 24, 22, 'ISA.24.22', 'They will be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and will be shut up in the prison; and after many days they will be visited.'),
('ISA', 24, 23, 'ISA.24.23', 'Then the moon will be confounded, and the sun ashamed; for the LORD of Armies will reign on Mount Zion and in Jerusalem; and glory will be before his elders.'),
('ISA', 25, 1, 'ISA.25.1', 'The LORD, you are my God. I will exalt you! I will praise your name, for you have done wonderful things, things planned long ago, in complete faithfulness and truth.'),
('ISA', 25, 2, 'ISA.25.2', 'For you have made a city into a heap, a fortified city into a ruin, a palace of strangers to be no city. It will never be built.'),
('ISA', 25, 3, 'ISA.25.3', 'Therefore a strong people will glorify you. A city of awesome nations will fear you.'),
('ISA', 25, 4, 'ISA.25.4', 'For you have been a stronghold to the poor, a stronghold to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm, a shade from the heat, when the blast of the dreaded ones is like a storm against the wall.'),
('ISA', 25, 5, 'ISA.25.5', 'As the heat in a dry place you will bring down the noise of strangers; as the heat by the shade of a cloud, the song of the dreaded ones will be brought low.'),
('ISA', 25, 6, 'ISA.25.6', 'In this mountain, the LORD of Armies will make all peoples a feast of choice meat, a feast of choice wines, of choice meat full of marrow, of well refined choice wines.'),
('ISA', 25, 7, 'ISA.25.7', 'He will destroy in this mountain the surface of the covering that covers all peoples, and the veil that is spread over all nations.'),
('ISA', 25, 8, 'ISA.25.8', 'He has swallowed up death forever! The Lord GOD will wipe away tears from off all faces. He will take the reproach of his people away from off all the earth, for the LORD has spoken it.'),
('ISA', 25, 9, 'ISA.25.9', 'It shall be said in that day, “Behold, this is our God! We have waited for him, and he will save us! This is the LORD! We have waited for him. We will be glad and rejoice in his salvation!”'),
('ISA', 25, 10, 'ISA.25.10', 'For the LORD’s hand will rest in this mountain. Moab will be trodden down in his place, even like straw is trodden down in the water of the dunghill.'),
('ISA', 25, 11, 'ISA.25.11', 'He will spread out his hands in the middle of it, like one who swims spreads out hands to swim, but his pride will be humbled together with the craft of his hands.'),
('ISA', 25, 12, 'ISA.25.12', 'He has brought the high fortress of your walls down, laid low, and brought to the ground, even to the dust.'),
('ISA', 26, 1, 'ISA.26.1', 'In that day, this song will be sung in the land of Judah: “We have a strong city. God appoints salvation for walls and bulwarks.'),
('ISA', 26, 2, 'ISA.26.2', 'Open the gates, that the righteous nation may enter: the one which keeps faith.'),
('ISA', 26, 3, 'ISA.26.3', 'You will keep whoever’s mind is steadfast in perfect peace, because he trusts in you.'),
('ISA', 26, 4, 'ISA.26.4', 'Trust in the LORD forever; for in the LORD, the LORD, is an everlasting Rock.'),
('ISA', 26, 5, 'ISA.26.5', 'For he has brought down those who dwell on high, the lofty city. He lays it low. He lays it low even to the ground. He brings it even to the dust.'),
('ISA', 26, 6, 'ISA.26.6', 'The foot shall tread it down, even the feet of the poor and the steps of the needy.”'),
('ISA', 26, 7, 'ISA.26.7', 'The way of the just is uprightness. You who are upright make the path of the righteous level.'),
('ISA', 26, 8, 'ISA.26.8', 'Yes, in the way of your judgments, LORD, we have waited for you. Your name and your renown are the desire of our soul.'),
('ISA', 26, 9, 'ISA.26.9', 'With my soul I have desired you in the night. Yes, with my spirit within me I will seek you earnestly; for when your judgments are on the earth, the inhabitants of the world learn righteousness.'),
('ISA', 26, 10, 'ISA.26.10', 'Let favor be shown to the wicked, yet he will not learn righteousness. In the land of uprightness he will deal wrongfully, and will not see the LORD’s majesty.'),
('ISA', 26, 11, 'ISA.26.11', 'LORD, your hand is lifted up, yet they don’t see; but they will see your zeal for the people and be disappointed. Yes, fire will consume your adversaries.'),
('ISA', 26, 12, 'ISA.26.12', 'LORD, you will ordain peace for us, for you have also done all our work for us.'),
('ISA', 26, 13, 'ISA.26.13', 'LORD our God, other lords besides you have had dominion over us, but we will only acknowledge your name.'),
('ISA', 26, 14, 'ISA.26.14', 'The dead shall not live. The departed spirits shall not rise. Therefore you have visited and destroyed them, and caused all memory of them to perish.'),
('ISA', 26, 15, 'ISA.26.15', 'You have increased the nation, O LORD. You have increased the nation! You are glorified! You have enlarged all the borders of the land.'),
('ISA', 26, 16, 'ISA.26.16', 'LORD, in trouble they have visited you. They poured out a prayer when your chastening was on them.'),
('ISA', 26, 17, 'ISA.26.17', 'Just as a woman with child, who draws near the time of her delivery, is in pain and cries out in her pangs, so we have been before you, LORD.'),
('ISA', 26, 18, 'ISA.26.18', 'We have been with child. We have been in pain. We gave birth, it seems, only to wind. We have not worked any deliverance on the earth; neither have the inhabitants of the world fallen.'),
('ISA', 26, 19, 'ISA.26.19', 'Your dead shall live. Their dead bodies shall arise. Awake and sing, you who dwell in the dust; for your dew is like the dew of herbs, and the earth will cast out the departed spirits.'),
('ISA', 26, 20, 'ISA.26.20', 'Come, my people, enter into your rooms, and shut your doors behind you. Hide yourself for a little moment, until the indignation is past.'),
('ISA', 26, 21, 'ISA.26.21', 'For, behold, the LORD comes out of his place to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity. The earth also will disclose her blood, and will no longer cover her slain.'),
('ISA', 27, 1, 'ISA.27.1', 'In that day, the LORD with his hard and great and strong sword will punish leviathan, the fleeing serpent, and leviathan, the twisted serpent; and he will kill the dragon that is in the sea.'),
('ISA', 27, 2, 'ISA.27.2', 'In that day, sing to her, “A pleasant vineyard!'),
('ISA', 27, 3, 'ISA.27.3', 'I, the LORD, am its keeper. I will water it every moment. Lest anyone damage it, I will keep it night and day.'),
('ISA', 27, 4, 'ISA.27.4', 'Wrath is not in me, but if I should find briers and thorns, I would do battle! I would march on them and I would burn them together.'),
('ISA', 27, 5, 'ISA.27.5', 'Or else let him take hold of my strength, that he may make peace with me. Let him make peace with me.”'),
('ISA', 27, 6, 'ISA.27.6', 'In days to come, Jacob will take root. Israel will blossom and bud. They will fill the surface of the world with fruit.'),
('ISA', 27, 7, 'ISA.27.7', 'Has he struck them as he struck those who struck them? Or are they killed like those who killed them were killed?'),
('ISA', 27, 8, 'ISA.27.8', 'In measure, when you send them away, you contend with them. He has removed them with his rough blast in the day of the east wind.'),
('ISA', 27, 9, 'ISA.27.9', 'Therefore by this the iniquity of Jacob will be forgiven, and this is all the fruit of taking away his sin: that he makes all the stones of the altar as chalk stones that are beaten in pieces, so that the Asherah poles and the incense altars shall rise no more.'),
('ISA', 27, 10, 'ISA.27.10', 'For the fortified city is solitary, a habitation deserted and forsaken, like the wilderness. The calf will feed there, and there he will lie down, and consume its branches.'),
('ISA', 27, 11, 'ISA.27.11', 'When its boughs are withered, they will be broken off. The women will come and set them on fire, for they are a people of no understanding. Therefore he who made them will not have compassion on them, and he who formed them will show them no favor.'),
('ISA', 27, 12, 'ISA.27.12', 'It will happen in that day that the LORD will thresh from the flowing stream of the Euphrates to the brook of Egypt; and you will be gathered one by one, children of Israel.'),
('ISA', 27, 13, 'ISA.27.13', 'It will happen in that day that a great trumpet will be blown; and those who were ready to perish in the land of Assyria, and those who were outcasts in the land of Egypt, shall come; and they will worship the LORD in the holy mountain at Jerusalem.'),
('ISA', 28, 1, 'ISA.28.1', 'Woe to the crown of pride of the drunkards of Ephraim, and to the fading flower of his glorious beauty, which is on the head of the fertile valley of those who are overcome with wine!'),
('ISA', 28, 2, 'ISA.28.2', 'Behold, the Lord has one who is mighty and strong. Like a storm of hail, a destroying storm, and like a storm of mighty waters overflowing, he will cast them down to the earth with his hand.'),
('ISA', 28, 3, 'ISA.28.3', 'The crown of pride of the drunkards of Ephraim will be trodden under foot.'),
('ISA', 28, 4, 'ISA.28.4', 'The fading flower of his glorious beauty, which is on the head of the fertile valley, shall be like the first-ripe fig before the summer, which someone picks and eats as soon as he sees it.'),
('ISA', 28, 5, 'ISA.28.5', 'In that day, the LORD of Armies will become a crown of glory and a diadem of beauty to the residue of his people,'),
('ISA', 28, 6, 'ISA.28.6', 'and a spirit of justice to him who sits in judgment, and strength to those who turn back the battle at the gate.'),
('ISA', 28, 7, 'ISA.28.7', 'They also reel with wine, and stagger with strong drink. The priest and the prophet reel with strong drink. They are swallowed up by wine. They stagger with strong drink. They err in vision. They stumble in judgment.'),
('ISA', 28, 8, 'ISA.28.8', 'For all tables are completely full of filthy vomit and filthiness.'),
('ISA', 28, 9, 'ISA.28.9', 'Whom will he teach knowledge? To whom will he explain the message? Those who are weaned from the milk, and drawn from the breasts?'),
('ISA', 28, 10, 'ISA.28.10', 'For it is precept on precept, precept on precept; line on line, line on line; here a little, there a little.'),
('ISA', 28, 11, 'ISA.28.11', 'But he will speak to this nation with stammering lips and in another language,'),
('ISA', 28, 12, 'ISA.28.12', 'to whom he said, “This is the resting place. Give rest to the weary,” and “This is the refreshing;” yet they would not hear.'),
('ISA', 28, 13, 'ISA.28.13', 'Therefore the LORD’s word will be to them precept on precept, precept on precept; line on line, line on line; here a little, there a little; that they may go, fall backward, be broken, be snared, and be taken.'),
('ISA', 28, 14, 'ISA.28.14', 'Therefore hear the LORD’s word, you scoffers, that rule this people in Jerusalem:'),
('ISA', 28, 15, 'ISA.28.15', '“Because you have said, ‘We have made a covenant with death, and we are in agreement with Sheol. When the overflowing scourge passes through, it won’t come to us; for we have made lies our refuge, and we have hidden ourselves under falsehood.’”'),
('ISA', 28, 16, 'ISA.28.16', 'Therefore the Lord GOD says, “Behold, I lay in Zion for a foundation a stone, a tried stone, a precious cornerstone of a sure foundation. He who believes shall not act hastily.'),
('ISA', 28, 17, 'ISA.28.17', 'I will make justice the measuring line, and righteousness the plumb line. The hail will sweep away the refuge of lies, and the waters will overflow the hiding place.'),
('ISA', 28, 18, 'ISA.28.18', 'Your covenant with death shall be annulled, and your agreement with Sheol shall not stand. When the overflowing scourge passes through, then you will be trampled down by it.'),
('ISA', 28, 19, 'ISA.28.19', 'As often as it passes through, it will seize you; for morning by morning it will pass through, by day and by night; and it will be nothing but terror to understand the message.”'),
('ISA', 28, 20, 'ISA.28.20', 'For the bed is too short to stretch out on, and the blanket is too narrow to wrap oneself in.'),
('ISA', 28, 21, 'ISA.28.21', 'For the LORD will rise up as on Mount Perazim. He will be angry as in the valley of Gibeon; that he may do his work, his unusual work, and bring to pass his act, his extraordinary act.'),
('ISA', 28, 22, 'ISA.28.22', 'Now therefore don’t be scoffers, lest your bonds be made strong; for I have heard a decree of destruction from the Lord, GOD of Armies, on the whole earth.'),
('ISA', 28, 23, 'ISA.28.23', 'Give ear, and hear my voice! Listen, and hear my speech!'),
('ISA', 28, 24, 'ISA.28.24', 'Does he who plows to sow plow continually? Does he keep turning the soil and breaking the clods?'),
('ISA', 28, 25, 'ISA.28.25', 'When he has leveled its surface, doesn’t he plant the dill, and scatter the cumin seed, and put in the wheat in rows, the barley in the appointed place, and the spelt in its place?'),
('ISA', 28, 26, 'ISA.28.26', 'For his God instructs him in right judgment and teaches him.'),
('ISA', 28, 27, 'ISA.28.27', 'For the dill isn’t threshed with a sharp instrument, neither is a cart wheel turned over the cumin; but the dill is beaten out with a stick, and the cumin with a rod.'),
('ISA', 28, 28, 'ISA.28.28', 'Bread flour must be ground; so he will not always be threshing it. Although he drives the wheel of his threshing cart over it, his horses don’t grind it.'),
('ISA', 28, 29, 'ISA.28.29', 'This also comes out from the LORD of Armies, who is wonderful in counsel, and excellent in wisdom.'),
('ISA', 29, 1, 'ISA.29.1', 'Woe to Ariel! Ariel, the city where David encamped! Add year to year; let the feasts come around;'),
('ISA', 29, 2, 'ISA.29.2', 'then I will distress Ariel, and there will be mourning and lamentation. She shall be to me as an altar hearth.'),
('ISA', 29, 3, 'ISA.29.3', 'I will encamp against you all around you, and will lay siege against you with posted troops. I will raise siege works against you.'),
('ISA', 29, 4, 'ISA.29.4', 'You will be brought down, and will speak out of the ground. Your speech will mumble out of the dust. Your voice will be as of one who has a familiar spirit, out of the ground, and your speech will whisper out of the dust.'),
('ISA', 29, 5, 'ISA.29.5', 'But the multitude of your foes will be like fine dust, and the multitude of the ruthless ones like chaff that blows away. Yes, it will be in an instant, suddenly.'),
('ISA', 29, 6, 'ISA.29.6', 'She will be visited by the LORD of Armies with thunder, with earthquake, with great noise, with whirlwind and storm, and with the flame of a devouring fire.'),
('ISA', 29, 7, 'ISA.29.7', 'The multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel, even all who fight against her and her stronghold, and who distress her, will be like a dream, a vision of the night.'),
('ISA', 29, 8, 'ISA.29.8', 'It will be like when a hungry man dreams, and behold, he eats; but he awakes, and his hunger isn’t satisfied; or like when a thirsty man dreams, and behold, he drinks; but he awakes, and behold, he is faint, and he is still thirsty. The multitude of all the nations that fight against Mount Zion will be like that.'),
('ISA', 29, 9, 'ISA.29.9', 'Pause and wonder! Blind yourselves and be blind! They are drunken, but not with wine; they stagger, but not with strong drink.'),
('ISA', 29, 10, 'ISA.29.10', 'For the LORD has poured out on you a spirit of deep sleep, and has closed your eyes, the prophets; and he has covered your heads, the seers.'),
('ISA', 29, 11, 'ISA.29.11', 'All vision has become to you like the words of a book that is sealed, which men deliver to one who is educated, saying, “Read this, please;” and he says, “I can’t, for it is sealed;”'),
('ISA', 29, 12, 'ISA.29.12', 'and the book is delivered to one who is not educated, saying, “Read this, please;” and he says, “I can’t read.”'),
('ISA', 29, 13, 'ISA.29.13', 'The Lord said, “Because this people draws near with their mouth and honors me with their lips, but they have removed their heart far from me, and their fear of me is a commandment of men which has been taught;'),
('ISA', 29, 14, 'ISA.29.14', 'therefore, behold, I will proceed to do a marvelous work among this people, even a marvelous work and a wonder; and the wisdom of their wise men will perish, and the understanding of their prudent men will be hidden.”'),
('ISA', 29, 15, 'ISA.29.15', 'Woe to those who deeply hide their counsel from the LORD, and whose deeds are in the dark, and who say, “Who sees us?” and “Who knows us?”'),
('ISA', 29, 16, 'ISA.29.16', 'You turn things upside down! Should the potter be thought to be like clay, that the thing made should say about him who made it, “He didn’t make me;” or the thing formed say of him who formed it, “He has no understanding”?'),
('ISA', 29, 17, 'ISA.29.17', 'Isn’t it yet a very little while, and Lebanon will be turned into a fruitful field, and the fruitful field will be regarded as a forest?'),
('ISA', 29, 18, 'ISA.29.18', 'In that day, the deaf will hear the words of the book, and the eyes of the blind will see out of obscurity and out of darkness.'),
('ISA', 29, 19, 'ISA.29.19', 'The humble also will increase their joy in the LORD, and the poor among men will rejoice in the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 29, 20, 'ISA.29.20', 'For the ruthless is brought to nothing, and the scoffer ceases, and all those who are alert to do evil are cut off—'),
('ISA', 29, 21, 'ISA.29.21', 'who cause a person to be indicted by a word, and lay a snare for one who reproves in the gate, and who deprive the innocent of justice with false testimony.'),
('ISA', 29, 22, 'ISA.29.22', 'Therefore the LORD, who redeemed Abraham, says concerning the house of Jacob: “Jacob shall no longer be ashamed, neither shall his face grow pale.'),
('ISA', 29, 23, 'ISA.29.23', 'But when he sees his children, the work of my hands, in the middle of him, they will sanctify my name. Yes, they will sanctify the Holy One of Jacob, and will stand in awe of the God of Israel.'),
('ISA', 29, 24, 'ISA.29.24', 'They also who err in spirit will come to understanding, and those who grumble will receive instruction.”'),
('ISA', 30, 1, 'ISA.30.1', '“Woe to the rebellious children”, says the LORD, “who take counsel, but not from me; and who make an alliance, but not with my Spirit, that they may add sin to sin;'),
('ISA', 30, 2, 'ISA.30.2', 'who set out to go down into Egypt without asking for my advice, to strengthen themselves in the strength of Pharaoh, and to take refuge in the shadow of Egypt!'),
('ISA', 30, 3, 'ISA.30.3', 'Therefore the strength of Pharaoh will be your shame, and the refuge in the shadow of Egypt your confusion.'),
('ISA', 30, 4, 'ISA.30.4', 'For their princes are at Zoan, and their ambassadors have come to Hanes.'),
('ISA', 30, 5, 'ISA.30.5', 'They shall all be ashamed because of a people that can’t profit them, that are not a help nor profit, but a shame, and also a reproach.”'),
('ISA', 30, 6, 'ISA.30.6', 'The burden of the animals of the South. Through the land of trouble and anguish, of the lioness and the lion, the viper and fiery flying serpent, they carry their riches on the shoulders of young donkeys, and their treasures on the humps of camels, to an unprofitable people.'),
('ISA', 30, 7, 'ISA.30.7', 'For Egypt helps in vain, and to no purpose; therefore I have called her Rahab who sits still.'),
('ISA', 30, 8, 'ISA.30.8', 'Now go, write it before them on a tablet, and inscribe it in a book, that it may be for the time to come forever and ever.'),
('ISA', 30, 9, 'ISA.30.9', 'For it is a rebellious people, lying children, children who will not hear the LORD’s law;'),
('ISA', 30, 10, 'ISA.30.10', 'who tell the seers, “Don’t see!” and the prophets, “Don’t prophesy to us right things. Tell us pleasant things. Prophesy deceits.'),
('ISA', 30, 11, 'ISA.30.11', 'Get out of the way. Turn away from the path. Cause the Holy One of Israel to cease from before us.”'),
('ISA', 30, 12, 'ISA.30.12', 'Therefore the Holy One of Israel says, “Because you despise this word, and trust in oppression and perverseness, and rely on it,'),
('ISA', 30, 13, 'ISA.30.13', 'therefore this iniquity shall be to you like a breach ready to fall, swelling out in a high wall, whose breaking comes suddenly in an instant.'),
('ISA', 30, 14, 'ISA.30.14', 'He will break it as a potter’s vessel is broken, breaking it in pieces without sparing, so that there won’t be found among the broken pieces a piece good enough to take fire from the hearth, or to dip up water out of the cistern.”'),
('ISA', 30, 15, 'ISA.30.15', 'For thus said the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel, “You will be saved in returning and rest. Your strength will be in quietness and in confidence.” You refused,'),
('ISA', 30, 16, 'ISA.30.16', 'but you said, “No, for we will flee on horses;” therefore you will flee; and, “We will ride on the swift;” therefore those who pursue you will be swift.'),
('ISA', 30, 17, 'ISA.30.17', 'One thousand will flee at the threat of one. At the threat of five, you will flee until you are left like a beacon on the top of a mountain, and like a banner on a hill.'),
('ISA', 30, 18, 'ISA.30.18', 'Therefore the LORD will wait, that he may be gracious to you; and therefore he will be exalted, that he may have mercy on you, for the LORD is a God of justice. Blessed are all those who wait for him.'),
('ISA', 30, 19, 'ISA.30.19', 'For the people will dwell in Zion at Jerusalem. You will weep no more. He will surely be gracious to you at the voice of your cry. When he hears you, he will answer you.'),
('ISA', 30, 20, 'ISA.30.20', 'Though the Lord may give you the bread of adversity and the water of affliction, yet your teachers won’t be hidden any more, but your eyes will see your teachers;'),
('ISA', 30, 21, 'ISA.30.21', 'and when you turn to the right hand, and when you turn to the left, your ears will hear a voice behind you, saying, “This is the way. Walk in it.”'),
('ISA', 30, 22, 'ISA.30.22', 'You shall defile the overlaying of your engraved images of silver, and the plating of your molten images of gold. You shall cast them away as an unclean thing. You shall tell it, “Go away!”'),
('ISA', 30, 23, 'ISA.30.23', 'He will give the rain for your seed, with which you will sow the ground; and bread of the increase of the ground will be rich and plentiful. In that day, your livestock will feed in large pastures.'),
('ISA', 30, 24, 'ISA.30.24', 'The oxen likewise and the young donkeys that till the ground will eat savory feed, which has been winnowed with the shovel and with the fork.'),
('ISA', 30, 25, 'ISA.30.25', 'There will be brooks and streams of water on every lofty mountain and on every high hill in the day of the great slaughter, when the towers fall.'),
('ISA', 30, 26, 'ISA.30.26', 'Moreover the light of the moon will be like the light of the sun, and the light of the sun will be seven times brighter, like the light of seven days, in the day that the LORD binds up the fracture of his people, and heals the wound they were struck with.'),
('ISA', 30, 27, 'ISA.30.27', 'Behold, the LORD’s name comes from far away, burning with his anger, and in thick rising smoke. His lips are full of indignation. His tongue is as a devouring fire.'),
('ISA', 30, 28, 'ISA.30.28', 'His breath is as an overflowing stream that reaches even to the neck, to sift the nations with the sieve of destruction. A bridle that leads to ruin will be in the jaws of the peoples.'),
('ISA', 30, 29, 'ISA.30.29', 'You will have a song, as in the night when a holy feast is kept, and gladness of heart, as when one goes with a flute to come to the LORD’s mountain, to Israel’s Rock.'),
('ISA', 30, 30, 'ISA.30.30', 'The LORD will cause his glorious voice to be heard, and will show the descent of his arm, with the indignation of his anger and the flame of a devouring fire, with a blast, storm, and hailstones.'),
('ISA', 30, 31, 'ISA.30.31', 'For through the LORD’s voice the Assyrian will be dismayed. He will strike him with his rod.'),
('ISA', 30, 32, 'ISA.30.32', 'Every stroke of the rod of punishment, which the LORD will lay on him, will be with the sound of tambourines and harps. He will fight with them in battles, brandishing weapons.'),
('ISA', 30, 33, 'ISA.30.33', 'For his burning place has long been ready. Yes, it is prepared for the king. He has made its pyre deep and large with fire and much wood. The LORD’s breath, like a stream of sulfur, kindles it.'),
('ISA', 31, 1, 'ISA.31.1', 'Woe to those who go down to Egypt for help, and rely on horses, and trust in chariots because they are many, and in horsemen because they are very strong, but they don’t look to the Holy One of Israel, and they don’t seek the LORD!'),
('ISA', 31, 2, 'ISA.31.2', 'Yet he also is wise, and will bring disaster, and will not call back his words, but will arise against the house of the evildoers, and against the help of those who work iniquity.'),
('ISA', 31, 3, 'ISA.31.3', 'Now the Egyptians are men, and not God; and their horses flesh, and not spirit. When the LORD stretches out his hand, both he who helps shall stumble, and he who is helped shall fall, and they all shall be consumed together.'),
('ISA', 31, 4, 'ISA.31.4', 'For the LORD says to me, “As the lion and the young lion growling over his prey, if a multitude of shepherds is called together against him, will not be dismayed at their voice, nor abase himself for their noise, so the LORD of Armies will come down to fight on Mount Zion and on its heights.'),
('ISA', 31, 5, 'ISA.31.5', 'As birds hovering, so the LORD of Armies will protect Jerusalem. He will protect and deliver it. He will pass over and preserve it.”'),
('ISA', 31, 6, 'ISA.31.6', 'Return to him from whom you have deeply revolted, children of Israel.'),
('ISA', 31, 7, 'ISA.31.7', 'For in that day everyone shall cast away his idols of silver and his idols of gold—sin which your own hands have made for you.'),
('ISA', 31, 8, 'ISA.31.8', '“The Assyrian will fall by the sword, not of man; and the sword, not of mankind, shall devour him. He will flee from the sword, and his young men will become subject to forced labor.'),
('ISA', 31, 9, 'ISA.31.9', 'His rock will pass away by reason of terror, and his princes will be afraid of the banner,” says the LORD, whose fire is in Zion, and his furnace in Jerusalem.'),
('ISA', 32, 1, 'ISA.32.1', 'Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness, and princes shall rule in justice.'),
('ISA', 32, 2, 'ISA.32.2', 'A man shall be as a hiding place from the wind, and a covert from the storm, as streams of water in a dry place, as the shade of a large rock in a weary land.'),
('ISA', 32, 3, 'ISA.32.3', 'The eyes of those who see will not be dim, and the ears of those who hear will listen.'),
('ISA', 32, 4, 'ISA.32.4', 'The heart of the rash will understand knowledge, and the tongue of the stammerers will be ready to speak plainly.'),
('ISA', 32, 5, 'ISA.32.5', 'The fool will no longer be called noble, nor the scoundrel be highly respected.'),
('ISA', 32, 6, 'ISA.32.6', 'For the fool will speak folly, and his heart will work iniquity, to practice profanity, and to utter error against the LORD, to make empty the soul of the hungry, and to cause the drink of the thirsty to fail.'),
('ISA', 32, 7, 'ISA.32.7', 'The ways of the scoundrel are evil. He devises wicked plans to destroy the humble with lying words, even when the needy speaks right.'),
('ISA', 32, 8, 'ISA.32.8', 'But the noble devises noble things, and he will continue in noble things.'),
('ISA', 32, 9, 'ISA.32.9', 'Rise up, you women who are at ease! Hear my voice! You careless daughters, give ear to my speech!'),
('ISA', 32, 10, 'ISA.32.10', 'For days beyond a year you will be troubled, you careless women; for the vintage will fail. The harvest won’t come.'),
('ISA', 32, 11, 'ISA.32.11', 'Tremble, you women who are at ease! Be troubled, you careless ones! Strip yourselves, make yourselves naked, and put sackcloth on your waist.'),
('ISA', 32, 12, 'ISA.32.12', 'Beat your breasts for the pleasant fields, for the fruitful vine.'),
('ISA', 32, 13, 'ISA.32.13', 'Thorns and briers will come up on my people’s land; yes, on all the houses of joy in the joyous city.'),
('ISA', 32, 14, 'ISA.32.14', 'For the palace will be forsaken. The populous city will be deserted. The hill and the watchtower will be for dens forever, a delight for wild donkeys, a pasture of flocks,'),
('ISA', 32, 15, 'ISA.32.15', 'until the Spirit is poured on us from on high, and the wilderness becomes a fruitful field, and the fruitful field is considered a forest.'),
('ISA', 32, 16, 'ISA.32.16', 'Then justice will dwell in the wilderness; and righteousness will remain in the fruitful field.'),
('ISA', 32, 17, 'ISA.32.17', 'The work of righteousness will be peace, and the effect of righteousness, quietness and confidence forever.'),
('ISA', 32, 18, 'ISA.32.18', 'My people will live in a peaceful habitation, in safe dwellings, and in quiet resting places,'),
('ISA', 32, 19, 'ISA.32.19', 'though hail flattens the forest, and the city is leveled completely.'),
('ISA', 32, 20, 'ISA.32.20', 'Blessed are you who sow beside all waters, who send out the feet of the ox and the donkey.'),
('ISA', 33, 1, 'ISA.33.1', 'Woe to you who destroy, but you weren’t destroyed, and who betray, but nobody betrayed you! When you have finished destroying, you will be destroyed; and when you have finished betrayal, you will be betrayed.'),
('ISA', 33, 2, 'ISA.33.2', 'LORD, be gracious to us. We have waited for you. Be our strength every morning, our salvation also in the time of trouble.'),
('ISA', 33, 3, 'ISA.33.3', 'At the noise of the thunder, the peoples have fled. When you lift yourself up, the nations are scattered.'),
('ISA', 33, 4, 'ISA.33.4', 'Your plunder will be gathered as the caterpillar gathers. Men will leap on it as locusts leap.'),
('ISA', 33, 5, 'ISA.33.5', 'The LORD is exalted, for he dwells on high. He has filled Zion with justice and righteousness.'),
('ISA', 33, 6, 'ISA.33.6', 'There will be stability in your times, abundance of salvation, wisdom, and knowledge. The fear of the LORD is your treasure.'),
('ISA', 33, 7, 'ISA.33.7', 'Behold, their valiant ones cry outside; the ambassadors of peace weep bitterly.'),
('ISA', 33, 8, 'ISA.33.8', 'The highways are desolate. The traveling man ceases. The covenant is broken. He has despised the cities. He doesn’t respect man.'),
('ISA', 33, 9, 'ISA.33.9', 'The land mourns and languishes. Lebanon is confounded and withers away. Sharon is like a desert, and Bashan and Carmel are stripped bare.'),
('ISA', 33, 10, 'ISA.33.10', '“Now I will arise,” says the LORD. “Now I will lift myself up. Now I will be exalted.'),
('ISA', 33, 11, 'ISA.33.11', 'You will conceive chaff. You will give birth to stubble. Your breath is a fire that will devour you.'),
('ISA', 33, 12, 'ISA.33.12', 'The peoples will be like the burning of lime, like thorns that are cut down and burned in the fire.'),
('ISA', 33, 13, 'ISA.33.13', 'Hear, you who are far off, what I have done; and, you who are near, acknowledge my might.”'),
('ISA', 33, 14, 'ISA.33.14', 'The sinners in Zion are afraid. Trembling has seized the godless ones. Who among us can live with the devouring fire? Who among us can live with everlasting burning?'),
('ISA', 33, 15, 'ISA.33.15', 'He who walks righteously and speaks blamelessly, he who despises the gain of oppressions, who gestures with his hands, refusing to take a bribe, who stops his ears from hearing of bloodshed, and shuts his eyes from looking at evil—'),
('ISA', 33, 16, 'ISA.33.16', 'he will dwell on high. His place of defense will be the fortress of rocks. His bread will be supplied. His waters will be sure.'),
('ISA', 33, 17, 'ISA.33.17', 'Your eyes will see the king in his beauty. They will see a distant land.'),
('ISA', 33, 18, 'ISA.33.18', 'Your heart will meditate on the terror. Where is he who counted? Where is he who weighed? Where is he who counted the towers?'),
('ISA', 33, 19, 'ISA.33.19', 'You will no longer see the fierce people, a people of a deep speech that you can’t comprehend, with a strange language that you can’t understand.'),
('ISA', 33, 20, 'ISA.33.20', 'Look at Zion, the city of our appointed festivals. Your eyes will see Jerusalem, a quiet habitation, a tent that won’t be removed. Its stakes will never be plucked up, nor will any of its cords be broken.'),
('ISA', 33, 21, 'ISA.33.21', 'But there the LORD will be with us in majesty, a place of wide rivers and streams, in which no galley with oars will go, neither will any gallant ship pass by there.'),
('ISA', 33, 22, 'ISA.33.22', 'For the LORD is our judge. The LORD is our lawgiver. The LORD is our king. He will save us.'),
('ISA', 33, 23, 'ISA.33.23', 'Your rigging is untied. They couldn’t strengthen the foot of their mast. They couldn’t spread the sail. Then the prey of a great plunder was divided. The lame took the prey.'),
('ISA', 33, 24, 'ISA.33.24', 'The inhabitant won’t say, “I am sick.” The people who dwell therein will be forgiven their iniquity.'),
('ISA', 34, 1, 'ISA.34.1', 'Come near, you nations, to hear! Listen, you peoples. Let the earth and all it contains hear, the world, and everything that comes from it.'),
('ISA', 34, 2, 'ISA.34.2', 'For the LORD is enraged against all the nations, and angry with all their armies. He has utterly destroyed them. He has given them over for slaughter.'),
('ISA', 34, 3, 'ISA.34.3', 'Their slain will also be cast out, and the stench of their dead bodies will come up. The mountains will melt in their blood.'),
('ISA', 34, 4, 'ISA.34.4', 'All of the army of the sky will be dissolved. The sky will be rolled up like a scroll, and all its armies will fade away, as a leaf fades from off a vine or a fig tree.'),
('ISA', 34, 5, 'ISA.34.5', 'For my sword has drunk its fill in the sky. Behold, it will come down on Edom, and on the people of my curse, for judgment.'),
('ISA', 34, 6, 'ISA.34.6', 'The LORD’s sword is filled with blood. It is covered with fat, with the blood of lambs and goats, with the fat of the kidneys of rams; for the LORD has a sacrifice in Bozrah, and a great slaughter in the land of Edom.'),
('ISA', 34, 7, 'ISA.34.7', 'The wild oxen will come down with them, and the young bulls with the mighty bulls; and their land will be drunken with blood, and their dust made greasy with fat.'),
('ISA', 34, 8, 'ISA.34.8', 'For the LORD has a day of vengeance, a year of recompense for the cause of Zion.'),
('ISA', 34, 9, 'ISA.34.9', 'Its streams will be turned into pitch, its dust into sulfur, and its land will become burning pitch.'),
('ISA', 34, 10, 'ISA.34.10', 'It won’t be quenched night or day. Its smoke will go up forever. From generation to generation, it will lie waste. No one will pass through it forever and ever.'),
('ISA', 34, 11, 'ISA.34.11', 'But the pelican and the porcupine will possess it. The owl and the raven will dwell in it. He will stretch the line of confusion over it, and the plumb line of emptiness.'),
('ISA', 34, 12, 'ISA.34.12', 'They shall call its nobles to the kingdom, but none shall be there; and all its princes shall be nothing.'),
('ISA', 34, 13, 'ISA.34.13', 'Thorns will come up in its palaces, nettles and thistles in its fortresses; and it will be a habitation of jackals, a court for ostriches.'),
('ISA', 34, 14, 'ISA.34.14', 'The wild animals of the desert will meet with the wolves, and the wild goat will cry to his fellow. Yes, the night creature shall settle there, and shall find herself a place of rest.'),
('ISA', 34, 15, 'ISA.34.15', 'The arrow snake will make her nest there, and lay, hatch, and gather under her shade. Yes, the kites will be gathered there, every one with her mate.'),
('ISA', 34, 16, 'ISA.34.16', 'Search in the book of the LORD, and read: not one of these will be missing. None will lack her mate. For my mouth has commanded, and his Spirit has gathered them.'),
('ISA', 34, 17, 'ISA.34.17', 'He has cast the lot for them, and his hand has divided it to them with a measuring line. They shall possess it forever. From generation to generation they will dwell in it.'),
('ISA', 35, 1, 'ISA.35.1', 'The wilderness and the dry land will be glad. The desert will rejoice and blossom like a rose.'),
('ISA', 35, 2, 'ISA.35.2', 'It will blossom abundantly, and rejoice even with joy and singing. Lebanon’s glory will be given to it, the excellence of Carmel and Sharon. They will see the LORD’s glory, the excellence of our God.'),
('ISA', 35, 3, 'ISA.35.3', 'Strengthen the weak hands, and make the feeble knees firm.'),
('ISA', 35, 4, 'ISA.35.4', 'Tell those who have a fearful heart, “Be strong! Don’t be afraid! Behold, your God will come with vengeance, God’s retribution. He will come and save you.'),
('ISA', 35, 5, 'ISA.35.5', 'Then the eyes of the blind will be opened, and the ears of the deaf will be unstopped.'),
('ISA', 35, 6, 'ISA.35.6', 'Then the lame man will leap like a deer, and the tongue of the mute will sing; for waters will break out in the wilderness, and streams in the desert.'),
('ISA', 35, 7, 'ISA.35.7', 'The burning sand will become a pool, and the thirsty ground springs of water. Grass with reeds and rushes will be in the habitation of jackals, where they lay.'),
('ISA', 35, 8, 'ISA.35.8', 'A highway will be there, a road, and it will be called ‘The Holy Way’. The unclean shall not pass over it, but it will be for those who walk in the Way. Wicked fools shall not go there.'),
('ISA', 35, 9, 'ISA.35.9', 'No lion will be there, nor will any ravenous animal go up on it. They will not be found there; but the redeemed will walk there.'),
('ISA', 35, 10, 'ISA.35.10', 'Then the LORD’s ransomed ones will return, and come with singing to Zion; and everlasting joy will be on their heads. They will obtain gladness and joy, and sorrow and sighing will flee away.”'),
('ISA', 36, 1, 'ISA.36.1', 'Now in the fourteenth year of King Hezekiah, Sennacherib king of Assyria attacked all of the fortified cities of Judah and captured them.'),
('ISA', 36, 2, 'ISA.36.2', 'The king of Assyria sent Rabshakeh from Lachish to Jerusalem to King Hezekiah with a large army. He stood by the aqueduct from the upper pool in the fuller’s field highway.'),
('ISA', 36, 3, 'ISA.36.3', 'Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, the son of Asaph the recorder came out to him.'),
('ISA', 36, 4, 'ISA.36.4', 'Rabshakeh said to them, “Now tell Hezekiah, ‘The great king, the king of Assyria, says, “What confidence is this in which you trust?'),
('ISA', 36, 5, 'ISA.36.5', 'I say that your counsel and strength for the war are only vain words. Now in whom do you trust, that you have rebelled against me?'),
('ISA', 36, 6, 'ISA.36.6', 'Behold, you trust in the staff of this bruised reed, even in Egypt, which if a man leans on it, it will go into his hand and pierce it. So is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all who trust in him.'),
('ISA', 36, 7, 'ISA.36.7', 'But if you tell me, ‘We trust in the LORD our God,’ isn’t that he whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah has taken away, and has said to Judah and to Jerusalem, ‘You shall worship before this altar’?”'),
('ISA', 36, 8, 'ISA.36.8', 'Now therefore, please make a pledge to my master the king of Assyria, and I will give you two thousand horses, if you are able on your part to set riders on them.'),
('ISA', 36, 9, 'ISA.36.9', 'How then can you turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master’s servants, and put your trust in Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?'),
('ISA', 36, 10, 'ISA.36.10', 'Have I come up now without the LORD against this land to destroy it? The LORD said to me, “Go up against this land, and destroy it.”’”'),
('ISA', 36, 11, 'ISA.36.11', 'Then Eliakim, Shebna and Joah said to Rabshakeh, “Please speak to your servants in Aramaic, for we understand it. Don’t speak to us in the Jews’ language in the hearing of the people who are on the wall.”'),
('ISA', 36, 12, 'ISA.36.12', 'But Rabshakeh said, “Has my master sent me only to your master and to you, to speak these words, and not to the men who sit on the wall, who will eat their own dung and drink their own urine with you?”'),
('ISA', 36, 13, 'ISA.36.13', 'Then Rabshakeh stood, and called out with a loud voice in the Jews’ language, and said, “Hear the words of the great king, the king of Assyria!'),
('ISA', 36, 14, 'ISA.36.14', 'The king says, ‘Don’t let Hezekiah deceive you; for he will not be able to deliver you.'),
('ISA', 36, 15, 'ISA.36.15', 'Don’t let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, “The LORD will surely deliver us. This city won’t be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.”’'),
('ISA', 36, 16, 'ISA.36.16', 'Don’t listen to Hezekiah, for the king of Assyria says, ‘Make your peace with me, and come out to me; and each of you eat from his vine, and each one from his fig tree, and each one of you drink the waters of his own cistern;'),
('ISA', 36, 17, 'ISA.36.17', 'until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of grain and new wine, a land of bread and vineyards.'),
('ISA', 36, 18, 'ISA.36.18', 'Beware lest Hezekiah persuade you, saying, “The LORD will deliver us.” Have any of the gods of the nations delivered their lands from the hand of the king of Assyria?'),
('ISA', 36, 19, 'ISA.36.19', 'Where are the gods of Hamath and Arpad? Where are the gods of Sepharvaim? Have they delivered Samaria from my hand?'),
('ISA', 36, 20, 'ISA.36.20', 'Who are they among all the gods of these countries that have delivered their country out of my hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of my hand?’”'),
('ISA', 36, 21, 'ISA.36.21', 'But they remained silent, and said nothing in reply, for the king’s commandment was, “Don’t answer him.”'),
('ISA', 36, 22, 'ISA.36.22', 'Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, the son of Asaph the recorder, came to Hezekiah with their clothes torn, and told him the words of Rabshakeh.'),
('ISA', 37, 1, 'ISA.37.1', 'When King Hezekiah heard it, he tore his clothes, covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the LORD’s house.'),
('ISA', 37, 2, 'ISA.37.2', 'He sent Eliakim, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz.'),
('ISA', 37, 3, 'ISA.37.3', 'They said to him, “Hezekiah says, ‘Today is a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and of rejection; for the children have come to the birth, and there is no strength to give birth.'),
('ISA', 37, 4, 'ISA.37.4', 'It may be the LORD your God will hear the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master has sent to defy the living God, and will rebuke the words which the LORD your God has heard. Therefore lift up your prayer for the remnant that is left.’”'),
('ISA', 37, 5, 'ISA.37.5', 'So the servants of King Hezekiah came to Isaiah.'),
('ISA', 37, 6, 'ISA.37.6', 'Isaiah said to them, “Tell your master, ‘The LORD says, “Don’t be afraid of the words that you have heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me.'),
('ISA', 37, 7, 'ISA.37.7', 'Behold, I will put a spirit in him and he will hear news, and will return to his own land. I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.”’”'),
('ISA', 37, 8, 'ISA.37.8', 'So Rabshakeh returned, and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah, for he heard that he had departed from Lachish.'),
('ISA', 37, 9, 'ISA.37.9', 'He heard news concerning Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, “He has come out to fight against you.” When he heard it, he sent messengers to Hezekiah, saying,'),
('ISA', 37, 10, 'ISA.37.10', '“Thus you shall speak to Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, ‘Don’t let your God in whom you trust deceive you, saying, “Jerusalem won’t be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.”'),
('ISA', 37, 11, 'ISA.37.11', 'Behold, you have heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands, by destroying them utterly. Shall you be delivered?'),
('ISA', 37, 12, 'ISA.37.12', 'Have the gods of the nations delivered them, which my fathers have destroyed, Gozan, Haran, Rezeph, and the children of Eden who were in Telassar?'),
('ISA', 37, 13, 'ISA.37.13', 'Where is the king of Hamath, and the king of Arpad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivvah?’”'),
('ISA', 37, 14, 'ISA.37.14', 'Hezekiah received the letter from the hand of the messengers and read it. Then Hezekiah went up to the LORD’s house, and spread it before the LORD.'),
('ISA', 37, 15, 'ISA.37.15', 'Hezekiah prayed to the LORD, saying,'),
('ISA', 37, 16, 'ISA.37.16', '“LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, who is enthroned among the cherubim, you are the God, even you alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth. You have made heaven and earth.'),
('ISA', 37, 17, 'ISA.37.17', 'Turn your ear, LORD, and hear. Open your eyes, LORD, and behold. Hear all of the words of Sennacherib, who has sent to defy the living God.'),
('ISA', 37, 18, 'ISA.37.18', 'Truly, LORD, the kings of Assyria have destroyed all the countries and their land,'),
('ISA', 37, 19, 'ISA.37.19', 'and have cast their gods into the fire; for they were no gods, but the work of men’s hands, wood and stone; therefore they have destroyed them.'),
('ISA', 37, 20, 'ISA.37.20', 'Now therefore, LORD our God, save us from his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that you are the LORD, even you only.”'),
('ISA', 37, 21, 'ISA.37.21', 'Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to Hezekiah, saying, “The LORD, the God of Israel says, ‘Because you have prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria,'),
('ISA', 37, 22, 'ISA.37.22', 'this is the word which the LORD has spoken concerning him: The virgin daughter of Zion has despised you and ridiculed you. The daughter of Jerusalem has shaken her head at you.'),
('ISA', 37, 23, 'ISA.37.23', 'Whom have you defied and blasphemed? Against whom have you exalted your voice and lifted up your eyes on high? Against the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 37, 24, 'ISA.37.24', 'By your servants, you have defied the Lord, and have said, “With the multitude of my chariots I have come up to the height of the mountains, to the innermost parts of Lebanon. I will cut down its tall cedars and its choice cypress trees. I will enter into its farthest height, the forest of its fruitful field.'),
('ISA', 37, 25, 'ISA.37.25', 'I have dug and drunk water, and with the sole of my feet I will dry up all the rivers of Egypt.”'),
('ISA', 37, 26, 'ISA.37.26', '“‘Have you not heard how I have done it long ago, and formed it in ancient times? Now I have brought it to pass, that it should be yours to destroy fortified cities, turning them into ruinous heaps.'),
('ISA', 37, 27, 'ISA.37.27', 'Therefore their inhabitants had little power. They were dismayed and confounded. They were like the grass of the field, and like the green herb, like the grass on the housetops, and like a field before its crop has grown.'),
('ISA', 37, 28, 'ISA.37.28', 'But I know your sitting down, your going out, your coming in, and your raging against me.'),
('ISA', 37, 29, 'ISA.37.29', 'Because of your raging against me, and because your arrogance has come up into my ears, therefore I will put my hook in your nose and my bridle in your lips, and I will turn you back by the way by which you came.'),
('ISA', 37, 30, 'ISA.37.30', '“‘This shall be the sign to you: You will eat this year that which grows of itself, and in the second year that which springs from it; and in the third year sow and reap and plant vineyards, and eat their fruit.'),
('ISA', 37, 31, 'ISA.37.31', 'The remnant that is escaped of the house of Judah will again take root downward, and bear fruit upward.'),
('ISA', 37, 32, 'ISA.37.32', 'For out of Jerusalem a remnant will go out, and survivors will escape from Mount Zion. The zeal of the LORD of Armies will perform this.’'),
('ISA', 37, 33, 'ISA.37.33', '“Therefore the LORD says concerning the king of Assyria, ‘He will not come to this city, nor shoot an arrow there, neither will he come before it with shield, nor cast up a mound against it.'),
('ISA', 37, 34, 'ISA.37.34', 'He will return the way that he came, and he won’t come to this city,’ says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 37, 35, 'ISA.37.35', '‘For I will defend this city to save it, for my own sake, and for my servant David’s sake.’”'),
('ISA', 37, 36, 'ISA.37.36', 'Then the LORD’s angel went out and struck one hundred and eighty-five thousand men in the camp of the Assyrians. When men arose early in the morning, behold, these were all dead bodies.'),
('ISA', 37, 37, 'ISA.37.37', 'So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, went away, returned to Nineveh, and stayed there.'),
('ISA', 37, 38, 'ISA.37.38', 'As he was worshiping in the house of Nisroch his god, Adrammelech and Sharezer his sons struck him with the sword; and they escaped into the land of Ararat. Esar Haddon his son reigned in his place.'),
('ISA', 38, 1, 'ISA.38.1', 'In those days Hezekiah was sick and near death. Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, came to him, and said to him, “The LORD says, ‘Set your house in order, for you will die, and not live.’”'),
('ISA', 38, 2, 'ISA.38.2', 'Then Hezekiah turned his face to the wall and prayed to the LORD,'),
('ISA', 38, 3, 'ISA.38.3', 'and said, “Remember now, LORD, I beg you, how I have walked before you in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in your sight.” Then Hezekiah wept bitterly.'),
('ISA', 38, 4, 'ISA.38.4', 'Then the LORD’s word came to Isaiah, saying,'),
('ISA', 38, 5, 'ISA.38.5', '“Go, and tell Hezekiah, ‘The LORD, the God of David your father, says, “I have heard your prayer. I have seen your tears. Behold, I will add fifteen years to your life.'),
('ISA', 38, 6, 'ISA.38.6', 'I will deliver you and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria, and I will defend this city.'),
('ISA', 38, 7, 'ISA.38.7', 'This shall be the sign to you from the LORD, that the LORD will do this thing that he has spoken.'),
('ISA', 38, 8, 'ISA.38.8', 'Behold, I will cause the shadow on the sundial, which has gone down on the sundial of Ahaz with the sun, to return backward ten steps.”’” So the sun returned ten steps on the sundial on which it had gone down.'),
('ISA', 38, 9, 'ISA.38.9', 'The writing of Hezekiah king of Judah, when he had been sick, and had recovered of his sickness:'),
('ISA', 38, 10, 'ISA.38.10', 'I said, “In the middle of my life I go into the gates of Sheol. I am deprived of the residue of my years.”'),
('ISA', 38, 11, 'ISA.38.11', 'I said, “I won’t see the LORD, the LORD in the land of the living. I will see man no more with the inhabitants of the world.'),
('ISA', 38, 12, 'ISA.38.12', 'My dwelling is removed, and is carried away from me like a shepherd’s tent. I have rolled up my life like a weaver. He will cut me off from the loom. From day even to night you will make an end of me.'),
('ISA', 38, 13, 'ISA.38.13', 'I waited patiently until morning. He breaks all my bones like a lion. From day even to night you will make an end of me.'),
('ISA', 38, 14, 'ISA.38.14', 'I chattered like a swallow or a crane. I moaned like a dove. My eyes weaken looking upward. Lord, I am oppressed. Be my security.”'),
('ISA', 38, 15, 'ISA.38.15', 'What will I say? He has both spoken to me, and himself has done it. I will walk carefully all my years because of the anguish of my soul.'),
('ISA', 38, 16, 'ISA.38.16', 'Lord, men live by these things; and my spirit finds life in all of them. You restore me, and cause me to live.'),
('ISA', 38, 17, 'ISA.38.17', 'Behold, for peace I had great anguish, but you have in love for my soul delivered it from the pit of corruption; for you have cast all my sins behind your back.'),
('ISA', 38, 18, 'ISA.38.18', 'For Sheol can’t praise you. Death can’t celebrate you. Those who go down into the pit can’t hope for your truth.'),
('ISA', 38, 19, 'ISA.38.19', 'The living, the living, he shall praise you, as I do today. The father shall make known your truth to the children.'),
('ISA', 38, 20, 'ISA.38.20', 'The LORD will save me. Therefore we will sing my songs with stringed instruments all the days of our life in the LORD’s house.'),
('ISA', 38, 21, 'ISA.38.21', 'Now Isaiah had said, “Let them take a cake of figs, and lay it for a poultice on the boil, and he shall recover.”'),
('ISA', 38, 22, 'ISA.38.22', 'Hezekiah also had said, “What is the sign that I will go up to the LORD’s house?”'),
('ISA', 39, 1, 'ISA.39.1', 'At that time, Merodach-baladan the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah, for he heard that he had been sick, and had recovered.'),
('ISA', 39, 2, 'ISA.39.2', 'Hezekiah was pleased with them, and showed them the house of his precious things, the silver, the gold, the spices, and the precious oil, and all the house of his armor, and all that was found in his treasures. There was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah didn’t show them.'),
('ISA', 39, 3, 'ISA.39.3', 'Then Isaiah the prophet came to King Hezekiah, and asked him, “What did these men say? From where did they come to you?” Hezekiah said, “They have come from a country far from me, even from Babylon.”'),
('ISA', 39, 4, 'ISA.39.4', 'Then he asked, “What have they seen in your house?” Hezekiah answered, “They have seen all that is in my house. There is nothing among my treasures that I have not shown them.”'),
('ISA', 39, 5, 'ISA.39.5', 'Then Isaiah said to Hezekiah, “Hear the word of the LORD of Armies:'),
('ISA', 39, 6, 'ISA.39.6', '‘Behold, the days are coming when all that is in your house, and that which your fathers have stored up until today, will be carried to Babylon. Nothing will be left,’ says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 39, 7, 'ISA.39.7', '‘They will take away your sons who will issue from you, whom you shall father, and they will be eunuchs in the king of Babylon’s palace.’”'),
('ISA', 39, 8, 'ISA.39.8', 'Then Hezekiah said to Isaiah, “The LORD’s word which you have spoken is good.” He said moreover, “For there will be peace and truth in my days.”'),
('ISA', 40, 1, 'ISA.40.1', '“Comfort, comfort my people,” says your God.'),
('ISA', 40, 2, 'ISA.40.2', '“Speak comfortably to Jerusalem, and call out to her that her warfare is accomplished, that her iniquity is pardoned, that she has received of the LORD’s hand double for all her sins.”'),
('ISA', 40, 3, 'ISA.40.3', 'The voice of one who calls out, “Prepare the way of the LORD in the wilderness! Make a level highway in the desert for our God.'),
('ISA', 40, 4, 'ISA.40.4', 'Every valley shall be exalted, and every mountain and hill shall be made low. The uneven shall be made level, and the rough places a plain.'),
('ISA', 40, 5, 'ISA.40.5', 'The LORD’s glory shall be revealed, and all flesh shall see it together; for the mouth of the LORD has spoken it.”'),
('ISA', 40, 6, 'ISA.40.6', 'The voice of one saying, “Cry out!” One said, “What shall I cry?” “All flesh is like grass, and all its glory is like the flower of the field.'),
('ISA', 40, 7, 'ISA.40.7', 'The grass withers, the flower fades, because the LORD’s breath blows on it. Surely the people are like grass.'),
('ISA', 40, 8, 'ISA.40.8', 'The grass withers, the flower fades; but the word of our God stands forever.”'),
('ISA', 40, 9, 'ISA.40.9', 'You who tell good news to Zion, go up on a high mountain. You who tell good news to Jerusalem, lift up your voice with strength! Lift it up! Don’t be afraid! Say to the cities of Judah, “Behold, your God!”'),
('ISA', 40, 10, 'ISA.40.10', 'Behold, the Lord GOD will come as a mighty one, and his arm will rule for him. Behold, his reward is with him, and his recompense before him.'),
('ISA', 40, 11, 'ISA.40.11', 'He will feed his flock like a shepherd. He will gather the lambs in his arm, and carry them in his bosom. He will gently lead those who have their young.'),
('ISA', 40, 12, 'ISA.40.12', 'Who has measured the waters in the hollow of his hand, and marked off the sky with his span, and calculated the dust of the earth in a measuring basket, and weighed the mountains in scales, and the hills in a balance?'),
('ISA', 40, 13, 'ISA.40.13', 'Who has directed the LORD’s Spirit, or has taught him as his counselor?'),
('ISA', 40, 14, 'ISA.40.14', 'Who did he take counsel with, and who instructed him, and taught him in the path of justice, and taught him knowledge, and showed him the way of understanding?'),
('ISA', 40, 15, 'ISA.40.15', 'Behold, the nations are like a drop in a bucket, and are regarded as a speck of dust on a balance. Behold, he lifts up the islands like a very little thing.'),
('ISA', 40, 16, 'ISA.40.16', 'Lebanon is not sufficient to burn, nor its animals sufficient for a burnt offering.'),
('ISA', 40, 17, 'ISA.40.17', 'All the nations are like nothing before him. They are regarded by him as less than nothing, and vanity.'),
('ISA', 40, 18, 'ISA.40.18', 'To whom then will you liken God? Or what likeness will you compare to him?'),
('ISA', 40, 19, 'ISA.40.19', 'A workman has cast an image, and the goldsmith overlays it with gold, and casts silver chains for it.'),
('ISA', 40, 20, 'ISA.40.20', 'He who is too impoverished for such an offering chooses a tree that will not rot. He seeks a skillful workman to set up a carved image for him that will not be moved.'),
('ISA', 40, 21, 'ISA.40.21', 'Haven’t you known? Haven’t you heard? Haven’t you been told from the beginning? Haven’t you understood from the foundations of the earth?'),
('ISA', 40, 22, 'ISA.40.22', 'It is he who sits above the circle of the earth, and its inhabitants are like grasshoppers; who stretches out the heavens like a curtain, and spreads them out like a tent to dwell in,'),
('ISA', 40, 23, 'ISA.40.23', 'who brings princes to nothing, who makes the judges of the earth meaningless.'),
('ISA', 40, 24, 'ISA.40.24', 'They are planted scarcely. They are sown scarcely. Their stock has scarcely taken root in the ground. He merely blows on them, and they wither, and the whirlwind takes them away as stubble.'),
('ISA', 40, 25, 'ISA.40.25', '“To whom then will you liken me? Who is my equal?” says the Holy One.'),
('ISA', 40, 26, 'ISA.40.26', 'Lift up your eyes on high, and see who has created these, who brings out their army by number. He calls them all by name. By the greatness of his might, and because he is strong in power, not one is lacking.'),
('ISA', 40, 27, 'ISA.40.27', 'Why do you say, Jacob, and speak, Israel, “My way is hidden from the LORD, and the justice due me is disregarded by my God”?'),
('ISA', 40, 28, 'ISA.40.28', 'Haven’t you known? Haven’t you heard? The everlasting God, the LORD, the Creator of the ends of the earth, doesn’t faint. He isn’t weary. His understanding is unsearchable.'),
('ISA', 40, 29, 'ISA.40.29', 'He gives power to the weak. He increases the strength of him who has no might.'),
('ISA', 40, 30, 'ISA.40.30', 'Even the youths faint and get weary, and the young men utterly fall;'),
('ISA', 40, 31, 'ISA.40.31', 'but those who wait for the LORD will renew their strength. They will mount up with wings like eagles. They will run, and not be weary. They will walk, and not faint.'),
('ISA', 41, 1, 'ISA.41.1', '“Keep silent before me, islands, and let the peoples renew their strength. Let them come near, then let them speak. Let’s meet together for judgment.'),
('ISA', 41, 2, 'ISA.41.2', 'Who has raised up one from the east? Who called him to his feet in righteousness? He hands over nations to him and makes him rule over kings. He gives them like the dust to his sword, like the driven stubble to his bow.'),
('ISA', 41, 3, 'ISA.41.3', 'He pursues them and passes by safely, even by a way that he had not gone with his feet.'),
('ISA', 41, 4, 'ISA.41.4', 'Who has worked and done it, calling the generations from the beginning? I, the LORD, the first, and with the last, I am he.”'),
('ISA', 41, 5, 'ISA.41.5', 'The islands have seen, and fear. The ends of the earth tremble. They approach, and come.'),
('ISA', 41, 6, 'ISA.41.6', 'Everyone helps his neighbor. They say to their brothers, “Be strong!”'),
('ISA', 41, 7, 'ISA.41.7', 'So the carpenter encourages the goldsmith. He who smooths with the hammer encourages him who strikes the anvil, saying of the soldering, “It is good;” and he fastens it with nails, that it might not totter.'),
('ISA', 41, 8, 'ISA.41.8', '“But you, Israel, my servant, Jacob whom I have chosen, the offspring of Abraham my friend,'),
('ISA', 41, 9, 'ISA.41.9', 'you whom I have taken hold of from the ends of the earth, and called from its corners, and said to you, ‘You are my servant. I have chosen you and have not cast you away.’'),
('ISA', 41, 10, 'ISA.41.10', 'Don’t you be afraid, for I am with you. Don’t be dismayed, for I am your God. I will strengthen you. Yes, I will help you. Yes, I will uphold you with the right hand of my righteousness.'),
('ISA', 41, 11, 'ISA.41.11', 'Behold, all those who are incensed against you will be disappointed and confounded. Those who strive with you will be like nothing, and shall perish.'),
('ISA', 41, 12, 'ISA.41.12', 'You will seek them, and won’t find them, even those who contend with you. Those who war against you will be as nothing, as a nonexistent thing.'),
('ISA', 41, 13, 'ISA.41.13', 'For I, the LORD your God, will hold your right hand, saying to you, ‘Don’t be afraid. I will help you.’'),
('ISA', 41, 14, 'ISA.41.14', 'Don’t be afraid, you worm Jacob, and you men of Israel. I will help you,” says the LORD. “Your Redeemer is the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 41, 15, 'ISA.41.15', 'Behold, I have made you into a new sharp threshing instrument with teeth. You will thresh the mountains, and beat them small, and will make the hills like chaff.'),
('ISA', 41, 16, 'ISA.41.16', 'You will winnow them, and the wind will carry them away, and the whirlwind will scatter them. You will rejoice in the LORD. You will glory in the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 41, 17, 'ISA.41.17', 'The poor and needy seek water, and there is none. Their tongue fails for thirst. I, the LORD, will answer them. I, the God of Israel, will not forsake them.'),
('ISA', 41, 18, 'ISA.41.18', 'I will open rivers on the bare heights, and springs in the middle of the valleys. I will make the wilderness a pool of water, and the dry land springs of water.'),
('ISA', 41, 19, 'ISA.41.19', 'I will put cedar, acacia, myrtle, and oil trees in the wilderness. I will set cypress trees, pine, and box trees together in the desert;'),
('ISA', 41, 20, 'ISA.41.20', 'that they may see, know, consider, and understand together, that the LORD’s hand has done this, and the Holy One of Israel has created it.'),
('ISA', 41, 21, 'ISA.41.21', 'Produce your cause,” says the LORD. “Bring out your strong reasons!” says the King of Jacob.'),
('ISA', 41, 22, 'ISA.41.22', '“Let them announce and declare to us what will happen! Declare the former things, what they are, that we may consider them, and know the latter end of them; or show us things to come.'),
('ISA', 41, 23, 'ISA.41.23', 'Declare the things that are to come hereafter, that we may know that you are gods. Yes, do good, or do evil, that we may be dismayed, and see it together.'),
('ISA', 41, 24, 'ISA.41.24', 'Behold, you are nothing, and your work is nothing. He who chooses you is an abomination.'),
('ISA', 41, 25, 'ISA.41.25', '“I have raised up one from the north, and he has come, from the rising of the sun, one who calls on my name, and he shall come on rulers as on mortar, and as the potter treads clay.'),
('ISA', 41, 26, 'ISA.41.26', 'Who has declared it from the beginning, that we may know? and before, that we may say, ‘He is right’? Surely, there is no one who declares. Surely, there is no one who shows. Surely, there is no one who hears your words.'),
('ISA', 41, 27, 'ISA.41.27', 'I am the first to say to Zion, ‘Behold, look at them;’ and I will give one who brings good news to Jerusalem.'),
('ISA', 41, 28, 'ISA.41.28', 'When I look, there is no man, even among them there is no counselor who, when I ask, can answer a word.'),
('ISA', 41, 29, 'ISA.41.29', 'Behold, all of their deeds are vanity and nothing. Their molten images are wind and confusion.'),
('ISA', 42, 1, 'ISA.42.1', '“Behold, my servant, whom I uphold, my chosen, in whom my soul delights: I have put my Spirit on him. He will bring justice to the nations.'),
('ISA', 42, 2, 'ISA.42.2', 'He will not shout, nor raise his voice, nor cause it to be heard in the street.'),
('ISA', 42, 3, 'ISA.42.3', 'He won’t break a bruised reed. He won’t quench a dimly burning wick. He will faithfully bring justice.'),
('ISA', 42, 4, 'ISA.42.4', 'He will not fail nor be discouraged, until he has set justice on the earth, and the islands wait for his law.”'),
('ISA', 42, 5, 'ISA.42.5', 'God the LORD, he who created the heavens and stretched them out, he who spread out the earth and that which comes out of it, he who gives breath to its people and spirit to those who walk in it, says:'),
('ISA', 42, 6, 'ISA.42.6', '“I, the LORD, have called you in righteousness. I will hold your hand. I will keep you, and make you a covenant for the people, as a light for the nations,'),
('ISA', 42, 7, 'ISA.42.7', 'to open the blind eyes, to bring the prisoners out of the dungeon, and those who sit in darkness out of the prison.'),
('ISA', 42, 8, 'ISA.42.8', '“I am the LORD. That is my name. I will not give my glory to another, nor my praise to engraved images.'),
('ISA', 42, 9, 'ISA.42.9', 'Behold, the former things have happened and I declare new things. I tell you about them before they come up.”'),
('ISA', 42, 10, 'ISA.42.10', 'Sing to the LORD a new song, and his praise from the end of the earth, you who go down to the sea, and all that is therein, the islands and their inhabitants.'),
('ISA', 42, 11, 'ISA.42.11', 'Let the wilderness and its cities raise their voices, with the villages that Kedar inhabits. Let the inhabitants of Sela sing. Let them shout from the top of the mountains!'),
('ISA', 42, 12, 'ISA.42.12', 'Let them give glory to the LORD, and declare his praise in the islands.'),
('ISA', 42, 13, 'ISA.42.13', 'The LORD will go out like a mighty man. He will stir up zeal like a man of war. He will raise a war cry. Yes, he will shout aloud. He will triumph over his enemies.'),
('ISA', 42, 14, 'ISA.42.14', '“I have been silent a long time. I have been quiet and restrained myself. Now I will cry out like a travailing woman. I will both gasp and pant.'),
('ISA', 42, 15, 'ISA.42.15', 'I will destroy mountains and hills, and dry up all their herbs. I will make the rivers islands, and will dry up the pools.'),
('ISA', 42, 16, 'ISA.42.16', 'I will bring the blind by a way that they don’t know. I will lead them in paths that they don’t know. I will make darkness light before them, and crooked places straight. I will do these things, and I will not forsake them.'),
('ISA', 42, 17, 'ISA.42.17', '“Those who trust in engraved images, who tell molten images, ‘You are our gods,’ will be turned back. They will be utterly disappointed.'),
('ISA', 42, 18, 'ISA.42.18', '“Hear, you deaf, and look, you blind, that you may see.'),
('ISA', 42, 19, 'ISA.42.19', 'Who is blind, but my servant? Or who is as deaf as my messenger whom I send? Who is as blind as he who is at peace, and as blind as the LORD’s servant?'),
('ISA', 42, 20, 'ISA.42.20', 'You see many things, but don’t observe. His ears are open, but he doesn’t listen.'),
('ISA', 42, 21, 'ISA.42.21', 'It pleased the LORD, for his righteousness’ sake, to magnify the law and make it honorable.'),
('ISA', 42, 22, 'ISA.42.22', 'But this is a robbed and plundered people. All of them are snared in holes, and they are hidden in prisons. They have become captives, and no one delivers, and a plunder, and no one says, ‘Restore them!’'),
('ISA', 42, 23, 'ISA.42.23', 'Who is there among you who will give ear to this? Who will listen and hear for the time to come?'),
('ISA', 42, 24, 'ISA.42.24', 'Who gave Jacob as plunder, and Israel to the robbers? Didn’t the LORD, he against whom we have sinned? For they would not walk in his ways, and they disobeyed his law.'),
('ISA', 42, 25, 'ISA.42.25', 'Therefore he poured the fierceness of his anger on him, and the strength of battle. It set him on fire all around, but he didn’t know. It burned him, but he didn’t take it to heart.”'),
('ISA', 43, 1, 'ISA.43.1', 'But now the LORD who created you, Jacob, and he who formed you, Israel, says: “Don’t be afraid, for I have redeemed you. I have called you by your name. You are mine.'),
('ISA', 43, 2, 'ISA.43.2', 'When you pass through the waters, I will be with you, and through the rivers, they will not overflow you. When you walk through the fire, you will not be burned, and flame will not scorch you.'),
('ISA', 43, 3, 'ISA.43.3', 'For I am the LORD your God, the Holy One of Israel, your Savior. I have given Egypt as your ransom, Ethiopia and Seba in your place.'),
('ISA', 43, 4, 'ISA.43.4', 'Since you have been precious and honored in my sight, and I have loved you, therefore I will give people in your place, and nations instead of your life.'),
('ISA', 43, 5, 'ISA.43.5', 'Don’t be afraid, for I am with you. I will bring your offspring from the east, and gather you from the west.'),
('ISA', 43, 6, 'ISA.43.6', 'I will tell the north, ‘Give them up!’ and tell the south, ‘Don’t hold them back! Bring my sons from far away, and my daughters from the ends of the earth—'),
('ISA', 43, 7, 'ISA.43.7', 'everyone who is called by my name, and whom I have created for my glory, whom I have formed, yes, whom I have made.’”'),
('ISA', 43, 8, 'ISA.43.8', 'Bring out the blind people who have eyes, and the deaf who have ears.'),
('ISA', 43, 9, 'ISA.43.9', 'Let all the nations be gathered together, and let the peoples be assembled. Who among them can declare this, and show us former things? Let them bring their witnesses, that they may be justified, or let them hear, and say, “That is true.”'),
('ISA', 43, 10, 'ISA.43.10', '“You are my witnesses,” says the LORD, “With my servant whom I have chosen; that you may know and believe me, and understand that I am he. Before me there was no God formed, neither will there be after me.'),
('ISA', 43, 11, 'ISA.43.11', 'I myself am the LORD. Besides me, there is no savior.'),
('ISA', 43, 12, 'ISA.43.12', 'I have declared, I have saved, and I have shown, and there was no strange god among you. Therefore you are my witnesses”, says the LORD, “and I am God.'),
('ISA', 43, 13, 'ISA.43.13', 'Yes, since the day was, I am he. There is no one who can deliver out of my hand. I will work, and who can hinder it?”'),
('ISA', 43, 14, 'ISA.43.14', 'The LORD, your Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel says: “For your sake, I have sent to Babylon, and I will bring all of them down as fugitives, even the Chaldeans, in the ships of their rejoicing.'),
('ISA', 43, 15, 'ISA.43.15', 'I am the LORD, your Holy One, the Creator of Israel, your King.”'),
('ISA', 43, 16, 'ISA.43.16', 'The LORD, who makes a way in the sea, and a path in the mighty waters,'),
('ISA', 43, 17, 'ISA.43.17', 'who brings out the chariot and horse, the army and the mighty man (they lie down together, they shall not rise; they are extinct, they are quenched like a wick) says:'),
('ISA', 43, 18, 'ISA.43.18', '“Don’t remember the former things, and don’t consider the things of old.'),
('ISA', 43, 19, 'ISA.43.19', 'Behold, I will do a new thing. It springs out now. Don’t you know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.'),
('ISA', 43, 20, 'ISA.43.20', 'The animals of the field, the jackals and the ostriches, shall honor me, because I give water in the wilderness and rivers in the desert, to give drink to my people, my chosen,'),
('ISA', 43, 21, 'ISA.43.21', 'the people which I formed for myself, that they might declare my praise.'),
('ISA', 43, 22, 'ISA.43.22', 'Yet you have not called on me, Jacob; but you have been weary of me, Israel.'),
('ISA', 43, 23, 'ISA.43.23', 'You have not brought me any of your sheep for burnt offerings, neither have you honored me with your sacrifices. I have not burdened you with offerings, nor wearied you with frankincense.'),
('ISA', 43, 24, 'ISA.43.24', 'You have bought me no sweet cane with money, nor have you filled me with the fat of your sacrifices, but you have burdened me with your sins. You have wearied me with your iniquities.'),
('ISA', 43, 25, 'ISA.43.25', 'I, even I, am he who blots out your transgressions for my own sake; and I will not remember your sins.'),
('ISA', 43, 26, 'ISA.43.26', 'Put me in remembrance. Let us plead together. Declare your case, that you may be justified.'),
('ISA', 43, 27, 'ISA.43.27', 'Your first father sinned, and your teachers have transgressed against me.'),
('ISA', 43, 28, 'ISA.43.28', 'Therefore I will profane the princes of the sanctuary; and I will make Jacob a curse, and Israel an insult.”'),
('ISA', 44, 1, 'ISA.44.1', 'Yet listen now, Jacob my servant, and Israel, whom I have chosen.'),
('ISA', 44, 2, 'ISA.44.2', 'This is what the LORD who made you, and formed you from the womb, who will help you says: “Don’t be afraid, Jacob my servant; and you, Jeshurun, whom I have chosen.'),
('ISA', 44, 3, 'ISA.44.3', 'For I will pour water on him who is thirsty, and streams on the dry ground. I will pour my Spirit on your descendants, and my blessing on your offspring;'),
('ISA', 44, 4, 'ISA.44.4', 'and they will spring up among the grass, as willows by the watercourses.'),
('ISA', 44, 5, 'ISA.44.5', 'One will say, ‘I am the LORD’s.’ Another will be called by the name of Jacob; and another will write with his hand ‘to the LORD,’ and honor the name of Israel.”'),
('ISA', 44, 6, 'ISA.44.6', 'This is what the LORD, the King of Israel, and his Redeemer, the LORD of Armies, says: “I am the first, and I am the last; and besides me there is no God.'),
('ISA', 44, 7, 'ISA.44.7', 'Who is like me? Who will call, and will declare it, and set it in order for me, since I established the ancient people? Let them declare the things that are coming, and that will happen.'),
('ISA', 44, 8, 'ISA.44.8', 'Don’t fear, neither be afraid. Haven’t I declared it to you long ago, and shown it? You are my witnesses. Is there a God besides me? Indeed, there is not. I don’t know any other Rock.”'),
('ISA', 44, 9, 'ISA.44.9', 'Everyone who makes a carved image is vain. The things that they delight in will not profit. Their own witnesses don’t see, nor know, that they may be disappointed.'),
('ISA', 44, 10, 'ISA.44.10', 'Who has fashioned a god, or molds an image that is profitable for nothing?'),
('ISA', 44, 11, 'ISA.44.11', 'Behold, all his fellows will be disappointed; and the workmen are mere men. Let them all be gathered together. Let them stand up. They will fear. They will be put to shame together.'),
('ISA', 44, 12, 'ISA.44.12', 'The blacksmith takes an ax, works in the coals, fashions it with hammers, and works it with his strong arm. He is hungry, and his strength fails; he drinks no water, and is faint.'),
('ISA', 44, 13, 'ISA.44.13', 'The carpenter stretches out a line. He marks it out with a pencil. He shapes it with planes. He marks it out with compasses, and shapes it like the figure of a man, with the beauty of a man, to reside in a house.'),
('ISA', 44, 14, 'ISA.44.14', 'He cuts down cedars for himself, and takes the cypress and the oak, and strengthens for himself one among the trees of the forest. He plants a cypress tree, and the rain nourishes it.'),
('ISA', 44, 15, 'ISA.44.15', 'Then it will be for a man to burn; and he takes some of it and warms himself. Yes, he burns it and bakes bread. Yes, he makes a god and worships it; he makes it a carved image, and falls down to it.'),
('ISA', 44, 16, 'ISA.44.16', 'He burns part of it in the fire. With part of it, he eats meat. He roasts a roast and is satisfied. Yes, he warms himself and says, “Aha! I am warm. I have seen the fire.”'),
('ISA', 44, 17, 'ISA.44.17', 'The rest of it he makes into a god, even his engraved image. He bows down to it and worships, and prays to it, and says, “Deliver me, for you are my god!”'),
('ISA', 44, 18, 'ISA.44.18', 'They don’t know, neither do they consider, for he has shut their eyes, that they can’t see, and their hearts, that they can’t understand.'),
('ISA', 44, 19, 'ISA.44.19', 'No one thinks, neither is there knowledge nor understanding to say, “I have burned part of it in the fire. Yes, I have also baked bread on its coals. I have roasted meat and eaten it. Shall I make the rest of it into an abomination? Shall I bow down to a tree trunk?”'),
('ISA', 44, 20, 'ISA.44.20', 'He feeds on ashes. A deceived heart has turned him aside; and he can’t deliver his soul, nor say, “Isn’t there a lie in my right hand?”'),
('ISA', 44, 21, 'ISA.44.21', 'Remember these things, Jacob and Israel, for you are my servant. I have formed you. You are my servant. Israel, you will not be forgotten by me.'),
('ISA', 44, 22, 'ISA.44.22', 'I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, your transgressions, and, as a cloud, your sins. Return to me, for I have redeemed you.'),
('ISA', 44, 23, 'ISA.44.23', 'Sing, you heavens, for the LORD has done it! Shout, you lower parts of the earth! Break out into singing, you mountains, O forest, all of your trees, for the LORD has redeemed Jacob, and will glorify himself in Israel.'),
('ISA', 44, 24, 'ISA.44.24', 'The LORD, your Redeemer, and he who formed you from the womb says: “I am the LORD, who makes all things; who alone stretches out the heavens; who spreads out the earth by myself;'),
('ISA', 44, 25, 'ISA.44.25', 'who frustrates the signs of the liars, and makes diviners mad; who turns wise men backward, and makes their knowledge foolish;'),
('ISA', 44, 26, 'ISA.44.26', 'who confirms the word of his servant, and performs the counsel of his messengers; who says of Jerusalem, ‘She will be inhabited;’ and of the cities of Judah, ‘They will be built,’ and ‘I will raise up its waste places;’'),
('ISA', 44, 27, 'ISA.44.27', 'who says to the deep, ‘Be dry,’ and ‘I will dry up your rivers,’'),
('ISA', 44, 28, 'ISA.44.28', 'who says of Cyrus, ‘He is my shepherd, and shall perform all my pleasure,’ even saying of Jerusalem, ‘She will be built;’ and of the temple, ‘Your foundation will be laid.’”'),
('ISA', 45, 1, 'ISA.45.1', 'The LORD says to his anointed, to Cyrus, whose right hand I have held to subdue nations before him and strip kings of their armor, to open the doors before him, and the gates shall not be shut:'),
('ISA', 45, 2, 'ISA.45.2', '“I will go before you and make the rough places smooth. I will break the doors of bronze in pieces and cut apart the bars of iron.'),
('ISA', 45, 3, 'ISA.45.3', 'I will give you the treasures of darkness and hidden riches of secret places, that you may know that it is I, the LORD, who calls you by your name, even the God of Israel.'),
('ISA', 45, 4, 'ISA.45.4', 'For Jacob my servant’s sake, and Israel my chosen, I have called you by your name. I have given you a title, though you have not known me.'),
('ISA', 45, 5, 'ISA.45.5', 'I am the LORD, and there is no one else. Besides me, there is no God. I will strengthen you, though you have not known me,'),
('ISA', 45, 6, 'ISA.45.6', 'that they may know from the rising of the sun, and from the west, that there is no one besides me. I am the LORD, and there is no one else.'),
('ISA', 45, 7, 'ISA.45.7', 'I form the light and create darkness. I make peace and create calamity. I am the LORD, who does all these things.'),
('ISA', 45, 8, 'ISA.45.8', 'Rain, you heavens, from above, and let the skies pour down righteousness. Let the earth open, that it may produce salvation, and let it cause righteousness to spring up with it. I, the LORD, have created it.'),
('ISA', 45, 9, 'ISA.45.9', 'Woe to him who strives with his Maker— a clay pot among the clay pots of the earth! Shall the clay ask him who fashions it, ‘What are you making?’ or your work, ‘He has no hands’?'),
('ISA', 45, 10, 'ISA.45.10', 'Woe to him who says to a father, ‘What have you become the father of?’ or to a mother, ‘What have you given birth to?’”'),
('ISA', 45, 11, 'ISA.45.11', 'The LORD, the Holy One of Israel and his Maker says: “You ask me about the things that are to come, concerning my sons, and you command me concerning the work of my hands!'),
('ISA', 45, 12, 'ISA.45.12', 'I have made the earth, and created man on it. I, even my hands, have stretched out the heavens. I have commanded all their army.'),
('ISA', 45, 13, 'ISA.45.13', 'I have raised him up in righteousness, and I will make all his ways straight. He shall build my city, and he shall let my exiles go free, not for price nor reward,” says the LORD of Armies.'),
('ISA', 45, 14, 'ISA.45.14', 'The LORD says: “The labor of Egypt, and the merchandise of Ethiopia, and the Sabeans, men of stature, will come over to you, and they will be yours. They will go after you. They shall come over in chains. They will bow down to you. They will make supplication to you: ‘Surely God is in you; and there is no one else. There is no other god.'),
('ISA', 45, 15, 'ISA.45.15', 'Most certainly you are a God who has hidden yourself, God of Israel, the Savior.’”'),
('ISA', 45, 16, 'ISA.45.16', 'They will be disappointed, yes, confounded, all of them. Those who are makers of idols will go into confusion together.'),
('ISA', 45, 17, 'ISA.45.17', 'Israel will be saved by the LORD with an everlasting salvation. You will not be disappointed nor confounded to ages everlasting.'),
('ISA', 45, 18, 'ISA.45.18', 'For the LORD who created the heavens, the God who formed the earth and made it, who established it and didn’t create it a waste, who formed it to be inhabited says: “I am the LORD. There is no other.'),
('ISA', 45, 19, 'ISA.45.19', 'I have not spoken in secret, in a place of the land of darkness. I didn’t say to the offspring of Jacob, ‘Seek me in vain.’ I, the LORD, speak righteousness. I declare things that are right.'),
('ISA', 45, 20, 'ISA.45.20', '“Assemble yourselves and come. Draw near together, you who have escaped from the nations. Those have no knowledge who carry the wood of their engraved image, and pray to a god that can’t save.'),
('ISA', 45, 21, 'ISA.45.21', 'Declare and present it. Yes, let them take counsel together. Who has shown this from ancient time? Who has declared it of old? Haven’t I, the LORD? There is no other God besides me, a just God and a Savior. There is no one besides me.'),
('ISA', 45, 22, 'ISA.45.22', '“Look to me, and be saved, all the ends of the earth; for I am God, and there is no other.'),
('ISA', 45, 23, 'ISA.45.23', 'I have sworn by myself. The word has gone out of my mouth in righteousness, and will not be revoked, that to me every knee shall bow, every tongue shall take an oath.'),
('ISA', 45, 24, 'ISA.45.24', 'They will say of me, ‘There is righteousness and strength only in the LORD.’” Even to him will men come. All those who raged against him will be disappointed.'),
('ISA', 45, 25, 'ISA.45.25', 'All the offspring of Israel will be justified in the LORD, and will rejoice!'),
('ISA', 46, 1, 'ISA.46.1', 'Bel bows down. Nebo stoops. Their idols are carried by animals, and on the livestock. The things that you carried around are heavy loads, a burden for the weary.'),
('ISA', 46, 2, 'ISA.46.2', 'They stoop and they bow down together. They could not deliver the burden, but they have gone into captivity.'),
('ISA', 46, 3, 'ISA.46.3', '“Listen to me, house of Jacob, and all the remnant of the house of Israel, that have been carried from their birth, that have been carried from the womb.'),
('ISA', 46, 4, 'ISA.46.4', 'Even to old age I am he, and even to gray hairs I will carry you. I have made, and I will bear. Yes, I will carry, and will deliver.'),
('ISA', 46, 5, 'ISA.46.5', '“To whom will you compare me, and consider my equal, and compare me, as if we were the same?'),
('ISA', 46, 6, 'ISA.46.6', 'Some pour out gold from the bag, and weigh silver in the balance. They hire a goldsmith, and he makes it a god. They fall down— yes, they worship.'),
('ISA', 46, 7, 'ISA.46.7', 'They bear it on their shoulder. They carry it, and set it in its place, and it stands there. It cannot move from its place. Yes, one may cry to it, yet it can not answer. It cannot save him out of his trouble.'),
('ISA', 46, 8, 'ISA.46.8', '“Remember this, and show yourselves men. Bring it to mind again, you transgressors.'),
('ISA', 46, 9, 'ISA.46.9', 'Remember the former things of old; for I am God, and there is no other. I am God, and there is none like me.'),
('ISA', 46, 10, 'ISA.46.10', 'I declare the end from the beginning, and from ancient times things that are not yet done. I say: My counsel will stand, and I will do all that I please.'),
('ISA', 46, 11, 'ISA.46.11', 'I call a ravenous bird from the east, the man of my counsel from a far country. Yes, I have spoken. I will also bring it to pass. I have planned. I will also do it.'),
('ISA', 46, 12, 'ISA.46.12', 'Listen to me, you stubborn-hearted, who are far from righteousness!'),
('ISA', 46, 13, 'ISA.46.13', 'I bring my righteousness near. It is not far off, and my salvation will not wait. I will grant salvation to Zion, my glory to Israel.'),
('ISA', 47, 1, 'ISA.47.1', '“Come down and sit in the dust, virgin daughter of Babylon. Sit on the ground without a throne, daughter of the Chaldeans. For you will no longer be called tender and delicate.'),
('ISA', 47, 2, 'ISA.47.2', 'Take the millstones and grind flour. Remove your veil, lift up your skirt, uncover your legs, and wade through the rivers.'),
('ISA', 47, 3, 'ISA.47.3', 'Your nakedness will be uncovered. Yes, your shame will be seen. I will take vengeance, and will spare no one.”'),
('ISA', 47, 4, 'ISA.47.4', 'Our Redeemer, the LORD of Armies is his name, is the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 47, 5, 'ISA.47.5', '“Sit in silence, and go into darkness, daughter of the Chaldeans. For you shall no longer be called the mistress of kingdoms.'),
('ISA', 47, 6, 'ISA.47.6', 'I was angry with my people. I profaned my inheritance and gave them into your hand. You showed them no mercy. You laid a very heavy yoke on the aged.'),
('ISA', 47, 7, 'ISA.47.7', 'You said, ‘I will be a princess forever,’ so that you didn’t lay these things to your heart, nor did you remember the results.'),
('ISA', 47, 8, 'ISA.47.8', '“Now therefore hear this, you who are given to pleasures, who sit securely, who say in your heart, ‘I am, and there is no one else besides me. I won’t sit as a widow, neither will I know the loss of children.’'),
('ISA', 47, 9, 'ISA.47.9', 'But these two things will come to you in a moment in one day: the loss of children and widowhood. They will come on you in their full measure, in the multitude of your sorceries, and the great abundance of your enchantments.'),
('ISA', 47, 10, 'ISA.47.10', 'For you have trusted in your wickedness. You have said, ‘No one sees me.’ Your wisdom and your knowledge has perverted you. You have said in your heart, ‘I am, and there is no one else besides me.’'),
('ISA', 47, 11, 'ISA.47.11', 'Therefore disaster will come on you. You won’t know when it dawns. Mischief will fall on you. You won’t be able to put it away. Desolation will come on you suddenly, which you don’t understand.'),
('ISA', 47, 12, 'ISA.47.12', '“Stand now with your enchantments and with the multitude of your sorceries, in which you have labored from your youth, as if you might profit, as if you might prevail.'),
('ISA', 47, 13, 'ISA.47.13', 'You are wearied in the multitude of your counsels. Now let the astrologers, the stargazers, and the monthly prognosticators stand up and save you from the things that will happen to you.'),
('ISA', 47, 14, 'ISA.47.14', 'Behold, they are like stubble. The fire will burn them. They won’t deliver themselves from the power of the flame. It won’t be a coal to warm at or a fire to sit by.'),
('ISA', 47, 15, 'ISA.47.15', 'The things that you labored in will be like this: those who have trafficked with you from your youth will each wander in his own way. There will be no one to save you.'),
('ISA', 48, 1, 'ISA.48.1', '“Hear this, house of Jacob, you who are called by the name of Israel, and have come out of the waters of Judah. You swear by the LORD’s name, and make mention of the God of Israel, but not in truth, nor in righteousness—'),
('ISA', 48, 2, 'ISA.48.2', 'for they call themselves citizens of the holy city, and rely on the God of Israel; the LORD of Armies is his name.'),
('ISA', 48, 3, 'ISA.48.3', 'I have declared the former things from of old. Yes, they went out of my mouth, and I revealed them. I did them suddenly, and they happened.'),
('ISA', 48, 4, 'ISA.48.4', 'Because I knew that you are obstinate, and your neck is an iron sinew, and your brow bronze;'),
('ISA', 48, 5, 'ISA.48.5', 'therefore I have declared it to you from of old; before it came to pass I showed it to you; lest you should say, ‘My idol has done them. My engraved image and my molten image has commanded them.’'),
('ISA', 48, 6, 'ISA.48.6', 'You have heard it. Now see all this. And you, won’t you declare it? “I have shown you new things from this time, even hidden things, which you have not known.'),
('ISA', 48, 7, 'ISA.48.7', 'They are created now, and not from of old. Before today, you didn’t hear them, lest you should say, ‘Behold, I knew them.’'),
('ISA', 48, 8, 'ISA.48.8', 'Yes, you didn’t hear. Yes, you didn’t know. Yes, from of old your ear was not opened, for I knew that you dealt very treacherously, and were called a transgressor from the womb.'),
('ISA', 48, 9, 'ISA.48.9', 'For my name’s sake, I will defer my anger, and for my praise, I hold it back for you so that I don’t cut you off.'),
('ISA', 48, 10, 'ISA.48.10', 'Behold, I have refined you, but not as silver. I have chosen you in the furnace of affliction.'),
('ISA', 48, 11, 'ISA.48.11', 'For my own sake, for my own sake, I will do it; for how would my name be profaned? I will not give my glory to another.'),
('ISA', 48, 12, 'ISA.48.12', '“Listen to me, O Jacob, and Israel my called: I am he. I am the first. I am also the last.'),
('ISA', 48, 13, 'ISA.48.13', 'Yes, my hand has laid the foundation of the earth, and my right hand has spread out the heavens. When I call to them, they stand up together.'),
('ISA', 48, 14, 'ISA.48.14', '“Assemble yourselves, all of you, and hear! Who among them has declared these things? He whom the LORD loves will do what he likes to Babylon, and his arm will be against the Chaldeans.'),
('ISA', 48, 15, 'ISA.48.15', 'I, even I, have spoken. Yes, I have called him. I have brought him and he shall make his way prosperous.'),
('ISA', 48, 16, 'ISA.48.16', '“Come near to me and hear this: “From the beginning I have not spoken in secret; from the time that it happened, I was there.” Now the Lord GOD has sent me with his Spirit.'),
('ISA', 48, 17, 'ISA.48.17', 'The LORD, your Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel, says: “I am the LORD your God, who teaches you to profit, who leads you by the way that you should go.'),
('ISA', 48, 18, 'ISA.48.18', 'Oh that you had listened to my commandments! Then your peace would have been like a river and your righteousness like the waves of the sea.'),
('ISA', 48, 19, 'ISA.48.19', 'Your offspring also would have been as the sand and the descendants of your body like its grains. His name would not be cut off nor destroyed from before me.”'),
('ISA', 48, 20, 'ISA.48.20', 'Leave Babylon! Flee from the Chaldeans! With the sound of joyful shouting announce this, tell it even to the end of the earth; say, “The LORD has redeemed his servant Jacob!”'),
('ISA', 48, 21, 'ISA.48.21', 'They didn’t thirst when he led them through the deserts. He caused the waters to flow out of the rock for them. He also split the rock and the waters gushed out.'),
('ISA', 48, 22, 'ISA.48.22', '“There is no peace”, says the LORD, “for the wicked.”'),
('ISA', 49, 1, 'ISA.49.1', 'Listen, islands, to me. Listen, you peoples, from afar: the LORD has called me from the womb; from the inside of my mother, he has mentioned my name.'),
('ISA', 49, 2, 'ISA.49.2', 'He has made my mouth like a sharp sword. He has hidden me in the shadow of his hand. He has made me a polished shaft. He has kept me close in his quiver.'),
('ISA', 49, 3, 'ISA.49.3', 'He said to me, “You are my servant, Israel, in whom I will be glorified.”'),
('ISA', 49, 4, 'ISA.49.4', 'But I said, “I have labored in vain. I have spent my strength in vain for nothing; yet surely the justice due to me is with the LORD, and my reward with my God.”'),
('ISA', 49, 5, 'ISA.49.5', 'Now the LORD, he who formed me from the womb to be his servant, says to bring Jacob again to him, and to gather Israel to him, for I am honorable in the LORD’s eyes, and my God has become my strength.'),
('ISA', 49, 6, 'ISA.49.6', 'Indeed, he says, “It is too light a thing that you should be my servant to raise up the tribes of Jacob, and to restore the preserved of Israel. I will also give you as a light to the nations, that you may be my salvation to the end of the earth.”'),
('ISA', 49, 7, 'ISA.49.7', 'The LORD, the Redeemer of Israel, and his Holy One, says to him whom man despises, to him whom the nation abhors, to a servant of rulers: “Kings shall see and rise up, princes, and they shall worship, because of the LORD who is faithful, even the Holy One of Israel, who has chosen you.”'),
('ISA', 49, 8, 'ISA.49.8', 'The LORD says, “I have answered you in an acceptable time. I have helped you in a day of salvation. I will preserve you and give you for a covenant of the people, to raise up the land, to make them inherit the desolate heritage,'),
('ISA', 49, 9, 'ISA.49.9', 'saying to those who are bound, ‘Come out!’; to those who are in darkness, ‘Show yourselves!’ “They shall feed along the paths, and their pasture shall be on all treeless heights.'),
('ISA', 49, 10, 'ISA.49.10', 'They shall not hunger nor thirst; neither shall the heat nor sun strike them, for he who has mercy on them will lead them. He will guide them by springs of water.'),
('ISA', 49, 11, 'ISA.49.11', 'I will make all my mountains a road, and my highways shall be exalted.'),
('ISA', 49, 12, 'ISA.49.12', 'Behold, these shall come from afar, and behold, these from the north and from the west, and these from the land of Sinim.”'),
('ISA', 49, 13, 'ISA.49.13', 'Sing, heavens, and be joyful, earth! Break out into singing, mountains! For the LORD has comforted his people, and will have compassion on his afflicted.'),
('ISA', 49, 14, 'ISA.49.14', 'But Zion said, “The LORD has forsaken me, and the Lord has forgotten me.”'),
('ISA', 49, 15, 'ISA.49.15', '“Can a woman forget her nursing child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? Yes, these may forget, yet I will not forget you!'),
('ISA', 49, 16, 'ISA.49.16', 'Behold, I have engraved you on the palms of my hands. Your walls are continually before me.'),
('ISA', 49, 17, 'ISA.49.17', 'Your children hurry. Your destroyers and those who devastated you will leave you.'),
('ISA', 49, 18, 'ISA.49.18', 'Lift up your eyes all around, and see: all these gather themselves together, and come to you. As I live,” says the LORD, “you shall surely clothe yourself with them all as with an ornament, and dress yourself with them, like a bride.'),
('ISA', 49, 19, 'ISA.49.19', '“For, as for your waste and your desolate places, and your land that has been destroyed, surely now that land will be too small for the inhabitants, and those who swallowed you up will be far away.'),
('ISA', 49, 20, 'ISA.49.20', 'The children of your bereavement will say in your ears, ‘This place is too small for me. Give me a place to live in.’'),
('ISA', 49, 21, 'ISA.49.21', 'Then you will say in your heart, ‘Who has conceived these for me, since I have been bereaved of my children and am alone, an exile, and wandering back and forth? Who has brought these up? Behold, I was left alone. Where were these?’”'),
('ISA', 49, 22, 'ISA.49.22', 'The Lord GOD says, “Behold, I will lift up my hand to the nations, and lift up my banner to the peoples. They shall bring your sons in their bosom, and your daughters shall be carried on their shoulders.'),
('ISA', 49, 23, 'ISA.49.23', 'Kings shall be your foster fathers, and their queens your nursing mothers. They will bow down to you with their faces to the earth, and lick the dust of your feet. Then you will know that I am the LORD; and those who wait for me won’t be disappointed.”'),
('ISA', 49, 24, 'ISA.49.24', 'Shall the plunder be taken from the mighty, or the lawful captives be delivered?'),
('ISA', 49, 25, 'ISA.49.25', 'But the LORD says, “Even the captives of the mighty shall be taken away, and the plunder retrieved from the fierce, for I will contend with him who contends with you and I will save your children.'),
('ISA', 49, 26, 'ISA.49.26', 'I will feed those who oppress you with their own flesh; and they will be drunk on their own blood, as with sweet wine. Then all flesh shall know that I, the LORD, am your Savior and your Redeemer, the Mighty One of Jacob.”'),
('ISA', 50, 1, 'ISA.50.1', 'The LORD says, “Where is the bill of your mother’s divorce, with which I have put her away? Or to which of my creditors have I sold you? Behold, you were sold for your iniquities, and your mother was put away for your transgressions.'),
('ISA', 50, 2, 'ISA.50.2', 'Why, when I came, was there no one? When I called, why was there no one to answer? Is my hand shortened at all, that it can’t redeem? Or have I no power to deliver? Behold, at my rebuke I dry up the sea. I make the rivers a wilderness. Their fish stink because there is no water, and die of thirst.'),
('ISA', 50, 3, 'ISA.50.3', 'I clothe the heavens with blackness. I make sackcloth their covering.”'),
('ISA', 50, 4, 'ISA.50.4', 'The Lord GOD has given me the tongue of those who are taught, that I may know how to sustain with words him who is weary. He awakens morning by morning, he awakens my ear to hear as those who are taught.'),
('ISA', 50, 5, 'ISA.50.5', 'The Lord GOD has opened my ear. I was not rebellious. I have not turned back.'),
('ISA', 50, 6, 'ISA.50.6', 'I gave my back to those who beat me, and my cheeks to those who plucked off the hair. I didn’t hide my face from shame and spitting.'),
('ISA', 50, 7, 'ISA.50.7', 'For the Lord GOD will help me. Therefore I have not been confounded. Therefore I have set my face like a flint, and I know that I won’t be disappointed.'),
('ISA', 50, 8, 'ISA.50.8', 'He who justifies me is near. Who will bring charges against me? Let us stand up together. Who is my adversary? Let him come near to me.'),
('ISA', 50, 9, 'ISA.50.9', 'Behold, the Lord GOD will help me! Who is he who will condemn me? Behold, they will all grow old like a garment. The moths will eat them up.'),
('ISA', 50, 10, 'ISA.50.10', 'Who among you fears the LORD and obeys the voice of his servant? He who walks in darkness and has no light, let him trust in the LORD’s name, and rely on his God.'),
('ISA', 50, 11, 'ISA.50.11', 'Behold, all you who kindle a fire, who adorn yourselves with torches around yourselves, walk in the flame of your fire, and among the torches that you have kindled. You will have this from my hand: you will lie down in sorrow.'),
('ISA', 51, 1, 'ISA.51.1', '“Listen to me, you who follow after righteousness, you who seek the LORD. Look to the rock you were cut from, and to the quarry you were dug from.'),
('ISA', 51, 2, 'ISA.51.2', 'Look to Abraham your father, and to Sarah who bore you; for when he was but one I called him, I blessed him, and made him many.'),
('ISA', 51, 3, 'ISA.51.3', 'For the LORD has comforted Zion. He has comforted all her waste places, and has made her wilderness like Eden, and her desert like the garden of the LORD. Joy and gladness will be found in them, thanksgiving, and the voice of melody.'),
('ISA', 51, 4, 'ISA.51.4', '“Listen to me, my people; and hear me, my nation, for a law will go out from me, and I will establish my justice for a light to the peoples.'),
('ISA', 51, 5, 'ISA.51.5', 'My righteousness is near. My salvation has gone out, and my arms will judge the peoples. The islands will wait for me, and they will trust my arm.'),
('ISA', 51, 6, 'ISA.51.6', 'Lift up your eyes to the heavens, and look at the earth beneath; for the heavens will vanish away like smoke, and the earth will wear out like a garment. Its inhabitants will die in the same way, but my salvation will be forever, and my righteousness will not be abolished.'),
('ISA', 51, 7, 'ISA.51.7', '“Listen to me, you who know righteousness, the people in whose heart is my law. Don’t fear the reproach of men, and don’t be dismayed at their insults.'),
('ISA', 51, 8, 'ISA.51.8', 'For the moth will eat them up like a garment, and the worm will eat them like wool; but my righteousness will be forever, and my salvation to all generations.”'),
('ISA', 51, 9, 'ISA.51.9', 'Awake, awake, put on strength, arm of the LORD! Awake, as in the days of old, the generations of ancient times. Isn’t it you who cut Rahab in pieces, who pierced the monster?'),
('ISA', 51, 10, 'ISA.51.10', 'Isn’t it you who dried up the sea, the waters of the great deep; who made the depths of the sea a way for the redeemed to pass over?'),
('ISA', 51, 11, 'ISA.51.11', 'Those ransomed by the LORD will return, and come with singing to Zion. Everlasting joy shall be on their heads. They will obtain gladness and joy. Sorrow and sighing shall flee away.'),
('ISA', 51, 12, 'ISA.51.12', '“I, even I, am he who comforts you. Who are you, that you are afraid of man who shall die, and of the son of man who will be made as grass?'),
('ISA', 51, 13, 'ISA.51.13', 'Have you forgotten the LORD your Maker, who stretched out the heavens, and laid the foundations of the earth? Do you live in fear continually all day because of the fury of the oppressor, when he prepares to destroy? Where is the fury of the oppressor?'),
('ISA', 51, 14, 'ISA.51.14', 'The captive exile will speedily be freed. He will not die and go down into the pit. His bread won’t fail.'),
('ISA', 51, 15, 'ISA.51.15', 'For I am the LORD your God, who stirs up the sea so that its waves roar. the LORD of Armies is his name.'),
('ISA', 51, 16, 'ISA.51.16', 'I have put my words in your mouth and have covered you in the shadow of my hand, that I may plant the heavens, and lay the foundations of the earth, and tell Zion, ‘You are my people.’”'),
('ISA', 51, 17, 'ISA.51.17', 'Awake, awake! Stand up, Jerusalem, you who have drunk from the LORD’s hand the cup of his wrath. You have drunken the bowl of the cup of staggering, and drained it.'),
('ISA', 51, 18, 'ISA.51.18', 'There is no one to guide her among all the sons to whom she has given birth; and there is no one who takes her by the hand among all the sons whom she has brought up.'),
('ISA', 51, 19, 'ISA.51.19', 'These two things have happened to you— who will grieve with you?— desolation and destruction, and famine and the sword. How can I comfort you?'),
('ISA', 51, 20, 'ISA.51.20', 'Your sons have fainted. They lie at the head of all the streets, like an antelope in a net. They are full of the LORD’s wrath, the rebuke of your God.'),
('ISA', 51, 21, 'ISA.51.21', 'Therefore now hear this, you afflicted, and drunken, but not with wine:'),
('ISA', 51, 22, 'ISA.51.22', 'Your Lord GOD, your God who pleads the cause of his people, says, “Behold, I have taken out of your hand the cup of staggering, even the bowl of the cup of my wrath. You will not drink it any more.'),
('ISA', 51, 23, 'ISA.51.23', 'I will put it into the hand of those who afflict you, who have said to your soul, ‘Bow down, that we may walk over you;’ and you have laid your back as the ground, like a street to those who walk over.”'),
('ISA', 52, 1, 'ISA.52.1', 'Awake, awake! Put on your strength, Zion. Put on your beautiful garments, Jerusalem, the holy city, for from now on the uncircumcised and the unclean will no more come into you.'),
('ISA', 52, 2, 'ISA.52.2', 'Shake yourself from the dust! Arise, sit up, Jerusalem! Release yourself from the bonds of your neck, captive daughter of Zion!'),
('ISA', 52, 3, 'ISA.52.3', 'For the LORD says, “You were sold for nothing; and you will be redeemed without money.”'),
('ISA', 52, 4, 'ISA.52.4', 'For the Lord GOD says: “My people went down at the first into Egypt to live there; and the Assyrian has oppressed them without cause.'),
('ISA', 52, 5, 'ISA.52.5', '“Now therefore, what do I do here,” says the LORD, “seeing that my people are taken away for nothing? Those who rule over them mock,” says the LORD, “and my name is blasphemed continually all day long.'),
('ISA', 52, 6, 'ISA.52.6', 'Therefore my people shall know my name. Therefore they shall know in that day that I am he who speaks. Behold, it is I.”'),
('ISA', 52, 7, 'ISA.52.7', 'How beautiful on the mountains are the feet of him who brings good news, who publishes peace, who brings good news, who proclaims salvation, who says to Zion, “Your God reigns!”'),
('ISA', 52, 8, 'ISA.52.8', 'Your watchmen lift up their voice. Together they sing; for they shall see eye to eye when the LORD returns to Zion.'),
('ISA', 52, 9, 'ISA.52.9', 'Break out into joy! Sing together, you waste places of Jerusalem; for the LORD has comforted his people. He has redeemed Jerusalem.'),
('ISA', 52, 10, 'ISA.52.10', 'The LORD has made his holy arm bare in the eyes of all the nations. All the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.'),
('ISA', 52, 11, 'ISA.52.11', 'Depart! Depart! Go out from there! Touch no unclean thing! Go out from among her! Cleanse yourselves, you who carry the LORD’s vessels.'),
('ISA', 52, 12, 'ISA.52.12', 'For you shall not go out in haste, neither shall you go by flight; for the LORD will go before you, and the God of Israel will be your rear guard.'),
('ISA', 52, 13, 'ISA.52.13', 'Behold, my servant will deal wisely. He will be exalted and lifted up, and will be very high.'),
('ISA', 52, 14, 'ISA.52.14', 'Just as many were astonished at you— his appearance was marred more than any man, and his form more than the sons of men—'),
('ISA', 52, 15, 'ISA.52.15', 'so he will cleanse many nations. Kings will shut their mouths at him; for they will see that which had not been told them, and they will understand that which they had not heard.'),
('ISA', 53, 1, 'ISA.53.1', 'Who has believed our message? To whom has the LORD’s arm been revealed?'),
('ISA', 53, 2, 'ISA.53.2', 'For he grew up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of dry ground. He has no good looks or majesty. When we see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him.'),
('ISA', 53, 3, 'ISA.53.3', 'He was despised and rejected by men, a man of suffering and acquainted with disease. He was despised as one from whom men hide their face; and we didn’t respect him.'),
('ISA', 53, 4, 'ISA.53.4', 'Surely he has borne our sickness and carried our suffering; yet we considered him plagued, struck by God, and afflicted.'),
('ISA', 53, 5, 'ISA.53.5', 'But he was pierced for our transgressions. He was crushed for our iniquities. The punishment that brought our peace was on him; and by his wounds we are healed.'),
('ISA', 53, 6, 'ISA.53.6', 'All we like sheep have gone astray. Everyone has turned to his own way; and the LORD has laid on him the iniquity of us all.'),
('ISA', 53, 7, 'ISA.53.7', 'He was oppressed, yet when he was afflicted he didn’t open his mouth. As a lamb that is led to the slaughter, and as a sheep that before its shearers is silent, so he didn’t open his mouth.'),
('ISA', 53, 8, 'ISA.53.8', 'He was taken away by oppression and judgment. As for his generation, who considered that he was cut off out of the land of the living and stricken for the disobedience of my people?'),
('ISA', 53, 9, 'ISA.53.9', 'They made his grave with the wicked, and with a rich man in his death, although he had done no violence, nor was any deceit in his mouth.'),
('ISA', 53, 10, 'ISA.53.10', 'Yet it pleased the LORD to bruise him. He has caused him to suffer. When you make his soul an offering for sin, he will see his offspring. He will prolong his days and the LORD’s pleasure will prosper in his hand.'),
('ISA', 53, 11, 'ISA.53.11', 'After the suffering of his soul, he will see the light and be satisfied. My righteous servant will justify many by the knowledge of himself; and he will bear their iniquities.'),
('ISA', 53, 12, 'ISA.53.12', 'Therefore I will give him a portion with the great. He will divide the plunder with the strong, because he poured out his soul to death and was counted with the transgressors; yet he bore the sins of many and made intercession for the transgressors.'),
('ISA', 54, 1, 'ISA.54.1', '“Sing, barren, you who didn’t give birth! Break out into singing, and cry aloud, you who didn’t travail with child! For more are the children of the desolate than the children of the married wife,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 54, 2, 'ISA.54.2', '“Enlarge the place of your tent, and let them stretch out the curtains of your habitations; don’t spare; lengthen your cords, and strengthen your stakes.'),
('ISA', 54, 3, 'ISA.54.3', 'For you will spread out on the right hand and on the left; and your offspring will possess the nations and settle in desolate cities.'),
('ISA', 54, 4, 'ISA.54.4', '“Don’t be afraid, for you will not be ashamed. Don’t be confounded, for you will not be disappointed. For you will forget the shame of your youth. You will remember the reproach of your widowhood no more.'),
('ISA', 54, 5, 'ISA.54.5', 'For your Maker is your husband; the LORD of Armies is his name. The Holy One of Israel is your Redeemer. He will be called the God of the whole earth.'),
('ISA', 54, 6, 'ISA.54.6', 'For the LORD has called you as a wife forsaken and grieved in spirit, even a wife of youth, when she is cast off,” says your God.'),
('ISA', 54, 7, 'ISA.54.7', '“For a small moment I have forsaken you, but I will gather you with great mercies.'),
('ISA', 54, 8, 'ISA.54.8', 'In overflowing wrath I hid my face from you for a moment, but with everlasting loving kindness I will have mercy on you,” says the LORD your Redeemer.'),
('ISA', 54, 9, 'ISA.54.9', '“For this is like the waters of Noah to me; for as I have sworn that the waters of Noah will no more go over the earth, so I have sworn that I will not be angry with you, nor rebuke you.'),
('ISA', 54, 10, 'ISA.54.10', 'For the mountains may depart, and the hills be removed, but my loving kindness will not depart from you, and my covenant of peace will not be removed,” says the LORD who has mercy on you.'),
('ISA', 54, 11, 'ISA.54.11', '“You afflicted, tossed with storms, and not comforted, behold, I will set your stones in beautiful colors, and lay your foundations with sapphires.'),
('ISA', 54, 12, 'ISA.54.12', 'I will make your pinnacles of rubies, your gates of sparkling jewels, and all your walls of precious stones.'),
('ISA', 54, 13, 'ISA.54.13', 'All your children will be taught by the LORD, and your children’s peace will be great.'),
('ISA', 54, 14, 'ISA.54.14', 'You will be established in righteousness. You will be far from oppression, for you will not be afraid, and far from terror, for it shall not come near you.'),
('ISA', 54, 15, 'ISA.54.15', 'Behold, they may gather together, but not by me. Whoever gathers together against you will fall because of you.'),
('ISA', 54, 16, 'ISA.54.16', '“Behold, I have created the blacksmith who fans the coals into flame, and forges a weapon for his work; and I have created the destroyer to destroy.'),
('ISA', 54, 17, 'ISA.54.17', 'No weapon that is formed against you will prevail; and you will condemn every tongue that rises against you in judgment. This is the heritage of the LORD’s servants, and their righteousness is of me,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 55, 1, 'ISA.55.1', '“Hey! Come, everyone who thirsts, to the waters! Come, he who has no money, buy, and eat! Yes, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price.'),
('ISA', 55, 2, 'ISA.55.2', 'Why do you spend money for that which is not bread, and your labor for that which doesn’t satisfy? Listen diligently to me, and eat that which is good, and let your soul delight itself in richness.'),
('ISA', 55, 3, 'ISA.55.3', 'Turn your ear, and come to me. Hear, and your soul will live. I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure mercies of David.'),
('ISA', 55, 4, 'ISA.55.4', 'Behold, I have given him for a witness to the peoples, a leader and commander to the peoples.'),
('ISA', 55, 5, 'ISA.55.5', 'Behold, you shall call a nation that you don’t know; and a nation that didn’t know you shall run to you, because of the LORD your God, and for the Holy One of Israel; for he has glorified you.”'),
('ISA', 55, 6, 'ISA.55.6', 'Seek the LORD while he may be found. Call on him while he is near.'),
('ISA', 55, 7, 'ISA.55.7', 'Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts. Let him return to the LORD, and he will have mercy on him, to our God, for he will freely pardon.'),
('ISA', 55, 8, 'ISA.55.8', '“For my thoughts are not your thoughts, and your ways are not my ways,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 55, 9, 'ISA.55.9', '“For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts.'),
('ISA', 55, 10, 'ISA.55.10', 'For as the rain comes down and the snow from the sky, and doesn’t return there, but waters the earth, and makes it grow and bud, and gives seed to the sower and bread to the eater;'),
('ISA', 55, 11, 'ISA.55.11', 'so is my word that goes out of my mouth: it will not return to me void, but it will accomplish that which I please, and it will prosper in the thing I sent it to do.'),
('ISA', 55, 12, 'ISA.55.12', 'For you shall go out with joy, and be led out with peace. The mountains and the hills will break out before you into singing; and all the trees of the fields will clap their hands.'),
('ISA', 55, 13, 'ISA.55.13', 'Instead of the thorn the cypress tree will come up; and instead of the brier the myrtle tree will come up. It will make a name for the LORD, for an everlasting sign that will not be cut off.”'),
('ISA', 56, 1, 'ISA.56.1', 'The LORD says: “Maintain justice and do what is right, for my salvation is near and my righteousness will soon be revealed.'),
('ISA', 56, 2, 'ISA.56.2', 'Blessed is the man who does this, and the son of man who holds it fast; who keeps the Sabbath without profaning it and keeps his hand from doing any evil.”'),
('ISA', 56, 3, 'ISA.56.3', 'Let no foreigner who has joined himself to the LORD speak, saying, “The LORD will surely separate me from his people.” Do not let the eunuch say, “Behold, I am a dry tree.”'),
('ISA', 56, 4, 'ISA.56.4', 'For the LORD says, “To the eunuchs who keep my Sabbaths, choose the things that please me, and hold fast to my covenant,'),
('ISA', 56, 5, 'ISA.56.5', 'I will give them in my house and within my walls a memorial and a name better than of sons and of daughters. I will give them an everlasting name that will not be cut off.'),
('ISA', 56, 6, 'ISA.56.6', 'Also the foreigners who join themselves to the LORD to serve him, and to love the LORD’s name, to be his servants, everyone who keeps the Sabbath from profaning it, and holds fast my covenant,'),
('ISA', 56, 7, 'ISA.56.7', 'I will bring these to my holy mountain, and make them joyful in my house of prayer. Their burnt offerings and their sacrifices will be accepted on my altar; for my house will be called a house of prayer for all peoples.”'),
('ISA', 56, 8, 'ISA.56.8', 'The Lord GOD, who gathers the outcasts of Israel, says, “I will yet gather others to him, in addition to his own who are gathered.”'),
('ISA', 56, 9, 'ISA.56.9', 'All you animals of the field, come to devour, all you animals in the forest.'),
('ISA', 56, 10, 'ISA.56.10', 'His watchmen are blind. They are all without knowledge. They are all mute dogs. They can’t bark— dreaming, lying down, loving to slumber.'),
('ISA', 56, 11, 'ISA.56.11', 'Yes, the dogs are greedy. They can never have enough. They are shepherds who can’t understand. They have all turned to their own way, each one to his gain, from every quarter.'),
('ISA', 56, 12, 'ISA.56.12', '“Come,” they say, “I will get wine, and we will fill ourselves with strong drink; and tomorrow will be as today, great beyond measure.”'),
('ISA', 57, 1, 'ISA.57.1', 'The righteous perish, and no one lays it to heart. Merciful men are taken away, and no one considers that the righteous is taken away from the evil.'),
('ISA', 57, 2, 'ISA.57.2', 'He enters into peace. They rest in their beds, each one who walks in his uprightness.'),
('ISA', 57, 3, 'ISA.57.3', '“But draw near here, you sons of a sorceress, you offspring of adulterers and prostitutes.'),
('ISA', 57, 4, 'ISA.57.4', 'Whom do you mock? Against whom do you make a wide mouth and stick out your tongue? Aren’t you children of disobedience and offspring of falsehood,'),
('ISA', 57, 5, 'ISA.57.5', 'you who inflame yourselves among the oaks, under every green tree; who kill the children in the valleys, under the clefts of the rocks?'),
('ISA', 57, 6, 'ISA.57.6', 'Among the smooth stones of the valley is your portion. They, they are your lot. You have even poured a drink offering to them. You have offered an offering. Shall I be appeased for these things?'),
('ISA', 57, 7, 'ISA.57.7', 'On a high and lofty mountain you have set your bed. You also went up there to offer sacrifice.'),
('ISA', 57, 8, 'ISA.57.8', 'You have set up your memorial behind the doors and the posts, for you have exposed yourself to someone besides me, and have gone up. You have enlarged your bed and made a covenant for yourself with them. You loved what you saw on their bed.'),
('ISA', 57, 9, 'ISA.57.9', 'You went to the king with oil, increased your perfumes, sent your ambassadors far off, and degraded yourself even to Sheol.'),
('ISA', 57, 10, 'ISA.57.10', 'You were wearied with the length of your ways; yet you didn’t say, ‘It is in vain.’ You found a reviving of your strength; therefore you weren’t faint.'),
('ISA', 57, 11, 'ISA.57.11', '“Whom have you dreaded and feared, so that you lie, and have not remembered me, nor laid it to your heart? Haven’t I held my peace for a long time, and you don’t fear me?'),
('ISA', 57, 12, 'ISA.57.12', 'I will declare your righteousness; and as for your works, they will not benefit you.'),
('ISA', 57, 13, 'ISA.57.13', 'When you cry, let those whom you have gathered deliver you, but the wind will take them. A breath will carry them all away, but he who takes refuge in me will possess the land, and will inherit my holy mountain.”'),
('ISA', 57, 14, 'ISA.57.14', 'He will say, “Build up, build up, prepare the way! Remove the stumbling-block out of the way of my people.”'),
('ISA', 57, 15, 'ISA.57.15', 'For the high and lofty One who inhabits eternity, whose name is Holy, says: “I dwell in the high and holy place, with him also who is of a contrite and humble spirit, to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite.'),
('ISA', 57, 16, 'ISA.57.16', 'For I will not contend forever, neither will I always be angry; for the spirit would faint before me, and the souls whom I have made.'),
('ISA', 57, 17, 'ISA.57.17', 'I was angry because of the iniquity of his covetousness and struck him. I hid myself and was angry; and he went on backsliding in the way of his heart.'),
('ISA', 57, 18, 'ISA.57.18', 'I have seen his ways, and will heal him. I will lead him also, and restore comforts to him and to his mourners.'),
('ISA', 57, 19, 'ISA.57.19', 'I create the fruit of the lips: Peace, peace, to him who is far off and to him who is near,” says the LORD; “and I will heal them.”'),
('ISA', 57, 20, 'ISA.57.20', 'But the wicked are like the troubled sea; for it can’t rest and its waters cast up mire and mud.'),
('ISA', 57, 21, 'ISA.57.21', '“There is no peace”, says my God, “for the wicked.”'),
('ISA', 58, 1, 'ISA.58.1', '“Cry aloud! Don’t spare! Lift up your voice like a trumpet! Declare to my people their disobedience, and to the house of Jacob their sins.'),
('ISA', 58, 2, 'ISA.58.2', 'Yet they seek me daily, and delight to know my ways. As a nation that did righteousness, and didn’t forsake the ordinance of their God, they ask of me righteous judgments. They delight to draw near to God.'),
('ISA', 58, 3, 'ISA.58.3', '‘Why have we fasted,’ they say, ‘and you don’t see? Why have we afflicted our soul, and you don’t notice?’ “Behold, in the day of your fast you find pleasure, and oppress all your laborers.'),
('ISA', 58, 4, 'ISA.58.4', 'Behold, you fast for strife and contention, and to strike with the fist of wickedness. You don’t fast today so as to make your voice to be heard on high.'),
('ISA', 58, 5, 'ISA.58.5', 'Is this the fast that I have chosen? A day for a man to humble his soul? Is it to bow down his head like a reed, and to spread sackcloth and ashes under himself? Will you call this a fast, and an acceptable day to the LORD?'),
('ISA', 58, 6, 'ISA.58.6', '“Isn’t this the fast that I have chosen: to release the bonds of wickedness, to undo the straps of the yoke, to let the oppressed go free, and that you break every yoke?'),
('ISA', 58, 7, 'ISA.58.7', 'Isn’t it to distribute your bread to the hungry, and that you bring the poor who are cast out to your house? When you see the naked, that you cover him; and that you not hide yourself from your own flesh?'),
('ISA', 58, 8, 'ISA.58.8', 'Then your light will break out as the morning, and your healing will appear quickly; then your righteousness shall go before you, and the LORD’s glory will be your rear guard.'),
('ISA', 58, 9, 'ISA.58.9', 'Then you will call, and the LORD will answer. You will cry for help, and he will say, ‘Here I am.’ “If you take away from among you the yoke, finger pointing, and speaking wickedly;'),
('ISA', 58, 10, 'ISA.58.10', 'and if you pour out your soul to the hungry, and satisfy the afflicted soul, then your light will rise in darkness, and your obscurity will be as the noonday;'),
('ISA', 58, 11, 'ISA.58.11', 'and the LORD will guide you continually, satisfy your soul in dry places, and make your bones strong. You will be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water whose waters don’t fail.'),
('ISA', 58, 12, 'ISA.58.12', 'Those who will be of you will build the old waste places. You will raise up the foundations of many generations. You will be called Repairer of the Breach, Restorer of Paths with Dwellings.'),
('ISA', 58, 13, 'ISA.58.13', '“If you turn away your foot from the Sabbath, from doing your pleasure on my holy day, and call the Sabbath a delight, and the holy of the LORD honorable, and honor it, not doing your own ways, nor finding your own pleasure, nor speaking your own words,'),
('ISA', 58, 14, 'ISA.58.14', 'then you will delight yourself in the LORD, and I will make you to ride on the high places of the earth, and I will feed you with the heritage of Jacob your father;” for the LORD’s mouth has spoken it.'),
('ISA', 59, 1, 'ISA.59.1', 'Behold, the LORD’s hand is not shortened, that it can’t save; nor his ear dull, that it can’t hear.'),
('ISA', 59, 2, 'ISA.59.2', 'But your iniquities have separated you and your God, and your sins have hidden his face from you, so that he will not hear.'),
('ISA', 59, 3, 'ISA.59.3', 'For your hands are defiled with blood, and your fingers with iniquity. Your lips have spoken lies. Your tongue mutters wickedness.'),
('ISA', 59, 4, 'ISA.59.4', 'No one sues in righteousness, and no one pleads in truth. They trust in vanity and speak lies. They conceive mischief and give birth to iniquity.'),
('ISA', 59, 5, 'ISA.59.5', 'They hatch adders’ eggs and weave the spider’s web. He who eats of their eggs dies; and that which is crushed breaks out into a viper.'),
('ISA', 59, 6, 'ISA.59.6', 'Their webs won’t become garments. They won’t cover themselves with their works. Their works are works of iniquity, and acts of violence are in their hands.'),
('ISA', 59, 7, 'ISA.59.7', 'Their feet run to evil, and they hurry to shed innocent blood. Their thoughts are thoughts of iniquity. Desolation and destruction are in their paths.'),
('ISA', 59, 8, 'ISA.59.8', 'They don’t know the way of peace; and there is no justice in their ways. They have made crooked paths for themselves; whoever goes in them doesn’t know peace.'),
('ISA', 59, 9, 'ISA.59.9', 'Therefore justice is far from us, and righteousness doesn’t overtake us. We look for light, but see darkness; for brightness, but we walk in obscurity.'),
('ISA', 59, 10, 'ISA.59.10', 'We grope for the wall like the blind. Yes, we grope as those who have no eyes. We stumble at noon as if it were twilight. Among those who are strong, we are like dead men.'),
('ISA', 59, 11, 'ISA.59.11', 'We all roar like bears and moan sadly like doves. We look for justice, but there is none, for salvation, but it is far off from us.'),
('ISA', 59, 12, 'ISA.59.12', 'For our transgressions are multiplied before you, and our sins testify against us; for our transgressions are with us, and as for our iniquities, we know them:'),
('ISA', 59, 13, 'ISA.59.13', 'transgressing and denying the LORD, and turning away from following our God, speaking oppression and revolt, conceiving and uttering from the heart words of falsehood.'),
('ISA', 59, 14, 'ISA.59.14', 'Justice is turned away backward, and righteousness stands far away; for truth has fallen in the street, and uprightness can’t enter.'),
('ISA', 59, 15, 'ISA.59.15', 'Yes, truth is lacking; and he who departs from evil makes himself a prey. The LORD saw it, and it displeased him that there was no justice.'),
('ISA', 59, 16, 'ISA.59.16', 'He saw that there was no man, and wondered that there was no intercessor. Therefore his own arm brought salvation to him; and his righteousness sustained him.'),
('ISA', 59, 17, 'ISA.59.17', 'He put on righteousness as a breastplate, and a helmet of salvation on his head. He put on garments of vengeance for clothing, and was clad with zeal as a mantle.'),
('ISA', 59, 18, 'ISA.59.18', 'According to their deeds, he will repay as appropriate: wrath to his adversaries, recompense to his enemies. He will repay the islands their due.'),
('ISA', 59, 19, 'ISA.59.19', 'So they will fear the LORD’s name from the west, and his glory from the rising of the sun; for he will come as a rushing stream, which the LORD’s breath drives.'),
('ISA', 59, 20, 'ISA.59.20', '“A Redeemer will come to Zion, and to those who turn from disobedience in Jacob,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 59, 21, 'ISA.59.21', '“As for me, this is my covenant with them,” says the LORD. “My Spirit who is on you, and my words which I have put in your mouth shall not depart out of your mouth, nor out of the mouth of your offspring, nor out of the mouth of your offspring’s offspring,” says the LORD, “from now on and forever.”'),
('ISA', 60, 1, 'ISA.60.1', '“Arise, shine; for your light has come, and the LORD’s glory has risen on you!'),
('ISA', 60, 2, 'ISA.60.2', 'For behold, darkness will cover the earth, and thick darkness the peoples; but the LORD will arise on you, and his glory shall be seen on you.'),
('ISA', 60, 3, 'ISA.60.3', 'Nations will come to your light, and kings to the brightness of your rising.'),
('ISA', 60, 4, 'ISA.60.4', '“Lift up your eyes all around, and see: they all gather themselves together. They come to you. Your sons will come from far away, and your daughters will be carried in arms.'),
('ISA', 60, 5, 'ISA.60.5', 'Then you shall see and be radiant, and your heart will thrill and be enlarged; because the abundance of the sea will be turned to you. The wealth of the nations will come to you.'),
('ISA', 60, 6, 'ISA.60.6', 'A multitude of camels will cover you, the dromedaries of Midian and Ephah. All from Sheba will come. They will bring gold and frankincense, and will proclaim the praises of the LORD.'),
('ISA', 60, 7, 'ISA.60.7', 'All the flocks of Kedar will be gathered together to you. The rams of Nebaioth will serve you. They will be accepted as offerings on my altar; and I will beautify my glorious house.'),
('ISA', 60, 8, 'ISA.60.8', '“Who are these who fly as a cloud, and as the doves to their windows?'),
('ISA', 60, 9, 'ISA.60.9', 'Surely the islands will wait for me, and the ships of Tarshish first, to bring your sons from far away, their silver and their gold with them, for the name of the LORD your God, and for the Holy One of Israel, because he has glorified you.'),
('ISA', 60, 10, 'ISA.60.10', '“Foreigners will build up your walls, and their kings will serve you; for in my wrath I struck you, but in my favor I have had mercy on you.'),
('ISA', 60, 11, 'ISA.60.11', 'Your gates also shall be open continually; they shall not be shut day nor night, that men may bring to you the wealth of the nations, and their kings led captive.'),
('ISA', 60, 12, 'ISA.60.12', 'For that nation and kingdom that will not serve you shall perish; yes, those nations shall be utterly wasted.'),
('ISA', 60, 13, 'ISA.60.13', '“The glory of Lebanon shall come to you, the cypress tree, the pine, and the box tree together, to beautify the place of my sanctuary; and I will make the place of my feet glorious.'),
('ISA', 60, 14, 'ISA.60.14', 'The sons of those who afflicted you will come bowing to you; and all those who despised you will bow themselves down at the soles of your feet. They will call you the LORD’s City, the Zion of the Holy One of Israel.'),
('ISA', 60, 15, 'ISA.60.15', '“Whereas you have been forsaken and hated, so that no one passed through you, I will make you an eternal excellency, a joy of many generations.'),
('ISA', 60, 16, 'ISA.60.16', 'You will also drink the milk of the nations, and will nurse from royal breasts. Then you will know that I, the LORD, am your Savior, your Redeemer, the Mighty One of Jacob.'),
('ISA', 60, 17, 'ISA.60.17', 'For bronze I will bring gold; for iron I will bring silver; for wood, bronze, and for stones, iron. I will also make peace your governor, and righteousness your ruler.'),
('ISA', 60, 18, 'ISA.60.18', 'Violence shall no more be heard in your land, nor desolation or destruction within your borders; but you will call your walls Salvation, and your gates Praise.'),
('ISA', 60, 19, 'ISA.60.19', 'The sun will be no more your light by day, nor will the brightness of the moon give light to you, but the LORD will be your everlasting light, and your God will be your glory.'),
('ISA', 60, 20, 'ISA.60.20', 'Your sun will not go down any more, nor will your moon withdraw itself; for the LORD will be your everlasting light, and the days of your mourning will end.'),
('ISA', 60, 21, 'ISA.60.21', 'Then your people will all be righteous. They will inherit the land forever, the branch of my planting, the work of my hands, that I may be glorified.'),
('ISA', 60, 22, 'ISA.60.22', 'The little one will become a thousand, and the small one a strong nation. I, the LORD, will do this quickly in its time.”'),
('ISA', 61, 1, 'ISA.61.1', 'The Lord GOD’s Spirit is on me, because the LORD has anointed me to preach good news to the humble. He has sent me to bind up the broken hearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives and release to those who are bound,'),
('ISA', 61, 2, 'ISA.61.2', 'to proclaim the year of the LORD’s favor and the day of vengeance of our God, to comfort all who mourn,'),
('ISA', 61, 3, 'ISA.61.3', 'to provide for those who mourn in Zion, to give to them a garland for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness, that they may be called trees of righteousness, the planting of the LORD, that he may be glorified.'),
('ISA', 61, 4, 'ISA.61.4', 'They will rebuild the old ruins. They will raise up the former devastated places. They will repair the ruined cities that have been devastated for many generations.'),
('ISA', 61, 5, 'ISA.61.5', 'Strangers will stand and feed your flocks. Foreigners will work your fields and your vineyards.'),
('ISA', 61, 6, 'ISA.61.6', 'But you will be called the LORD’s priests. Men will call you the servants of our God. You will eat the wealth of the nations. You will boast in their glory.'),
('ISA', 61, 7, 'ISA.61.7', 'Instead of your shame you will have double. Instead of dishonor, they will rejoice in their portion. Therefore in their land they will possess double. Everlasting joy will be to them.'),
('ISA', 61, 8, 'ISA.61.8', '“For I, the LORD, love justice. I hate robbery and iniquity. I will give them their reward in truth and I will make an everlasting covenant with them.'),
('ISA', 61, 9, 'ISA.61.9', 'Their offspring will be known among the nations, and their offspring among the peoples. All who see them will acknowledge them, that they are the offspring which the LORD has blessed.”'),
('ISA', 61, 10, 'ISA.61.10', 'I will greatly rejoice in the LORD! My soul will be joyful in my God, for he has clothed me with the garments of salvation. He has covered me with the robe of righteousness, as a bridegroom decks himself with a garland and as a bride adorns herself with her jewels.'),
('ISA', 61, 11, 'ISA.61.11', 'For as the earth produces its bud, and as the garden causes the things that are sown in it to spring up, so the Lord GOD will cause righteousness and praise to spring up before all the nations.'),
('ISA', 62, 1, 'ISA.62.1', 'For Zion’s sake I will not hold my peace, and for Jerusalem’s sake I will not rest, until her righteousness shines out like the dawn, and her salvation like a burning lamp.'),
('ISA', 62, 2, 'ISA.62.2', 'The nations will see your righteousness, and all kings your glory. You will be called by a new name, which the LORD’s mouth will name.'),
('ISA', 62, 3, 'ISA.62.3', 'You will also be a crown of beauty in the LORD’s hand, and a royal diadem in your God’s hand.'),
('ISA', 62, 4, 'ISA.62.4', 'You will not be called Forsaken any more, nor will your land be called Desolate any more; but you will be called Hephzibah, and your land Beulah; for the LORD delights in you, and your land will be married.'),
('ISA', 62, 5, 'ISA.62.5', 'For as a young man marries a virgin, so your sons will marry you. As a bridegroom rejoices over his bride, so your God will rejoice over you.'),
('ISA', 62, 6, 'ISA.62.6', 'I have set watchmen on your walls, Jerusalem. They will never be silent day nor night. You who call on the LORD, take no rest,'),
('ISA', 62, 7, 'ISA.62.7', 'and give him no rest until he establishes, and until he makes Jerusalem a praise on the earth.'),
('ISA', 62, 8, 'ISA.62.8', 'The LORD has sworn by his right hand, and by the arm of his strength, “Surely I will no more give your grain to be food for your enemies, and foreigners will not drink your new wine, for which you have labored,'),
('ISA', 62, 9, 'ISA.62.9', 'but those who have harvested it will eat it, and praise the LORD. Those who have gathered it will drink it in the courts of my sanctuary.”'),
('ISA', 62, 10, 'ISA.62.10', 'Go through, go through the gates! Prepare the way of the people! Build up, build up the highway! Gather out the stones! Lift up a banner for the peoples.'),
('ISA', 62, 11, 'ISA.62.11', 'Behold, the LORD has proclaimed to the end of the earth: “Say to the daughter of Zion, ‘Behold, your salvation comes! Behold, his reward is with him, and his recompense before him!’”'),
('ISA', 62, 12, 'ISA.62.12', 'They will call them “The Holy People, The LORD’s Redeemed”. You will be called “Sought Out, A City Not Forsaken”.'),
('ISA', 63, 1, 'ISA.63.1', 'Who is this who comes from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah? Who is this who is glorious in his clothing, marching in the greatness of his strength? “It is I who speak in righteousness, mighty to save.”'),
('ISA', 63, 2, 'ISA.63.2', 'Why is your clothing red, and your garments like him who treads in the wine vat?'),
('ISA', 63, 3, 'ISA.63.3', '“I have trodden the wine press alone. Of the peoples, no one was with me. Yes, I trod them in my anger and trampled them in my wrath. Their lifeblood is sprinkled on my garments, and I have stained all my clothing.'),
('ISA', 63, 4, 'ISA.63.4', 'For the day of vengeance was in my heart, and the year of my redeemed has come.'),
('ISA', 63, 5, 'ISA.63.5', 'I looked, and there was no one to help; and I wondered that there was no one to uphold. Therefore my own arm brought salvation to me. My own wrath upheld me.'),
('ISA', 63, 6, 'ISA.63.6', 'I trod down the peoples in my anger and made them drunk in my wrath. I poured their lifeblood out on the earth.”'),
('ISA', 63, 7, 'ISA.63.7', 'I will tell of the loving kindnesses of the LORD and the praises of the LORD, according to all that the LORD has given to us, and the great goodness toward the house of Israel, which he has given to them according to his mercies, and according to the multitude of his loving kindnesses.'),
('ISA', 63, 8, 'ISA.63.8', 'For he said, “Surely, they are my people, children who will not deal falsely;” so he became their Savior.'),
('ISA', 63, 9, 'ISA.63.9', 'In all their affliction he was afflicted, and the angel of his presence saved them. In his love and in his pity he redeemed them. He bore them, and carried them all the days of old.'),
('ISA', 63, 10, 'ISA.63.10', 'But they rebelled and grieved his Holy Spirit. Therefore he turned and became their enemy, and he himself fought against them.'),
('ISA', 63, 11, 'ISA.63.11', 'Then he remembered the days of old, Moses and his people, saying, “Where is he who brought them up out of the sea with the shepherds of his flock? Where is he who put his Holy Spirit among them?”'),
('ISA', 63, 12, 'ISA.63.12', 'Who caused his glorious arm to be at Moses’ right hand? Who divided the waters before them, to make himself an everlasting name?'),
('ISA', 63, 13, 'ISA.63.13', 'Who led them through the depths, like a horse in the wilderness, so that they didn’t stumble?'),
('ISA', 63, 14, 'ISA.63.14', 'As the livestock that go down into the valley, the LORD’s Spirit caused them to rest. So you led your people to make yourself a glorious name.'),
('ISA', 63, 15, 'ISA.63.15', 'Look down from heaven, and see from the habitation of your holiness and of your glory. Where are your zeal and your mighty acts? The yearning of your heart and your compassion is restrained toward me.'),
('ISA', 63, 16, 'ISA.63.16', 'For you are our Father, though Abraham doesn’t know us, and Israel does not acknowledge us. You, LORD, are our Father. Our Redeemer from everlasting is your name.'),
('ISA', 63, 17, 'ISA.63.17', 'O LORD, why do you make us wander from your ways, and harden our heart from your fear? Return for your servants’ sake, the tribes of your inheritance.'),
('ISA', 63, 18, 'ISA.63.18', 'Your holy people possessed it but a little while. Our adversaries have trodden down your sanctuary.'),
('ISA', 63, 19, 'ISA.63.19', 'We have become like those over whom you never ruled, like those who were not called by your name.'),
('ISA', 64, 1, 'ISA.64.1', 'Oh that you would tear the heavens, that you would come down, that the mountains might quake at your presence—'),
('ISA', 64, 2, 'ISA.64.2', 'as when fire kindles the brushwood, and the fire causes the water to boil. Make your name known to your adversaries, that the nations may tremble at your presence!'),
('ISA', 64, 3, 'ISA.64.3', 'When you did awesome things which we didn’t look for, you came down, and the mountains quaked at your presence.'),
('ISA', 64, 4, 'ISA.64.4', 'For from of old men have not heard, nor perceived by the ear, nor has the eye seen a God besides you, who works for him who waits for him.'),
('ISA', 64, 5, 'ISA.64.5', 'You meet him who rejoices and does righteousness, those who remember you in your ways. Behold, you were angry, and we sinned. We have been in sin for a long time. Shall we be saved?'),
('ISA', 64, 6, 'ISA.64.6', 'For we have all become like one who is unclean, and all our righteousness is like a polluted garment. We all fade like a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, take us away.'),
('ISA', 64, 7, 'ISA.64.7', 'There is no one who calls on your name, who stirs himself up to take hold of you; for you have hidden your face from us, and have consumed us by means of our iniquities.'),
('ISA', 64, 8, 'ISA.64.8', 'But now, LORD, you are our Father. We are the clay and you our potter. We all are the work of your hand.'),
('ISA', 64, 9, 'ISA.64.9', 'Don’t be furious, LORD. Don’t remember iniquity forever. Look and see, we beg you, we are all your people.'),
('ISA', 64, 10, 'ISA.64.10', 'Your holy cities have become a wilderness. Zion has become a wilderness, Jerusalem a desolation.'),
('ISA', 64, 11, 'ISA.64.11', 'Our holy and our beautiful house where our fathers praised you is burned with fire. All our pleasant places are laid waste.'),
('ISA', 64, 12, 'ISA.64.12', 'Will you hold yourself back for these things, LORD? Will you keep silent and punish us very severely?'),
('ISA', 65, 1, 'ISA.65.1', '“I am inquired of by those who didn’t ask. I am found by those who didn’t seek me. I said, ‘See me, see me,’ to a nation that was not called by my name.'),
('ISA', 65, 2, 'ISA.65.2', 'I have spread out my hands all day to a rebellious people, who walk in a way that is not good, after their own thoughts;'),
('ISA', 65, 3, 'ISA.65.3', 'a people who provoke me to my face continually, sacrificing in gardens, and burning incense on bricks;'),
('ISA', 65, 4, 'ISA.65.4', 'who sit among the graves, and spend nights in secret places; who eat pig’s meat, and broth of abominable things is in their vessels;'),
('ISA', 65, 5, 'ISA.65.5', 'who say, ‘Stay by yourself, don’t come near to me, for I am holier than you.’ These are smoke in my nose, a fire that burns all day.'),
('ISA', 65, 6, 'ISA.65.6', '“Behold, it is written before me: I will not keep silence, but will repay, yes, I will repay into their bosom'),
('ISA', 65, 7, 'ISA.65.7', 'your own iniquities and the iniquities of your fathers together”, says the LORD, “who have burned incense on the mountains, and blasphemed me on the hills. Therefore I will first measure their work into their bosom.”'),
('ISA', 65, 8, 'ISA.65.8', 'The LORD says, “As the new wine is found in the cluster, and one says, ‘Don’t destroy it, for a blessing is in it:’ so I will do for my servants’ sake, that I may not destroy them all.'),
('ISA', 65, 9, 'ISA.65.9', 'I will bring offspring out of Jacob, and out of Judah an inheritor of my mountains. My chosen will inherit it, and my servants will dwell there.'),
('ISA', 65, 10, 'ISA.65.10', 'Sharon will be a fold of flocks, and the valley of Achor a place for herds to lie down in, for my people who have sought me.'),
('ISA', 65, 11, 'ISA.65.11', '“But you who forsake the LORD, who forget my holy mountain, who prepare a table for Fortune, and who fill up mixed wine to Destiny;'),
('ISA', 65, 12, 'ISA.65.12', 'I will destine you to the sword, and you will all bow down to the slaughter; because when I called, you didn’t answer. When I spoke, you didn’t listen; but you did that which was evil in my eyes, and chose that in which I didn’t delight.”'),
('ISA', 65, 13, 'ISA.65.13', 'Therefore the Lord GOD says, “Behold, my servants will eat, but you will be hungry; behold, my servants will drink, but you will be thirsty. Behold, my servants will rejoice, but you will be disappointed.'),
('ISA', 65, 14, 'ISA.65.14', 'Behold, my servants will sing for joy of heart, but you will cry for sorrow of heart, and will wail for anguish of spirit.'),
('ISA', 65, 15, 'ISA.65.15', 'You will leave your name for a curse to my chosen, and the Lord GOD will kill you. He will call his servants by another name,'),
('ISA', 65, 16, 'ISA.65.16', 'so that he who blesses himself on the earth will bless himself in the God of truth; and he who swears on the earth will swear by the God of truth; because the former troubles are forgotten, and because they are hidden from my eyes.'),
('ISA', 65, 17, 'ISA.65.17', '“For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth; and the former things will not be remembered, nor come into mind.'),
('ISA', 65, 18, 'ISA.65.18', 'But be glad and rejoice forever in that which I create; for, behold, I create Jerusalem to be a delight, and her people a joy.'),
('ISA', 65, 19, 'ISA.65.19', 'I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and delight in my people; and the voice of weeping and the voice of crying will be heard in her no more.'),
('ISA', 65, 20, 'ISA.65.20', '“No more will there be an infant who only lives a few days, nor an old man who has not filled his days; for the child will die one hundred years old, and the sinner being one hundred years old will be accursed.'),
('ISA', 65, 21, 'ISA.65.21', 'They will build houses and inhabit them. They will plant vineyards and eat their fruit.'),
('ISA', 65, 22, 'ISA.65.22', 'They will not build and another inhabit. They will not plant and another eat; for the days of my people will be like the days of a tree, and my chosen will long enjoy the work of their hands.'),
('ISA', 65, 23, 'ISA.65.23', 'They will not labor in vain nor give birth for calamity; for they are the offspring of the LORD’s blessed and their descendants with them.'),
('ISA', 65, 24, 'ISA.65.24', 'It will happen that before they call, I will answer; and while they are yet speaking, I will hear.'),
('ISA', 65, 25, 'ISA.65.25', 'The wolf and the lamb will feed together. The lion will eat straw like the ox. Dust will be the serpent’s food. They will not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 66, 1, 'ISA.66.1', 'The LORD says: “Heaven is my throne, and the earth is my footstool. What kind of house will you build to me? Where will I rest?'),
('ISA', 66, 2, 'ISA.66.2', 'For my hand has made all these things, and so all these things came to be,” says the LORD: “but I will look to this man, even to he who is poor and of a contrite spirit, and who trembles at my word.'),
('ISA', 66, 3, 'ISA.66.3', 'He who kills an ox is as he who kills a man; he who sacrifices a lamb, as he who breaks a dog’s neck; he who offers an offering, as he who offers pig’s blood; he who burns frankincense, as he who blesses an idol. Yes, they have chosen their own ways, and their soul delights in their abominations.'),
('ISA', 66, 4, 'ISA.66.4', 'I also will choose their delusions, and will bring their fears on them, because when I called, no one answered; when I spoke, they didn’t listen, but they did that which was evil in my eyes, and chose that in which I didn’t delight.”'),
('ISA', 66, 5, 'ISA.66.5', 'Hear the LORD’s word, you who tremble at his word: “Your brothers who hate you, who cast you out for my name’s sake, have said, ‘Let the LORD be glorified, that we may see your joy;’ but it is those who shall be disappointed.'),
('ISA', 66, 6, 'ISA.66.6', 'A voice of tumult from the city, a voice from the temple, a voice of the LORD that repays his enemies what they deserve.'),
('ISA', 66, 7, 'ISA.66.7', '“Before she travailed, she gave birth. Before her pain came, she delivered a son.'),
('ISA', 66, 8, 'ISA.66.8', 'Who has heard of such a thing? Who has seen such things? Shall a land be born in one day? Shall a nation be born at once? For as soon as Zion travailed, she gave birth to her children.'),
('ISA', 66, 9, 'ISA.66.9', 'Shall I bring to the birth, and not cause to be delivered?” says the LORD. “Shall I who cause to give birth shut the womb?” says your God.'),
('ISA', 66, 10, 'ISA.66.10', '“Rejoice with Jerusalem, and be glad for her, all you who love her. Rejoice for joy with her, all you who mourn over her;'),
('ISA', 66, 11, 'ISA.66.11', 'that you may nurse and be satisfied at the comforting breasts; that you may drink deeply, and be delighted with the abundance of her glory.”'),
('ISA', 66, 12, 'ISA.66.12', 'For the LORD says, “Behold, I will extend peace to her like a river, and the glory of the nations like an overflowing stream, and you will nurse. You will be carried on her side, and will be dandled on her knees.'),
('ISA', 66, 13, 'ISA.66.13', 'As one whom his mother comforts, so I will comfort you. You will be comforted in Jerusalem.”'),
('ISA', 66, 14, 'ISA.66.14', 'You will see it, and your heart shall rejoice, and your bones will flourish like the tender grass. The LORD’s hand will be known among his servants; and he will have indignation against his enemies.'),
('ISA', 66, 15, 'ISA.66.15', 'For, behold, the LORD will come with fire, and his chariots will be like the whirlwind; to give his anger with fierceness, and his rebuke with flames of fire.'),
('ISA', 66, 16, 'ISA.66.16', 'For the LORD will execute judgment by fire and by his sword on all flesh; and those slain by the LORD will be many.'),
('ISA', 66, 17, 'ISA.66.17', '“Those who sanctify themselves and purify themselves to go to the gardens, following one in the middle, eating pig’s meat, abominable things, and the mouse, they shall come to an end together,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 66, 18, 'ISA.66.18', '“For I know their works and their thoughts. The time comes that I will gather all nations and languages, and they will come, and will see my glory.'),
('ISA', 66, 19, 'ISA.66.19', '“I will set a sign among them, and I will send those who escape of them to the nations, to Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, who draw the bow, to Tubal and Javan, to far-away islands, who have not heard my fame, nor have seen my glory; and they shall declare my glory among the nations.'),
('ISA', 66, 20, 'ISA.66.20', 'They shall bring all your brothers out of all the nations for an offering to the LORD, on horses, in chariots, in litters, on mules, and on camels, to my holy mountain Jerusalem, says the LORD, as the children of Israel bring their offering in a clean vessel into the LORD’s house.'),
('ISA', 66, 21, 'ISA.66.21', 'Of them I will also select priests and Levites,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 66, 22, 'ISA.66.22', '“For as the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me,” says the LORD, “so your offspring and your name shall remain.'),
('ISA', 66, 23, 'ISA.66.23', 'It shall happen that from one new moon to another, and from one Sabbath to another, all flesh will come to worship before me,” says the LORD.'),
('ISA', 66, 24, 'ISA.66.24', '“They will go out, and look at the dead bodies of the men who have transgressed against me; for their worm will not die, nor will their fire be quenched, and they will be loathsome to all mankind.”'),
('JER', 1, 1, 'JER.1.1', 'The words of Jeremiah the son of Hilkiah, one of the priests who were in Anathoth in the land of Benjamin.'),
('JER', 1, 2, 'JER.1.2', 'The LORD’s word came to him in the days of Josiah the son of Amon, king of Judah, in the thirteenth year of his reign.'),
('JER', 1, 3, 'JER.1.3', 'It came also in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, to the end of the eleventh year of Zedekiah, the son of Josiah, king of Judah, to the carrying away of Jerusalem captive in the fifth month.'),
('JER', 1, 4, 'JER.1.4', 'Now the LORD’s word came to me, saying,'),
('JER', 1, 5, 'JER.1.5', '“Before I formed you in the womb, I knew you. Before you were born, I sanctified you. I have appointed you a prophet to the nations.”'),
('JER', 1, 6, 'JER.1.6', 'Then I said, “Ah, Lord GOD! Behold, I don’t know how to speak; for I am a child.”'),
('JER', 1, 7, 'JER.1.7', 'But the LORD said to me, “Don’t say, ‘I am a child;’ for you must go to whomever I send you, and you must say whatever I command you.'),
('JER', 1, 8, 'JER.1.8', 'Don’t be afraid because of them, for I am with you to rescue you,” says the LORD.'),
('JER', 1, 9, 'JER.1.9', 'Then the LORD stretched out his hand and touched my mouth. Then the LORD said to me, “Behold, I have put my words in your mouth.'),
('JER', 1, 10, 'JER.1.10', 'Behold, I have today set you over the nations and over the kingdoms, to uproot and to tear down, to destroy and to overthrow, to build and to plant.”'),
('JER', 1, 11, 'JER.1.11', 'Moreover the LORD’s word came to me, saying, “Jeremiah, what do you see?” I said, “I see a branch of an almond tree.”'),
('JER', 1, 12, 'JER.1.12', 'Then the LORD said to me, “You have seen well; for I watch over my word to perform it.”'),
('JER', 1, 13, 'JER.1.13', 'The LORD’s word came to me the second time, saying, “What do you see?” I said, “I see a boiling cauldron; and it is tipping away from the north.”'),
('JER', 1, 14, 'JER.1.14', 'Then the LORD said to me, “Out of the north, evil will break out on all the inhabitants of the land.'),
('JER', 1, 15, 'JER.1.15', 'For behold, I will call all the families of the kingdoms of the north,” says the LORD. “They will come, and they will each set his throne at the entrance of the gates of Jerusalem, and against all its walls all around, and against all the cities of Judah.'),
('JER', 1, 16, 'JER.1.16', 'I will utter my judgments against them concerning all their wickedness, in that they have forsaken me, and have burned incense to other gods, and worshiped the works of their own hands.'),
('JER', 1, 17, 'JER.1.17', '“You therefore put your belt on your waist, arise, and say to them all that I command you. Don’t be dismayed at them, lest I dismay you before them.'),
('JER', 1, 18, 'JER.1.18', 'For behold, I have made you today a fortified city, an iron pillar, and bronze walls against the whole land—against the kings of Judah, against its princes, against its priests, and against the people of the land.'),
('JER', 1, 19, 'JER.1.19', 'They will fight against you, but they will not prevail against you; for I am with you”, says the LORD, “to rescue you.”'),
('JER', 2, 1, 'JER.2.1', 'The LORD’s word came to me, saying,'),
('JER', 2, 2, 'JER.2.2', '“Go and proclaim in the ears of Jerusalem, saying, ‘The LORD says, “I remember for you the kindness of your youth, your love as a bride, how you went after me in the wilderness, in a land that was not sown.'),
('JER', 2, 3, 'JER.2.3', 'Israel was holiness to the LORD, the first fruits of his increase. All who devour him will be held guilty. Evil will come on them,”’ says the LORD.”'),
('JER', 2, 4, 'JER.2.4', 'Hear the LORD’s word, O house of Jacob, and all the families of the house of Israel!'),
('JER', 2, 5, 'JER.2.5', 'The LORD says, “What unrighteousness have your fathers found in me, that they have gone far from me, and have walked after worthless vanity, and have become worthless?'),
('JER', 2, 6, 'JER.2.6', 'They didn’t say, ‘Where is the LORD who brought us up out of the land of Egypt, who led us through the wilderness, through a land of deserts and of pits, through a land of drought and of the shadow of death, through a land that no one passed through, and where no man lived?’'),
('JER', 2, 7, 'JER.2.7', 'I brought you into a plentiful land to eat its fruit and its goodness; but when you entered, you defiled my land, and made my heritage an abomination.'),
('JER', 2, 8, 'JER.2.8', 'The priests didn’t say, ‘Where is the LORD?’ and those who handle the law didn’t know me. The rulers also transgressed against me, and the prophets prophesied by Baal and followed things that do not profit.'),
('JER', 2, 9, 'JER.2.9', '“Therefore I will yet contend with you,” says the LORD, “and I will contend with your children’s children.'),
('JER', 2, 10, 'JER.2.10', 'For pass over to the islands of Kittim, and see. Send to Kedar, and consider diligently, and see if there has been such a thing.'),
('JER', 2, 11, 'JER.2.11', 'Has a nation changed its gods, which really are no gods? But my people have changed their glory for that which doesn’t profit.'),
('JER', 2, 12, 'JER.2.12', '“Be astonished, you heavens, at this and be horribly afraid. Be very desolate,” says the LORD.'),
('JER', 2, 13, 'JER.2.13', '“For my people have committed two evils: they have forsaken me, the spring of living waters, and cut out cisterns for themselves: broken cisterns that can’t hold water.'),
('JER', 2, 14, 'JER.2.14', 'Is Israel a slave? Is he born into slavery? Why has he become a captive?'),
('JER', 2, 15, 'JER.2.15', 'The young lions have roared at him and raised their voices. They have made his land waste. His cities are burned up, without inhabitant.'),
('JER', 2, 16, 'JER.2.16', 'The children also of Memphis and Tahpanhes have broken the crown of your head.'),
('JER', 2, 17, 'JER.2.17', '“Haven’t you brought this on yourself, in that you have forsaken the LORD your God, when he led you by the way?'),
('JER', 2, 18, 'JER.2.18', 'Now what do you gain by going to Egypt, to drink the waters of the Shihor? Or why do you go on the way to Assyria, to drink the waters of the River?'),
('JER', 2, 19, 'JER.2.19', '“Your own wickedness will correct you, and your backsliding will rebuke you. Know therefore and see that it is an evil and bitter thing, that you have forsaken the LORD your God, and that my fear is not in you,” says the Lord, GOD of Armies.'),
('JER', 2, 20, 'JER.2.20', '“For long ago I broke off your yoke, and burst your bonds. You said, ‘I will not serve;’ for on every high hill and under every green tree you bowed yourself, playing the prostitute.'),
('JER', 2, 21, 'JER.2.21', 'Yet I had planted you a noble vine, a pure and faithful seed. How then have you turned into the degenerate branches of a foreign vine to me?'),
('JER', 2, 22, 'JER.2.22', 'For though you wash yourself with lye, and use much soap, yet your iniquity is marked before me,” says the Lord GOD.'),
('JER', 2, 23, 'JER.2.23', '“How can you say, ‘I am not defiled. I have not gone after the Baals’? See your way in the valley. Know what you have done. You are a swift dromedary traversing her ways,'),
('JER', 2, 24, 'JER.2.24', 'a wild donkey used to the wilderness, that sniffs the wind in her craving. When she is in heat, who can turn her away? All those who seek her will not weary themselves. In her month, they will find her.'),
('JER', 2, 25, 'JER.2.25', '“Keep your feet from being bare, and your throat from thirst. But you said, ‘It is in vain. No, for I have loved strangers, and I will go after them.’'),
('JER', 2, 26, 'JER.2.26', 'As the thief is ashamed when he is found, so the house of Israel is ashamed— they, their kings, their princes, their priests, and their prophets,'),
('JER', 2, 27, 'JER.2.27', 'who tell wood, ‘You are my father,’ and a stone, ‘You have given birth to me,’ for they have turned their back to me, and not their face, but in the time of their trouble they will say, ‘Arise, and save us!’'),
('JER', 2, 28, 'JER.2.28', '“But where are your gods that you have made for yourselves? Let them arise, if they can save you in the time of your trouble, for you have as many gods as you have towns, O Judah.'),
('JER', 2, 29, 'JER.2.29', '“Why will you contend with me? You all have transgressed against me,” says the LORD.'),
('JER', 2, 30, 'JER.2.30', '“I have struck your children in vain. They received no correction. Your own sword has devoured your prophets, like a destroying lion.'),
('JER', 2, 31, 'JER.2.31', 'Generation, consider the LORD’s word. Have I been a wilderness to Israel? Or a land of thick darkness? Why do my people say, ‘We have broken loose. We will come to you no more’?'),
('JER', 2, 32, 'JER.2.32', '“Can a virgin forget her ornaments, or a bride her attire? Yet my people have forgotten me for days without number.'),
('JER', 2, 33, 'JER.2.33', 'How well you prepare your way to seek love! Therefore you have even taught the wicked women your ways.'),
('JER', 2, 34, 'JER.2.34', 'Also the blood of the souls of the innocent poor is found in your skirts. You didn’t find them breaking in, but it is because of all these things.'),
('JER', 2, 35, 'JER.2.35', '“Yet you said, ‘I am innocent. Surely his anger has turned away from me.’ “Behold, I will judge you, because you say, ‘I have not sinned.’'),
('JER', 2, 36, 'JER.2.36', 'Why do you go about so much to change your ways? You will be ashamed of Egypt also, as you were ashamed of Assyria.'),
('JER', 2, 37, 'JER.2.37', 'You will also leave that place with your hands on your head; for the LORD has rejected those in whom you trust, and you won’t prosper with them.')
) as x(osis, chapter, verse, ref, body)
join public.books b on b.osis_code = x.osis
join public.bible_versions v on v.id = b.version_id and v.code = 'WEB'
join public.chapters c on c.book_id = b.id and c.number = x.chapter
on conflict (chapter_id, number) do update set osis_ref = excluded.osis_ref, text = excluded.text;
